{"parentUuid":"0c64b8de-b3e8-4671-b62d-1e51df58338c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"99b16262-9f33-47ea-9479-3426552856d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01THJZLzJhrxoR2GHsxwui1q","type":"tool_result","content":"36 matches in 1 files:\n\n1:# TokensNotes.md — every idea tried on entire-graph token savings\n11:## 0. The one law everything else obeys\n26:## 1. LIVE — not yet refuted\n28:### 1.1 MOD vs ADD task kind ⭐ best current idea\n56:### 1.2 One call must remove more than one message\n62:### 1.3 Harness suppression\n71:## 2. STRUCK — do not re-propose\n73:### ~~2.1 Session-length routing~~\n80:### ~~2.2 Language / repo gating~~\n85:### ~~2.3 Payload quality — eleven metrics~~\n91:### ~~2.4 \"Post-edit dominates 3.4×\"~~\n95:### ~~2.5 \"Grep dominates post-edit cost\"~~\n99:### ~~2.6 Per-loser repair~~\n103:### ~~2.7 Graph-call dose-response (1–3 calls is the sweet spot)~~\n111:### ~~2.8 Confidence / score-gap gating~~\n114:### ~~2.9 Locate-call reduction as a token lever~~\n118:### ~~2.10 Raising the turn cap~~\n121:### ~~2.11 Prefetching the search from issue text~~\n125:### ~~2.12 `EG_VERIFY_MODE=noworld`~~\n129:### ~~2.13 MCP as a token lever~~\n136:### ~~2.14 \"Restore the +22% by reverting the prompt fix\"~~\n143:## 3. Open questions\n145:### 3.1 A pre-run MOD/ADD classifier that actually works\n151:### 3.2 Why does Fable win where Opus doesn't?\n158:### 3.3 Is the ADD penalty avoidable rather than routable?\n  +11 more in /.../graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md [see remaining: tail -n +26 ~/Library/Application Support/rtk/tee/1786176650_grep_0_aph_bench_results_TokensNotes_md.log]\n===TAIL===\n\nEvery one passes the no-tool-arm test — they would help an arm with no tool — so this is the exact\ninstruction-class defect that turned a published −35% into +9.1% when removed.\n\n**Scope, verified:** `TOOLNOTE` reaches the prompt only at `run_3arm.sh:2327`, inside the `else`\nbranch of `if [ \"${PUBLISHED_EXACT:-0}\" = 1 ]` (`:2295`). **All cells in this campaign ran\n`PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`**, and a direct arm-diff of FABLEMAX confirmed the only difference is the\n11-line tool block. So FABLEMAX / OPUSHIGH / FABLEFIX / OPUSFIX / GEM300 are unaffected.\neg-vs-cmm is also unaffected (both arms get identical text via the same `sym_rules` call).\n**What IS invalid: any baseline-inclusive result produced through the legacy path.**\n\n### 7.7 graphmark PR verdicts (independent review, 7 agents)\n- **#53 → CLOSE.** Superseded: #54 contains every one of its commits\n  (`git merge-base --is-ancestor c10609c origin/eg-p1p2p3-nav-source-alias` = YES) and exists\n  specifically to delete what #53 adds. Its titled \"tightened search-only note\" is **not in the\n  diff** — reverted by 5d79ab1.\n- **#53 adds a real arm advantage.** `_egsrc.py:63-69,103-123` reads worktree files **off disk**\n  and prints up to `SRC_MAX_BYTES=2600` of verbatim source into the eg arm's search output; the cmm\n  arm gets locations only (`cmm-q:15`). The *harness*, not the tool, performs the read — free\n  edit-context that would otherwise cost a Read turn, measured against a turns/tokens metric.\n  #54's own rewritten header calls this \"a harness fairness violation\", naming #53's commit 55d967c.\n- **#53 adds a silent failure, inherited unfixed by #54.** `_egsrc.py:50-53`: `kept = hits` is a\n  no-op when `hits` is empty → `IndexError`. With `eg-q:18` swallowing stderr (`2>/dev/null`), any\n  binary failure or output-format drift makes **every** eg search return a traceback with the\n  ranked list destroyed — the \"payload announced but never shipped\" class again.\n- **#53's body claims a `netjail/git` block that does not exist** at head (11 files, none named\n  `git`), and `run_3arm.sh:129-130` says the opposite: \"git keeps network\". The repo-cache answer\n  leak is **unfixed** there.\n- Netjail itself is **symmetric and legitimate** — applied once at the shared `claude -p` call\n  before any arm branch.","is_error"