{"parentUuid":"610af71a-f81e-4cee-8b19-1a9428d6fa1d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdpwdfc7TDnSubjsJ4vc7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FUgjLMGYTsGeUqBrdSsRAC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n '1,30p;143,175p' /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md","description":"Read ledger head and open questions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2030,"cache_read_input_tokens":93251,"output_tokens":281,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2030,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":281,"cache_read_input_tokens":93251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2030,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2030},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpwdeNT8KPSgSEgTAnHk","type":"assistant","uuid":"6592a0da-7283-4685-ad32-3bd9906e9611","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:10:55.253Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"6592a0da-7283-4685-ad32-3bd9906e9611","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"99b16262-9f33-47ea-9479-3426552856d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FUgjLMGYTsGeUqBrdSsRAC","type":"tool_result","content":"# TokensNotes.md — every idea tried on entire-graph token savings\n\nRunning ledger. **Struck ideas stay struck, with the reason** — the failure modes here repeat, and\nre-proposing a dead lever has cost real money more than once.\n\nSign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**\nLast updated 2026-08-07. Owner: graph-bench agent. Companion channel: `AGENT-COMMS.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 0. The one law everything else obeys\n\n**Tokens are messages.** `log(tok) ~ log(msgs)`, elasticity **1.682**, r=**0.957**, n=536.\nMessage-adjusted residual saving is **0.000** in every model tested.\n\nConsequences, and they are hard constraints not preferences:\n- Nothing *inside* a message can move the metric. Only message **count** can.\n- An extra tool call is an extra message is **~+1.7% tokens**, mechanically.\n- Any lever must be expressed as \"removes N messages/session\" or it is not a lever.\n- `−1% messages = −1.68% tokens`.\n\nThis is why eleven payload-quality metrics died. It was never about payload quality.\n\n---\n\n## 1. LIVE — not yet refuted\n\n### 1.1 MOD vs ADD task kind ⭐ best current idea\nThe graph pays when the code to change **already exists and is broken**; it costs when the task is\nto **add behaviour that isn't there yet**.\n## 3. Open questions\n\n### 3.1 A pre-run MOD/ADD classifier that actually works\nKeyword approach failed (§1.1). Options not yet tried: a small LLM classification pass over the\nproblem statement (cheap, and it would have to be applied to *both* arms' routing decision to stay\nsymmetric); or a structural signal — does the issue name an existing symbol that resolves in the\ngraph? The second is appealing because the graph itself can answer it.\n\n### 3.2 Why does Fable win where Opus doesn't?\nFable pool **+19.1%** CI [+5.4, +30.0] n=26 (excludes zero); Opus pool **−1.4%** CI [−8.7, +5.6]\nn=197 (null). Fable emits ~37.5K output tok/session vs Opus ~20K, so it has more to save per\nmessage removed. **But** the within-instance model contrast on the 23 instances present in both a\nFable and an Opus cell is **+15.8pt [−3.0, +32.1] — spans zero.** Model × effort × cell ×\ninstance-set are perfectly confounded in FABLEMAX.\n\n### 3.3 Is the ADD penalty avoidable rather than routable?\nIf the graph could say *\"the thing you're describing does not exist here\"* instead of returning a\nplausible wrong hit, the ADD penalty might vanish without any routing. No verb does this today.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Workflow / method ideas (what to run, not what to believe)\n\n- **Adversarial refutation as standard.** Every finding gets N skeptics told to default to\n  *refuted* unless they can independently reproduce it. In the two workflows run today this killed\n  **9 of 20** claims, including three of my own.\n- **Count endpoints, not ratios.** A count (Δgrep, Δmsgs) is readable at n=30; a token geomean is\n  not (MDE 25–26pt). Any ratio with baseline in the denominator inherits division bias —\n  slope(log eg ~ log base) = **0.814**, so ~19% of *any* baseline-correlated predictor converts\n  mechanically into \"saving\".\n- **Never replicate an instance; always add instances.** Run-level noise is **86.9%** of paired\n  outcome variance. Var(mean) is minimised at k=1 runs per instance.\n- **Pre-register before spending.** Population, prediction, PASS/WEAK/FAIL, cost — written to a","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"24407bb7-92dc-4054-8bde-887692d37cda","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:10:55.296Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# TokensNotes.md — every idea tried on entire-graph token savings\n\nRunning ledger. **Struck ideas stay struck, with the reason** — the failure modes here repeat, and\nre-proposing a dead lever has cost real money more than once.\n\nSign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**\nLast updated 2026-08-07. Owner: graph-bench agent. Companion channel: `AGENT-COMMS.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 0. The one law everything else obeys\n\n**Tokens are messages.** `log(tok) ~ log(msgs)`, elasticity **1.682**, r=**0.957**, n=536.\nMessage-adjusted residual saving is **0.000** in every model tested.\n\nConsequences, and they are hard constraints not preferences:\n- Nothing *inside* a message can move the metric. Only message **count** can.\n- An extra tool call is an extra message is **~+1.7% tokens**, mechanically.\n- Any lever must be expressed as \"removes N messages/session\" or it is not a lever.\n- `−1% messages = −1.68% tokens`.\n\nThis is why eleven payload-quality metrics died. It was never about payload quality.\n\n---\n\n## 1. LIVE — not yet refuted\n\n### 1.1 MOD vs ADD task kind ⭐ best current idea\nThe graph pays when the code to change **already exists and is broken**; it costs when the task is\nto **add behaviour that isn't there yet**.\n## 3. Open questions\n\n### 3.1 A pre-run MOD/ADD classifier that actually works\nKeyword approach failed (§1.1). Options not yet tried: a small LLM classification pass over the\nproblem statement (cheap, and it would have to be applied to *both* arms' routing decision to stay\nsymmetric); or a structural signal — does the issue name an existing symbol that resolves in the\ngraph? The second is appealing because the graph itself can answer it.\n\n### 3.2 Why does Fable win where Opus doesn't?\nFable pool **+19.1%** CI [+5.4, +30.0] n=26 (excludes zero); Opus pool **−1.4%** CI [−8.7, +5.6]\nn=197 (null). Fable emits ~37.5K output tok/session vs Opus ~20K, so it has more to save per\nmessage removed. **But** the within-instance model contrast on the 23 instances present in both a\nFable and an Opus cell is **+15.8pt [−3.0, +32.1] — spans zero.** Model × effort × cell ×\ninstance-set are perfectly confounded in FABLEMAX.\n\n### 3.3 Is the ADD penalty avoidable rather than routable?\nIf the graph could say *\"the thing you're describing does not exist here\"* instead of returning a\nplausible wrong hit, the ADD penalty might vanish without any routing. No verb does this today.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Workflow / method ideas (what to run, not what to believe)\n\n- **Adversarial refutation as standard.** Every finding gets N skeptics told to default to\n  *refuted* unless they can independently reproduce it. In the two workflows run today this killed\n  **9 of 20** claims, including three of my own.\n- **Count endpoints, not ratios.** A count (Δgrep, Δmsgs) is readable at n=30; a token geomean is\n  not (MDE 25–26pt). Any ratio with baseline in the denominator inherits division bias —\n  slope(log eg ~ log base) = **0.814**, so ~19% of *any* baseline-correlated predictor converts\n  mechanically into \"saving\".\n- **Never replicate an instance; always add instances.** Run-level noise is **86.9%** of paired\n  outcome variance. Var(mean) is minimised at k=1 runs per instance.\n- **Pre-register before spending.** Population, prediction, PASS/WEAK/FAIL, cost — written to a","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6592a0da-7283-4685-ad32-3bd9906e9611","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"24407bb7-92dc-4054-8bde-887692d37cda","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdpwe1u19eM9YZaF6LQmV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1570,"cache_read_input_tokens":95281,"output_tokens":1812,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1570,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1812,"cache_read_input_tokens":95281,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1570},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpwdyrxwGazH3rzDNght","type":"assistant","uuid":"491184fb-4014-457b-87f8-6f35e61e95ff","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:11:06.367Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"491184fb-4014-457b-87f8-6f35e61e95ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdpwe1u19eM9YZaF6LQmV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XGNQHTsZwHvBgNVdCR4uzu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"P=graph-benchmarks-504800\nperl -e 'alarm shift; exec @ARGV' 280 gcloud compute ssh graphbench-c --project=$P --zone=us-east1-b --tunnel-through-iap --quiet --command='cd ~/work/graphmark/agentic-swebench && python3 - <<\"PY\"\nimport json,glob,os,math\ndef load(tag,arm):\n    d={}\n    for f in glob.glob(f\"results/{tag}/{arm}/*/cc_out.json\"):\n        iid=os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(f))\n        try: j=json.load(open(f))\n        except: continue\n        if j.get(\"subtype\")!=\"success\": continue\n        p=os.path.join(os.path.dirname(f),\"patch.diff\")\n        if not(os.path.exists(p) and os.path.getsize(p)>0): continue\n        u=j.get(\"usage\",{})\n        tok=sum(u.get(k,0) for k in (\"input_tokens\",\"output_tokens\",\"cache_read_input_tokens\",\"cache_creation_input_tokens\"))\n        d[iid]=dict(tok=tok,turns=j.get(\"num_turns\",0),out=u.get(\"output_tokens\",0))\n    return d\ntag=None\nfor t in [\"REP50_r1\",\"REP50\"]:\n    if os.path.isdir(f\"results/{t}_eg\") or os.path.isdir(f\"results/{t}\"): tag=t;break\ncands=[d for d in os.listdir(\"results\") if \"REP50\" in d.upper()]\nprint(\"dirs:\",sorted(cands)[:12])\ndef pick(arm):\n    for d in sorted(cands):\n        if d.lower().endswith(arm) or f\"_{arm}\" in d.lower():\n            if os.path.isdir(f\"results/{d}/{arm}\"): return f\"{d}\"\n    return None\nbe,bb=pick(\"eg\"),pick(\"baseline\")\nprint(\"using\",be,bb)\nE,B=load(be,\"eg\"),load(bb,\"baseline\")\nks=sorted(set(E)&set(B))\nte=sum(E[k][\"tok\"] for k in ks); tb=sum(B[k][\"tok\"] for k in ks)\nme=sum(E[k][\"turns\"] for k in ks); mb=sum(B[k][\"turns\"] for k in ks)\noe=sum(E[k][\"out\"] for k in ks); ob=sum(B[k][\"out\"] for k in ks)\nprint(f\"n={len(ks)}\")\nprint(f\"tokens  eg={te/1e6:.2f}M base={tb/1e6:.2f}M  TOKEN={(1-te/tb)*100:+.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"turns   eg={me} base={mb}  dTurns={(1-me/mb)*100:+.2f}%  ({me-mb:+d})\")\nprint(f\"output  eg={oe/1e3:.0f}k base={ob/1e3:.0f}k  d={(1-oe/ob)*100:+.2f}%\")\nneed=35/1.682\nprint(f\"LAW: 35% tokens needs {need:.1f}% fewer messages = {mb*need/100:.0f} of {mb} baseline turns removed\")\nprint(f\"     eg today removes {mb-me:+d} turns ({(1-me/mb)*100:+.1f}%)\")\nPY' 2>&1 | grep -vE 'NumPy|tcp-forward|WARNING|Warning'","description":"Compute rep50 turn budget vs 35% requirement","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1570,"cache_read_input_tokens":95281,"output_tokens":1812,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1570,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1812,"cache_read_input_tokens":95281,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1570},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpwdyrxwGazH3rzDNght","type":"assistant","uuid":"56e100f6-9a3f-459c-9fd1-6f72f6e26018","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:11:18.788Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
