{"parentUuid":"64cc099b-0744-4ce8-8eda-f93b33d440ad","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"99b16262-9f33-47ea-9479-3426552856d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HuVuNjRHPpdZ3F3sMuhSrf","type":"tool_result","content":"122\t# graph calls that returned NOTHING -- every one of them a `def` or `grep`, never a `search`. Their\n123\t# median token delta was -30.2% against +8.9% for sessions that got real content, and the prior\n124\t# live-session finding was harsher still: 3 of 4 sessions abandoned the tool permanently after one\n125\t# refusal. The failing calls are concrete: `def DatabaseManager`, `grep resubscribe`,\n126\t# `grep atan2|ATAN2`, `def FieldNamingPolicy`, `grep hide_qt_warning`, `grep netrc`, `grep heredoc`.\n127\t# A refusal costs a turn AND sends the agent back to shell exploration, which is exactly the\n128\t# behaviour that loses tokens (corr(delta tool-calls, delta tokens) = -0.854).\n129\t# So: never refuse. If def/grep yields nothing usable, degrade to the ranked search for the same\n130\t# term. This is a TOOL-OUTPUT change -- it ships no instruction, and the no-tool arm is untouched,\n131\t# so it cannot introduce arm asymmetry.\n132\t_egq_empty() {   # $1 = file holding candidate output\n133\t  grep -qE '[^[:space:]]' \"$1\" || return 0\n134\t  grep -qE '^\\((no symbol named|no matches|0 matches|grep failed)' \"$1\" && return 0\n135\t  return 1\n136\t}\n137\t_egq_out=\"$(mktemp 2>/dev/null || echo /tmp/egq_out.$$)\"\n138\t{\n139\tcase \"$verb\" in"}]},"uuid":"c2a33f86-2f12-4334-aa47-ad6a51711bdf","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:20:57.946Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench/tools/eg-q","content":"# graph calls that returned NOTHING -- every one of them a `def` or `grep`, never a `search`. Their\n# median token delta was -30.2% against +8.9% for sessions that got real content, and the prior\n# live-session finding was harsher still: 3 of 4 sessions abandoned the tool permanently after one\n# refusal. The failing calls are concrete: `def DatabaseManager`, `grep resubscribe`,\n# `grep atan2|ATAN2`, `def FieldNamingPolicy`, `grep hide_qt_warning`, `grep netrc`, `grep heredoc`.\n# A refusal costs a turn AND sends the agent back to shell exploration, which is exactly the\n# behaviour that loses tokens (corr(delta tool-calls, delta tokens) = -0.854).\n# So: never refuse. If def/grep yields nothing usable, degrade to the ranked search for the same\n# term. This is a TOOL-OUTPUT change -- it ships no instruction, and the no-tool arm is untouched,\n# so it cannot introduce arm asymmetry.\n_egq_empty() {   # $1 = file holding candidate output\n  grep -qE '[^[:space:]]' \"$1\" || return 0\n  grep -qE '^\\((no symbol named|no matches|0 matches|grep failed)' \"$1\" && return 0\n  return 1\n}\n_egq_out=\"$(mktemp 2>/dev/null || echo /tmp/egq_out.$$)\"\n{\ncase \"$verb\" in","numLines":18,"startLine":122,"totalLines":520}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"64cc099b-0744-4ce8-8eda-f93b33d440ad","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
