{"parentUuid":"b7b8b182-245c-46cf-8736-c8ff496aa2ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpxkHSfzsAHCr76zXT4k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017sSs7sUZ6p8zQLsJ8z41Fk","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/search.go","old_string":"\tresponse, err := sem.SearchRepository(ctx, repo, opts.Version, flags.Query, sem.SearchOptions{\n\t\tWorktree:              flags.Worktree,\n\t\tIgnoreFiles:           flags.IgnoreFiles,\n\t\tIncludeFiles:          flags.IncludeFiles,\n\t\tProfile:               profile,\n\t\tTopK:                  flags.TopK,","new_string":"\t// PATH SCOPE. The single largest class of shell exploration the graph fails to displace:\n\t// of 357 greps recorded across the 49 rep50 tool-arm sessions, 233 (65%) name a file or a\n\t// directory -- `grep -n \"retry_wait\\|backoff\" test/plugin/test_output_as_buffered_retries.rb`,\n\t// `grep -rn \"greater than\" tests/Validation/`. The agent already knows WHERE; it is asking\n\t// what is in there. Before this, search had no way to be told, and `--include-file` is not it\n\t// (that names a patterns file, .graphinclude-style, so passing a source path made search read\n\t// the file as ignore rules and still return out-of-scope hits).\n\t//\n\t// Over-fetch before filtering, because scoping after a top-8 cut usually leaves nothing: the\n\t// in-scope regions are rarely the globally top-ranked ones, which is the whole reason the agent\n\t// scoped in the first place.\n\tsearchTopK := flags.TopK\n\tif len(flags.PathScope) > 0 && searchTopK > 0 {\n\t\tsearchTopK = minInt(searchTopK*pathScopeOverfetch, pathScopeMaxFetch)\n\t}\n\tresponse, err := sem.SearchRepository(ctx, repo, opts.Version, flags.Query, sem.SearchOptions{\n\t\tWorktree:              flags.Worktree,\n\t\tIgnoreFiles:           flags.IgnoreFiles,\n\t\tIncludeFiles:          flags.IncludeFiles,\n\t\tProfile:  