{"parentUuid":"4249ab74-98c7-47e7-b0df-86f9256108a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpyJbpMzwbbGtLbubyk6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014VDuLX3PM7msJhqEiqgi2x","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && git add -A internal/cli && git status --short | head && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfeat(search,def): scope search by path, answer batched names in one call\n\nBoth verbs exist to displace shell exploration, and on rep50 they did not: the\ntool arm made 94 graph calls and still ran 905 shell exploration calls against\nthe no-tool arm's 995. That is 0.96 shell calls displaced per graph call, which\nis why the arm's turn count went UP by 38 while its token delta sat at +1.35%.\n\nClassifying all 357 greps those sessions ran says what they were asking for:\n\n  scoped to a file or directory   233  (65%)\n  batched multi-symbol             68  (19%, 192 names)\n  free text                        36  (10%)\n  single symbol                    20  ( 6%)\n\nsearch --path <dir|file|glob>\n  The largest class. The agent already knows WHERE and is asking what is in\n  there; there was no way to tell the graph. --include-file is not it: that\n  names a patterns file, so passing a source path made search read it as ignore\n  rules and still return out-of-scope hits. Over-fetches before filtering,\n  because in-scope regions are rarely the globally top-ranked ones -- that is\n  the whole reason the caller scoped. Falls back to the unscoped head when a\n  scope matches nothing, and renumbers ranks so a scoped payload does not open\n  at \"2.\" and read as though its top hit was lost in transit.\n\ndef --brief\n  The binary already accepted several names; with bodies it lost the contest it\n  exists to win. Measured on this repo for the same five names: batched grep\n  1,889 B, def with bodies 11,482 B, def --brief 895 B. Only the last wins on\n  bytes and messages at once. Single-symbol def is untouched and still ships the\n  full body -- that contract is measured, and \"show me this one function\" is a\n  read, not a survey.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit entire-graph changes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":596,"cache_read_input_tokens":180209,"output_tokens":2434,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":596,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2434,"cache_read_input_tokens":180209,"cache_creation_input_tokens":596,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":596},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpyJaU1Cd9evC4h61BJk","type":"assistant","uuid":"0c05e4f3-d7a9-4179-bf20-3d707e66cf6a","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:33:23.308Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
