{"parentUuid":"99fd99ba-db10-4b86-98ad-215ce0101fa0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdpzvJTxAWimY4Ky3ZW75","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"G3 is live — 6 drivers, both arms on binary `af18d641288a9135`, 12 instances spanning +71.0% to −127.4%.\n\n**Where this stands:**\n\nI was wrong about the ceiling, and the error was a denominator. I computed \"addressable\" on the *delta between arms*, which silently assumes eg's current behaviour is fixed. Measured against the baseline's own exploration pool instead:\n\n| | baseline | eg |\n|---|---|---|\n| shell exploration calls | 995 | 905 |\n| graph calls | 0 | 94 |\n\n**0.96 shell calls displaced per graph call** — substitution, not saving, which is why turns rose 38 while tokens sat at +1.35%. `corr(exploration eliminated, tokens saved) = +0.485` across all 49 pairs, and the instances already achieving 25–50% elimination run +28.4% mean.\n\nClassifying all 357 recorded greps found the tool simply couldn't answer them: 65% named a file or directory (**no path scoping existed**), 19% batched multiple symbols (**existed in the binary, unreachable through eg-q — it joined the names into one string and returned a no-match card**). Both are now fixed, committed (`607b2a4`, `8d6262ff`), 2210 tests green, and the byte economics inverted: for five names, batched grep 1,889 B vs `def --brief` **895 B**.\n\n**Two results I owe you:**\n- **G2 (post-edit rider): n=9, −14.48% total, median −24.82%, wins 3/9.** It lost. The rider fired 0/5 because 42/49 sessions make no post-edit graph call — that route is closed, as predicted.\n- A and B were preempted; I stood up E as a build host to produce the linux binary.\n\nG3 gates on displacement ratio (≥2.0, from 0.96), not tokens — at n=12 the token MDE is ~30pt against a ~100pt noise floor, so I won't make a token claim from it either way. If displacement moves, the population arithmetic reaches the mid-20s and 35% becomes a question of how much further the remaining classes go; if it doesn't, adoption is the wall and I'll say so."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":209394,"output_tokens":1592,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":671,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1592,"cache_read_input_tokens":209394,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":671},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdpzvGvgZRKgYJqzmqSe1","type":"assistant","uuid":"39c23142-e69c-4518-afc3-6c14ca7b048c","timestamp":"2026-08-08T08:54:23.164Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
