{"parentUuid":"8b6b65e9-81bb-4e22-b4ae-534888703056","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md","snippet":"1\t# entire-graph → 35%: the route, the arithmetic, and the one intervention that reaches it\n2\t\n3\t**Written 2026-08-08. Supersedes `PLAN-TO-35PCT.md`, whose gate ladder ran to completion and\n4\tfailed at G1, G2 and G3.** Every number here is measured on the rep50 cell (49 gated pairs,\n5\tClaude Opus, SWE-bench Multilingual) unless marked as a projection.\n6\t\n7\tSign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## 0. The problem, in one ratio\n12\t\n13\tAcross all 49 pairs:\n14\t\n15\t| | count |\n16\t|---|---|\n17\t| graph calls made by the eg arm | **94** |\n18\t| shell-exploration calls eliminated | 72 |\n19\t| harness runs eliminated | 31 |\n20\t| **messages eliminated, total** | **103** |\n21\t| **net messages saved** (103 − 94) | **9** |\n22\t\n23\t**Eliminations per graph call: 1.10.**\n24\t\n25\tNine messages out of 2,671 is 0.34% of the message count. Under the governing law\n26\t(`log tok ~ log msgs`, elasticity **1.682**, r=**0.957**, n=536) that predicts ≈ +0.6% tokens.\n27\tMeasured headline: **+1.35%**. The model and the measurement agree.\n28\t\n29\t**35% requires removing 556 of the 2,671 baseline turns.** At the current call volume that means\n30\teach graph call must eliminate **6.9 messages instead of 1.10** — a **6.3× move**. This single\n31\tnumber is the whole problem, and every proposal below is judged against it.\n32\t\n33\t---\n34\t\n35\t## 1. Where the removable turns actually are\n36\t\n37\tBaseline, all 49 sessions, phase-split at the first `Edit`/`Write`:\n38\t\n39\t| bucket | calls | share of 2,671 | eg's count | eliminated |\n40\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n41\t| shell exploration | **855** | 32.0% | 783 | 72 (8.4%) |\n42\t| harness runs (test/build) | **576** | 21.6% | 545 | 31 (5.4%) |\n43\t| other bash | 524 | 19.6% | 524 | 0 |\n44\t| edits | 397 | 14.9% | 414 | −17 |\n45\t| file reads | 240 | 9.0% | 238 | 2 |\n46\t| waits / kills | 62 | 2.3% | 62 | 0 |\n47\t| graph calls | 0 | — | 94 | −94 |\n48\t\n49\tShell exploration breakdown (baseline): `grep` 409, `ls` 263, `sed` 161, `cat` 107, `find` 36.\n50\t\n51\t**Only two buckets are addressable by a code graph — exploration (855) and harness (576).**\n52\tTogether they are 1,431 turns, so 556 is 39% of the addressable pool. It is not arithmetically\n53\timpossible. It is behaviourally hard, for the reason in §2.\n54\t\n55\t---\n56\t\n57\t## 2. The mechanism, measured — and a correction to the previous plan\n58\t\n59\tSplit the 49 pairs by outcome:\n60\t\n61\t| | n | pts | eg shell | base shell | shell elim. | eg harness | base harness | harness elim. | graph calls |\n62\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n63\t| **lift** | 24 | +21.21 | 370 | 440 | **+70** | 229 | 344 | **+115** | 50 |\n64\t| **drag** | 25 | −19.86 | **413** | **415** | **+2** | 316 | 232 | **−84** | 44 |\n65\t\n66\tThree things follow, and two of them correct claims I previously made.\n67\t\n68\t**2.1 — In the losing half the graph displaced nothing.** 413 vs 415 shell calls. Two out of 415.\n69\tThe payload was delivered and the agent explored exactly as much as it would have without it.\n70\tGraph-call counts are near-identical between the halves (44 vs 50), so this is *not* a usage\n71\tdifference. It is whether the answer landed.\n72\t\n73\t**2.2 — CORRECTION: eg does not verify more than the baseline. It verifies less.**\n74\tPopulation: **eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576**. Post-edit specifically: **eg 384 vs 422**.\n75\tThe earlier claim (\"eg runs `./runtest` 11× vs baseline 7×\") was computed on the *8 worst\n76\tlosers* — a set selected on the outcome. Over-verification is what a losing session looks like in\n77\t*either* arm:\n78\t\n79\t| group | eg runs/session | base runs/session |\n80\t|---|---|---|\n81\t| eg won (24) | 6.3 | 10.0 |\n82\t| eg lost (25) | 9.3 | 7.3 |\n83\t| 8 worst losers | 12.4 | 7.9 |\n84\t\n85\t`corr(Δharness runs, tokens saved) = −0.612`, n=49. Verification looping *is* the loss mechanism,\n86\tbut eg's defect is **variance, not tendency**. Excluding three blow-up sessions the arm runs\n87\t**327 vs 402**. This also answers the external objection directly: the baseline is not cheaper at\n88\ttesting, and eg is not running more tests.\n89\t\n90\t**2.3 — The biggest win is the baseline blowing up, not eg being efficient.**\n91\t`lombok-3674` (+6.09 pts, +71.0%) — baseline ran `javac` **70 times**, eg ran it 23. Same\n92\tmechanism as the losses, opposite arm. The headline is the difference of two blow-up processes\n93\tthat hit either arm at roughly a coin flip: drag −19.86, lift +21.21, net +1.35.\n94\t\n95\t---\n96\t\n97\t## 3. The ceiling of loser repair, computed exactly\n98\t\n99\tThe drag pool is **−19.86 points** spread over 25 instances; the top five carry **−11.42 (57%)**.\n100\t\n101\t> **If every losing instance were made exactly neutral, the headline would be +21.21%.**\n102\t\n103\tThat is not a projection — it is the sum of the lift pool. **Loser repair cannot reach 35%\n104\tby definition.** Reaching 35% additionally requires the *winners* to improve by ~65% beyond what\n105\tthey already deliver.\n106\t\n107\tAnd loser repair is not even available at full strength: **~93% of losing instances flip sign\n108\tbetween cells** (median same-instance swing 99.9 pts, max 294). \"The 22 losers\" is not a stable\n109\ttarget set; only a change applied to every instance can work.\n110\t\n111\t---\n112\t\n113\t## 4. Why three built capabilities changed nothing\n114\t\n115\t| capability | where advertised | adoption |\n116\t|---|---|---|\n117\t| `impact` | affordance tail | **0 / 49** |\n118\t| `changed` (G1) | affordance tail | **0 / 5** |\n119\t| `--path` scoping (G3) | affordance tail | **0 / 12** |\n120\t| `search` | primary instruction | 33 / 49 |\n121\t| `grep` | primary instruction | 34 / 49 |\n122\t| `def` | primary instruction | 19 / 49 |\n123\t\n124\t**Everything named in the primary instruction gets used. Everything in the tail gets ~zero.**\n125\tG3 is the cleanest read: adding two genuinely useful capabilities moved graph calls *up*\n126\t(1.9 → 3.1 per session) and displacement *down* (0.96 → 0.76). More calls, less removed.\n127\t\n128\t**Consequence, and it is binding on everything below: any proposal that requires the agent to\n129\tchoose to reach for something new has a measured 0/66 track record. Do not build a fourth.**\n130\t\n131\t---\n132\t\n133\t## 5. The route: attack the ratio's two sides separately\n134\t\n135\t`eliminations per call = messages_removed / calls_made`. There are exactly two ways up.\n136\t\n137\t### R-A — Drive the denominator to zero: zero-toll delivery *(fair, cheap, untested on this metric)*\n138\t\n139\tThe graph's 94 calls are 94 messages of pure overhead. The tool already implements free delivery:\n140\t`internal/cli/search.go` — *\"ZERO-TOLL DELIVERY. When the caller has already computed this\n141\tsession's payload and handed it to the agent inside context the session pays for anyway, this\n142\tcall must cost nothing: echo those bytes and return.\"* (`opts.Env.PresearchPath`.)\n143\t\n144\tCompute the payload from the issue text before the session starts and place it in turn 0.\n145\t\n146\t- **Effect:** removes 94 messages outright = 3.5% of messages ≈ **+5.9% tokens**.\n147\t- **Risk:** prefetched retrieval is worse than the agent's own distilled query — gold-visible@5\n148\t  **0.567 vs 0.715**. If eliminations fall 103 → ~70, net becomes 70 vs today's 9.\n149\t- **Projected headline: +5% to +9%.**\n150\t- **Why it was previously dismissed, and why that was wrong:** prefetch was struck on *retrieval\n151\t  quality*. Under the message law retrieval quality is not the metric — message count is. A\n152\t  worse payload delivered for free can beat a better payload that costs a turn. This has never\n153\t  been measured on tokens.\n154\t- **Fairness:** payload, not instruction. It ships no advice; the no-tool arm cannot produce it.\n155\t  Same class as the search result itself. **Fair.**\n156\t\n157\t### R-B — Drive the numerator up: answer the command the agent already types *(reaches 35%, but changes the claim)*\n158\t\n159\tThe agent types `grep` **409 times** across 49 sessions and `entire` 94 times. Adoption of the\n160\tgraph is 1.9 calls/session; adoption of grep is 8.3.\n161\t\n162\t**Put the graph behind `grep` itself** — a PATH shim in the eg arm that answers a grep with the\n163\tenclosing symbol, its complete body and its callers, instead of matching lines.\n164\t\n\n... [98 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bea0e956-26d6-4cde-817b-a165cb8a927f","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:29:45.145Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"bea0e956-26d6-4cde-817b-a165cb8a927f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqSXaN4Esss8Nohuq3Wu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013n3dXeMF3KeKjYwxsEdLLR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"P=graph-benchmarks-504800\ncat > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49/scratchpad/h1.py <<'PY'\n# H1 falsification: after each grep, what does the agent do NEXT?\n# A graph-backed grep can only remove the follow-up if the follow-up is a read/grep of\n# something the grep already pointed at.\nimport json,glob,os,re,collections\nIDX={os.path.basename(f)[:-6]:f for f in glob.glob(os.path.expanduser(\"~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl\"))}\nSHELL=(\"grep\",\"rg\",\"ls\",\"sed\",\"cat\",\"find\",\"head\",\"tail\",\"awk\")\ndef seq(tag,arm):\n    out=[]\n    for cj in glob.glob(f\"results/{tag}/{arm}/*/cc_out.json\"):\n        try: j=json.load(open(cj))\n        except: continue\n        if j.get(\"subtype\")!=\"success\": continue\n        p=os.path.join(os.path.dirname(cj),\"patch.diff\")\n        if not(os.path.exists(p) and os.path.getsize(p)>0): continue\n        tf=IDX.get(j.get(\"session_id\"))\n        if not tf: continue\n        calls=[]; res={}\n        for line in open(tf,errors=\"ignore\"):\n            try: m=json.loads(line)\n            except: continue\n            msg=m.get(\"message\") or {}\n            if msg.get(\"role\")==\"assistant\":\n                for b in (msg.get(\"content\") or []):\n                    if isinstance(b,dict) and b.get(\"type\")==\"tool_use\":\n                        calls.append((b.get(\"id\"),b.get(\"name\"),(b.get(\"input\") or {})))\n            elif msg.get(\"role\")==\"user\":\n                for b in (msg.get(\"content\") or []):\n                    if isinstance(b,dict) and b.get(\"type\")==\"tool_result\":\n                        t=b.get(\"content\")\n                        if isinstance(t,list): t=\" \".join(x.get(\"text\",\"\") for x in t if isinstance(x,dict))\n                        res[b.get(\"tool_use_id\")]=(t or \"\")[:20000]\n        out.append((calls,res))\n    return out\nPATH_RX=re.compile(r'([A-Za-z0-9_./\\-]+\\.(?:py|go|rb|php|rs|js|ts|tsx|java|c|cc|cpp|h|hpp|tcl|scala|kt|cs|swift))')\ndef analyse(sessions,lbl):\n    nxt=collections.Counter(); tot=0; covered=0; grep_ret=collections.Counter()\n    for calls,res in sessions:\n        for i,(cid,name,inp) in enumerate(calls):\n            if name!=\"Bash\": continue\n            cmd=(inp.get(\"command\") or \"\").strip()\n            h=os.path.basename(cmd.split()[0]) if cmd.split() else \"\"\n            if h not in (\"grep\",\"rg\"): continue\n            tot+=1\n            out=res.get(cid,\"\")\n            files=set(PATH_RX.findall(out))\n            grep_ret[\"files_\"+(\"0\" if not files else \"1\" if len(files)==1 else \"2-5\" if len(files)<=5 else \"6+\")]+=1\n            # what is the next tool call?\n            if i+1>=len(calls): nxt[\"<end>\"]+=1; continue\n            _,n2,i2=calls[i+1]\n            if n2==\"Read\":\n                fp=str(i2.get(\"file_path\",\"\"))\n                nxt[\"Read\"]+=1\n                if any(f in fp or fp.endswith(f) for f in files): covered+=1; nxt[\"Read-in-grep-output\"]+=1\n            elif n2 in (\"Edit\",\"Write\",\"MultiEdit\"):\n                fp=str(i2.get(\"file_path\",\"\"))\n                nxt[\"Edit\"]+=1\n                if any(f in fp or fp.endswith(f) for f in files): covered+=1; nxt[\"Edit-in-grep-output\"]+=1\n            elif n2==\"Bash\":\n                c2=(i2.get(\"command\") or \"\").strip()\n                h2=os.path.basename(c2.split()[0]) if c2.split() else \"\"\n                if h2 in (\"grep\",\"rg\"): nxt[\"grep-again\"]+=1; covered+=1\n                elif h2 in (\"sed\",\"cat\",\"head\",\"tail\"):\n                    nxt[\"read-shell\"]+=1\n                    if any(f in c2 for f in files): covered+=1; nxt[\"read-shell-in-output\"]+=1\n                elif h2 in SHELL: nxt[\"other-shell\"]+=1\n                else: nxt[\"bash-other\"]+=1\n            else: nxt[n2 or \"?\"]+=1\n    print(f\"--- {lbl}: {tot} greps\")\n    print(f\"    files named in grep OUTPUT: {dict(grep_ret)}\")\n    for k,v in nxt.most_common(12): print(f\"    next={k:26s} {v:4d}  {v/max(tot,1)*100:4.1f}%\")\n    print(f\"    ADDRESSABLE follow-ups (next action targets something the grep already surfaced,\")\n    print(f\"    or is another grep): {covered}/{tot} = {covered/max(tot,1)*100:.1f}%\")\nanalyse(seq(\"REP50_r1_eg\",\"eg\"),\"eg arm\")\nanalyse(seq(\"REP50_r1_baseline\",\"baseline\"),\"baseline arm\")\nPY\nperl -e 'alarm shift; exec @ARGV' 600 gcloud compute ssh graphbench-c --project=$P --zone=us-east1-b --tunnel-through-iap --quiet --command=\"cd ~/work/graphmark/agentic-swebench && cat > /tmp/h1.py <<'EOF'\n$(cat /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49/scratchpad/h1.py)\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/h1.py\" 2>&1 | grep -vE 'NumPy|tcp-forward|WARNING|Warning'","description":"H1 falsification: what follows each grep","timeout":700000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4140,"cache_read_input_tokens":413935,"output_tokens":2169,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4140,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2169,"cache_read_input_tokens":413935,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4140},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqSXVxtaJv8kqDJta3jq","attributionSkill":"artifact-design","type":"assistant","uuid":"bf1c9803-624d-4d4e-9732-9716be0fcfc1","timestamp":"2026-0