{"parentUuid":"bf1c9803-624d-4d4e-9732-9716be0fcfc1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d6032c5e-0887-4a82-a3cb-2a093f118b85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013n3dXeMF3KeKjYwxsEdLLR","type":"tool_result","content":"--- eg arm: 357 greps\n    files named in grep OUTPUT: {'files_2-5': 130, 'files_0': 106, 'files_1': 78, 'files_6+': 43}\n    next=grep-again                   97  27.2%\n    next=read-shell                   73  20.4%\n    next=bash-other                   65  18.2%\n    next=Read                         53  14.8%\n    next=other-shell                  38  10.6%\n    next=Edit                         31   8.7%\n    next=Read-in-grep-output          21   5.9%\n    next=read-shell-in-output         20   5.6%\n    next=Edit-in-grep-output           1   0.3%\n    ADDRESSABLE follow-ups (next action targets something the grep already surfaced,\n    or is another grep): 139/357 = 38.9%\n--- baseline arm: 409 greps\n    files named in grep OUTPUT: {'files_2-5': 130, 'files_1': 103, 'files_0': 124, 'files_6+': 52}\n    next=grep-again                  112  27.4%\n    next=bash-other                   85  20.8%\n    next=read-shell                   84  20.5%\n    next=Read                         51  12.5%\n    next=other-shell                  44  10.8%\n    next=Edit                         31   7.6%\n    next=Read-in-grep-output          24   5.9%\n    next=read-shell-in-output         20   4.9%\n    next=Edit-in-grep-output           2   0.5%\n    next=<end>                         2   0.5%\n    ADDRESSABLE follow-ups (next action targets something the grep already surfaced,\n    or is another grep): 158/409 = 38.6%","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ae9a018a-3c47-4fd1-b6ae-5beca069cafc","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:30:14.389Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"--- eg arm: 357 greps\n    files named in grep OUTPUT: {'files_2-5': 130, 'files_0': 106, 'files_1': 78, 'files_6+': 43}\n    next=grep-again                   97  27.2%\n    next=read-shell                   73  20.4%\n    next=bash-other                   65  18.2%\n    next=Read                         53  14.8%\n    next=other-shell                  38  10.6%\n    next=Edit                         31   8.7%\n    next=Read-in-grep-output          21   5.9%\n    next=read-shell-in-output         20   5.6%\n    next=Edit-in-grep-output           1   0.3%\n    ADDRESSABLE follow-ups (next action targets something the grep already surfaced,\n    or is another grep): 139/357 = 38.9%\n--- baseline arm: 409 greps\n    files named in grep OUTPUT: {'files_2-5': 130, 'files_1': 103, 'files_0': 124, 'files_6+': 52}\n    next=grep-again                  112  27.4%\n    next=bash-other                   85  20.8%\n    next=read-shell                   84  20.5%\n    next=Read                         51  12.5%\n    next=other-shell                  44  10.8%\n    next=Edit                         31   7.6%\n    next=Read-in-grep-output          24   5.9%\n    next=read-shell-in-output         20   4.9%\n    next=Edit-in-grep-output           2   0.5%\n    next=<end>                         2   0.5%\n    ADDRESSABLE follow-ups (next action targets something the grep already surfaced,\n    or is another grep): 158/409 = 38.6%","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf1c9803-624d-4d4e-9732-9716be0fcfc1","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"ae9a018a-3c47-4fd1-b6ae-5beca069cafc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqSZonFyGtHKnhT1Gx5w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2727,"cache_read_input_tokens":418075,"output_tokens":4573,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2727,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4573,"cache_read_input_tokens":418075,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2727},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqSZen2UvxqiATkJ8wsd","attributionSkill":"artifact-design","type":"assistant","uuid":"210f2bf6-b90f-4eb5-b07a-f75df939ae0b","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:30:39.712Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"210f2bf6-b90f-4eb5-b07a-f75df939ae0b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqSZonFyGtHKnhT1Gx5w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My own kill criterion just fired. H1 was pre-registered as *\"if under 40%, R-B does not reach 35% — stop\"*:\n\n| next action after a grep | eg | baseline |\n|---|---|---|\n| another grep | 27.2% | 27.4% |\n| read of a file the grep surfaced | 5.9% | 5.9% |\n| shell-read of a surfaced file | 5.6% | 4.9% |\n| **addressable total** | **38.9%** | 38.6% |\n| bash-other / other-shell / reads elsewhere | 61.1% | 61.4% |\n\n**38.9%.** And it corrects my own projection: I assumed every shimmed grep removes one follow-up (~400 messages, +25%). Only **139** have an addressable follow-up.\n\n- R-B realistic: 139 messages = 5.1% of turns = **+8.6% tokens** (conservative, excluding re-greps: **+2.6%**)\n- R-A: 94 messages = **+5.9%**\n- **Both, working perfectly: ~+15%**\n\nThat is the seventh independent route landing in the same place as the best fair cell ever measured (+17.21%). Recording the falsification:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2727,"cache_read_input_tokens":418075,"output_tokens":4573,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2727,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4573,"cache_read_input_tokens":418075,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2727},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqSZen2UvxqiATkJ8wsd","attributionSkill":"artifact-design","type":"assistant","uuid":"d430af71-e12c-475d-aa4d-d073fb477c73","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:30:43.701Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"d430af71-e12c-475d-aa4d-d073fb477c73","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqSZonFyGtHKnhT1Gx5w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K2nA4yzWVhp1gbVzAvZqHu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md'; s=open(p).read()\n\nold_rb = s[s.index(\"- **Effect if each shimmed grep removes one follow-up read/grep:**\"):s.index(\"### R-C\")]\nnew_rb = \"\"\"- **STATUS: FALSIFIED BY H1 (offline, $0, run 2026-08-08). See §7.1.**\n- The projection below was wrong by ~3× and the offline replay caught it before a cell was spent.\n\n  | claimed | measured |\n  |---|---|\n  | every shimmed grep removes ~1 follow-up → ~400 messages → +25% | only **38.9%** of greps have an addressable follow-up → **139 messages** → **+8.6%** |\n\n- **Realistic effect: +2.6% (conservative) to +8.6% (generous).** Conservative excludes the 27.2%\n  of cases where the next action is another grep, since a graph-backed grep may equally *cause*\n  a re-grep when its output shape is unfamiliar.\n- **Fairness — the decision is now moot, but recorded for the file.**\n  - *For:* it is tool output. No instruction is added. The baseline has real grep, the tool arm a\n    code-aware grep — same class as having `entire graph search`, same mechanism as the existing\n    `entire` PATH shim.\n  - *Against:* it silently redefines a standard command, so the arms no longer run the same\n    program. That is environment divergence rather than tool provision.\n  - **Assessment: defensible under the letter of the doctrine, but it changes the claim from\n    \"a code graph saves tokens\" to \"replacing grep with a code-aware grep saves tokens.\"** It\n    would have had to be labelled as such. Since it does not reach the goal either, the question\n    does not need deciding.\n  - Residual risk if built anyway: the agent greps logs, build files and changelogs, not only\n    code. A shim that mangles those sends it back to `/usr/bin/grep` and costs a turn.\n\n\"\"\"\ns = s.replace(old_rb, new_rb)\n\n# Rewrite §7 gates with the H1 result, and §8 with the settled ceiling.\ni7 = s.index(\"## 7. Gates\"); i8 = s.index(\"## 8. What is true regardless\")\ns = s[:i7] + \"\"\"## 7. Gates — H1 has run, and it stopped the plan\n\nMechanism counts only below n≈30. MDE is ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor,\nso **no token claim may be made from a small cell in either direction** — a discipline G3\nviolated in spirit by swinging −37.7 → +9.8 → −1.2 across three polls of the same cell.\n\n| gate | what | n | criterion | result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **H0** | offline, $0 | 0 | shim answers recorded greps, degrades on non-code | not run |\n| **H1** | replay, $0 | 766 greps | ≥60% of greps have a follow-up a graph answer could remove | **38.9% — FAILED** |\n| H2 | live, both arms | 12 | eliminations per graph call ≥3.0 | not reached |\n| H3 | live, both arms | 30 | ≥5.0 per call | not reached |\n| H4 | full rep50 | 49 | first token claim, bootstrap CI, total and median | not reached |\n\n### 7.1 H1, in full\n\nFor every recorded grep in both arms, what the agent did on the *very next* tool call:\n\n| next action | eg (357 greps) | baseline (409) | addressable? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| another grep | 27.2% | 27.4% | generously |\n| `Read` of a file the grep surfaced | 5.9% | 5.9% | yes |\n| shell-read (`sed`/`cat`/`head`) of a surfaced file | 5.6% | 4.9% | yes |\n| `Edit` of a surfaced file | 0.3% | 0.5% | yes |\n| `Read` of a file the grep did *not* surface | 8.9% | 6.6% | no |\n| shell-read elsewhere | 14.8% | 15.6% | no |\n| other bash | 18.2% | 20.8% | no |\n| other shell | 10.6% | 10.8% | no |\n| `Edit` elsewhere | 8.4% | 7.1% | no |\n| **addressable total** | **38.9%** | **38.6%** | |\n\nAlso measured: **106 of 357 eg greps (29.7%) returned no file at all** — a failed search. The\narms are statistically identical on every row, which is itself informative: grep behaviour is a\nproperty of the agent, not of whether it has a graph.\n\n**Pre-registered kill criterion #1 fired.** R-B does not reach 35%.\n\n\"\"\" + s[i8:]\n\nold8 = s[s.index(\"## 8. What is true regardless\"):s.index(\"## 9. Open defects\")]\nnew8 = \"\"\"## 8. Settled: the honest ceiling, and it is not 35%\n\nAdding every route on the table, assuming each works perfectly and they do not overlap:\n\n| | messages saved | of 2,671 | tokens (×1.682) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| achieved today | 9 | 0.3% | +1.35% (measured) |\n| R-A zero-toll delivery | +94 | 3.5% | +5.9% |\n| R-B graph-backed grep (generous) | +139 | 5.2% | +8.6% |\n| **all three** | **242** | **9.1%** | **≈ +15%** |\n\n**35% needs 556 messages. Everything on the table sums to 242.**\n\nIndependent estimates, all converging:\n\n| route | ceiling |\n|---|---|\n| loser repair made perfect (= the lift pool, exact) | **+21.21%** |\n| best fair cell ever measured (opus xhigh, n=26) | **+17.21%** |\n| R-A + R-B + current, perfect execution | **≈ +15%** |\n| directly addressable post-edit waste (hand-classified, 763 calls) | +2.67% to +4.57% |\n| expensive-baseline tercile (78% of token mass) | +8.07% |\n\n**Conclusion: 35% is not reachable on this benchmark by any fair tool-side change.** The graph\nremoves 8.4% of exploration and 5.4% of harness runs; adding capability made both worse (G3);\nthe follow-up structure of the agent's greps caps interception at 38.9%; and the loser pool is\nonly 19.86 points wide. The one class of intervention that *would* reach 35% is an instruction\ntelling the agent to explore and re-test less — which passes no fairness test, because it would\nhelp a no-tool arm equally. **That is precisely what the withdrawn −35% contained**, and it is\nwhy removing two such sentences moved the same cell from −14.9% to +9.1%.\n\n**What to say instead.** The tool is worth a high-single-digit to mid-teens token saving on this\nworkload, it is *negative* on short sessions, and its variance is larger than its mean. The\ndefensible claim to publish is the fair paired measurement with its interval, alongside what it\ndoes for correctness and latency — not a headline percentage.\n\n\"\"\"\ns = s.replace(old8, new8)\ns = s.replace(\"# entire-graph → 35%: the route, the arithmetic, and the one intervention that reaches it\",\n              \"# entire-graph → 35%: the routes, the arithmetic, and why none of them reach it\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"updated\", len(s), \"bytes\")\nPY\ngrep -n \"FAILED\\|38.9%\\|≈ +15%\\|not reachable\" EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md | head","description":"Record H1 falsification in plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2727,"cache_read_input_tokens":418075,"output_tokens":4573,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2727,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4573,"cache_read_input_tokens":418075,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2727},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqSZen2UvxqiATkJ8wsd","attributionSkill":"artifact-design","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4c074f5-8881-4de1-9399-71534a085dec","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:31:16.597Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
