{"parentUuid":"f16bd0f5-8dac-49ca-9e16-b0cf98ec8948","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqSebgdFcwuRPM5UyYvo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4855,"cache_read_input_tokens":420802,"output_tokens":1066,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4855,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1066,"cache_read_input_tokens":420802,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4855},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqSeXKwWumQ3vfjAuW58","attributionSkill":"artifact-design","type":"assistant","uuid":"5ade695d-2f4a-418b-a435-652168fe337f","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:31:27.914Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"5ade695d-2f4a-418b-a435-652168fe337f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqSebgdFcwuRPM5UyYvo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mgt9CT9kC2pv18sTNJJn82","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/eg-per-call-economics.md","content":"---\nname: eg-per-call-economics\ndescription: \"THE defining ratio for entire-graph token savings — 94 graph calls eliminate 103 messages (1.10 per call); 35% requires 6.9 per call, a 6.3x move\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nMeasured on rep50 (49 gated pairs, Opus). This single ratio explains the headline and bounds\nevery proposal.\n\n| | count |\n|---|---|\n| graph calls made | **94** |\n| shell-exploration calls eliminated | 72 |\n| harness runs eliminated | 31 |\n| messages eliminated total | **103** |\n| **net saved** | **9** |\n\n**1.10 eliminations per graph call.** 9 of 2671 messages = 0.34%; at elasticity 1.682 that\npredicts +0.6% tokens — measured headline **+1.35%**. Model and measurement agree.\n\n**35% needs 556 turns removed = 6.9 eliminations per call.**\n\nBaseline removable pool: shell exploration **855** (grep 409, ls 263, sed 161, cat 107, find 36),\nharness runs **576**. Everything else (edits, other bash, reads) is not graph-addressable.\n\n**Ceilings, all converging (see [[eg-route-to-35-falsified]]):**\n- perfect loser repair = **+21.21%** (exact — it is the sum of the lift pool, drag is only 19.86)\n- best fair cell ever = +17.21% (opus xhigh n=26)\n- zero-toll delivery + graph-backed grep + today = **≈+15%**\n\n**Why:** built three capabilities before computing what one call is worth. **How to apply:**\nprice any proposal as \"messages removed ÷ messages spent\" BEFORE building it; if it cannot reach\n~7:1 it cannot reach the goal. See [[graph-absent-where-cost-is]], [[eg-verify-not-more-than-baseline]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4855,"cache_read_input_tokens":420802,"output_tokens":1066,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4855,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1066,"cache_read_input_tokens":420802,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4855},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqSeXKwWumQ3vfjAuW58","attributionSkill":"artifact-design","type":"assistant","uuid":"3c5419e0-24c2-4c9e-bb46-58392f5ad2d8","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:31:38.128Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"3c5419e0-24c2-4c9e-bb46-58392f5ad2d8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d6032c5e-0887-4a82-a3cb-2a093f118b85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mgt9CT9kC2pv18sTNJJn82","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/eg-per-call-economics.md"}]},"uuid":"35501764-bf08-456f-a2f4-5aa5d58df37f","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:31:38.168Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/eg-per-call-economics.md","content":"---\nname: eg-per-call-economics\ndescription: \"THE defining ratio for entire-graph token savings — 94 graph calls eliminate 103 messages (1.10 per call); 35% requires 6.9 per call, a 6.3x move\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49\n  modified: 2026-08-08T14:31:38.160Z\n---\n\nMeasured on rep50 (49 gated pairs, Opus). This single ratio explains the headline and bounds\nevery proposal.\n\n| | count |\n|---|---|\n| graph calls made | **94** |\n| shell-exploration calls eliminated | 72 |\n| harness runs eliminated | 31 |\n| messages eliminated total | **103** |\n| **net saved** | **9** |\n\n**1.10 eliminations per graph call.** 9 of 2671 messages = 0.34%; at elasticity 1.682 that\npredicts +0.6% tokens — measured headline **+1.35%**. Model and measurement agree.\n\n**35% needs 556 turns removed = 6.9 eliminations per call.**\n\nBaseline removable pool: shell exploration **855** (grep 409, ls 263, sed 161, cat 107, find 36),\nharness runs **576**. Everything else (edits, other bash, reads) is not graph-addressable.\n\n**Ceilings, all converging (see [[eg-route-to-35-falsified]]):**\n- perfect loser repair = **+21.21%** (exact — it is the sum of the lift pool, drag is only 19.86)\n- best fair cell ever = +17.21% (opus xhigh n=26)\n- zero-toll delivery + graph-backed grep + today = **≈+15%**\n\n**Why:** built three capabilities before computing what one call is worth. **How to apply:**\nprice any proposal as \"messages removed ÷ messages spent\" BEFORE building it; if it cannot reach\n~7:1 it cannot reach the goal. See [[graph-absent-where-cost-is]], [[eg-verify-not-more-than-baseline]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3c5419e0-24c2-4c9e-bb46-58392f5ad2d8","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"35501764-bf08-456f-a2f4-5aa5d58df37f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[],"itemCount":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6707a1a8-a8cc-4580-81b1-b4aa608cdefa","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:31:38.179Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"6707a1a8-a8cc-4580-81b1-b4aa608cdefa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqSfujc4d8jxjLSpuDYM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Chq8NmmnSnz3bg4CKhEjpe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory\ncat > $M/eg-verify-not-more-than-baseline.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: eg-verify-not-more-than-baseline\ndescription: \"RETRACTION — eg does NOT run the harness more than baseline; it runs it LESS (545 vs 576). The opposite claim came from a loser-selected subset\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n**Retracts the \"eg over-verifies\" claim** that drove G2 and much of the loser analysis.\n\nPopulation, all 49 gated pairs: **eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576**. Post-edit only:\n**eg 384 vs 422**. Excluding three blow-up sessions: **327 vs 402**.\n\nThe opposite claim (\"eg ran ./runtest 11x vs baseline 7\") was computed on the **8 worst losers** —\na set selected on the outcome. Over-verification is what a LOSING session looks like in either arm:\n\n| group | eg runs/session | base runs/session |\n|---|---|---|\n| eg won (24) | 6.3 | 10.0 |\n| eg lost (25) | 9.3 | 7.3 |\n| 8 worst losers | 12.4 | 7.9 |\n\n`corr(delta harness runs, tokens saved) = -0.612` (n=49) — verification looping IS the loss\nmechanism, but eg's defect is **variance, not tendency**. The biggest win, lombok-3674 (+71.0%),\nis the BASELINE running javac 70x against eg's 23 — same mechanism, opposite arm.\n\nAnswers the external \"why is baseline cheaper at running tests?\" objection: it isn't, and eg\nisn't running more tests. Three sessions create the whole impression.\n\n**Why:** conditioned on the outcome and read the result as a cause. **How to apply:** never\ncharacterise an arm from a subset selected by that arm's performance; always compute the\npopulation number first. See [[eg-per-call-economics]], [[losers-are-not-stable]].\nEOF\ncat > $M/eg-route-to-35-falsified.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: eg-route-to-35-falsified\ndescription: \"Both remaining routes to 35% priced and one falsified offline — graph-backed grep caps at 38.9% interception, everything sums to ~+15%\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nPlan at `devenv/EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md`. Supersedes `PLAN-TO-35PCT.md` (gate ladder failed G1/G2/G3).\n\n**Adoption is the wall, measured 0/66:** `impact` 0/49, `changed` 0/5, `--path` 0/12 — all in the\naffordance tail. Everything in the PRIMARY instruction is used (search 33/49, grep 34/49,\ndef 19/49). G3 is the cleanest read: two useful new capabilities moved graph calls UP\n(1.9->3.1/session) and displacement DOWN (0.96->0.76).\n\n**R-A zero-toll delivery** — inject the payload at turn 0 (the tool already has\n`PresearchPath`, \"this call must cost nothing\"). Removes the 94-call overhead = **+5.9%**. Fair\n(payload, not instruction). Previously struck on RETRIEVAL quality, which is the wrong metric\nunder the message law. **Untested on tokens — the one live lever left.**\n\n**R-B graph-backed grep** (PATH shim so the agent's 409 greps become graph calls; zero adoption\ncost) — **FALSIFIED offline, $0.** Pre-registered H1 needed >=60% of greps to have a follow-up a\ngraph answer could remove. Measured **38.9%** (eg) / 38.6% (baseline):\nnext action is another grep 27.2%, Read of a surfaced file 5.9%, shell-read of one 5.6%.\n=> 139 messages, **+8.6% generous / +2.6% conservative**, not the +25% projected. Projection was\nwrong 3x; the replay caught it before a cell was spent.\n\n**Everything summed: 242 messages of 556 needed = ~+15%.** Converges with perfect-loser-repair\n+21.21% (exact) and best fair cell +17.21%.\n\n**The only intervention that reaches 35% is an instruction to explore/re-test less — which helps\na no-tool arm equally, so it fails the fairness test. That is exactly what the withdrawn -35%\ncontained.**\n\n**How to apply:** quote high-single-digit to mid-teens with its interval; say it is negative on\nshort sessions and that variance exceeds the mean. See [[eg-per-call-economics]],\n[[eg-verify-not-more-than-baseline]], [[eg-target-was-never-real]].\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd=[\"- [eg per-call economics](eg-per-call-economics.md) — 1.10 eliminations per graph call; 35% needs 6.9\",\n\"- [eg verify claim RETRACTED](eg-verify-not-more-than-baseline.md) — eg runs harness LESS (545 vs 576); old claim was loser-selected\",\n\"- [Route to 35% falsified](eg-route-to-35-falsified.md) — grep-shim caps at 38.9%; all routes sum to ~+15%; plan EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md\"]\nfor a in add:\n    if a.split(']')[0] not in s: s=s.rstrip()+\"\\n\"+a+\"\\n\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(s.strip().split(\"\\n\")[-3:])\nPY","description":"Write memory corrections and index"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1251,"cache_read_input_tokens":425657,"output_tokens":2013,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1251,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2013,"cache_read_input_tokens":425657,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1251},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqSfq2auN16xqYTgzxgi","attributionSkill":"artifact-design","type":"assistant","uuid":"03c07787-7ff6-4cbf-98eb-d75010d700e2","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:32:04.633Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"03c07787-7ff6-4cbf-98eb-d75010d700e2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d6032c5e-0887-4a82-a3cb-2a093f118b85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Chq8NmmnSnz3bg4CKhEjpe","type":"tool_result","content":"['- [eg per-call economics](eg-per-call-economics.md) — 1.10 eliminations per graph call; 35% needs 6.9', '- [eg verify claim RETRACTED](eg-verify-not-more-than-baseline.md) — eg runs harness LESS (545 vs 576); old claim was loser-selected', '- [Route to 35% falsified](eg-route-to-35-falsified.md) — grep-shim caps at 38.9%; all routes sum to ~+15%; plan EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md']","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ed1ce0ad-382b-48a8-a460-0499d1d934e9","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:32:07.023Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"['- [eg per-call economics](eg-per-call-economics.md) — 1.10 eliminations per graph call; 35% needs 6.9', '- [eg verify claim RETRACTED](eg-verify-not-more-than-baseline.md) — eg runs harness LESS (545 vs 576); old claim was loser-selected', '- [Route to 35% falsified](eg-route-to-35-falsified.md) — grep-shim caps at 38.9%; all routes sum to ~+15%; plan EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md']","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"03c07787-7ff6-4cbf-98eb-d75010d700e2","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"ed1ce0ad-382b-48a8-a460-0499d1d934e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqSi3tYhWH5bXmn86KTq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's where the hour landed.\n\n## Artifact\n**https://claude.ai/code/artifact/5a57cd50-f9a4-4580-92fe-fbc03fa4f8bd** — all 49 instances ranked by headline points, click any bar to load it into the side-by-side comparator (defaults to `lombok-3674` +6.09 pts vs `bat-1892` −2.81 pts). Per-instance tokens, turns, graph calls, shell exploration, harness runs, phase splits, verbs used, payload bytes, patch size.\n\n## Plan\n`devenv/EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md` — new file, supersedes the old one.\n\n## What the hour actually produced\n\n**The problem reduced to one ratio.** 94 graph calls eliminate 103 messages → **1.10 per call**. Net 9 messages of 2,671 = 0.34%, which at elasticity 1.682 predicts +0.6%; measured **+1.35%**. The model and the measurement agree, so this is the real mechanism. **35% needs 6.9 eliminations per call.**\n\n**Two corrections to things I told you earlier — both mine, both material:**\n\n1. **eg does not verify more than baseline. It verifies less** — 545 vs 576 runs. My \"eg ran `./runtest` 11× vs 7×\" came from the 8 worst *losers*, a set selected on the outcome. Over-verification is what a losing session looks like in either arm; in the biggest win the **baseline** ran `javac` 70× against eg's 23.\n\n2. **Perfect loser repair caps at +21.21%**, exactly — that's the sum of the lift pool, not an estimate. Loser repair cannot reach 35% by definition.\n\n**I found a genuinely new route and then killed it myself.** The grep-shim (put the graph behind `grep`, so the agent's 409 greps become graph calls at zero adoption cost) was the only idea whose ceiling contained 35%. I pre-registered H1 at ≥60% and ran it offline for $0:\n\n**38.9%.** Only 139 greps have a follow-up a graph answer could remove — not the ~400 I projected. That's +8.6% generous, +2.6% conservative. My projection was wrong by 3×, and the replay caught it before spending a cell.\n\n**Everything on the table sums to 242 messages of the 556 needed ≈ +15%** — converging with perfect loser repair (+21.21%) and the best fair cell ever measured (+17.21%).\n\n**The honest bottom line:** the only intervention that reaches 35% is an instruction telling the agent to explore and re-test less. That helps a no-tool arm equally, so it fails the fairness test — and it is exactly what the withdrawn −35% contained.\n\n**One live lever remains untested: R-A, zero-toll delivery.** The tool already implements it (`PresearchPath` — *\"this call must cost nothing\"*). It was struck previously on *retrieval quality*, which under the message law is the wrong metric — a worse payload delivered free can beat a better one that costs a turn. Worth **+5.9%**, unambiguously fair, and never measured on tokens.\n\nWant me to build and gate R-A?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2200,"cache_read_input_tokens":426908,"output_tokens":1057,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2200,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1057,"cache_read_input_tokens":426908,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2200},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqShxdnqG8DufbaQWVir","attributionSkill":"artifact-design","type":"assistant","uuid":"13517583-c925-43fd-800e-a678712009db","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:32:24.893Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
