{"parentUuid":"56e2f877-478d-4ade-91fd-cfce59289b4c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqTqyMnR619QKaa6tXx3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JuJhFdXGaujgLjp5CsG9LY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n '254,300p' internal/cli/search.go","description":"Read presearch echo implementation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1385,"cache_read_input_tokens":451022,"output_tokens":116,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1385,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":116,"cache_read_input_tokens":451022,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1385},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqTqsMsXEL4k7W5naCwR","type":"assistant","uuid":"0cd09f58-2ccb-448a-b6c3-24487ebfb360","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:47:05.375Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"0cd09f58-2ccb-448a-b6c3-24487ebfb360","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dc9db703-bd0b-4f0e-8845-0094c652b703","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JuJhFdXGaujgLjp5CsG9LY","type":"tool_result","content":"// echoPresearchPayload returns a payload that was computed before the agent started, verbatim.\n//\n// The toll this removes is the MESSAGE, not the bytes. Measured over 178 gated benchmark pairs,\n// the number of graph calls a session makes is invariant — 1.00 / 1.03 / 1.00 per session across\n// baseline-exploration bands <10 / 10-19 / >=20 turns — while what the call buys back is not:\n// greps displaced go 1.35 / 2.16 / 3.74 over the same bands, and the cost ratio with it (1.140 CI\n// [1.063,1.224] n=51 / 0.950 n=108 / 0.841 CI [0.704,0.998] n=19). Split by outcome instead of by\n// band, the two cohorts separate cleanly: sessions where the call displaced no grep at all (n=43)\n// cost 1.165 CI [1.073,1.264] and ran +1.21 turns, sessions where it displaced greps (n=135) cost\n// 0.938 CI [0.889,0.990] and ran -2.07 turns. corr(turn delta, log cost ratio) = +0.735 CI\n// [0.661,0.800] pair-level, +0.802 CI [0.662,0.885] repo-level — the strongest correlate in the\n// set. Independently, a regression holding call count fixed still prices a +7.0% CI [1.9,13.2]\n// tax on merely having made the call, and prices one call at 1.61 messages rather than 1.\n//\n// The toll is also unpredictable: no static feature of a payload predicts that its call will turn\n// out to be a no-op (AUC 0.553 top score, 0.560 spread, 0.563 gap, 0.690 entropy, at a 28% base\n// rate). Selective skipping is therefore not implementable — pre-delivery is the only form the\n// fix can take, and it must be universal.\n//\n// Echoing rather than re-querying is what makes the delivery free: a call the agent still makes\n// costs one message and adds zero information, so it cannot re-open the phase the pre-delivery\n// closed. Retrieval is unaffected because the agent's own query adds almost nothing over the\n// issue text the payload was derived from: of 188 pre-edit greps not covered by the payload, 2\n// (1.1%) named a literal that was in the agent's query and not in the issue.\n//\n// A caller that names a payload it cannot produce gets an error, not a live query. Falling back\n// silently would leave the arm measuring whichever mode each session happened to land in — the\n// same reason an unknown --reference-blocks name is an error rather than a no-op.\n//\n// Note for whoever wires the caller: the payload must be computed with the SAME binary, flags and\n// cached graph the session would have used, and the instruction telling the agent to search first\n// has to go with it — the tool cannot be left un-called while that directive stands.\nfunc echoPresearchPayload(out interface{ Write([]byte) (int, error) }, path string) error {\n\tpayload, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s: %w\", envPresearch, err)\n\t}\n\t_, err = out.Write(payload)\n\treturn err\n}\n\n// writeNdjsonSearch streams a payload as one record per line: a header, the blocks that are their own\n// records, every ranked result, and a summary that carries the rest.\nfunc writeNdjsonSearch(out interface{ Write([]byte) (int, error) }, response sem.SearchResponse) error {\n\t{\n\t\tencoder := json.NewEncoder(out)\n\t\tencoder.SetEscapeHTML(false)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6e17226f-1e74-4fe4-a875-58f8aa260990","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:47:05.431Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"// echoPresearchPayload returns a payload that was computed before the agent started, verbatim.\n//\n// The toll this removes is the MESSAGE, not the bytes. Measured over 178 gated benchmark pairs,\n// the number of graph calls a session makes is invariant — 1.00 / 1.03 / 1.00 per session across\n// baseline-exploration bands <10 / 10-19 / >=20 turns — while what the call buys back is not:\n// greps displaced go 1.35 / 2.16 / 3.74 over the same bands, and the cost ratio with it (1.140 CI\n// [1.063,1.224] n=51 / 0.950 n=108 / 0.841 CI [0.704,0.998] n=19). Split by outcome instead of by\n// band, the two cohorts separate cleanly: sessions where the call displaced no grep at all (n=43)\n// cost 1.165 CI [1.073,1.264] and ran +1.21 turns, sessions where it displaced greps (n=135) cost\n// 0.938 CI [0.889,0.990] and ran -2.07 turns. corr(turn delta, log cost ratio) = +0.735 CI\n// [0.661,0.800] pair-level, +0.802 CI [0.662,0.885] repo-level — the strongest correlate in the\n// set. Independently, a regression holding call count fixed still prices a +7.0% CI [1.9,13.2]\n// tax on merely having made the call, and prices one call at 1.61 messages rather than 1.\n//\n// The toll is also unpredictable: no static feature of a payload predicts that its call will turn\n// out to be a no-op (AUC 0.553 top score, 0.560 spread, 0.563 gap, 0.690 entropy, at a 28% base\n// rate). Selective skipping is therefore not implementable — pre-delivery is the only form the\n// fix can take, and it must be universal.\n//\n// Echoing rather than re-querying is what makes the delivery free: a call the agent still makes\n// costs one message and adds zero information, so it cannot re-open the phase the pre-delivery\n// closed. Retrieval is unaffected because the agent's own query adds almost nothing over the\n// issue text the payload was derived from: of 188 pre-edit greps not covered by the payload, 2\n// (1.1%) named a literal that was in the agent's query and not in the issue.\n//\n// A caller that names a payload it cannot produce gets an error, not a live query. Falling back\n// silently would leave the arm measuring whichever mode each session happened to land in — the\n// same reason an unknown --reference-blocks name is an error rather than a no-op.\n//\n// Note for whoever wires the caller: the payload must be computed with the SAME binary, flags and\n// cached graph the session would have used, and the instruction telling the agent to search first\n// has to go with it — the tool cannot be left un-called while that directive stands.\nfunc echoPresearchPayload(out interface{ Write([]byte) (int, error) }, path string) error {\n\tpayload, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s: %w\", envPresearch, err)\n\t}\n\t_, err = out.Write(payload)\n\treturn err\n}\n\n// writeNdjsonSearch streams a payload as one record per line: a header, the blocks that are their own\n// records, every ranked result, and a summary that carries the rest.\nfunc writeNdjsonSearch(out interface{ Write([]byte) (int, error) }, response sem.SearchResponse) error {\n\t{\n\t\tencoder := json.NewEncoder(out)\n\t\tencoder.SetEscapeHTML(false)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0cd09f58-2ccb-448a-b6c3-24487ebfb360","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"6e17226f-1e74-4fe4-a875-58f8aa260990","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqTrHArHonPK4fwBepwT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1307,"cache_read_input_tokens":452407,"output_tokens":3248,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1307,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3248,"cache_read_input_tokens":452407,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1307},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqTrCPN4Udd6QrMU9Jss","type":"assistant","uuid":"9db1ec64-5ad2-4121-8dbe-459f39f69f47","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:47:22.675Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"9db1ec64-5ad2-4121-8dbe-459f39f69f47","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqTrHArHonPK4fwBepwT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found something material — the zero-toll implementation carries its own measurement base, from **178 pairs**, and it corrects my R-A estimate upward while dissolving the risk I flagged:\n\n| prior finding (in `search.go:254`) | implication |\n|---|---|\n| graph calls per session are **invariant** (1.00 / 1.03 / 1.00 across exploration bands) | you cannot get more value by inducing more calls — consistent with G3 |\n| calls that displaced no grep (n=43): cost ratio **1.165** [1.073, 1.224], **+1.21 turns**; calls that did (n=135): **0.938** [0.889, 0.990], **−2.07 turns** | the call is a coin flip that costs when it misses |\n| regression holding call count fixed prices **+7.0% [1.9, 13.2]** tax on merely having made the call, and one call at **1.61 messages**, not 1 | **removing 94 calls removes ~151 messages, not 94** |\n| no static feature predicts a no-op call (best AUC 0.553 at 28% base rate) | selective skipping is impossible; pre-delivery must be universal |\n| of 188 pre-edit greps the payload missed, **2 (1.1%)** named a literal in the agent's query but not the issue | **the retrieval objection is already measured away** |\n\nThat last row kills the main risk I put on R-A in the plan. I priced it at +5.9% assuming the payload would be worse because prefetched retrieval scores lower on gold-visible@5. But the agent's own query adds ~1% over the issue text, and the earlier strike was on retrieval, not tokens.\n\n**Revised: R-A is worth +7% to +9.5%**, not +5.9% — and it's the only lever with no adoption dependency and no fairness qualification.\n\nOne design constraint the comment flags, which I'd have missed: pre-delivery requires *removing* the \"search first\" directive from the eg prompt, or the agent searches anyway and pays a message to receive an echo. Removing an eg-only instruction can't bias toward eg — it strictly reduces the asymmetry.\n\nUpdating the plan and building it:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1307,"cache_read_input_tokens":452407,"output_tokens":3248,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1307,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3248,"cache_read_input_tokens":452407,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1307},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqTrCPN4Udd6QrMU9Jss","type":"assistant","uuid":"1a9af92e-f585-4676-a9be-ff3d3ed9722a","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:47:32.565Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"1a9af92e-f585-4676-a9be-ff3d3ed9722a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqTrHArHonPK4fwBepwT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014VxbjXcMhjV8uf8CCRSUPK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv && python3 - <<'PY'\np='EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"### R-A — Drive the denominator to zero\"); j=s.index(\"### R-B —\")\nnew = \"\"\"### R-A — Drive the denominator to zero: zero-toll delivery *(fair, no adoption dependency, BEST REMAINING)*\n\n**Revised upward 2026-08-08** after reading the prior measurement embedded at\n`internal/cli/search.go:254`, which rests on **178 gated pairs** — a larger base than this cell.\n\nThe graph's calls are not merely overhead, they are *taxed* overhead:\n\n| prior finding | value |\n|---|---|\n| graph calls per session | **invariant**: 1.00 / 1.03 / 1.00 across exploration bands <10 / 10–19 / ≥20 turns |\n| greps displaced per call, same bands | 1.35 / 2.16 / 3.74 |\n| call displaced NO grep (n=43) | cost ratio **1.165** CI [1.073, 1.264], **+1.21 turns** |\n| call displaced greps (n=135) | cost ratio **0.938** CI [0.889, 0.990], **−2.07 turns** |\n| corr(turn delta, log cost ratio) | **+0.735** CI [0.661, 0.800] pair-level; +0.802 repo-level — strongest correlate in the set |\n| regression holding call count fixed | **+7.0% CI [1.9, 13.2]** tax on merely having made the call |\n| price of one call | **1.61 messages**, not 1 |\n| predictability of a no-op call | none — best AUC **0.553** at a 28% base rate |\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n1. **Removing 94 calls removes ~151 messages** (94 × 1.61), = 5.7% of turns ≈ **+9.5% tokens**.\n   The independent regression route gives **+7.0%**. Call it **+7% to +9.5%**.\n2. **Selective skipping is not implementable** — nothing predicts which call will be a no-op — so\n   pre-delivery must be universal.\n\n**The retrieval risk I previously assigned to R-A is already measured away.** Of 188 pre-edit\ngreps the payload did not cover, **2 (1.1%)** named a literal that was in the agent's query and\nnot in the issue text. The old \"prefetch is dominated\" strike was made on *retrieval quality*\n(gold-visible@5 0.567 vs 0.715), which under the message law is not the metric.\n\n**Design constraint, from the implementation note:** pre-delivery requires *removing* the\n\"search first\" directive from the eg prompt — otherwise the agent searches anyway and pays a\nmessage to receive an echo. Removing an eg-only instruction strictly reduces arm asymmetry, so\nthis improves fairness rather than straining it.\n\n**Fairness: unqualified.** The payload is tool output, ships no advice, and the no-tool arm\ncannot produce it. Same class as the search result itself.\n\n\"\"\"\ns = s[:i] + new + s[j:]\n# update the ceiling table\ns = s.replace(\"| R-A zero-toll delivery | +94 | 3.5% | +5.9% |\",\n              \"| R-A zero-toll delivery | +151 | 5.7% | +7.0% to +9.5% |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| **all three** | **242** | **9.1%** | **≈ +15%** |\",\n              \"| **all three** | **299** | **11.2%** | **≈ +17%** |\")\ns = s.replace(\"| R-A + R-B + current, perfect execution | **≈ +15%** |\",\n              \"| R-A + R-B + current, perfect execution | **≈ +17%** |\")\ns = s.replace(\"**35% needs 556 messages. Everything on the table sums to 242.**\",\n              \"**35% needs 556 messages. Everything on the table sums to 299.**\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"plan updated;\",\"1.61 messages\" in s, \"+9.5%\" in s)\nPY\ngrep -n \"299\\|+7.0% to +9.5%\\|≈ +17%\" EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md | head","description":"Revise R-A estimate in plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1307,"cache_read_input_tokens":452407,"output_tokens":3248,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemer