{"parentUuid":"926cd38a-4cb8-46b8-93b7-6c6e4c1599ab","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dc9db703-bd0b-4f0e-8845-0094c652b703","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012JgSUuwAh62RLNrZBqdLww","type":"tool_result","content":"      fi\n    fi\n    if [ -s \"$out/prefetch.payload\" ]; then\n      # EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1 -- drop \"you do not need to run it yourself\".\n      #\n      # Measured on PUB_r1 (Opus, published prompt, n=20): the agent makes 0.20 graph calls per\n      # session against 24.40 shell greps -- the graph is 0.7% of all locate operations, and 16 of\n      # 20 sessions never call it at all. Across 490 thinking blocks it is mentioned ONCE. So the\n      # tool is invisible as an interactive resource: read once as a briefing, then abandoned, while\n      # ~11-12 graph-answerable locate ops per session go to the shell instead.\n      # This preamble is a prime suspect -- it states outright that the agent need not run the tool.\n      # The replacement keeps the same factual content (a search has run, here is the result) and\n      # keeps follow-up availability, without telling the agent its work is done.\n      elif [ \"${EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS:-0}\" = 1 ]; then\n      PREFETCH_BLOCK=\"\n\nA code-graph search has already been run for this issue and its result is below. The tool is live:\nquery it again whenever you need something the result below does not already answer -- another\nsearch, or def / callers / impact / grep on any symbol.\n\n<graph_search_result>\n$(cat \"$out/prefetch.payload\")\n</graph_search_result>$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\" ] && printf '\\n\\n<graph_impact_result>\\nBlast radius of the top hit -- the other places this change lands.\\n\\n%s\\n</graph_impact_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\")\" )$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_test.payload\" ] && printf '\\n\\n<graph_test_result>\\nExisting tests that cover this code.\\n\\n%s\\n</graph_test_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_test.payload\")\" )\"\n      else\n      PREFETCH_BLOCK=\"\n\nA code-graph search has ALREADY been run for this issue. Its result is below -- you do not need to\nrun it yourself, and the same tool is still available for follow-ups.\n\n<graph_search_result>\n$(cat \"$out/prefetch.payload\")\n</graph_search_result>$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\" ] && printf '\\n\\n<graph_impact_result>\\nBlast radius of the top hit -- the other places this change lands. You do not need to look these\\nup yourself.\\n\\n%s\\n</graph_impact_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_impact.payload\")\" )$( [ -s \"$out/prefetch_test.payload\" ] && printf '\\n\\n<graph_test_result>\\nExisting tests that cover this code.\\n\\n%s\\n</graph_test_result>' \"$(cat \"$out/prefetch_test.payload\")\" )\"\n      fi\n    fi\n  fi\n  # EG_MCP=1 — expose the graph's verbs as NATIVE MCP TOOLS instead of a shell string.\n  #\n  # Measured across the ten losing Sonnet repos: graph calls 1.0/session vs 9.3 shell searches, and\n  # 58% of those shell searches ask a question a graph verb already answers (immutable-js 100%,\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fa0b06c8-9d51-4b1c-a0dc-15b53f9e81ff","timestamp":"2026-08-08T14:49:19.425Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"      fi\n    fi\n    if [ -s \"$out/prefetch.payload\" ]; then\n      # EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1 -- drop \"you do not need to run it yourself\".\n      #\n      # Measured on PUB_r1 (Opus, published prompt, n=20): the agent makes 0.20 graph calls per\n      # session against 24.40 shell greps -- the graph is 0.7% of all locate operations, and 16 of\n      # 20 sessions never call it at all. Across 490 thinking blocks it is mentioned ONCE. So the\n      # tool is invisible as an interactive resource: read once as a briefing, then abandoned, while\n      # ~11-12 graph-answerable locate ops per session go to the shell instead.\n      # This preamble is a prime suspect -- it states outright that the agent need not run th