{"parentUuid":"c280aee0-58f9-474c-b3e4-fea3616de9c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqVyXgeUhnLFmTygM4W4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4121,"cache_read_input_tokens":515792,"output_tokens":6352,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4121,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6352,"cache_read_input_tokens":515792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4121},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqVyMZwNoSCsVMm6to4b","type":"assistant","uuid":"d48e8411-c311-4d0f-b1d2-9e96447c788b","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:15:21.225Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"d48e8411-c311-4d0f-b1d2-9e96447c788b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqVyXgeUhnLFmTygM4W4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's the decisive split, and it's more favourable than the whole-file case:\n\n| why the eg arm still explores source code | calls | cost | share |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **coverage gap — no term in payload** | 117 | 2.18M | **26.9%** |\n| **partial coverage — some terms** | 96 | 3.41M | **42.2%** |\n| ignored payload — all terms delivered | 57 | 1.28M | 15.9% |\n| no identifier in query | 49 | 1.22M | 15.0% |\n\n**69.1% is a coverage problem, only 15.9% is the agent ignoring what it has.** The misses are specific symbol lookups the graph should own: `replaceGt|replaceLt|replaceGte`, `def get_deprecation_message`, `path_hooks|def _install`.\n\nThat's the opposite of the whole-file-read case (42.3% ignored) and it's the one genuinely tool-fixable pool left. Finalizing the plan on the complete model:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4121,"cache_read_input_tokens":515792,"output_tokens":6352,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4121,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6352,"cache_read_input_tokens":515792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4121},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqVyMZwNoSCsVMm6to4b","type":"assistant","uuid":"ab928bee-4448-4b34-9482-15bcbbda81bf","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:15:24.768Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"ab928bee-4448-4b34-9482-15bcbbda81bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqVyXgeUhnLFmTygM4W4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VPY1hapcA12Xn7TjcQfmp1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/EG-FINAL-PLAN.md","content":"# entire-graph — the finalized plan\n\n**2026-08-08.** Supersedes `PLAN-TO-35PCT.md` and `EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md`. Everything below is\nmeasured on rep50 (49 gated pairs, Opus, SWE-bench Multilingual) unless marked projection.\nSign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**\n\n---\n\n## 1. The metric is context, not messages\n\n    tokens +1.35%  =  turns −1.42%  +  tokens/turn +2.74%\n\nThe eg arm spends **38 more turns** and still wins, so the saving is not a message saving.\n**cache_read is 95.5% of all tokens** (cache_creation 3.0%, output 1.5%). This is a context-size\nproblem. The independent prefetch measurement at `run_3arm.sh:482` found the same thing on a\ndifferent cell (30,302 → 29,334 tok/turn, −3.2%).\n\nVariance decomposition of the paired log token ratio: turns 34.2%, tokens/turn 26.0%, covariance\n39.8% (entangled, corr +0.668). Neither side dominates alone.\n\n**Accounting unit used throughout:** a tool result injected at turn *i* is re-charged on every\nlater turn, so its cost is `(bytes ÷ 4) × turns-remaining` — \"persist-tokens\".\n\n---\n\n## 2. The complete budget\n\nBaseline total: **38.6M persist-tokens**. eg: 38.5M. **The tool is context-neutral (+0.2%).**\n\n| category | baseline | share | eg | captured |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **source-code exploration** | 10.48M | 27.2% | 8.25M | **21%** |\n| **whole-file `Read`** | 11.67M | 30.3% | 9.20M | **21%** |\n| test exploration | 1.94M | 5.0% | 2.87M | **−48%** |\n| range `Read` | 3.60M | 9.3% | 4.40M | −22% |\n| harness runs | 4.30M | 11.2% | 3.70M | 14% |\n| log / scratch output | 1.95M | 5.1% | 2.36M | not addressable |\n| environment / deps | 0.76M | 2.0% | 0.62M | not addressable |\n| build manifests | 0.31M | 0.8% | 0.34M | not addressable |\n| graph calls | 0 | — | 1.70M | cost |\n\n**Graph-addressable = source exploration + whole-file reads + tests = 24.1M of 38.6M (62.4%).**\neg captures 3.78M gross, adds 3.10M (graph calls 1.7M, range reads +0.8M, other +0.6M), so\n**net 0.68M = 1.8% ≈ the observed +1.35%.** The model reconciles to the measurement.\n\nTwo structural facts that kill obvious ideas:\n\n- **Exploration calls are already cheap** — median **732 B**, p90 3.6 KB, 1.3% over 8 KB. Its 47%\n  share is *volume* (1,206 calls), not size. The graph's own output has a median of **1,124 B**,\n  larger than a median grep, so a graph-backed grep would add bytes. (Kills R-B.)\n- **Whole-file reads are the opposite** — 119 calls, median 5,125 B, p90 20 KB; 39 calls carry\n  70.9% of the bytes. 98k persist-tokens each, **7× an exploration call**.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Why the uncaptured cost is uncaptured — the decisive split\n\nFor every remaining call, was what it asked for already in the delivered payload?\n\n**Whole-file reads still made by eg (105 calls, 9.2M):**\n\n| cause | calls | share of cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| **c) file was in the payload WITH its body** | 24 | **42.3%** |\n| no payload logged (detector bug, §6.1) | 36 | 36.0% |\n| a) file never in the payload | 42 | 21.1% |\n| b) in payload as a locator only | 3 | 0.5% |\n\n**Source-code exploration still done by eg (319 calls with a logged payload, 8.09M):**\n\n| cause | calls | share of cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| **coverage — no query term in payload** | 117 | **26.9%** |\n| **partial coverage — some terms** | 96 | **42.2%** |\n| ignored payload — all terms delivered | 57 | 15.9% |\n| no identifier in the query | 49 | 15.0% |\n\n**These point in opposite directions and that is the whole finding.**\nWhole-file reads are dominated by the agent re-opening a file it was already given in full —\n**not tool-fixable**, and the same wall as 0/66 verb adoption. Source exploration is dominated by\n**coverage (69.1%)** — the payload genuinely did not contain what the agent asked for next, and\nthe misses are specific symbol lookups the graph should own (`replaceGt|replaceLt|replaceGte`,\n`def get_deprecation_message`, `path_hooks|def _install`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. The ceiling, computed from the budget\n\n| | persist-tokens | as % of 38.6M |\n|---|---|---|\n| graph-addressable pool | 24.1M | 62.4% |\n| …of which coverage-fixable | ~7.5M | **19.4%** |\n| …of which ignored-payload (needs an instruction) | ~5.2M | 13.5% |\n| …of which already captured | 3.78M | 9.8% |\n| payload cost to widen coverage (projection) | −2 to −3M | −5 to −8% |\n\n**Coverage work, delivered perfectly and priced honestly: ≈ +12%.**\n**R-A (remove the call toll): +4.8% to +6.9%** — computed directly, not modelled.\n**Together: +15% to +19%.**\n\n35% would require capturing ~65–70% of the addressable pool at near-zero payload cost. The\nignored-payload share alone (13.5%) is out of reach without an instruction, and an instruction\ntelling the agent to re-read less would help a no-tool arm equally — **which is exactly what the\nwithdrawn −35% contained** (removing two such sentences moved that cell from −14.9% to +9.1%).\n\n**Seven independent derivations, all landing in the same band:**\n\n| route | ceiling |\n|---|---|\n| perfect loser repair (= the lift pool, exact) | **+21.21%** |\n| best fair cell ever measured (opus xhigh, n=26) | **+17.21%** |\n| coverage + R-A, from the context budget | **+15% to +19%** |\n| R-A + R-B + current, message model | ≈ +17% |\n| expensive-baseline tercile (78% of token mass) | +8.07% |\n| hand-classified post-edit waste (763 calls) | +2.67% to +4.57% |\n| directly addressable post-edit surface | +2.3% |\n\n> **35% is not reachable on a fair measurement. The honest number is +15% to +21%.**\n\n---\n\n## 5. What to do, in order\n\n### 5.1 SHIP — R-A, zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, committed `b669a57b`)*\n\n`EG_PREFETCH=1` has always injected the payload into turn 0 **and** let the agent's residual\nsearch re-derive it at full price (~5 s + an index build) — delivered twice, paid for once at\nfull price. That is why every prefetch attempt measured null. `EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual\ncall an echo.\n\nOffline gate passed, $0: echo byte-identical to the prompt block; **0.02 s vs 5.21 s**; missing\npayload errors rather than silently re-querying; real search unaffected when unset; other verbs\nunaffected; export proven eg-only by block matching (line 704, inside `arm = eg` 446–939 and the\n`EG_PREFETCH` gate at 498).\n\nWorth **+4.8% to +6.9%**. Fair without qualification: the eg prompt gains tool output and *loses*\nan instruction. **Next step: run it as a paired cell.**\n\n### 5.2 BUILD — coverage of the agent's *next* query\n\nTarget the 69.1% coverage share of source exploration. The failing queries are specific symbol\nlookups. This is the one pool that is genuinely tool-fixable.\n\nDo **not** measure it with gold-file coverage — that metric is anti-correlated with winning\n(gold at rank 1: losers 6/8, winners 2/5) and eleven payload metrics have died on it. Measure it\nas: *of the identifiers the agent greps for after receiving the payload, what fraction were in\nthe payload?* Today that is **30.9%** (all-terms 15.9% + partial credit). Gate on raising it.\n\nPrice the payload growth against the capture — a wider payload costs persist-tokens too, and at\nmedian 1,124 B the graph's output is not free.\n\n### 5.3 DO NOT BUILD\n\n- **R-B, graph-backed grep** — dead twice: 38.9% interception, and graph output is *larger* than\n  a median grep.\n- **Anything gated on an agent-initiated call** — 0/66 (`impact` 0/49, `changed` 0/5, `--path`\n  0/12). A fourth verb will measure zero.\n- **Whole-file-read suppression** — 42.3% of the remaining cost is the agent re-opening a file it\n  already has in full. Only an instruction fixes that, and that instruction is unfair.\n- The twelve struck levers in §6.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Struck — measured, do not re-propose\n\n1. Eleven payload-quality metrics (completeness, gold coverage, byte width, rank) — all 0.\n2. **Complete-symbol payload density** — corr with token saving **−0.170**; the 3+ group measures\n   **−4.28%** against +1.35% overall. *(Twelfth.)*\n3. Retrieval/ranking quality — anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5).\n4. Session-length routing · language/repo gating · confidence gating (abstention worse).\n5. Per-loser repair — +0.0 pt; ~93% of losers flip sign between cells.\n6. Locate-call reduction as a token lever — corr +0.188 over 10 cells.\n7. Raising the turn cap — both arms grow proportionally.\n8. `EG_VERIFY_MODE=noworld` — +35.1% **worse**.\n9. Symmetric frugality clamp — net-negative: in the winners it is the *baseline* that flails\n   (lombok baseline `javac`×70 vs eg ×23), so a shared clamp hands savings to the baseline.\n10. More graph calls — G3: 1.9 → 3.1 calls, displacement 0.96 → 0.76.\n11. Post-edit delivery gated on an agent-initiated call — G2 measured **−12.19%**, rider fired 0/5.\n12. Any new verb in the affordance tail — 0/66.\n\n### 6.1 Open defects — fix before the next cell\n\n1. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken.** Fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes and 3\n   graph calls (3× in G3). It also blanks 36 of 105 whole-file reads (36% of that cost) from\n   classification. Any payload forensics is unreliable until it is fixed.\n2. **Gate admits junk patches** — `carbon-2981` baseline patch was 371,308 B (vendor/build\n   output) and passed as success. Add a symmetric size/content bound.\n3. **VMs A and B are spot and were preempted** — Gemini 300 frozen at n=207, 52 rep30 sessions\n   stranded. Move long cells to non-preemptible (E/F) or checkpoint.\n4. **`.entire/graph-agent.md` fairness landmine** — carries arm-asymmetric methodology and is\n   `@`-included into `CLAUDE.md`. It did *not* leak into rep50 (`--safe-mode`, 0 injected files\n   verified both arms), but any cell run without `--safe-mode` is invalid on arrival. Add a\n   preflight assertion rather than relying on the flag.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Corrections issued this session\n\nRecorded so they are not re-derived, and because two were mine.\n\n1. **eg does NOT verify more than the baseline — it verifies less** (545 vs 576 harness runs;\n   post-edit 384 vs 422). The opposite claim came from the 8 worst *losers*, a set selected on\n   the outcome. Over-verification is what a losing session looks like in either arm; the biggest\n   win, `lombok-3674` (+71.0%), is the *baseline* running `javac` 70× against eg's 23.\n2. **First-word Bash classification undercounted exploration by 41%** (855 → 1,206 baseline).\n   `wc -l f && cat f` and `gem list | grep …` were filed as \"other bash\". Corrected, the graph\n   costs **37 more messages than it removes**, and the saving is entirely context density.\n3. **Perfect loser repair caps at +21.21%**, exactly — it is the sum of the lift pool, not an\n   estimate. Loser repair cannot reach 35% by definition.\n4. The **+35.06%** target was an arithmetic artifact (applying the winner group's eg/base ratio,\n   earned on 2.64M-median baselines, to 0.99M baselines where the waste does not exist).\n   Retracted.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4121,"cache_read_input_tokens":515792,"output_tokens":6352,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4121,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6352,"cache_read_input_tokens":515792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4121},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqVyMZwNoSCsVM