{"parentUuid":"424ebfb1-7127-4f38-ba91-0b095ed26964","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"82948d44-f96f-4a9c-bbef-d92853afff75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TTv6ke1ws2ePX3TnETuoeC","type":"tool_result","content":"addressable pool        24.09M = 62.4% of 38.6M\ncaptured gross          3.77M\nadded by the tool       2.80M  (graph calls 1.70 + range reads 0.80 + logs 0.41 + misc)\nnet                     0.97M = +2.51% of context\nmeasured headline       +1.35%   -> reconciles: False\n\ncoverage-fixable        7.53M = 19.5%\nignored-payload         5.18M = 13.4%  (needs an instruction -> unfair)\ncoverage minus payload cost (2-3M): +13.0%\n+ R-A 4.8-6.9%  =>  17.8% to 19.9%\n=== files ===\n-rw-r--r--  1 suhaan  staff  10873 Aug  8 11:16 EG-FINAL-PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 suhaan  staff  19616 Aug  8 11:04 EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 suhaan  staff   9067 Aug  7 23:37 PLAN-TO-35PCT.md\n=== git state of the two shipped commits ===\n607b2a4 feat(search,def): scope search by path, answer batched names in one call\nb669a57b zero-toll: stop the pre-delivered payload being re-derived at full price\n8d6262ff harness: reach the batched-name and path-scoped forms from the arm","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e36f1678-fd61-46c0-a118-d928b19d7da5","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:16:35.646Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"addressable pool        24.09M = 62.4% of 38.6M\ncaptured gross          3.77M\nadded by the tool       2.80M  (graph calls 1.70 + range reads 0.80 + logs 0.41 + misc)\nnet                     0.97M = +2.51% of context\nmeasured headline       +1.35%   -> reconciles: False\n\ncoverage-fixable        7.53M = 19.5%\nignored-payload         5.18M = 13.4%  (needs an instruction -> unfair)\ncoverage minus payload cost (2-3M): +13.0%\n+ R-A 4.8-6.9%  =>  17.8% to 19.9%\n=== files ===\n-rw-r--r--  1 suhaan  staff  10873 Aug  8 11:16 EG-FINAL-PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 suhaan  staff  19616 Aug  8 11:04 EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 suhaan  staff   9067 Aug  7 23:37 PLAN-TO-35PCT.md\n=== git state of the two shipped commits ===\n607b2a4 feat(search,def): scope search by path, answer batched names in one call\nb669a57b zero-toll: stop the pre-delivered payload being re-derived at full price\n8d6262ff harness: reach the batched-name and path-scoped forms from the arm","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"424ebfb1-7127-4f38-ba91-0b095ed26964","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"e36f1678-fd61-46c0-a118-d928b19d7da5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqW6mdVPLFEM8YXfd5wE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_read_input_tokens":526451,"output_tokens":2771,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1302,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2771,"cache_read_input_tokens":526451,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1302},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqW6gjK91VnerUwqAJSB","type":"assistant","uuid":"9bb8a121-164b-43bd-b5fc-da94c3d68a15","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:16:49.902Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"9bb8a121-164b-43bd-b5fc-da94c3d68a15","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqW6mdVPLFEM8YXfd5wE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The verification caught an error in my own plan. I claimed the model reconciles to the measurement; it doesn't:\n\n- persist-model predicts **+2.51%** of context saved\n- measured headline is **+1.35%**\n\nThe persist model (`bytes ÷ 4 × turns-remaining`) **over-predicts by ~1.9×** — it ignores prompt/system/thinking tokens and treats cache reads as per-injection rather than per-turn on the full context. Every projection derived from it needs that discount. Correcting:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_read_input_tokens":526451,"output_tokens":2771,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1302,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2771,"cache_read_input_tokens":526451,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1302},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqW6gjK91VnerUwqAJSB","type":"assistant","uuid":"7a366023-2cb9-4c4e-9a54-490eb467377d","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:16:52.099Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"7a366023-2cb9-4c4e-9a54-490eb467377d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqW6mdVPLFEM8YXfd5wE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GTQuYaXC65mf7ChSCnWfmp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='EG-FINAL-PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\n\ns = s.replace(\n\"\"\"**Graph-addressable = source exploration + whole-file reads + tests = 24.1M of 38.6M (62.4%).**\neg captures 3.78M gross, adds 3.10M (graph calls 1.7M, range reads +0.8M, other +0.6M), so\n**net 0.68M = 1.8% ≈ the observed +1.35%.** The model reconciles to the measurement.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Graph-addressable = source exploration + whole-file reads + tests = 24.1M of 38.6M (62.4%).**\neg captures 3.77M gross and adds 2.80M (graph calls 1.70M, range reads +0.80M, logs +0.41M,\nmisc −0.11M), so **net 0.97M = +2.51% of context**.\n\n**CALIBRATION — the model over-predicts by ~1.9×.** Measured headline is **+1.35%**, so\npersist-tokens are not proportional to billed tokens: the unit ignores prompt, system and\nthinking tokens, and it charges each injection once against remaining turns rather than charging\nthe whole context on every turn. **Multiply every projection derived from this model by 0.54.**\nFailing to do so is how the +2.51% above would have become a false claim of reconciliation.\"\"\")\n\ns = s.replace(\n\"\"\"| | persist-tokens | as % of 38.6M |\n|---|---|---|\n| graph-addressable pool | 24.1M | 62.4% |\n| …of which coverage-fixable | ~7.5M | **19.4%** |\n| …of which ignored-payload (needs an instruction) | ~5.2M | 13.5% |\n| …of which already captured | 3.78M | 9.8% |\n| payload cost to widen coverage (projection) | −2 to −3M | −5 to −8% |\n\n**Coverage work, delivered perfectly and priced honestly: ≈ +12%.**\n**R-A (remove the call toll): +4.8% to +6.9%** — computed directly, not modelled.\n**Together: +15% to +19%.**\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| | persist-tokens | raw % of 38.6M | **calibrated ×0.54** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| graph-addressable pool | 24.1M | 62.4% | 33.7% |\n| …of which coverage-fixable | 7.53M | 19.5% | **10.5%** |\n| …of which ignored-payload (needs an instruction) | 5.18M | 13.4% | 7.2% |\n| …of which already captured | 3.77M | 9.8% | 5.3% |\n| payload cost to widen coverage (projection) | −2 to −3M | −5 to −8% | −3 to −4% |\n\n**Coverage work, delivered perfectly and priced honestly: ≈ +7%** (13.0% raw × 0.54).\n**R-A (remove the call toll): +4.8% to +6.9%** — computed directly from turns × tokens/turn, so\nit needs **no** calibration.\n**Together: +12% to +14%.**\n\nNote the calibrated addressable pool is **33.7%** — so even capturing *the entire* graph-\naddressable surface at zero payload cost would land at roughly 34%, and 13.4% raw / 7.2%\ncalibrated of it is ignored-payload that no tool change reaches.\"\"\")\n\ns = s.replace(\"| coverage + R-A, from the context budget | **+15% to +19%** |\",\n              \"| coverage + R-A, from the calibrated context budget | **+12% to +14%** |\")\ns = s.replace(\"> **35% is not reachable on a fair measurement. The honest number is +15% to +21%.**\",\n              \"> **35% is not reachable on a fair measurement. The honest number is +12% to +21%**, and the\\n> two estimates built from this session's context budget sit at the bottom of that range.\")\ns = s.replace(\"Today that is **30.9%** (all-terms 15.9% + partial credit). Gate on raising it.\",\n              \"Today that is **30.9%** (all-terms 15.9% + partial credit). Gate on raising it.\\nExpected value after calibration: **≈ +7%**, not the +12% the raw model suggests.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"calibrated:\", \"×0.54\" in s, \"| +12% to +14%\" in s or \"+12% to +14%\" in s)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\n# independent re-verification of the calibrated total\nraw_cov=7.53; base=38.6; payload=2.5; cal=1.35/2.51\nnet_raw=(raw_cov-payload)/base*100\nprint(f\"coverage net raw {net_raw:.1f}%  calibrated {net_raw*cal:.1f}%\")\nprint(f\"+ R-A 4.8-6.9% (uncalibrated, measured directly)\")\nprint(f\"TOTAL {net_raw*cal+4.8:.1f}% to {net_raw*cal+6.9:.1f}%\")\nprint(f\"calibrated addressable ceiling: {24.09/base*100*cal:.1f}%\")\nPY","description":"Apply calibration and re-verify totals"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_read_input_tokens":526451,"output_tokens":2771,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1302,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2771,"cache_read_input_tokens":526451,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1302},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqW6gjK91VnerUwqAJSB","type":"assistant","uuid":"cd09661e-eaf3-43c3-af02-357e5a31225d","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:17:10.828Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"cd09661e-eaf3-43c3-af02-357e5a31225d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"82948d44-f96f-4a9c-bbef-d92853afff75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GTQuYaXC65mf7ChSCnWfmp","type":"tool_result","content":"calibrated: True True\ncoverage net raw 13.0%  calibrated 7.0%\n+ R-A 4.8-6.9% (uncalibrated, measured directly)\nTOTAL 11.8% to 13.9%\ncalibrated addressable ceiling: 33.6%","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"28d10dde-48b2-44ba-951d-628e0c7f274a","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:17:18.906Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"calibrated: True True\ncoverage net raw 13.0%  calibrated 7.0%\n+ R-A 4.8-6.9% (uncalibrated, measured directly)\nTOTAL 11.8% to 13.9%\ncalibrated addressable ceiling: 33.6%","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cd09661e-eaf3-43c3-af02-357e5a31225d","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"28d10dde-48b2-44ba-951d-628e0c7f274a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/EG-FINAL-PLAN.md","snippet":"1\t# entire-graph — the finalized plan\n2\t\n3\t**2026-08-08.** Supersedes `PLAN-TO-35PCT.md` and `EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md`. Everything below is\n4\tmeasured on rep50 (49 gated pairs, Opus, SWE-bench Multilingual) unless marked projection.\n5\tSign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. The metric is context, not messages\n10\t\n11\t    tokens +1.35%  =  turns −1.42%  +  tokens/turn +2.74%\n12\t\n13\tThe eg arm spends **38 more turns** and still wins, so the saving is not a message saving.\n14\t**cache_read is 95.5% of all tokens** (cache_creation 3.0%, output 1.5%). This is a context-size\n15\tproblem. The independent prefetch measurement at `run_3arm.sh:482` found the same thing on a\n16\tdifferent cell (30,302 → 29,334 tok/turn, −3.2%).\n17\t\n18\tVariance decomposition of the paired log token ratio: turns 34.2%, tokens/turn 26.0%, covariance\n19\t39.8% (entangled, corr +0.668). Neither side dominates alone.\n20\t\n21\t**Accounting unit used throughout:** a tool result injected at turn *i* is re-charged on every\n22\tlater turn, so its cost is `(bytes ÷ 4) × turns-remaining` — \"persist-tokens\".\n23\t\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t## 2. The complete budget\n27\t\n28\tBaseline total: **38.6M persist-tokens**. eg: 38.5M. **The tool is context-neutral (+0.2%).**\n29\t\n30\t| category | baseline | share | eg | captured |\n31\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n32\t| **source-code exploration** | 10.48M | 27.2% | 8.25M | **21%** |\n33\t| **whole-file `Read`** | 11.67M | 30.3% | 9.20M | **21%** |\n34\t| test exploration | 1.94M | 5.0% | 2.87M | **−48%** |\n35\t| range `Read` | 3.60M | 9.3% | 4.40M | −22% |\n36\t| harness runs | 4.30M | 11.2% | 3.70M | 14% |\n37\t| log / scratch output | 1.95M | 5.1% | 2.36M | not addressable |\n38\t| environment / deps | 0.76M | 2.0% | 0.62M | not addressable |\n39\t| build manifests | 0.31M | 0.8% | 0.34M | not addressable |\n40\t| graph calls | 0 | — | 1.70M | cost |\n41\t\n42\t**Graph-addressable = source exploration + whole-file reads + tests = 24.1M of 38.6M (62.4%).**\n43\teg captures 3.77M gross and adds 2.80M (graph calls 1.70M, range reads +0.80M, logs +0.41M,\n44\tmisc −0.11M), so **net 0.97M = +2.51% of context**.\n45\t\n46\t**CALIBRATION — the model over-predicts by ~1.9×.** Measured headline is **+1.35%**, so\n47\tpersist-tokens are not proportional to billed tokens: the unit ignores prompt, system and\n48\tthinking tokens, and it charges each injection once against remaining turns rather than charging\n49\tthe whole context on every turn. **Multiply every projection derived from this model by 0.54.**\n50\tFailing to do so is how the +2.51% above would have become a false claim of reconciliation.\n51\t\n52\tTwo structural facts that kill obvious ideas:\n53\t\n54\t- **Exploration calls are already cheap** — median **732 B**, p90 3.6 KB, 1.3% over 8 KB. Its 47%\n55\t  share is *volume* (1,206 calls), not size. The graph's own output has a median of **1,124 B**,\n56\t  larger than a median grep, so a graph-backed grep would add bytes. (Kills R-B.)\n57\t- **Whole-file reads are the opposite** — 119 calls, median 5,125 B, p90 20 KB; 39 calls carry\n58\t  70.9% of the bytes. 98k persist-tokens each, **7× an exploration call**.\n59\t\n60\t---\n61\t\n62\t## 3. Why the uncaptured cost is uncaptured — the decisive split\n63\t\n64\tFor every remaining call, was what it asked for already in the delivered payload?\n65\t\n66\t**Whole-file reads still made by eg (105 calls, 9.2M):**\n67\t\n68\t| cause | calls | share of cost |\n69\t|---|---|---|\n70\t| **c) file was in the payload WITH its body** | 24 | **42.3%** |\n71\t| no payload logged (detector bug, §6.1) | 36 | 36.0% |\n72\t| a) file never in the payload | 42 | 21.1% |\n73\t| b) in payload as a locator only | 3 | 0.5% |\n74\t\n75\t**Source-code exploration still done by eg (319 calls with a logged payload, 8.09M):**\n76\t\n77\t| cause | calls | share of cost |\n78\t|---|---|---|\n79\t| **coverage — no query term in payload** | 117 | **26.9%** |\n80\t| **partial coverage — some terms** | 96 | **42.2%** |\n81\t| ignored payload — all terms delivered | 57 | 15.9% |\n82\t| no identifier in the query | 49 | 15.0% |\n83\t\n84\t**These point in opposite directions and that is the whole finding.**\n85\tWhole-file reads are dominated by the agent re-opening a file it was already given in full —\n86\t**not tool-fixable**, and the same wall as 0/66 verb adoption. Source exploration is dominated by\n87\t**coverage (69.1%)** — the payload genuinely did not contain what the agent asked for next, and\n88\tthe misses are specific symbol lookups the graph should own (`replaceGt|replaceLt|replaceGte`,\n89\t`def get_deprecation_message`, `path_hooks|def _install`).\n90\t\n91\t---\n92\t\n93\t## 4. The ceiling, computed from the budget\n94\t\n95\t| | persist-tokens | raw % of 38.6M | **calibrated ×0.54** |\n96\t|---|---|---|---|\n97\t| graph-addressable pool | 24.1M | 62.4% | 33.7% |\n98\t| …of which coverage-fixable | 7.53M | 19.5% | **10.5%** |\n99\t| …of which ignored-payload (needs an instruction) | 5.18M | 13.4% | 7.2% |\n100\t| …of which already captured | 3.77M | 9.8% | 5.3% |\n101\t| payload cost to widen coverage (projection) | −2 to −3M | −5 to −8% | −3 to −4% |\n102\t\n103\t**Coverage work, delivered perfectly and priced honestly: ≈ +7%** (13.0% raw × 0.54).\n104\t**R-A (remove the call toll): +4.8% to +6.9%** — computed directly from turns × tokens/turn, so\n105\tit needs **no** calibration.\n106\t**Together: +12% to +14%.**\n107\t\n108\tNote the calibrated addressable pool is **33.7%** — so even capturing *the entire* graph-\n109\taddressable surface at zero payload cost would land at roughly 34%, and 13.4% raw / 7.2%\n110\tcalibrated of it is ignored-payload that no tool change reaches.\n111\t\n112\t35% would require capturing ~65–70% of the addressable pool at near-zero payload cost. The\n113\tignored-payload share alone (13.5%) is out of reach without an instruction, and an instruction\n114\ttelling the agent to re-read less would help a no-tool arm equally — **which is exactly what the\n115\twithdrawn −35% contained** (removing two such sentences moved that cell from −14.9% to +9.1%).\n116\t\n117\t**Seven independent derivations, all landing in the same band:**\n118\t\n119\t| route | ceiling |\n120\t|---|---|\n121\t| perfect loser repair (= the lift pool, exact) | **+21.21%** |\n122\t| best fair cell ever measured (opus xhigh, n=26) | **+17.21%** |\n123\t| coverage + R-A, from the calibrated context budget | **+12% to +14%** |\n124\t| R-A + R-B + current, message model | ≈ +17% |\n125\t| expensive-baseline tercile (78% of token mass) | +8.07% |\n126\t| hand-classified post-edit waste (763 calls) | +2.67% to +4.57% |\n127\t| directly addressable post-edit surface | +2.3% |\n128\t\n129\t> **35% is not reachable on a fair measurement. The honest number is +12% to +21%**, and the\n130\t> two estimates built from this session's context budget sit at the bottom of that range.\n131\t\n132\t---\n133\t\n134\t## 5. What to do, in order\n135\t\n136\t### 5.1 SHIP — R-A, zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, committed `b669a57b`)*\n137\t\n138\t`EG_PREFETCH=1` has always injected the payload into turn 0 **and** let the agent's residual\n139\tsearch re-derive it at full price (~5 s + an index build) — delivered twice, paid for once at\n140\tfull price. That is why every prefetch attempt measured null. `EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual\n141\tcall an echo.\n142\t\n143\tOffline gate passed, $0: echo byte-identical to the prompt block; **0.02 s vs 5.21 s**; missing\n144\tpayload errors rather than silently re-querying; real search unaffected when unset; other verbs\n145\tunaffected; export proven eg-only by block matching (line 704, inside `arm = eg` 446–939 and the\n146\t`EG_PREFETCH` gate at 498).\n147\t\n148\tWorth **+4.8% to +6.9%**. Fair without qualification: the eg prompt gains tool output and *loses*\n149\tan instruction. **Next step: run it as a paired cell.**\n150\t\n151\t### 5.2 BUILD — coverage of the agent's *next* query\n152\t\n153\tTarget the 69.1% coverage share of source exploration. The failing queries are specific symbol\n154\tlookups. This is the one pool that is genuinely tool-fixable.\n155\t\n156\tDo **not** measure it with gold-file coverage — that metric is anti-correlated with winning\n157\t(gold at rank 1: losers 6/8, winners 2/5) and eleven payload metrics have died on it. Measure it\n\n... [68 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1c0897df-546d-41a8-97bc-296bc9fb07aa","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:17:18.919Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"1c0897df-546d-41a8-97bc-296bc9fb07aa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqWA5xtUqkdMJTiRKZG9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hour's work is finalized and verified. `devenv/EG-FINAL-PLAN.md`.\n\n## What the verification caught\n\nI nearly shipped a plan claiming the context model \"reconciles to the measurement.\" It doesn't — the persist-token model predicts **+2.51%** against a measured **+1.35%**, over-predicting by **~1.9×**. Every projection built on it now carries a **×0.54 calibration**, which pulled my own coverage estimate from +12% down to **+7%**.\n\n## The finalized position\n\n**The metric is context, not messages.** `tokens +1.35% = turns −1.42% + tok/turn +2.74%` — eg spends 38 *more* turns and still wins. cache_read is 95.5% of all tokens.\n\n**The complete budget** (38.6M persist-tokens, baseline):\n\n| category | share | eg captures |\n|---|---|---|\n| whole-file `Read` | 30.3% | 21% |\n| source-code exploration | 27.2% | 21% |\n| harness · tests · ranges · logs · env · manifests | 42.5% | ~0 |\n\nGraph-addressable = **62.4% raw, 33.7% calibrated**. So even capturing the *entire* addressable surface at zero payload cost lands at ~34% — and 7.2% of that is ignored-payload no tool change reaches.\n\n**The decisive split — and the two pools point opposite ways:**\n\n- **Whole-file reads: 42.3% of remaining cost is the agent re-opening a file the payload already gave it in full.** Not tool-fixable. Same wall as 0/66 verb adoption.\n- **Source exploration: 69.1% is a genuine coverage gap** — the misses are specific symbol lookups (`replaceGt|replaceLt|replaceGte`, `def get_deprecation_message`). This is the one genuinely fixable pool.\n\n## The answer on 35%\n\n**Not reachable on a fair measurement.** Seven independent derivations, and the two built this hour from the context budget sit at the *bottom* of the band:\n\n| route | ceiling |\n|---|---|\n| perfect loser repair (exact — the lift pool) | +21.21% |\n| best fair cell ever measured | +17.21% |\n| **calibrated context budget: coverage + R-A** | **+12% to +14%** |\n\nReaching 35% requires an instruction telling the agent to explore and re-read less — which helps a no-tool arm equally, and is precisely what the withdrawn −35% contained.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. **Ship R-A** — built, offline-gated, committed `b669a57b`. Fixes a real defect: prefetch injected the payload into turn 0 *and* let the agent re-derive it at full price. Worth **+4.8–6.9%**, fair without qualification. Ready to run as a cell.\n2. **Build next-query coverage** — gate on \"fraction of identifiers the agent greps for that were in the payload,\" today **30.9%**. Not gold-file coverage, which is anti-correlated with winning. Worth ~**+7%**.\n3. **Don't build**: R-B (dead twice), any fourth tail verb (0/66), whole-file suppression (42.3% is ignored payload).\n\nAlso in the file: four corrections issued this session, two of them to my own earlier claims, and four open defects to fix before the next cell."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6551,"cache_read_input_tokens":527753,"output_tokens":1106,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6551,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1106,"cache_read_input_tokens":527753,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6551},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqW9szZUDWmMoprcAxjP","type":"assistant","uuid":"70d85bcf-cc54-451a-b7e2-51bba5c97c9c","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:17:38.481Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/