{"parentUuid":"732ddbd6-9bff-4b89-ace2-1e6b910658ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqXKFFrXqCZnxhueL35W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Status**\n\n| cell | arm | n | TOKEN | CI | median | wins |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| rep50 4-arm | eg | 49/49 | +1.35% | [−16.9, +18.1] | −4.2% | 24/49 |\n| | cmm | 49/49 | −5.95% | [−28.2, +13.3] | −2.9% | 22/49 |\n| | graphify | 48/49 | −0.50% | [−16.4, +13.9] | −8.1% | 18/48 |\n| G2 (rider) | eg vs base | 10 | −12.19% | — | −14.45% | 3/10 |\n| G3 (displacement) | eg vs base | 11 | −1.24% | — | −0.40% | 5/11 |\n| Gemini 300 | — | 207 | −8.78% | — | — | VM A terminated |\n| rep30 | — | — | — | — | — | VM B terminated, 52 unfinished |\n\n**Flags:** wt 0 · cmm SKIP 0 · graphify SKIP 0 · max-turns 1 · none arm-asymmetric. Open: `carbon-2981` 371 KB patch, `EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector bug. C idle.\n\n**Changed — R-A verified, and it needs a caveat I hadn't stated.** Counterfactual on all 49 pairs, holding each session's own tokens/turn fixed (sanity check reproduces +1.35% exactly at zero removal):\n\n| | point | bootstrap CI |\n|---|---|---|\n| R-A at 1.00 msg/call | **+4.26%** | [−14.44, +21.18] |\n| R-A at 1.61 msg/call | **+6.04%** | [−11.21, +22.20] |\n\nThe point estimates hold (+4.3% to +6.0%, slightly below the +4.8–6.9% in the plan — correcting), **but the CI spans zero**. At n=49 with this noise floor, R-A is not separable from zero in a single cell — it would need ~2–3× the instances, or paired replication, to demonstrate rather than merely estimate.\n\nSensitivity is reassuring though: even if pre-delivery degrades the payload enough to cost back 40 extra greps suite-wide, it still lands **+4.74%**. The mechanism is robust; the *measurement* of it is what's underpowered.\n\nUpdating the plan with the CI and the corrected range, then continuing on the 69.1% coverage claim."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,