{"parentUuid":"c6e9789f-a366-425d-8e4f-351fb19b3d7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqY1NNrFeZGrgSfQgNR2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JT98DDWqMioNZeDyQjWY62","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='EG-FINAL-PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"**Coverage work, delivered perfectly and priced honestly: ≈ +10.7%** (13.0% net raw × 0.822).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Coverage work, delivered perfectly and priced honestly: ≈ +4%.**\n\nThat is down from an earlier +10.7% in this same document, because the coverage gap is mostly\n*not graph-answerable*. Of the 481 identifiers the agent grepped for that were absent from the\npayload:\n\n| | count | share | fixable? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| symbol exists in the graph, payload omitted it | 137 | **40.4%** | yes — budget/ranking |\n| not a graph symbol at all | 202 | **59.6%** | **no** |\n\nThe unfixable majority are stdlib and builtins (`deepcopy`, `assert`, `__version__`,\n`path_hooks`), string literals that are not definitions (`required_if`), local variables\n(`_play_iterator`), and test functions the payload deliberately demotes\n(`test_play_iterator_nested`). None is a question a code graph answers.\n\nSo: 69.1% of source-exploration cost is a coverage gap, but only ~40% of that gap is reachable\n→ 5.6M × 0.404 = 2.26M raw → ×0.822 = 1.86M → **4.8%**, less the payload growth needed to carry\nthose symbols (~1M raw, 0.8M calibrated) → **≈ +3.7%**.\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"**Together: +15.0% to +16.7%.**\",\"**Together: +8% to +10%.**\")\ns = s.replace(\"| coverage + R-A, calibrated context budget (slope 0.822) | **+15.0% to +16.7%** |\",\n              \"| coverage + R-A, calibrated context budget (slope 0.822) | **+8% to +10%** |\")\ns = s.replace(\"Today that is **30.9%** (all-terms 15.9% + partial credit). Gate on raising it.\\nExpected value after calibration (slope 0.822): **≈ +10.7%**.\",\n              \"Today that is **30.9%** (all-terms 15.9% + partial credit). Gate on raising it.\\nExpected value: **≈ +4%** — and note that ~60% of the gap is unreachable (stdlib, literals,\\nlocals, demoted tests), so the realistic gate is raising coverage of the **40% that are real\\nsymbols**, not of all missed terms.\")\ns = s.replace(\"> **35% is not reachable on a fair measurement. The honest number is +15% to +21%**, and the\\n> estimate built from this session's calibrated context budget (+15.5% to +17.6%) sits squarely\\n> on the best fair cell ever measured (+17.21%, n=26).\",\n              \"> **35% is not reachable on a fair measurement.** The honest band across seven derivations is\\n> **+8% to +21%**, and the estimate built from this session's calibrated context budget — the\\n> most carefully derived of them — is the *lowest*: **+8% to +10%**. Every time a claim in this\\n> document has been checked, the addressable pool has shrunk.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"updated:\", \"≈ +4%\" in s, \"+8% to +10%\" in s)\nPY\ngrep -n \"+8% to +10%\\|40.4%\\|≈ +4%\" EG-FINAL-PLAN.md | head","description":"Correct coverage lever in plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3333,"cache_read_input_tokens":557728,"output_tokens":2399,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3333,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2399,"cache_read_input_tokens":557728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3333},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqY1HEnVDdrvcTQiWatT","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"65b13e4b-7a64-43ea-ac8f-1dc94c872570","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:42:06.678Z","effort":