{"parentUuid":"0b9343e8-c548-4547-9269-2c11247c5792","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqYpcn5kmQycwvCB1eXZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0181kHvjdZRMc5rBrMyN95Up","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='EG-FINAL-PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"**Coverage work, delivered perfectly and priced honestly: ≈ +4%.**\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Coverage work, delivered perfectly and priced honestly: ≈ +0.5%. Effectively closed.**\n\nTwo screens, applied in sequence, take this from a headline lever to nothing:\n\n**Screen 1 — is the missed identifier even a graph symbol?** Of 481 grepped-for identifiers\nabsent from the payload, only **137 (40.4%)** exist in the graph. The rest are stdlib and\nbuiltins (`deepcopy`, `assert`, `__version__`, `path_hooks`), string literals that are not\ndefinitions (`required_if`), local variables (`_play_iterator`), and test functions the payload\ndeliberately demotes (`test_play_iterator_nested`).\n\n**Screen 2 — for the 40.4% that ARE symbols, is the omission a budget problem?** Replayed 14\nsessions' recorded queries at the shipped 16 KB budget and at 4× (64 KB):\n\n| | found | share of 64 wanted |\n|---|---|---|\n| @16 KB (shipped) | 3 | 5% |\n| @64 KB (4×) | 7 | 11% |\n| **budget-fixable** | +4 | **6%** |\n| **still missing at 4× budget** | 57 | **89%** |\n\nQuadrupling the payload recovers 6% of the gap. **89% is ranking-limited, not budget-limited** —\nthe graph knows the symbol and still does not surface it for that query at any budget worth\nshipping. And ranking is the one lever the corpus has refuted head-on: sessions where the gold\nfile ranked first *lost* more often (losers 6/8 at rank 1 vs winners 2/5).\n\nNet: 69.1% coverage gap × 40.4% are-symbols × ~11% recoverable ≈ **3% of source-exploration\ncost**, calibrated ≈ **+0.5%**, before paying for the wider payload. **Do not build this.**\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"**Together: +8% to +10%.**\",\"**Together: +4.3% to +6.0% — R-A alone. The coverage lever is closed.**\")\ns = s.replace(\"| coverage + R-A, calibrated context budget (slope 0.822) | **+8% to +10%** |\",\n              \"| R-A alone (coverage lever closed by two screens) | **+4.3% to +6.0%** |\")\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"> **35% is not reachable on a fair measurement.** The honest band across seven derivations is\n> **+8% to +21%**, and the estimate built from this session's calibrated context budget — the\n> most carefully derived of them — is the *lowest*: **+8% to +10%**. Every time a claim in this\n> document has been checked, the addressable pool has shrunk.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"> **35% is not reachable on a fair measurement.** The band across eight derivations is\n> **+4% to +21%**, and the more carefully a route is checked the lower it lands. The best-founded\n> remaining number is **R-A at +4.3% to +6.0%**, with a bootstrap CI that spans zero at n=49.\n>\n> **Five consecutive corrections this session, every one downward:** +35.06% → artifact;\n> message-displacement → context density; ×0.54 → validated slope 0.822; R-A +4.8–6.9% →\n> +4.3–6.0%; coverage +10.7% → +4% → **+0.5%**. Nothing has moved the other way. That pattern is\n> itself the finding.\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"### 5.2 BUILD — coverage of the agent's *next* query\"\"\",\n\"\"\"### 5.2 ~~BUILD — coverage of the agent's next query~~ **CLOSED, do not build**\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"updated:\", \"Effectively closed\" in s, \"+4.3% to +6.0% — R-A alone\" in s)\nPY\nP=graph-benchmarks-504800\nperl -e 'alarm shift; exec @ARGV' 300 gcloud compute ssh graphbench-c --project=$P --zone=us-east1-b --tunnel-through-iap --quiet --command='cd ~/work/graphmark/agentic-swebench\npython3 ~/sc50.py 2>/dev/null | head -4\necho \"live=$(ps -A -o command=|grep -c \"[c]laude -p\")\"\necho \"FLAGS wt=$(find logs -name \"sv50_*.log\" 2>/dev/null|xargs grep -l \"wt fail\" 2>/dev/null|wc -l) cmmskip=$(find logs -name \"sv50_cmm_*.log\" 2>/dev/null|xargs grep -l SKIP 2>/dev/null|wc -l) gfyskip=$(find logs -name \"sv50_graphify_*.log\" 2>/dev/null|xargs grep -l SKIP 2>/dev/null|wc -l) TO50=$(grep -rl \"error_max_turns\" results/REP50_r1_*/*/*/cc_out.json 2>/dev/null|wc -l)\"' 2>&1 | grep -vE 'NumPy|tcp-forward|WARNING|Warning'","description":"Close coverage lever in plan and refresh status","timeout":500000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1031,"cache_read_input_tokens":569746,"output_tokens":1891,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1031,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1891,"cache_read_input_tokens":569746,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1031},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqYpW3H7koS43u4gjRTT","type":"assistant","uuid":"573a2498-472d-4c4b-a261-3317bcea8dad","timestamp":"2026-08-08T15:52:43.033Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
