{"parentUuid":"8c49742b-5879-4743-a22f-d930a0aef59f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"37885c6d-495e-4e04-97c8-d84e0ad59295","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Give a benchmark status update: rep50 4-arm cell (baseline/eg/cmm/graphify) pair counts and token results per arm, plus Gemini 300 and any remaining rep30 cells. Flag any wt fails, cmm/graphify SKIPs, or arm-asymmetric problems. Keep it short — a table and anything that changed."},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"23da1520-4f42-48f1-a325-8cc6bea80f03","timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:11:18.850Z","permissionMode":"auto","promptSource":"system","queuePriority":"later","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"23da1520-4f42-48f1-a325-8cc6bea80f03","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqaGoy8DSEi6XtZJNJQR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AAg4rbrZCFQNBTX58MU4E1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='EG-FINAL-PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"**So the honest characterisation of the tool is not \"saves tokens\".** It is: *centrally neutral,\nwith occasional protection against a catastrophic baseline blow-up.* That is a real property and\nworth claiming — tail risk is expensive — but it is a different claim, it needs a different\nestimator (something like P(cost ratio > 1.5), which is far cheaper to power), and it should not\nbe reported as a mean token saving.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**So the honest characterisation of the tool is not \"saves tokens\".** It is *centrally neutral*,\nwith the positive headline resting on a few extreme pairs.\n\n**8.3a — and the \"tail insurance\" reading is RETRACTED, tested and refuted.**\nI proposed P(cost ratio > T) as a cheaper endpoint. Measured on the same 49 pairs, the arms blow\nup at indistinguishable rates:\n\n| threshold | eg | baseline | McNemar p |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| >1.25× | 17/49 | 17/49 | 1.000 |\n| >1.5× | 11/49 | 10/49 | 1.000 |\n| >2.0× | 4/49 | 4/49 | 1.000 |\n| >2.5× | 0/49 | **3/49** | 0.250 |\n| >3.0× | 0/49 | **2/49** | 0.500 |\n\nAt 1.5× the rates are 22.4% vs 20.4%, needing **n=6,338 (~$50,450)** — **13× worse than the mean\nendpoint**, because a proportion this close to 50/50 is the most expensive thing to resolve.\nThe only signal is at ≥2.5×, where the extremes are all baseline (3–0, 2–0) — consistent with\n`lombok-3674`, but p=0.25 at n=49. Suggestive, not evidence.\n\n**Every endpoint tried is now either null or unmeasurable: mean tokens, robust mean, tail risk.**\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"**8.4 Recommendation.** Do **not** run R-A on a rep50; it would return another uninterpretable\nnumber. Either fund ~220–500 pairs, or switch the endpoint to tail risk, or stop optimising\ntokens on this benchmark and report the tool on axes it can resolve.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**8.4 Recommendation.** Do **not** run R-A on a rep50 — it would return another uninterpretable\nnumber. The endpoint-switch escape is closed (§8.3a). That leaves two honest options:\n\n1. **Fund the measurement** — ~220 pairs winsorised (~$1,775) or ~500 raw (~$3,972) to resolve a\n   +6% effect. Worth it only if a +5% token saving is itself worth $4k to prove.\n2. **Stop optimising tokens on this benchmark** and report the tool on axes it can resolve:\n   resolution/correctness, latency to first correct edit, or whole-file-read suppression\n   (119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B, >8 KB tail 39 → 25) — all measurable at n=49.\n\nOption 2 is the recommendation. The tool does a real, demonstrable thing; token savings is\nsimply not the axis on which it can be shown at this sample size.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"updated:\", \"RETRACTED, tested and refuted\" in s, \"Option 2 is the recommendation\" in s)\nPY\nP=graph-benchmarks-504800\nperl -e 'alarm shift; exec @ARGV' 300 gcloud compute ssh graphbench-c --project=$P --zone=us-east1-b --tunnel-through-iap --quiet --command='cd ~/work/graphmark/agentic-swebench\npython3 ~/sc50.py 2>/dev/null | head -4\necho \"live=$(ps -A -o command=|grep -c \"[c]laude -p\")\"\necho \"FLAGS wt=$(find logs -name \"sv50_*.log\" 2>/dev/null|xargs grep -l \"wt fail\" 2>/dev/null|wc -l) cmmskip=$(find logs -name \"sv50_cmm_*.log\" 2>/dev/null|xargs grep -l SKIP 2>/dev/null|wc -l) gfyskip=$(find logs -name \"sv50_graphify_*.log\" 2>/dev/null|xargs grep -l SKIP 2>/dev/null|wc -l) TO50=$(grep -rl \"error_max_turns\" results/REP50_r1_*/*/*/cc_out.json 2>/dev/null|wc -l)\"' 2>&1 | grep -vE 'NumPy|tcp-forward|WARNING|Warning'","description":"Record tail-risk retraction and refresh status","timeout":500000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_seq