{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"38a5d957-2b95-482e-9b0b-47010ca39c8e","snapshotMessageId":"2c4c390a-e3ac-45ef-b38b-273488560a58","trackingPath":"PREREG-FABLE82.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-08-08T16:41:56.954Z","realParentDir":"/Users/suhaan/devenv"},"timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:41:56.988Z"}
{"parentUuid":"fa4379fd-54fc-41a0-91cb-ea99b12ab416","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqcZt6NrDxPLBwkBYFhX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0169eUjTxdbiFXA3V5xksVPY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/PREREG-FABLE82.md","content":"# Pre-registration — fable/max 82-pair cell\n\n**Written 2026-08-08, BEFORE launch.** Doctrine requires the prediction and its falsification\nbounds be fixed in writing before any session runs. Nothing below may be edited after launch;\namendments go in a dated appendix.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Why this cell and not another rep50\n\nEvery lever measured inside the rep50 cell (opus/max) tops out at +6%, and rep50's own headline\n(**+1.35%, t = −0.17**) is indistinguishable from zero. Scoring all model×effort cells together\nshows configuration dominates every tool change:\n\n| cell | n | TOTAL | geomean | 95% CI | median | wins |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **fable/max** | 19 | **+18.02%** | **+14.59%** | [−6.3, +32.0] | +16.42% | 13/19 |\n| opus/max (rep50) | 49 | +1.35% | +1.21% | [−13.5, +14.1] | −4.16% | 24/49 |\n| opus/max (SW) | 18 | −25.04% | −25.97% | [−66.3, +3.4] | −22.77% | 7/18 |\n\nDecisive asymmetry — **what it costs to demonstrate each cell's own observed effect**:\n\n| | fable/max | opus/max |\n|---|---|---|\n| observed geomean | +14.59% | +1.21% |\n| sd (paired log-ratio) | 0.508 | 0.494 |\n| **n to demonstrate its own effect** | **82 pairs ≈ $689** | **12,900 pairs ≈ $78,491** |\n\nFable's effect is provable for less than the G3 cell already spent. Opus's is not provable at any\nprice. **Fairness: both arms run the same model, so this is a benchmark-configuration choice, not\nan arm asymmetry.**\n\n## 2. Hypothesis and prediction\n\n**H1.** On fable/max, the graph arm's paired geomean token saving is **> 0** at α=0.05.\n\n**Point prediction: +14.6%**, from the n=19 pilot.\n**Pre-registered interval: [+5%, +25%].**\n\nPowered for 80% at α=0.05 (two-sided) to detect +14.6% given sd=0.508 → **n = 82 gated pairs.**\n\n## 3. PASS / WEAK / FAIL, fixed now\n\n| outcome | criterion |\n|---|---|\n| **PASS** | geomean > 0 with 95% CI excluding zero, AND point estimate ≥ +5% |\n| **WEAK** | point estimate ≥ +5% but CI includes zero → underpowered, report as such, do not claim |\n| **FAIL** | point estimate < +5%, or CI excludes zero on the negative side |\n\n**35% is NOT the target and will not be claimed.** Fable's pilot CI upper bound is +32.0%, so 35%\nis outside the range this cell can support. The honest target is **+15–20%, demonstrated**.\n\n## 4. Sample and launch parameters\n\n- **Launch ~90 pairs to land 82.** The pilot lost 25→19 (24%) to 0-byte `cc_out.json`.\n- Instances: the standard rep50 list plus the next 41 by the existing selection order. **Fixed\n  before launch; no post-hoc substitution.** Any instance that fails to produce a gated pair is\n  reported as a loss, not replaced.\n- Config: `CC_MODEL=fable`, `CC_EFFORT=max`, everything else identical to rep50\n  (`EG_PREFETCH=0`, `EG_TOPK=5`, `EG_MAXBYTES=32768`, `EG_PROFILE=full`, `EG_VERIFY_MODE=full`).\n- **`EG_ZEROTOLL` / R-A stays OFF.** One variable per cell. R-A is a separate future test.\n- Both arms fresh. Shards ≤ 6 drivers (sshd has wedged at 8+ three times).\n\n## 5. Preflight, required before launch\n\n1. **0-byte `cc_out.json` must retry, not silently drop.** Diagnosed cause of the pilot's 24%\n   loss: 9 files of 0 bytes, 4 of 5 affected instances failing in *both* arms (infrastructure,\n   not bias — but it costs sample).\n2. Assert prompt symmetry: diff both arms' `prompt.txt` and account for every differing line.\n   The only permitted difference is the capability-only tool block.\n3. Assert `--safe-mode` (or an explicit equivalent), so `.entire/graph-agent.md` cannot leak.\n4. Fix the `EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector before launch, or payload forensics on this cell is unusable.\n5. Verify graphs exist for every selected instance.\n\n## 6. Analysis plan, fixed now\n\n- **Primary:** paired geomean of the token ratio, bootstrap 95% CI (3,000 resamples).\n- **Reported alongside, always:** total (Σeg/Σbase), median, win count, Δturns.\n- **Secondary, pre-specified:** winsorised 20/80 geomean. The rep50 headline did *not* survive\n  winsorising (+1.21% → −0.26%); if fable's does not either, the effect is tail-carried and must\n  be reported as such.\n- **No subgroup analysis.** MDE is ~25–30 pts at n≈30; sub-groups of 3–7 are how the withdrawn\n  \"VERIFY-off is a −12pt lever\" and \"payload width costs 10.6pt\" claims were produced.\n- Cost split reported separately as cache_read / cache_creation / output.\n\n## 7. Known confounds, stated before seeing the result\n\n- **Model × effort × cell × instance-set are confounded in the pilot.** The within-instance\n  Fable–Opus contrast on 23 shared instances is **+15.8pt [−3.0, +32.1]** — spans zero. This cell\n  tests whether Fable's effect is real; it does **not** establish that Fable beats Opus.\n- Fable emits ~37.5K output tok/session against Opus's ~20K, so it has more to save per message\n  removed. That is a mechanism, not an artifact, but it limits generalisation to other models.\n- Run-level noise is ~87% of paired variance. This cell adds instances rather than replicates,\n  which is the variance-minimising choice at fixed budget.\n\n## 8. Cost\n\n82 gated pairs ≈ 90 launched × 2 arms × $4.20 ≈ **$756**. Cheaper than the G3 cell already spent.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":876,"cache_read_input_tokens":616613,"output_tokens":2326,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":876,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2326,"cache_read_input_tokens":616613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":876},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqcZi9qQgKMbsBi3esP7","type":"assistant","uuid":"38a5d957-2b95-482e-9b0b-47010ca39c8e","timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:41:56.947Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"38a5d957-2b95-482e-9b0b-47010ca39c8e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b6a2835a-45cd-43ea-8533-1504fefbc65f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0169eUjTxdbiFXA3V5xksVPY","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/suhaan/devenv/PREREG-FABLE82.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"2abb6600-b9d3-4e76-9308-66673153eadd","timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:41:57.001Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/PREREG-FABLE82.md","content":"# Pre-registration — fable/max 82-pair cell\n\n**Written 2026-08-08, BEFORE launch.** Doctrine requires the prediction and its falsification\nbounds be fixed in writing before any session runs. Nothing below may be edited after launch;\namendments go in a dated appendix.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Why this cell and not another rep50\n\nEvery lever measured inside the rep50 cell (opus/max) tops out at +6%, and rep50's own headline\n(**+1.35%, t = −0.17**) is indistinguishable from zero. Scoring all model×effort cells together\nshows configuration dominates every tool change:\n\n| cell | n | TOTAL | geomean | 95% CI | median | wins |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **fable/max** | 19 | **+18.02%** | **+14.59%** | [−6.3, +32.0] | +16.42% | 13/19 |\n| opus/max (rep50) | 49 | +1.35% | +1.21% | [−13.5, +14.1] | −4.16% | 24/49 |\n| opus/max (SW) | 18 | −25.04% | −25.97% | [−66.3, +3.4] | −22.77% | 7/18 |\n\nDecisive asymmetry — **what it costs to demonstrate each cell's own observed effect**:\n\n| | fable/max | opus/max |\n|---|---|---|\n| observed geomean | +14.59% | +1.21% |\n| sd (paired log-ratio) | 0.508 | 0.494 |\n| **n to demonstrate its own effect** | **82 pairs ≈ $689** | **12,900 pairs ≈ $78,491** |\n\nFable's effect is provable for less than the G3 cell already spent. Opus's is not provable at any\nprice. **Fairness: both arms run the same model, so this is a benchmark-configuration choice, not\nan arm asymmetry.**\n\n## 2. Hypothesis and prediction\n\n**H1.** On fable/max, the graph arm's paired geomean token saving is **> 0** at α=0.05.\n\n**Point prediction: +14.6%**, from the n=19 pilot.\n**Pre-registered interval: [+5%, +25%].**\n\nPowered for 80% at α=0.05 (two-sided) to detect +14.6% given sd=0.508 → **n = 82 gated pairs.**\n\n## 3. PASS / WEAK / FAIL, fixed now\n\n| outcome | criterion |\n|---|---|\n| **PASS** | geomean > 0 with 95% CI excluding zero, AND point estimate ≥ +5% |\n| **WEAK** | point estimate ≥ +5% but CI includes zero → underpowered, report as such, do not claim |\n| **FAIL** | point estimate < +5%, or CI excludes zero on the negative side |\n\n**35% is NOT the target and will not be claimed.** Fable's pilot CI upper bound is +32.0%, so 35%\nis outside the range this cell can support. The honest target is **+15–20%, demonstrated**.\n\n## 4. Sample and launch parameters\n\n- **Launch ~90 pairs to land 82.** The pilot lost 25→19 (24%) to 0-byte `cc_out.json`.\n- Instances: the standard rep50 list plus the next 41 by the existing selection order. **Fixed\n  before launch; no post-hoc substitution.** Any instance that fails to produce a gated pair is\n  reported as a loss, not replaced.\n- Config: `CC_MODEL=fable`, `CC_EFFORT=max`, everything else identical to rep50\n  (`EG_PREFETCH=0`, `EG_TOPK=5`, `EG_MAXBYTES=32768`, `EG_PROFILE=full`, `EG_VERIFY_MODE=full`).\n- **`EG_ZEROTOLL` / R-A stays OFF.** One variable per cell. R-A is a separate future test.\n- Both arms fresh. Shards ≤ 6 drivers (sshd has wedged at 8+ three times).\n\n## 5. Preflight, required before launch\n\n1. **0-byte `cc_out.json` must retry, not silently drop.** Diagnosed cause of the pilot's 24%\n   loss: 9 files of 0 bytes, 4 of 5 affected instances failing in *both* arms (infrastructure,\n   not bias — but it costs sample).\n2. Assert prompt symmetry: diff both arms' `prompt.txt` and account for every differing line.\n   The only permitted difference is the capability-only tool block.\n3. Assert `--safe-mode` (or an explicit equivalent), so `.entire/graph-agent.md` cannot leak.\n4. Fix the `EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector before launch, or payload forensics on this cell is unusable.\n5. Verify graphs exist for every selected instance.\n\n## 6. Analysis plan, fixed now\n\n- **Primary:** paired geomean of the token ratio, bootstrap 95% CI (3,000 resamples).\n- **Reported alongside, always:** total (Σeg/Σbase), median, win count, Δturns.\n- **Secondary, pre-specified:** winsorised 20/80 geomean. The rep50 headline did *not* survive\n  winsorising (+1.21% → −0.26%); if fable's does not either, the effect is tail-carried and must\n  be reported as such.\n- **No subgroup analysis.** MDE is ~25–30 pts at n≈30; sub-groups of 3–7 are how the withdrawn\n  \"VERIFY-off is a −12pt lever\" and \"payload width costs 10.6pt\" claims were produced.\n- Cost split reported separately as cache_read / cache_creation / output.\n\n## 7. Known confounds, stated before seeing the result\n\n- **Model × effort × cell × instance-set are confounded in the pilot.** The within-instance\n  Fable–Opus contrast on 23 shared instances is **+15.8pt [−3.0, +32.1]** — spans zero. This cell\n  tests whether Fable's effect is real; it does **not** establish that Fable beats Opus.\n- Fable emits ~37.5K output tok/session against Opus's ~20K, so it has more to save per message\n  removed. That is a mechanism, not an artifact, but it limits generalisation to other models.\n- Run-level noise is ~87% of paired variance. This cell adds instances rather than replicates,\n  which is the variance-minimising choice at fixed budget.\n\n## 8. Cost\n\n82 gated pairs ≈ 90 launched × 2 arms × $4.20 ≈ **$756**. Cheaper than the G3 cell already spent.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"38a5d957-2b95-482e-9b0b-47010ca39c8e","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
