{"parentUuid":"a7f1d9b0-ac19-4758-9661-67cba33eaff3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqd9FPTpLggJe9Vf8Ky4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good catch and a genuine save. Two findings:\n\n**Configs are effectively identical** — only `O35_ARGV_PARITY` differs in the template files (rep50=1, r100=0), and `sweep60.sh` explicitly overrides it to 1 at launch. `CC_MAX_TURNS=120` in both. My confound worry there was unfounded.\n\n**But the instance sets are different, and that's real.** The fable pilot covered 26 instances drawn from `multilingual_300` (lucene, ruff, carbon, caddy, docusaurus, faker…), *not* rep50's 49. So my headline comparison — fable/max +18.02% vs rep50 opus/max +1.35% — is across **different instance sets**, which is exactly the confound the ledger warns about. Launching my pre-reg against `rep50_run.json` as written would not have reproduced the pilot at all.\n\nThe matched comparison is fable/max vs **SW_opus_max** (same launcher, same pool): **+18.02% vs −25.04%**. Fixing the pre-reg:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2198,"cache_read_input_tokens":634078,"output_tokens":2642,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2198,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2642,"cache_read_input_tokens":634078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2198},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqd96oXmBvmmbjsgA4CB","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"2c80c0b8-fccc-48b6-a099-4dee38e0351e","timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:49:20.513Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"2c80c0b8-fccc-48b6-a099-4dee38e0351e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqd9FPTpLggJe9Vf8Ky4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WmM2wAA8TKJiMm99kT546b","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='PREREG-FABLE82.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"- Instances: the standard rep50 list plus the next 41 by the existing selection order. **Fixed\n  before launch; no post-hoc substitution.** Any instance that fails to produce a gated pair is\n  reported as a loss, not replaced.\n- Config: `CC_MODEL=fable`, `CC_EFFORT=max`, everything else identical to rep50\n  (`EG_PREFETCH=0`, `EG_TOPK=5`, `EG_MAXBYTES=32768`, `EG_PROFILE=full`, `EG_VERIFY_MODE=full`).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Instances: drawn from `tasks/multilingual_300.json`, NOT `tasks/rep50_run.json`.**\n  *(Corrected before launch.)* The pilot covered 26 instances from the 300-pool (lucene, ruff,\n  carbon, caddy, docusaurus, faker…). rep50's 49 are a different set, so launching against them\n  would not reproduce the pilot conditions and would confound instance-set with model. Take the\n  pilot's 26 plus the next 64 from the 300-pool by existing selection order, requiring\n  `graphs/<iid>/graph.edges.ndjson` to exist (310 graphs are built).\n  **Fixed before launch; no post-hoc substitution.** Any instance failing to yield a gated pair\n  is reported as a loss, not replaced.\n- Config: `CC_MODEL=fable`, `CC_EFFORT=max`, `CC_MAX_TURNS=120`, `O35_ARGV_PARITY=1`, and\n  otherwise the shipped defaults (`EG_PREFETCH=0`, `EG_TOPK=5`, `EG_MAXBYTES=32768`,\n  `EG_PROFILE=full`, `EG_VERIFY_MODE=full`, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`, `PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`).\n  Verified: `run_REP50.sh` and `run_r100.sh` differ only on `O35_ARGV_PARITY`, which `sweep60.sh`\n  overrides to 1 at launch — so the pilot and rep50 ran the same tool config.\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"| **fable/max** | 19 | **+18.02%** | **+14.59%** | [−6.3, +32.0] | +16.42% | 13/19 |\n| opus/max (rep50) | 49 | +1.35% | +1.21% | [−13.5, +14.1] | −4.16% | 24/49 |\n| opus/max (SW) | 18 | −25.04% | −25.97% | [−66.3, +3.4] | −22.77% | 7/18 |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| **fable/max** | 19 | **+18.02%** | **+14.59%** | [−6.3, +32.0] | +16.42% | 13/19 |\n| opus/max (SW — **same launcher and pool**) | 18 | −25.04% | −25.97% | [−66.3, +3.4] | −22.77% | 7/18 |\n| opus/max (rep50 — *different instance set*) | 49 | +1.35% | +1.21% | [−13.5, +14.1] | −4.16% | 24/49 |\n\n**The matched contrast is fable/max vs SW opus/max** (same launcher, same 300-pool):\n+18.02% against −25.04%. The rep50 row is a different instance set and must not be used as the\ncomparator — doing so confounds instance-set with model.\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"- **Model × effort × cell × instance-set are confounded in the pilot.**\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Instance-set was nearly confounded with model in my own first analysis** — caught during\n  preflight. The pilot draws from the 300-pool; rep50 uses its own 49. This cell uses the\n  300-pool so the comparison is matched.\n- **Model × effort × cell × instance-set are confounded in the pilot.**\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"prereg corrected:\", \"multilingual_300.json`, NOT\" in s, \"same launcher and pool\" in s)\nPY\ngrep -n \"multilingual_300\\|matched contrast\" PREREG-FABLE82.md | head","description":"Correct instance pool in pre-registration"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2198,"cache_read_input_tokens":634078,"output_tokens":2642,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2198,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2642,"cache_read_input_tokens":634078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2198},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqd96oXmBvmmbjsgA4CB","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"add33aa9-a802-48cb-882c-fd8a7b508555","timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:49:35.272Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"add33aa9-a802-48cb-882c-fd8a7b508555","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7929b287-8faf-473a-99e0-6edfdea4140b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WmM2wAA8TKJiMm99kT546b","type":"tool_result","content":"prereg corrected: True True\n21:**The matched contrast is fable/max vs SW opus/max** (same launcher, same 300-pool):\n60:- **Instances: drawn from `tasks/multilingual_300.json`, NOT `tasks/rep50_run.json`.**","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"489d5117-eecf-4a60-91e9-9030d95baa61","timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:49:37.585Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"prereg corrected: True True\n21:**The matched contrast is fable/max vs SW opus/max** (same launcher, same 300-pool):\n60:- **Instances: drawn from `tasks/multilingual_300.json`, NOT `tasks/rep50_run.json`.**","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"add33aa9-a802-48cb-882c-fd8a7b508555","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"489d5117-eecf-4a60-91e9-9030d95baa61","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/PREREG-FABLE82.md","snippet":"1\t# Pre-registration — fable/max 82-pair cell\n2\t\n3\t**Written 2026-08-08, BEFORE launch.** Doctrine requires the prediction and its falsification\n4\tbounds be fixed in writing before any session runs. Nothing below may be edited after launch;\n5\tamendments go in a dated appendix.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Why this cell and not another rep50\n10\t\n11\tEvery lever measured inside the rep50 cell (opus/max) tops out at +6%, and rep50's own headline\n12\t(**+1.35%, t = −0.17**) is indistinguishable from zero. Scoring all model×effort cells together\n13\tshows configuration dominates every tool change:\n14\t\n15\t| cell | n | TOTAL | geomean | 95% CI | median | wins |\n16\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n17\t| **fable/max** | 19 | **+18.02%** | **+14.59%** | [−6.3, +32.0] | +16.42% | 13/19 |\n18\t| opus/max (SW — **same launcher and pool**) | 18 | −25.04% | −25.97% | [−66.3, +3.4] | −22.77% | 7/18 |\n19\t| opus/max (rep50 — *different instance set*) | 49 | +1.35% | +1.21% | [−13.5, +14.1] | −4.16% | 24/49 |\n20\t\n21\t**The matched contrast is fable/max vs SW opus/max** (same launcher, same 300-pool):\n22\t+18.02% against −25.04%. The rep50 row is a different instance set and must not be used as the\n23\tcomparator — doing so confounds instance-set with model.\n24\t\n25\tDecisive asymmetry — **what it costs to demonstrate each cell's own observed effect**:\n26\t\n27\t| | fable/max | opus/max |\n28\t|---|---|---|\n29\t| observed geomean | +14.59% | +1.21% |\n30\t| sd (paired log-ratio) | 0.508 | 0.494 |\n31\t| **n to demonstrate its own effect** | **82 pairs ≈ $689** | **12,900 pairs ≈ $78,491** |\n32\t\n33\tFable's effect is provable for less than the G3 cell already spent. Opus's is not provable at any\n34\tprice. **Fairness: both arms run the same model, so this is a benchmark-configuration choice, not\n35\tan arm asymmetry.**\n36\t\n37\t## 2. Hypothesis and prediction\n38\t\n39\t**H1.** On fable/max, the graph arm's paired geomean token saving is **> 0** at α=0.05.\n40\t\n41\t**Point prediction: +14.6%**, from the n=19 pilot.\n42\t**Pre-registered interval: [+5%, +25%].**\n43\t\n44\tPowered for 80% at α=0.05 (two-sided) to detect +14.6% given sd=0.508 → **n = 82 gated pairs.**\n45\t\n46\t## 3. PASS / WEAK / FAIL, fixed now\n47\t\n48\t| outcome | criterion |\n49\t|---|---|\n50\t| **PASS** | geomean > 0 with 95% CI excluding zero, AND point estimate ≥ +5% |\n51\t| **WEAK** | point estimate ≥ +5% but CI includes zero → underpowered, report as such, do not claim |\n52\t| **FAIL** | point estimate < +5%, or CI excludes zero on the negative side |\n53\t\n54\t**35% is NOT the target and will not be claimed.** Fable's pilot CI upper bound is +32.0%, so 35%\n55\tis outside the range this cell can support. The honest target is **+15–20%, demonstrated**.\n56\t\n57\t## 4. Sample and launch parameters\n58\t\n59\t- **Launch ~90 pairs to land 82.** The pilot lost 25→19 (24%) to 0-byte `cc_out.json`.\n60\t- **Instances: drawn from `tasks/multilingual_300.json`, NOT `tasks/rep50_run.json`.**\n61\t  *(Corrected before launch.)* The pilot covered 26 instances from the 300-pool (lucene, ruff,\n62\t  carbon, caddy, docusaurus, faker…). rep50's 49 are a different set, so launching against them\n63\t  would not reproduce the pilot conditions and would confound instance-set with model. Take the\n64\t  pilot's 26 plus the next 64 from the 300-pool by existing selection order, requiring\n65\t  `graphs/<iid>/graph.edges.ndjson` to exist (310 graphs are built).\n66\t  **Fixed before launch; no post-hoc substitution.** Any instance failing to yield a gated pair\n67\t  is reported as a loss, not replaced.\n68\t- Config: `CC_MODEL=fable`, `CC_EFFORT=max`, `CC_MAX_TURNS=120`, `O35_ARGV_PARITY=1`, and\n69\t  otherwise the shipped defaults (`EG_PREFETCH=0`, `EG_TOPK=5`, `EG_MAXBYTES=32768`,\n70\t  `EG_PROFILE=full`, `EG_VERIFY_MODE=full`, `GQ_SEARCH_CAP=0`, `PUBLISHED_EXACT=1`).\n71\t  Verified: `run_REP50.sh` and `run_r100.sh` differ only on `O35_ARGV_PARITY`, which `sweep60.sh`\n72\t  overrides to 1 at launch — so the pilot and rep50 ran the same tool config.\n73\t- **`EG_ZEROTOLL` / R-A stays OFF.** One variable per cell. R-A is a separate future test.\n74\t- Both arms fresh. Shards ≤ 6 drivers (sshd has wedged at 8+ three times).\n75\t\n76\t## 5. Preflight, required before launch\n77\t\n78\t1. **0-byte `cc_out.json` must retry, not silently drop.** Diagnosed cause of the pilot's 24%\n79\t   loss: 9 files of 0 bytes, 4 of 5 affected instances failing in *both* arms (infrastructure,\n80\t   not bias — but it costs sample).\n81\t2. Assert prompt symmetry: diff both arms' `prompt.txt` and account for every differing line.\n82\t   The only permitted difference is the capability-only tool block.\n83\t3. Assert `--safe-mode` (or an explicit equivalent), so `.entire/graph-agent.md` cannot leak.\n84\t4. Fix the `EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector before launch, or payload forensics on this cell is unusable.\n85\t5. Verify graphs exist for every selected instance.\n86\t\n87\t## 6. Analysis plan, fixed now\n88\t\n89\t- **Primary:** paired geomean of the token ratio, bootstrap 95% CI (3,000 resamples).\n90\t- **Reported alongside, always:** total (Σeg/Σbase), median, win count, Δturns.\n91\t- **Secondary, pre-specified:** winsorised 20/80 geomean. The rep50 headline did *not* survive\n92\t  winsorising (+1.21% → −0.26%); if fable's does not either, the effect is tail-carried and must\n93\t  be reported as such.\n94\t- **No subgroup analysis.** MDE is ~25–30 pts at n≈30; sub-groups of 3–7 are how the withdrawn\n95\t  \"VERIFY-off is a −12pt lever\" and \"payload width costs 10.6pt\" claims were produced.\n96\t- Cost split reported separately as cache_read / cache_creation / output.\n97\t\n98\t## 7. Known confounds, stated before seeing the result\n99\t\n100\t- **Instance-set was nearly confounded with model in my own first analysis** — caught during\n101\t  preflight. The pilot draws from the 300-pool; rep50 uses its own 49. This cell uses the\n102\t  300-pool so the comparison is matched.\n103\t- **Model × effort × cell × instance-set are confounded in the pilot.** The within-instance\n104\t  Fable–Opus contrast on 23 shared instances is **+15.8pt [−3.0, +32.1]** — spans zero. This cell\n105\t  tests whether Fable's effect is real; it does **not** establish that Fable beats Opus.\n106\t- Fable emits ~37.5K output tok/session against Opus's ~20K, so it has more to save per message\n107\t  removed. That is a mechanism, not an artifact, but it limits generalisation to other models.\n108\t- Run-level noise is ~87% of paired variance. This cell adds instances rather than replicates,\n109\t  which is the variance-minimising choice at fixed budget.\n110\t\n111\t## 8. Cost\n112\t\n113\t82 gated pairs ≈ 90 launched × 2 arms × $4.20 ≈ **$756**. Cheaper than the G3 cell already spent."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"94ae9e5c-d0b5-4e74-9dc3-b74cd464c6e7","timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:49:37.594Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"94ae9e5c-d0b5-4e74-9dc3-b74cd464c6e7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[],"itemCount":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"eefd0480-cd39-4c65-96ab-fc04459832ad","timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:49:37.594Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"eefd0480-cd39-4c65-96ab-fc04459832ad","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqdCF1E8zKCBomtnRq8V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm self-pacing this loop — no Monitor, since this iteration was preflight work against files already on disk. Ran it now.\n\n**This iteration caught a design error in my own pre-registration before it cost money.** The fable pilot was launched by `sweep60.sh` against `tasks/multilingual_300.json`; rep50 uses its own 49-instance set. My pre-reg said \"everything else identical to rep50\" and would have selected rep50's instances — **confounding instance-set with model in the very cell built to isolate model.** Corrected: the cell now draws from the 300-pool, and the matched comparator is `SW_opus_max` (same launcher, same pool, **−25.04%**), not rep50's +1.35%.\n\nPreflight otherwise green: 310 graphs built, safe-mode enforced, `PUBLISHED_EXACT` on, auth/claude/binary present, `EG_PREFETCH=0` as required, 0 sessions live, 702 G free. Config diff between the two templates is a single variable (`O35_ARGV_PARITY`) which `sweep60.sh` already overrides — so pilot and rep50 ran the same *tool* config, and the model contrast is clean.\n\n**One preflight item remains genuinely blocking:** the 0-byte `cc_out.json` guard. Line 155 skips on `[ -s ... ]`, which is false for empty files, so a resume *would* re-run them — but nothing re-ran the pilot, which is why 24% of its sample was lost. I'll add an explicit retry before launch rather than accept a 24% loss on a $756 cell.\n\nNext iteration: implement that retry, then launch. Scheduling 20 minutes — enough to write and verify the guard properly rather than bolt it on."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5988,"cache_read_input_tokens":636276,"output_tokens":787,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"s