{"parentUuid":"024cdb5b-6ce1-48f2-98bb-9db6b11eb018","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqfSsCD1dQhHEjrqQND3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm self-pacing this loop; no Monitor, since the cell reports through files I poll on the status cadence anyway. This iteration ran the critical verification and launched.\n\n**Smoke passed on the second attempt: `model=claude-fable-5`, $2.84.** The first abort was my own bug — `modelUsage` lists several models per session (main + Haiku for auxiliary calls) and I read the wrong key. Selecting by cost share fixes it: fable-5 at 837,821 tokens/$2.75 vs haiku at 1,721 tokens/$0.0018.\n\nWorth noting the abort was still the right behaviour — it stopped a $756 run on a model-identity doubt rather than spending first and checking later, which is exactly what that check exists for. And verifying it forced me to confirm the pilot cells too: `SW_fable_max` genuinely recorded **claude-fable-5**, so the +18.02% basis is intact.\n\n**FAB82 is now launching** — 90 pre-registered instances (26 from the pilot, 64 new, all with graphs), 3 shards × 2 arms = 6 drivers, `EG_PREFETCH=0` so zero-toll stays inert as the pre-reg requires, 0-byte guard live.\n\nPredictions are fixed in `devenv/PREREG-FABLE82.md` and cannot move: **point +14.6%, interval [+5%, +25%], PASS requires CI excluding zero and ≥+5%. 35% is explicitly not claimable from this cell.**\n\nNext iteration checks driver health and early pair counts — 20 minutes is the right spacing since fable sessions ran ~25 turns in the smoke and the first completions won't land much sooner."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1924,"cache_read_input_tokens":661451,"output_tokens":752,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1924,"ephemeral_5m