{"parentUuid":"a9fd8dcd-c52f-4887-907d-0416ca541f87","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqgSy1KZeW8sYeez7ddv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011mTkYJop1tnuB3cy9TMzft","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2746,"cache_read_input_tokens":673989,"output_tokens":629,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2746,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":673989,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2746,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2746},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqgSsKmP4CbomGpjRvmE","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa41a651-f092-4d58-b2f0-c4074fd1093b","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:32:28.914Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"aa41a651-f092-4d58-b2f0-c4074fd1093b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b0f46be0-2c71-4d1c-96bc-346a5d0deab4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011mTkYJop1tnuB3cy9TMzft","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# entire-graph: the honest ceiling is ~+17%, and what to build to reach it\n2\t\n3\t## ⛔ FINAL MECHANISM (measured 2026-08-08) — why the ceiling is structural\n4\t\n5\tAcross all 49 rep50 eg sessions, keyed off transcripts:\n6\t\n7\t| | sessions |\n8\t|---|---|\n9\t| never called the graph | 0 |\n10\t| **called it ONLY before the first edit** | **42** |\n11\t| called it after an edit | **7** (8 calls total) |\n12\t\n13\t**86% of sessions stop using the graph the moment they start editing**, while **97.7% of the\n14\ttoken loss is post-edit** (ΔPre +0.40M vs ΔPost +17.31M).\n15\t\n16\t**The tool is absent from where the cost is.** Its addressable surface is the pre-edit phase =\n17\t**2.3% of the delta**. Every lever ever quantified — ranking 0.0, routing 0.0, harness\n18\tsuppression 0.0, payload +3.0, empty-payload +1.5–3.2 — is a lever on that 2.3%. That is the\n19\tceiling, and no amount of payload or ranking work moves it.\n20\t\n21\tIt also explains the corpus's strangest result: gold-at-rank-1 sessions LOST more often\n22\t(losers 6/8, winners 2/5). Retrieval governs the 2.3%; it has no purchase on the 97.7%.\n23\t\n24\t**Two gates failed for this reason, not for adoption:** G1 (`changed` verb, 0/5 despite being\n25\tadvertised at prompt line 48) and G2 (post-edit rider, 0/3). Both ride on an agent-initiated\n26\tgraph call. With 42/49 sessions making none post-edit, max reach is 14%. **Unreachable by\n27\tconstruction.** I built both before measuring whether the moment exists — one offline query\n28\tover existing data would have prevented both.\n29\t\n30\t### The only remaining route, and why it is blocked\n31\t\n32\tPost-edit help must not depend on the agent choosing to call the tool → a plugin hook firing\n33\tafter Edit/Write. Feasibility, checked:\n34\t\n35\t- `--safe-mode` disables ALL customizations **including hooks** (`run_3arm.sh:2364`), applied to\n36\t  every arm via `ISO_ARGS`. It exists because the operator's config leaked 9.4KB of skill +\n37\t  3.1KB subagent + 0.7KB deferred-tool listings into turn-0.\n38\t- There IS precedent for dropping it: `CC_NO_SAFE_MODE=1` (`:2391`) drops it **symmetrically**\n39\t  from every arm, and `EG_MCP=1` already uses this to give the tool arm an MCP server the\n40\t  baseline lacks — audited as \"tool availability only, no instruction\".\n41\t- **BLOCKER:** Claude Code reads hooks from a project-local `.claude/settings.json`. Writing\n42\t  that into the checkout puts an untracked file in the tree that `collect_patch.sh` scores via\n43\t  `git add -N && git diff` — **the hook config would land in the graded patch.** Fixable with\n44\t  `.git/info/exclude`, but that modifies the scoring path.\n45\t\n46\t**Verdict:** the route is real but requires changing how patches are collected. Do not attempt\n47\tit without deciding (a) whether unsolicited post-edit injection is fair — it is graph output\n48\tabout the agent's own edit, unlike a test runner, but the baseline has no analogue — and (b)\n49\twhether the patch-collection change is acceptable.\n50\t\n51\t> **VERDICT: 35% is not reachable on a fair measurement.** Six independent estimates converge on\n52\t> **+15–21%**, the directly addressable waste is **+2.67–4.57%**, and the best fair cell ever\n53\t> measured is **+17.21%** (opus xhigh, n=26). The original +35.06% target was an arithmetic\n54\t> artifact and is retracted below. This plan targets **+17–21%** and says plainly what it cannot do.\n55\t\n56\t| route | ceiling |\n57\t|---|---|\n58\t| directly addressable post-edit waste | **+2.67% to +4.57%** |\n59\t| expensive-baseline tercile (78% of mass) | +8.07% |\n60\t| fair symmetric ceiling (all post-edit pools) | +14.99% |"}]},"uuid":"b569e063-f29a-482d-9f00-7527bf5904bb","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:32:28.947Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","content":"# entire-graph: the honest ceiling is ~+17%, and what to build to reach it\n\n## ⛔ FINAL MECHANISM (measured 2026-08-08) — why the ceiling is structural\n\nAcross all 49 rep50 eg sessions, keyed off transcripts:\n\n| | sessions |\n|---|---|\n| never called the graph | 0 |\n| **called it ONLY before the first edit** | **42** |\n| called it after an edit | **7** (8 calls total) |\n\n**86% of sessions stop using the graph the moment they start editing**, while **97.7% of the\ntoken loss is post-edit** (ΔPre +0.40M vs ΔPost +17.31M).\n\n**The tool is absent from where the cost is.** Its addressable surface is the pre-edit phase =\n**2.3% of the delta**. Every lever ever quantified — ranking 0.0, routing 0.0, harness\nsuppression 0.0, payload +3.0, empty-payload +1.5–3.2 — is a lever on that 2.3%. That is the\nceiling, and no amount of payload or ranking work moves it.\n\nIt also explains the corpus's strangest result: gold-at-rank-1 sessions LOST more often\n(losers 6/8, winners 2/5). Retrieval governs the 2.3%; it has no purchase on the 97.7%.\n\n**Two gates failed for this reason, not for adoption:** G1 (`changed` verb, 0/5 despite being\nadvertised at prompt line 48) and G2 (post-edit rider, 0/3). Both ride on an agent-initiated\ngraph call. With 42/49 sessions making none post-edit, max reach is 14%. **Unreachable by\nconstruction.** I built both before measuring whether the moment exists — one offline query\nover existing data would have prevented both.\n\n### The only remaining route, and why it is blocked\n\nPost-edit help must not depend on the agent choosing to call the tool → a plugin hook firing\nafter Edit/Write. Feasibility, checked:\n\n- `--safe-mode` disables ALL customizations **including hooks** (`run_3arm.sh:2364`), applied to\n  every arm via `ISO_ARGS`. It exists because the operator's config leaked 9.4KB of skill +\n  3.1KB subagent + 0.7KB deferred-tool listings into turn-0.\n- There IS precedent for dropping it: `CC_NO_SAFE_MODE=1` (`:2391`) drops it **symmetrically**\n  from every arm, and `EG_MCP=1` already uses this to give the tool arm an MCP server the\n  baseline lacks — audited as \"tool availability only, no instruction\".\n- **BLOCKER:** Claude Code reads hooks from a project-local `.claude/settings.json`. Writing\n  that into the checkout puts an untracked file in the tree that `collect_patch.sh` scores via\n  `git add -N && git diff` — **the hook config would land in the graded patch.** Fixable with\n  `.git/info/exclude`, but that modifies the scoring path.\n\n**Verdict:** the route is real but requires changing how patches are collected. Do not attempt\nit without deciding (a) whether unsolicited post-edit injection is fair — it is graph output\nabout the agent's own edit, unlike a test runner, but the baseline has no analogue — and (b)\nwhether the patch-collection change is acceptable.\n\n> **VERDICT: 35% is not reachable on a fair measurement.** Six independent estimates converge on\n> **+15–21%**, the directly addressable waste is **+2.67–4.57%**, and the best fair cell ever\n> measured is **+17.21%** (opus xhigh, n=26). The original +35.06% target was an arithmetic\n> artifact and is retracted below. This plan targets **+17–21%** and says plainly what it cannot do.\n\n| route | ceiling |\n|---|---|\n| directly addressable post-edit waste | **+2.67% to +4.57%** |\n| expensive-baseline tercile (78% of mass) | +8.07% |\n| fair symmetric ceiling (all post-edit pools) | +14.99% |","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":515}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aa41a651-f092-4d58-b2f0-c4074fd1093b","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
