{"parentUuid":"10291ad2-f411-44c1-9fc5-c821cc0e895a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqgfeJYQqpB3HGtrSPVH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While that runs, checking the canonical ledger for live ideas I haven't tested:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4999,"cache_read_input_tokens":688118,"output_tokens":364,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4999,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":688118,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4999},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqgfWUW9UbKwPBsTphnt","type":"assistant","uuid":"346a9fc5-b064-49e6-b48c-5c80a6977514","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:35:15.972Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"346a9fc5-b064-49e6-b48c-5c80a6977514","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqgfeJYQqpB3HGtrSPVH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P6jiu4GBBYox3zrHumFRUe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n '26,72p' /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md","description":"Read live ideas from the ledger"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4999,"cache_read_input_tokens":688118,"output_tokens":364,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4999,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":688118,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4999},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqgfWUW9UbKwPBsTphnt","type":"assistant","uuid":"ceb65819-5ecb-43e3-a4dc-f8b233afcb5d","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:35:16.614Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"ceb65819-5ecb-43e3-a4dc-f8b233afcb5d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b0f46be0-2c71-4d1c-96bc-346a5d0deab4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P6jiu4GBBYox3zrHumFRUe","type":"tool_result","content":"## 1. LIVE — not yet refuted\n\n### 1.1 MOD vs ADD task kind ⭐ best current idea\nThe graph pays when the code to change **already exists and is broken**; it costs when the task is\nto **add behaviour that isn't there yet**.\n\n| cell | MOD | ADD |\n|---|---|---|\n| FABLEMAX | +21.1% (n=11) | +4.6% (n=8) |\n| OPUSHIGH | +13.4% (n=13) | −2.7% (n=8) |\n| FABLEFIX | +15.7% (n=5) | −21.5% (n=2) |\n| OPUSFIX | +1.0% (n=7) | −10.3% (n=3) |\n| **pooled** | **+14.35%** (n=36) | **−3.37%** (n=21) |\n\nSame sign **4/4 cells**, across both prompts and both models. ~17.7pt gap.\nMechanism: search always returns *something*; a confident wrong hit costs more than no hit.\nWorst instance in the campaign is a pure ADD — fluentd *\"add_tag_prefix parameter for in_http\nplugin\"*, **−263.6%**. Corroborated by an earlier measurement: gold at rank 2–3 (−85.3%) is worse\nthan gold not found at all (−25.6%).\n\n**Why this one is different from the dead levers:** it is a property of the **task**, knowable\nbefore the run. It cannot be division bias and cannot be a post-treatment artifact.\n\n**Status:** individual CIs overlap; not significant alone. Sign-consistency across 4 cells is the\nevidence. **Next: replicate at n=100 (rep100), split post-hoc by gold patch.**\n\n**BLOCKER — the rule is not deployable yet.** Routing on the gold patch is answer leakage. A\nkeyword classifier over the problem statement scores **57.5% against a 56% base rate**, ADD\nrecall **0.10** (10 of 100). See §3.1. Needs a better pre-run classifier before it can ship.\n\n### 1.2 One call must remove more than one message\nCurrently a graph call removes **zero**: on Opus the eg arm runs **+1.50 more greps** than the\nno-tool arm, against 32.25 greps/session. Substitution rate ≈ 0%.\nPool: pre+post grep = **32.25 msgs/session = 39.3% of the session**. Capturing 25% of it ≈ **−16%\ntokens**. Untested — every step from \"payload delivered\" to \"grep displaced\" is unproven.\n\n### 1.3 Harness suppression\nControlled for total post-edit call count, an extra grep costs nothing distinguishable, but an\nextra **throwaway harness** costs **+39,527 tok/call**, CI [+16.5K, +63.7K], stable to drop-10,\nnegative in 3/4 cells. The lever is giving the agent a verification command that actually **runs**,\nso it doesn't improvise one. Related: a VERIFY command that fails on the *environment* rather than\nthe patch sends the agent into 20–34 post-edit repair calls.\n\n---\n\n## 2. STRUCK — do not re-propose","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"761495f7-da26-4dc4-b8fe-e7a042c6bc2e","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:35:16.678Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 1. LIVE — not yet refuted\n\n### 1.1 MOD vs ADD task kind ⭐ best current idea\nThe graph pays when the code to change **already exists and is broken**; it costs when the task is\nto **add behaviour that isn't there yet**.\n\n| cell | MOD | ADD |\n|---|---|---|\n| FABLEMAX | +21.1% (n=11) | +4.6% (n=8) |\n| OPUSHIGH | +13.4% (n=13) | −2.7% (n=8) |\n| FABLEFIX | +15.7% (n=5) | −21.5% (n=2) |\n| OPUSFIX | +1.0% (n=7) | −10.3% (n=3) |\n| **pooled** | **+14.35%** (n=36) | **−3.37%** (n=21) |\n\nSame sign **4/4 cells**, across both prompts and both models. ~17.7pt gap.\nMechanism: search always returns *something*; a confident wrong hit costs more than no hit.\nWorst instance in the campaign is a pure ADD — fluentd *\"add_tag_prefix parameter for in_http\nplugin\"*, **−263.6%**. Corroborated by an earlier measurement: gold at rank 2–3 (−85.3%) is worse\nthan gold not found at all (−25.6%).\n\n**Why this one is different from the dead levers:** it is a property of the **task**, knowable\nbefore the run. It cannot be division bias and cannot be a post-treatment artifact.\n\n**Status:** individual CIs overlap; not significant alone. Sign-consistency across 4 cells is the\nevidence. **Next: replicate at n=100 (rep100), split post-hoc by gold patch.**\n\n**BLOCKER — the rule is not deployable yet.** Routing on the gold patch is answer leakage. A\nkeyword classifier over the problem statement scores **57.5% against a 56% base rate**, ADD\nrecall **0.10** (10 of 100). See §3.1. Needs a better pre-run classifier before it can ship.\n\n### 1.2 One call must remove more than one message\nCurrently a graph call removes **zero**: on Opus the eg arm runs **+1.50 more greps** than the\nno-tool arm, against 32.25 greps/session. Substitution rate ≈ 0%.\nPool: pre+post grep = **32.25 msgs/session = 39.3% of the session**. Capturing 25% of it ≈ **−16%\ntokens**. Untested — every step from \"payload delivered\" to \"grep displaced\" is unproven.\n\n### 1.3 Harness suppression\nControlled for total post-edit call count, an extra grep costs nothing distinguishable, but an\nextra **throwaway harness** costs **+39,527 tok/call**, CI [+16.5K, +63.7K], stable to drop-10,\nnegative in 3/4 cells. The lever is giving the agent a verification command that actually **runs**,\nso it doesn't improvise one. Related: a VERIFY command that fails on the *environment* rather than\nthe patch sends the agent into 20–34 post-edit repair calls.\n\n---\n\n## 2. STRUCK — do not re-propose","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ceb65819-5ecb-43e3-a4dc-f8b233afcb5d","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
