{"parentUuid":"08c72646-bcbd-4a3d-8ddc-f9c803c2af29","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqgk5YCrAk3FaFBtaWMt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4461,"cache_read_input_tokens":694536,"output_tokens":6184,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4461,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6184,"cache_read_input_tokens":694536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4461,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4461},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqgjwL6BZcPWdherQZ3o","type":"assistant","uuid":"038deec4-b045-49ad-a3af-ea3c5e867fed","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:36:39.451Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"038deec4-b045-49ad-a3af-ea3c5e867fed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqgk5YCrAk3FaFBtaWMt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fresh data confirms the ledger's live lever — **harness environment failures**:\n\n| | losers (eg/base) | winners (eg/base) |\n|---|---|---|\n| harness ENV failures | 102 / 80 → **+22** | 85 / 130 → **−45** |\n| throwaway scripts run | 163 / 147 → +16 | 159 / 207 → −48 |\n\n`corr(Δ env-failures, saving) = **−0.442**`. When eg's verification commands fail on the *environment* rather than the patch, the session loses. Winners show the mirror image.\n\nLet me draft the plan while the design review completes."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4461,"cache_read_input_tokens":694536,"output_tokens":6184,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4461,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6184,"cache_read_input_tokens":694536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4461,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4461},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqgjwL6BZcPWdherQZ3o","type":"assistant","uuid":"6a686fbe-c12f-422b-92d4-4175cf32cb70","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:36:41.162Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"6a686fbe-c12f-422b-92d4-4175cf32cb70","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqgk5YCrAk3FaFBtaWMt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YGALLyquwQKS8NjmWXPxzt","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","content":"# entire-graph on Opus — what the data says, and the only plan that survives it\n\n## Context\n\nThe goal set for this work is **35% token savings on rep50, fairly measured, on Opus**. This plan\nexists because that target is now refuted by the data, and continuing to aim at it would mean\neither fabricating it or measuring something else and calling it that. What follows is the\nevidence, the loser/winner analysis requested, and the plan that is actually supported.\n\nAll numbers: rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs, SWE-bench Multilingual.\nSign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Where Opus actually stands\n\n| | value |\n|---|---|\n| headline | **+1.35%** |\n| t-statistic | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n| median | −4.2% |\n| wins | 24 / 49 |\n| paired sd (log-ratio) | 0.494 |\n| n to *demonstrate* +1.35% | **12,900 pairs ≈ $78,491** |\n| n to demonstrate +6% | 499 pairs ≈ $3,972 |\n| n to demonstrate 35% | **11 pairs ≈ $88** |\n\n**35% would have been the cheapest result in the project to prove.** It is not provable because\nit is not there. Every robust estimator drives the headline to zero or below — winsorised 20/80\n**−0.26%**, dropping the 3 most extreme pairs **−6.19%** — so the positive sign is tail-carried.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Loser analysis (requested)\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts across 25 instances; top five carry −11.42 (57%).**\n\nGroup sums, eg minus baseline:\n\n| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n|---|---|---|\n| turns | **+296** | −258 |\n| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n| post-edit exploration | **+159** | −81 |\n| post-edit harness | **+50** | −88 |\n| edits | +42 | −25 |\n| graph calls | 44 (43 pre) | 50 (48 pre) |\n\n**The single most important line is pre-edit exploration: the graph works in BOTH groups\n(−46 / −58).** Localization is not what separates them. The entire divergence is post-edit, where\n**91 of 94 graph calls never happen** — 42/49 sessions make no graph call after their first edit.\n\nWorst five, with the pattern visible per-instance:\n\n| instance | pts | tok | eg/base turns | eg/base expl | eg/base harness |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `bat-1892` | −2.81 | −79.8% | 100/65 | 44/18 | 23/14 |\n| `valkey-790` | −2.72 | −127.4% | 93/54 | 57/34 | 20/11 |\n| `ansible-395e` | −2.58 | −68.1% | 116/91 | 48/38 | 9/5 |\n| `prometheus-9248` | −1.68 | −74.6% | 110/68 | 68/38 | 9/8 |\n| `tokio-4867` | −1.63 | −114.4% | 69/38 | 26/10 | 25/17 |\n\n**Correlates with token saving, ranked:**\n\n| | r |\n|---|---|\n| Δ harness runs | **−0.612** |\n| Δ exploration eliminated | +0.485 |\n| Δ repeat edits to same file | −0.457 |\n| Δ edit calls | −0.449 |\n| **Δ harness ENV failures** | **−0.442** |\n| Δ throwaway scripts run | −0.350 |\n| Δ first-edit turn | −0.342 |\n\n**Mechanism:** losers run verification that fails on the *environment* rather than the patch\n(eg 102 vs base 80 in the loser group), then improvise throwaway harnesses (+16) and re-explore\nto repair them (+159 post-edit exploration). Winners show the exact mirror: **−45 env failures,\n−48 throwaway scripts, −88 harness runs**. This is the ledger's §1.3 lever, independently\nreproduced here.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Winner analysis — what must not regress\n\n**Lift +21.21 pts across 24 instances. `lombok-3674` alone is +6.09 pts = 29% of ALL lift.**\n\n| instance | pts | eg/base turns | eg/base harness |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `lombok-3674` | **+6.09** | 67/122 | **23/70** |\n| `fmt-2457` | +2.18 | 38/67 | 12/13 |\n| `qutebrowser-c580` | +1.89 | 88/105 | 23/33 |\n| `vuejs-11739` | +1.35 | 70/80 | 24/19 |\n| `redis-11510` | +1.29 | 34/56 | 3/12 |\n\n**Winners win because the BASELINE flails and eg converges** — lombok's baseline ran `javac`\n**70 times** against eg's 23. eg is not doing something clever; it is failing to blow up.\n\n**Two consequences that constrain every proposal below:**\n\n1. **A symmetric frugality clamp is net-negative.** Suppressing over-verification helps the\n   baseline more than eg in exactly the instances eg currently wins. Already modelled; do not\n   ship one.\n2. **Any intervention that adds post-edit content risks converting a winner into a loser**, since\n   winners win by *doing less* after the first edit. Winner protection is therefore not a\n   formality — it is the main risk.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What is already closed (do not rebuild)\n\n| route | verdict |\n|---|---|\n| new verb in the affordance tail | **0/66 adoption** (`impact` 0/49, `changed` 0/5, `--path` 0/12) |\n| post-edit rider (G2) | **−12.19%**, fired 0/5 |\n| displacement via better verbs (G3) | ratio **0.76** vs 0.96 baseline — went backwards |\n| graph-backed grep | 38.9% interception ceiling; graph output (1,124 B median) is *larger* than a median grep (732 B) |\n| next-query coverage | only 40.4% of missed identifiers are graph symbols; of those 89% stay missing at 4× payload budget |\n| payload quality | 12 metrics dead, incl. complete-symbol density (r = **−0.170**) |\n| retrieval/ranking | anti-correlated — gold-at-rank-1 sessions lost more often |\n| tail-risk endpoint | arms blow up at identical rates (22.4% vs 20.4%); n=6,338 to resolve |\n\n---\n\n## 5. The plan\n\n### 5.1 Accept the honest target\n\n**Stop targeting 35% on Opus.** Target **loser repair**, whose exact ceiling is the lift pool:\n**+21.21%** if every losing instance were made precisely neutral. That is arithmetic, not\nprojection. Reaching it requires eliminating the drag pool entirely; a realistic fraction is\nworth +5–10%.\n\n### 5.2 Build: VERIFY runnability probe *(primary — targets the measured mechanism)*\n\n**Files:** `internal/sem/search_verify.go` (derivation + probe), `internal/cli/search.go`\n(VERIFY block emission).\n\nToday the only check is `exec.LookPath` on the runner (`search_verify.go:1526`) — it confirms\n`pytest` exists, never that the derived command *runs*. Add a **collect-only probe** before\nemitting: `pytest --collect-only -q`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`, `cargo test --no-run`,\n`mvn -q -DskipTests compile`. On failure, drop to the next rung rather than emitting a command\nthat will fail on the environment.\n\nAlso raise VERIFY coverage — it appears in only **8 of 33** payloads, so 76% of sessions get no\nverification command at all and improvise one.\n\n**Fair:** the derived command is tool output computed from the repo, same class as a ranked hit.\nShips no instruction; the baseline is untouched.\n\n**Expected: +0.5% to +1.5%.** Stated honestly — 22 avoided env-failures × ~39.5K tok ≈ 0.6% of\nthe pool. This is a real mechanism with a small effect, not a headline.\n\n### 5.3 Ship: R-A zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, deployed)*\n\nAlready committed (`b669a57b`) and deployed. `EG_PREFETCH=1` injected the payload into turn 0 and\nstill let the agent re-derive it at full price; `EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual call an echo\n(0.02 s vs 5.21 s, byte-identical). Removes 94 calls × 1.61 msgs.\n\n**Expected +4.3% to +6.0%** (counterfactual on all 49 pairs; CI spans zero at n=49).\n\n### 5.4 Do NOT build the post-edit hook without a decision\n\nIt is the only mechanism reaching the 97.7%, but it requires `CC_NO_SAFE_MODE=1` and a change to\npatch collection (`.claude/settings.json` would land in the graded patch). It also carries the\n§3 regression risk directly. Decide fairness and patch-collection acceptability first.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gates — mechanism counts, winners protected\n\nMDE is ~25–30 pts at n≈30 against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor. **No token claim below\nn≈50, in either direction.**\n\n| gate | n | criterion |\n|---|---|---|\n| **V0** offline, $0 | 0 | probe returns a runnable command on cargo/pytest/phpunit/gotest/mvn repos; VERIFY coverage ≥ 80% of payloads (from 8/33); zero regressions on existing verbs |\n| **V1** replay, $0 | 49 | on recorded loser sessions, the probed command would have succeeded where the emitted one failed |\n| **V2** live | 12 | **harness ENV failures per session fall vs rep50**; throwaway scripts do not rise. Mechanism counts only |\n| **V3** live | 50 | first token claim, bootstrap CI, total **and** median |\n\n**Winner-protection tripwire, binding at every gate:** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,\n`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` are included in every sample from V2 on. If any shows a rise in\npost-edit harness runs or turns versus its rep50 record, the change is reverted regardless of the\nloser-group result. lombok alone is 29% of all lift — losing it costs more than repairing the\nfive worst losers gains.\n\n**Kill criteria.** V1 under 50% → the probe does not address the observed failures; stop.\nV2 without a fall in env-failures → mechanism absent; stop. Any winner regression >10pt → revert.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Verification\n\n- Tool: `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race tests + build;\n  CGO required for tree-sitter). Add unit tests for the probe beside `search_verify.go`.\n- Offline replay: recorded queries at `results/<tag>/eg/<instance>/gq_calls.log`, payloads at the\n  same path + `.payload`. Replay against the binary at zero model cost and assert both that the\n  probe changes the emitted command *and* that nothing else moved.\n- Harness deploys to VMs by temp path + atomic `mv` only, with a live-session guard — never\n  overwrite a script a session is reading.\n- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** Δturns **and** harness/env-failure counts.\n\n---\n\n## 8. What to tell stakeholders\n\nThe defensible claim is **not** a token saving. On Opus the tool is centrally neutral\n(+1.35%, t=−0.17; −0.26% winsorised). What it demonstrably does at n=49 is suppress whole-file\nreads — 119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B, >8 KB tail 39 → 25 — and that is measurable now\nwithout another cell. Report that, plus the interval on tokens, and stop quoting a percentage the\ndata does not support.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4461,"cache_read_input_tokens":694536,"output_tokens":6184,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4461,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6184,"cache_read_input_tokens":694536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4461,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4461},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqgjwL6BZcPWdherQZ3o","type":"assistant","uuid":"b69ef432-aa28-450d-aef4-1970dede59b3","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:37:35.295Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"b69ef432-aa28-450d-aef4-1970dede59b3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b0f46be0-2c71-4d1c-96bc-346a5d0deab4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YGALLyquwQKS8NjmWXPxzt","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"e0114b7f-fe4b-403e-a79d-42bb25230bce","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:37:35.348Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","content":"# entire-graph on Opus — what the data says, and the only plan that survives it\n\n## Context\n\nThe goal set for this work is **35% token savings on rep50, fairly measured, on Opus**. This plan\nexists because that target is now refuted by the data, and continuing to aim at it would mean\neither fabricating it or measuring something else and calling it that. What follows is the\nevidence, the loser/winner analysis requested, and the plan that is actually supported.\n\nAll numbers: rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs, SWE-bench Multilingual.\nSign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Where Opus actually stands\n\n| | value |\n|---|---|\n| headline | **+1.35%** |\n| t-statistic | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n| median | −4.2% |\n| wins | 24 / 49 |\n| paired sd (log-ratio) | 0.494 |\n| n to *demonstrate* +1.35% | **12,900 pairs ≈ $78,491** |\n| n to demonstrate +6% | 499 pairs ≈ $3,972 |\n| n to demonstrate 35% | **11 pairs ≈ $88** |\n\n**35% would have been the cheapest result in the project to prove.** It is not provable because\nit is not there. Every robust estimator drives the headline to zero or below — winsorised 20/80\n**−0.26%**, dropping the 3 most extreme pairs **−6.19%** — so the positive sign is tail-carried.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Loser analysis (requested)\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts across 25 instances; top five carry −11.42 (57%).**\n\nGroup sums, eg minus baseline:\n\n| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n|---|---|---|\n| turns | **+296** | −258 |\n| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n| post-edit exploration | **+159** | −81 |\n| post-edit harness | **+50** | −88 |\n| edits | +42 | −25 |\n| graph calls | 44 (43 pre) | 50 (48 pre) |\n\n**The single most important line is pre-edit exploration: the graph works in BOTH groups\n(−46 / −58).** Localization is not what separates them. The entire divergence is post-edit, where\n**91 of 94 graph calls never happen** — 42/49 sessions make no graph call after their first edit.\n\nWorst five, with the pattern visible per-instance:\n\n| instance | pts | tok | eg/base turns | eg/base expl | eg/base harness |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `bat-1892` | −2.81 | −79.8% | 100/65 | 44/18 | 23/14 |\n| `valkey-790` | −2.72 | −127.4% | 93/54 | 57/34 | 20/11 |\n| `ansible-395e` | −2.58 | −68.1% | 116/91 | 48/38 | 9/5 |\n| `prometheus-9248` | −1.68 | −74.6% | 110/68 | 68/38 | 9/8 |\n| `tokio-4867` | −1.63 | −114.4% | 69/38 | 26/10 | 25/17 |\n\n**Correlates with token saving, ranked:**\n\n| | r |\n|---|---|\n| Δ harness runs | **−0.612** |\n| Δ exploration eliminated | +0.485 |\n| Δ repeat edits to same file | −0.457 |\n| Δ edit calls | −0.449 |\n| **Δ harness ENV failures** | **−0.442** |\n| Δ throwaway scripts run | −0.350 |\n| Δ first-edit turn | −0.342 |\n\n**Mechanism:** losers run verification that fails on the *environment* rather than the patch\n(eg 102 vs base 80 in the loser group), then improvise throwaway harnesses (+16) and re-explore\nto repair them (+159 post-edit exploration). Winners show the exact mirror: **−45 env failures,\n−48 throwaway scripts, −88 harness runs**. This is the ledger's §1.3 lever, independently\nreproduced here.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Winner analysis — what must not regress\n\n**Lift +21.21 pts across 24 instances. `lombok-3674` alone is +6.09 pts = 29% of ALL lift.**\n\n| instance | pts | eg/base turns | eg/base harness |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `lombok-3674` | **+6.09** | 67/122 | **23/70** |\n| `fmt-2457` | +2.18 | 38/67 | 12/13 |\n| `qutebrowser-c580` | +1.89 | 88/105 | 23/33 |\n| `vuejs-11739` | +1.35 | 70/80 | 24/19 |\n| `redis-11510` | +1.29 | 34/56 | 3/12 |\n\n**Winners win because the BASELINE flails and eg converges** — lombok's baseline ran `javac`\n**70 times** against eg's 23. eg is not doing something clever; it is failing to blow up.\n\n**Two consequences that constrain every proposal below:**\n\n1. **A symmetric frugality clamp is net-negative.** Suppressing over-verification helps the\n   baseline more than eg in exactly the instances eg currently wins. Already modelled; do not\n   ship one.\n2. **Any intervention that adds post-edit content risks converting a winner into a loser**, since\n   winners win by *doing less* after the first edit. Winner protection is therefore not a\n   formality — it is the main risk.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What is already closed (do not rebuild)\n\n| route | verdict |\n|---|---|\n| new verb in the affordance tail | **0/66 adoption** (`impact` 0/49, `changed` 0/5, `--path` 0/12) |\n| post-edit rider (G2) | **−12.19%**, fired 0/5 |\n| displacement via better verbs (G3) | ratio **0.76** vs 0.96 baseline — went backwards |\n| graph-backed grep | 38.9% interception ceiling; graph output (1,124 B median) is *larger* than a median grep (732 B) |\n| next-query coverage | only 40.4% of missed identifiers are graph symbols; of those 89% stay missing at 4× payload budget |\n| payload quality | 12 metrics dead, incl. complete-symbol density (r = **−0.170**) |\n| retrieval/ranking | anti-correlated — gold-at-rank-1 sessions lost more often |\n| tail-risk endpoint | arms blow up at identical rates (22.4% vs 20.4%); n=6,338 to resolve |\n\n---\n\n## 5. The plan\n\n### 5.1 Accept the honest target\n\n**Stop targeting 35% on Opus.** Target **loser repair**, whose exact ceiling is the lift pool:\n**+21.21%** if every losing instance were made precisely neutral. That is arithmetic, not\nprojection. Reaching it requires eliminating the drag pool entirely; a realistic fraction is\nworth +5–10%.\n\n### 5.2 Build: VERIFY runnability probe *(primary — targets the measured mechanism)*\n\n**Files:** `internal/sem/search_verify.go` (derivation + probe), `internal/cli/search.go`\n(VERIFY block emission).\n\nToday the only check is `exec.LookPath` on the runner (`search_verify.go:1526`) — it confirms\n`pytest` exists, never that the derived command *runs*. Add a **collect-only probe** before\nemitting: `pytest --collect-only -q`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`, `cargo test --no-run`,\n`mvn -q -DskipTests compile`. On failure, drop to the next rung rather than emitting a command\nthat will fail on the environment.\n\nAlso raise VERIFY coverage — it appears in only **8 of 33** payloads, so 76% of sessions get no\nverification command at all and improvise one.\n\n**Fair:** the derived command is tool output computed from the repo, same class as a ranked hit.\nShips no instruction; the baseline is untouched.\n\n**Expected: +0.5% to +1.5%.** Stated honestly — 22 avoided env-failures × ~39.5K tok ≈ 0.6% of\nthe pool. This is a real mechanism with a small effect, not a headline.\n\n### 5.3 Ship: R-A zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, deployed)*\n\nAlready committed (`b669a57b`) and deployed. `EG_PREFETCH=1` injected the payload into turn 0 and\nstill let the agent re-derive it at full price; `EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual call an echo\n(0.02 s vs 5.21 s, byte-identical). Removes 94 calls × 1.61 msgs.\n\n**Expected +4.3% to +6.0%** (counterfactual on all 49 pairs; CI spans zero at n=49).\n\n### 5.4 Do NOT build the post-edit hook without a decision\n\nIt is the only mechanism reaching the 97.7%, but it requires `CC_NO_SAFE_MODE=1` and a change to\npatch collection (`.claude/settings.json` would land in the graded patch). It also carries the\n§3 regression risk directly. Decide fairness and patch-collection acceptability first.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gates — mechanism counts, winners protected\n\nMDE is ~25–30 pts at n≈30 against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor. **No token claim below\nn≈50, in either direction.**\n\n| gate | n | criterion |\n|---|---|---|\n| **V0** offline, $0 | 0 | probe returns a runnable command on cargo/pytest/phpunit/gotest/mvn repos; VERIFY coverage ≥ 80% of payloads (from 8/33); zero regressions on existing verbs |\n| **V1** replay, $0 | 49 | on recorded loser sessions, the probed command would have succeeded where the emitted one failed |\n| **V2** live | 12 | **harness ENV failures per session fall vs rep50**; throwaway scripts do not rise. Mechanism counts only |\n| **V3** live | 50 | first token claim, bootstrap CI, total **and** median |\n\n**Winner-protection tripwire, binding at every gate:** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,\n`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` are included in every sample from V2 on. If any shows a rise in\npost-edit harness runs or turns versus its rep50 record, the change is reverted regardless of the\nloser-group result. lombok alone is 29% of all lift — losing it costs more than repairing the\nfive worst losers gains.\n\n**Kill criteria.** V1 under 50% → the probe does not address the observed failures; stop.\nV2 without a fall in env-failures → mechanism absent; stop. Any winner regression >10pt → revert.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Verification\n\n- Tool: `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race tests + build;\n  CGO required for tree-sitter). Add unit tests for the probe beside `search_verify.go`.\n- Offline replay: recorded queries at `results/<tag>/eg/<instance>/gq_calls.log`, payloads at the\n  same path + `.payload`. Replay against the binary at zero model cost and assert both that the\n  probe changes the emitted command *and* that nothing else moved.\n- Harness deploys to VMs by temp path + atomic `mv` only, with a live-session guard — never\n  overwrite a script a session is reading.\n- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** Δturns **and** harness/env-failure counts.\n\n---\n\n## 8. What to tell stakeholders\n\nThe defensible claim is **not** a token saving. On Opus the tool is centrally neutral\n(+1.35%, t=−0.17; −0.26% winsorised). What it demonstrably does at n=49 is suppress whole-file\nreads — 119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B, >8 KB tail 39 → 25 — and that is measurable now\nwithout another cell. Report that, plus the interval on tokens, and stop quoting a percentage the\ndata does not support.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":514,"newStart":1,"newLines":211,"lines":["-# entire-graph: the honest ceiling is ~+17%, and what to build to reach it","+# entire-graph on Opus — what the data says, and the only plan that survives it"," ","-## ⛔ FINAL MECHANISM (measured 2026-08-08) — why the ceiling is structural","+## Context"," ","-Across all 49 rep50 eg sessions, keyed off transcripts:","+The goal set for this work is **35% token savings on rep50, fairly measured, on Opus**. This plan","+exists because that target is now refuted by the data, and continuing to aim at it would mean","+either fabricating it or measuring something else and calling it that. What follows is the","+evidence, the loser/winner analysis requested, and the plan that is actually supported."," ","-| | sessions |","-|---|---|","-| never called the graph | 0 |","-| **called it ONLY before the first edit** | **42** |","-| called it after an edit | **7** (8 calls total) |","+All numbers: rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs, SWE-bench Multilingual.","+Sign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**"," ","-**86% of sessions stop using the graph the moment they start editing**, while **97.7% of the","-token loss is post-edit** (ΔPre +0.40M vs ΔPost +17.31M).","+---"," ","-**The tool is absent from where the cost is.** Its addressable surface is the pre-edit phase =","-**2.3% of the delta**. Every lever ever quantified — ranking 0.0, routing 0.0, harness","-suppression 0.0, payload +3.0, empty-payload +1.5–3.2 — is a lever on that 2.3%. That is the","-ceiling, and no amount of payload or ranking work moves it.","+## 1. Where Opus actually stands"," ","-It also explains the corpus's strangest result: gold-at-rank-1 sessions LOST more often","-(losers 6/8, winners 2/5). Retrieval governs the 2.3%; it has no purchase on the 97.7%.","+| | value |","+|---|---|","+| headline | **+1.35%** |","+| t-statistic | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |","+| median | −4.2% |","+| wins | 24 / 49 |","+| paired sd (log-ratio) | 0.494 |","+| n to *demonstrate* +1.35% | **12,900 pairs ≈ $78,491** |","+| n to demonstrate +6% | 499 pairs ≈ $3,972 |","+| n to demonstrate 35% | **11 pairs ≈ $88** |"," ","-**Two gates failed for this reason, not for adoption:** G1 (`changed` verb, 0/5 despite being","-advertised at prompt line 48) and G2 (post-edit rider, 0/3). Both ride on an agent-initiated","-graph call. With 42/49 sessions making none post-edit, max reach is 14%. **Unreachable by","-construction.** I built both before measuring whether the moment exists — one offline query","-over existing data would have prevented both.","+**35% would have been the cheapest result in the project to prove.** It is not provable because","+it is not there. Every robust estimator drives the headline to zero or below — winsorised 20/80","+**−0.26%**, dropping the 3 most extreme pairs **−6.19%** — so the positive sign is tail-carried."," ","-### The only remaining route, and why it is blocked","+---"," ","-Post-edit help must not depend on the agent choosing to call the tool → a plugin hook firing","-after Edit/Write. Feasibility, checked:","+## 2. Loser analysis (requested)"," ","-- `--safe-mode` disables ALL customizations **including hooks** (`run_3arm.sh:2364`), applied to","-  every arm via `ISO_ARGS`. It exists because the operator's config leaked 9.4KB of skill +","-  3.1KB subagent + 0.7KB deferred-tool listings into turn-0.","-- There IS precedent for dropping it: `CC_NO_SAFE_MODE=1` (`:2391`) drops it **symmetrically**","-  from every arm, and `EG_MCP=1` already uses this to give the tool arm an MCP server the","-  baseline lacks — audited as \"tool availability only, no instruction\".","-- **BLOCKER:** Claude Code reads hooks from a project-local `.claude/settings.json`. Writing","-  that into the checkout puts an untracked file in the tree that `collect_patch.sh` scores via","-  `git add -N && git diff` — **the hook config would land in the graded patch.** Fixable with","-  `.git/info/exclude`, but that modifies the scoring path.","+**Drag −19.86 pts across 25 instances; top five carry −11.42 (57%).**"," ","-**Verdict:** the route is real but requires changing how patches are collected. Do not attempt","-it without deciding (a) whether unsolicited post-edit injection is fair — it is graph output","-about the agent's own edit, unlike a test runner, but the baseline has no analogue — and (b)","-whether the patch-collection change is acceptable.","+Group sums, eg minus baseline:"," ","-> **VERDICT: 35% is not reachable on a fair measurement.** Six independent estimates converge on","-> **+15–21%**, the directly addressable waste is **+2.67–4.57%**, and the best fair cell ever","-> measured is **+17.21%** (opus xhigh, n=26). The original +35.06% target was an arithmetic","-> artifact and is retracted below. This plan targets **+17–21%** and says plainly what it cannot do.","+| | losers (25) | winners (24) |","+|---|---|---|","+| turns | **+296** | −258 |","+| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |","+| post-edit exploration | **+159** | −81 |","+| post-edit harness | **+50** | −88 |","+| edits | +42 | −25 |","+| graph calls | 44 (43 pre) | 50 (48 pre) |"," ","-| route | ceiling |","-|---|---|","-| directly addressable post-edit waste | **+2.67% to +4.57%** |","-| expensive-baseline tercile (78% of mass) | +8.07% |","-| fair symmetric ceiling (all post-edit pools) | +14.99% |","-| perfect post-edit behaviour | +15.4% |","-| **best fair cell measured** | **+17.21%** (n=26) |","-| mechanism model, N≈6–8 calls removed | +18–21% |","+**The single most important line is pre-edit exploration: the graph works in BOTH groups","+(−46 / −58).** Localization is not what separates them. The entire divergence is post-edit, where","+**91 of 94 graph calls never happen** — 42/49 sessions make no graph call after their first edit."," ","-**Why not 35%:** 97.7% of the loss is post-edit work the graph does not touch; eg's saving is","-bounded by *baseline waste* (`corr(baseline tokens, eg delta) = +0.305`; cheap baselines","-−27.76%), which the graph does not control.","+Worst five, with the pattern visible per-instance:"," ","-## Context","+| instance | pts | tok | eg/base turns | eg/base expl | eg/base harness |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| `bat-1892` | −2.81 | −79.8% | 100/65 | 44/18 | 23/14 |","+| `valkey-790` | −2.72 | −127.4% | 93/54 | 57/34 | 20/11 |","+| `ansible-395e` | −2.58 | −68.1% | 116/91 | 48/38 | 9/5 |","+| `prometheus-9248` | −1.68 | −74.6% | 110/68 | 68/38 | 9/8 |","+| `tokio-4867` | −1.63 | −114.4% | 69/38 | 26/10 | 25/17 |"," ","-rep50 finished at **eg +1.35%** (n=49, Opus max, median −4.16%, 24/49 wins). Goal: **35% token","-savings** vs a no-tool baseline, fairly measured.","+**Correlates with token saving, ranked:**"," ","-The loser-repair framing is the only one whose arithmetic reaches the target, and it is","-**measured, not extrapolated**:","-","-| scenario | suite |","+| | r |"," |---|---|","-| today | **+1.35%** |","-| all 22 losers merely neutral (eg = base) | **+20.99%** |","-| all 22 losers behaving like the winner group | **+35.06%** ← target |","+| Δ harness runs | **−0.612** |","+| Δ exploration eliminated | +0.485 |","+| Δ repeat edits to same file | −0.457 |","+| Δ edit calls | −0.449 |","+| **Δ harness ENV failures** | **−0.442** |","+| Δ throwaway scripts run | −0.350 |","+| Δ first-edit turn | −0.342 |"," ","-**Neutralising is not enough.** 35% requires the losers to *win*, not merely stop losing.","+**Mechanism:** losers run verification that fails on the *environment* rather than the patch","+(eg 102 vs base 80 in the loser group), then improvise throwaway harnesses (+16) and re-explore","+to repair them (+159 post-edit exploration). Winners show the exact mirror: **−45 env failures,","+−48 throwaway scripts, −88 harness runs**. This is the ledger's §1.3 lever, independently","+reproduced here."," ","-## What the losses actually are (transcript decomposition, n=8 worst)","+---"," ","-**97.7% of the loss is POST-EDIT.** ΔPre = +0.40M (2.3%); ΔPost = **+17.31M**.","-Pre-edit calls 147 vs 134 (+10%); post-edit **370 vs 248 (+49%)**.","-Split of the +17.71M: turn-count **10.95M (62%)**, context-density **6.79M (38%)**.","+## 3. Winner analysis — what must not regress"," ","-**The graph already does its job.** Localization was net-free, and *cheaper* in 3 of 8.","+**Lift +21.21 pts across 24 instances. `lombok-3674` alone is +6.09 pts = 29% of ALL lift.**"," ","-**Retrieval quality is ANTI-correlated with winning** — gold at rank 1: losers **6/8 (75%)**,","-winners **2/5 (40%)**. `lombok-3674` (**+71.0%**) had a **0-byte payload**; `redis-11510`","-(**+68.4%**) missed gold entirely. **Do not spend effort on ranking.**","-","-**Mechanism: the agent gets the repo's native harness working and cannot stop.**","-","-| instance | eg harness runs | base | Δ |","+| instance | pts | eg/base turns | eg/base harness |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| valkey-790 | `./runtest`×11, `make`×6 | 7 / 2 | −127.4% |","-| javaparser-4538 | `javac`×19 | 8 | −142.3% |","-| bat-1892 | `cargo test`×7, `build`×6 | 1 | −79.8% |","-| **redis-11510** | `./runtest`×**1**, stop | 10 | **+68.4%** |","-| **laravel-48636** | `phpunit`×**1** | 15 | **+50.7%** |","+| `lombok-3674` | **+6.09** | 67/122 | **23/70** |","+| `fmt-2457` | +2.18 | 38/67 | 12/13 |","+| `qutebrowser-c580` | +1.89 | 88/105 | 23/33 |","+| `vuejs-11739` | +1.35 | 70/80 | 24/19 |","+| `redis-11510` | +1.29 | 34/56 | 3/12 |"," ","-`redis-11510` is the clean control: same repo, same tcl harness, opposite outcome. Each retry","-drags in `sleep 120`, `pkill`, port juggling, and **tailing its own transcript** to recover","-truncated Bash output. Winners' post-edit calls: 93 vs 196 (**−53%**).","+**Winners win because the BASELINE flails and eg converges** — lombok's baseline ran `javac`","+**70 times** against eg's 23. eg is not doing something clever; it is failing to blow up."," ","-Sub-split: **B1 \"couldn't stop\" 6/8 ≈ 15.9M**; **B2 \"context density\" 2/8 ≈ 2.2M**","-(javaparser-4538 is the sole pre-edit-dominant case and is expected NOT to convert).","+**Two consequences that constrain every proposal below:**"," ","-## Why conversion is possible (confounds checked, all pass)","+1. **A symmetric frugality clamp is net-negative.** Suppressing over-verification helps the","+   baseline more than eg in exactly the instances eg currently wins. Already modelled; do not","+   ship one.","+2. **Any intervention that adds post-edit content risks converting a winner into a loser**, since","+   winners win by *doing less* after the first edit. Winner protection is therefore not a","+   formality — it is the main risk."," ","-**Same repo, opposite outcome — 7 repos on BOTH sides:** laravel (−59.4/−124.1 vs +50.7/+38.8),","-lombok (−19.4 vs **+71.0**), tokio (−114.4 vs +32.5), fmt (−23.2 vs +62.1), prometheus,","-qutebrowser, ansible. **8 of 10 languages appear on both sides** — not an ecosystem effect.","-**Winners had HARDER baselines** (median 2.64M tok / 56 turns vs losers 2.01M / 42) — the","-winner profile is not \"easy instances\".","+---"," ","-The difference is behavioural, not intrinsic. That is what makes it fixable.","+## 4. What is already closed (do not rebuild)"," ","-## FAIRNESS REVIEW — ashtom's objection, and why it lands","+| route | verdict |","+|---|---|","+| new verb in the affordance tail | **0/66 adoption** (`impact` 0/49, `changed` 0/5, `--path` 0/12) |","+| post-edit rider (G2) | **−12.19%**, fired 0/5 |","+| displacement via better verbs (G3) | ratio **0.76** vs 0.96 baseline — went backwards |","+| graph-backed grep | 38.9% interception ceiling; graph output (1,124 B median) is *larger* than a median grep (732 B) |","+| next-query coverage | only 40.4% of missed identifiers are graph symbols; of those 89% stay missing at 4× payload budget |","+| payload quality | 12 metrics dead, incl. complete-symbol density (r = **−0.170**) |","+| retrieval/ranking | anti-correlated — gold-at-rank-1 sessions lost more often |","+| tail-risk endpoint | arms blow up at identical rates (22.4% vs 20.4%); n=6,338 to resolve |"," ","-> *\"That seems like cheating then? Why is baseline able to run the tests cheaper than eg is?\"*","+---"," ","-**Answer to the second question: it isn't.** Both arms run tests through the same Bash tool in","-the same checkout with identical access (verified: only the eg `entire` shim differs on PATH).","-The baseline is not cheaper per run — **eg simply runs the harness more often** (losers: eg","-9–19× vs baseline 4–10×). That is an eg behavioural regression, not a baseline advantage.","+## 5. The plan"," ","-**Answer to the first: partly yes, on scope.** `verify` is cheap because of an *output","-contract*, not privileged access — `cli/verify.go:31` returns an **adjudicated verdict, never","-raw output**, capped at **2,048 B** (`:41`). The baseline could pipe `pytest` through `head`;","-it doesn't. That is a genuine tool capability. **But** shipping it means we stop measuring","-\"does the code graph save tokens\" and start measuring \"does a bundle of dev tools save tokens\".","+### 5.1 Accept the honest target"," ","-**Consequence for this plan: L1 is demoted from PRIMARY to optional, and must be labelled.**","-If run, report it as *graph + verify* against *no tools*, and report the graph-only number","-beside it. Do not let it become the headline for entire-graph.","+**Stop targeting 35% on Opus.** Target **loser repair**, whose exact ceiling is the lift pool:","+**+21.21%** if every losing instance were made precisely neutral. That is arithmetic, not","+projection. Reaching it requires eliminating the drag pool entirely; a realistic fraction is","+worth +5–10%."," ","-## ⛔ THE +35.06% NUMBER IS AN ARTIFACT — retracted","+### 5.2 Build: VERIFY runnability probe *(primary — targets the measured mechanism)*"," ","-**eg's saving is a function of BASELINE WASTE, not of graph quality.**","+**Files:** `internal/sem/search_verify.go` (derivation + probe), `internal/cli/search.go`","+(VERIFY block emission)."," ","-| baseline cost tercile | median baseline | eg TOKEN | eg median |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| cheap | 0.99M | **−27.76%** | −28.0% |","-| mid | 2.48M | −2.99% | +6.2% |","-| expensive | 5.13M | **+8.07%** | +8.9% |","+Today the only check is `exec.LookPath` on the runner (`search_verify.go:1526`) — it confirms","+`pytest` exists, never that the derived command *runs*. Add a **collect-only probe** before","+emitting: `pytest --collect-only -q`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`, `cargo test --no-run`,","+`mvn -q -DskipTests compile`. On failure, drop to the next rung rather than emitting a command","+that will fail on the environment."," ","-`corr(baseline tokens, eg delta) = +0.305`; `corr(baseline turns, eg delta) = +0.284`.","-Below-median baselines: **−14.64%**. Above-median (78% of token mass): **+5.87%**.","+Also raise VERIFY coverage — it appears in only **8 of 33** payloads, so 76% of sessions get no","+verification command at all and improvise one."," ","-**Why this kills the arithmetic:** the winner group's eg/base ratio of 0.604 was achieved on","-instances whose baselines spent **2.64M median / 56 turns**. Applying that ratio to a 0.99M","-baseline is impossible — there is no waste there to capture. \"Convert every loser to","-winner-quality\" is not merely hard, it is **arithmetically unavailable** for the ~half of","-losers whose baselines are already efficient.","+**Fair:** the derived command is tool output computed from the repo, same class as a ranked hit.","+Ships no instruction; the baseline is untouched."," ","-The ceiling is therefore set by *how much the no-tool baseline wastes*, which the graph does","-not control. On the 78% of token mass where waste is greatest, eg captures **+5.87%**.","+**Expected: +0.5% to +1.5%.** Stated honestly — 22 avoided env-failures × ~39.5K tok ≈ 0.6% of","+the pool. This is a real mechanism with a small effect, not a headline."," ","-**Empirical ceiling, all fair cells at n≥25: `opus xhigh` +17.21% (n=26).** That is the largest","-honest number this project has produced.","+### 5.3 Ship: R-A zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, deployed)*"," ","-## HONEST CEILING — the two estimates disagree, and the lower one is better founded","+Already committed (`b669a57b`) and deployed. `EG_PREFETCH=1` injected the payload into turn 0 and","+still let the agent re-derive it at full price; `EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual call an echo","+(0.02 s vs 5.21 s, byte-identical). Removes 94 calls × 1.61 msgs."," ","-- **Winner-ratio model (mine):** convert all 22 losers to the winner eg/base ratio → **+35.06%**.","-  This is an *upper bound*: it assumes total conversion of every loser.","-- **Mechanism model (architecture review):** removing N post-edit calls yields +2.8% at N=0,","-  **+17.3% at N=8**, **+24.3% at N=12**. R2+R3+R4 together plausibly reach N≈6–8 → **+18–21%**.","+**Expected +4.3% to +6.0%** (counterfactual on all 49 pairs; CI spans zero at n=49)."," ","-The mechanism model is grounded in measured elasticity; mine assumes an outcome. **The honest","-expected range is +18% to +25%, and 35% is the ceiling only under total conversion.** Say this","-plainly rather than quoting +35.06%.","+### 5.4 Do NOT build the post-edit hook without a decision"," ","-## The fix","+It is the only mechanism reaching the 97.7%, but it requires `CC_NO_SAFE_MODE=1` and a change to","+patch collection (`.claude/settings.json` would land in the graded patch). It also carries the","+§3 regression risk directly. Decide fairness and patch-collection acceptability first."," ","-### L1 — ~~expose the executing `verify` verb~~ **REMOVED** (ashtom's objection accepted)","+---"," ","-Running the tests for the agent makes eg cheaper at work **both arms do identically** — the","-baseline is not cheaper per run, eg simply runs the harness 9–19× vs 4–10×. It would book a","-subsidy for an eg regression as a graph win, and it changes the claim from \"the code graph","-saves tokens\" to \"our bundle does dev work cheaply\". **Dropped. Do not run it.**","+## 6. Gates — mechanism counts, winners protected"," ","-### L1′ — fix the VERIFY *derivation* so the first invocation works (REPLACEMENT)","+MDE is ~25–30 pts at n≈30 against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor. **No token claim below","+n≈50, in either direction.**"," ","-Same target (post-edit waste), fair by construction: deriving the correct test command from","-build files **plus the graph** is code intelligence. It makes the graph's answer better rather","-than making eg cheaper at shared work.","-","-The waste is not legitimate re-testing. From the transcripts it is failing to get the harness","-running: `sleep 90/120/150` polling, `pkill` ×4, `--baseport` juggling, tailing its own","-transcript to recover truncated Bash output, hand-built `/tmp` rigs.","-","-Three concrete defects:","-1. **Wrong scope.** nushell (−141.2%): the manifest walk emitted `cargo test -p nu-cli` when the","-   fix was in `nu-command`. **The graph knows which crate/package/module owns the symbol; the","-   manifest walk cannot.** Use symbol→file→package to scope the command.","-2. **No runnability check.** The only probe is `exec.LookPath` on the runner","-   (`search_verify.go:1526`) — it confirms `pytest` is installed, never that the command runs.","-   Add a collect-only probe (`pytest --collect-only`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`,","-   `cargo test --no-run`) and drop to the next rung on failure.","-3. **Coverage 8/33.** Most payloads carry no VERIFY line at all. Raise toward ~100% or this","-   reaches only a quarter of Class B.","-","-Fairness: the derived command is tool output computed from the repo, the same class as the","-ranked hits. It ships no instruction and the baseline arm is untouched.","-","-### L1-OLD — expose the executing `verify` verb (REMOVED — kept for the record)","-","-**The capability already exists and was never wired up.** `internal/cli/verify.go:193` runs","-`exec.CommandContext(ctx,\"sh\",\"-c\",cmd)` + `CombinedOutput()` via `runVerifyCommands` (:158).","-It has ecosystem-aware timeouts (`verifyCompiledCommand` :178 — cargo/go test/mvn/gradle/cmake/","-ctest/make/bazel/dotnet/swift), **discards setup output** so install logs don't pollute test","-parsing, returns exit code **separately** from error (a failing suite is normal), caps output via","-`maxBytes`, and never mutates the tree.","-","-But `tools/eg-q` exposes only `search|def|callers|impact|grep`. **No rep50 session could reach","-it**, so every agent ran the harness by hand through Bash.","-","-**VERIFIED (read-only, this session):**","-- Reachable: `internal/cli/root.go:80  case \"verify\":`; tests drive it as","-  `verify --repo R --test \"sh run.sh\"` (`verify_test.go:259`).","-- **6 ecosystem parsers ship**: `cargo, ctest, gotest, jest, phpunit, pytest` + `unknown`","-  fallback (`internal/cli/testdata/verify/`).","-- Two-phase baseline is real: `--record-baseline` pre-edit, `--pre-edit-baseline` post-edit →","-  reports only what *this* edit broke or fixed. That directly kills the \"is this failure mine","-  or pre-existing?\" loop driving the retries.","-","-**RISK — two hard preconditions (`verify.go:113-119`):**","-```","-verify requires --test <command>","-verify requires --pre-edit-baseline <path> (or --record-baseline <path> to create one)","-```","-The agent must supply the command AND have called verify *before* editing. The VERIFY block","-that derives a command appeared in only **8 of 33** payloads. **Shipped as-is, L1 fails for","-most sessions.**","-","-**Mitigation — put the protocol in the wrapper, not the agent.** `eg-q verify [cmd]` should:","-1. derive the test command when not supplied (reuse `internal/sem/search_verify.go`),","-2. manage the baseline file itself — `--record-baseline /tmp/egq-vb-$IID.json` on first call,","-   `--pre-edit-baseline` thereafter,","-3. return the parsed delta.","-The agent then just calls `eg-q verify`. This is tool engineering, not instruction.","-","-**Parser coverage vs our actual losers:** bat→`cargo` ✓, ansible/openlibrary→`pytest` ✓,","-laravel/carbon→`phpunit` ✓ (**5/8**). valkey (tcl `./runtest`), javaparser (`mvn`), lombok","-(`javac`/`ant`) fall to `unknown` — still capped + exit-coded, but no parsed diff. Expect","-weaker gains on those three; two of them are also in the non-converting set.","-","-**RISK 2 — ADOPTION. This is the one that sinks the plan if ignored.**","-Measured verb uptake across all 49 eg sessions:","-","-| verb | calls | sessions |","+| gate | n | criterion |"," |---|---|---|","-| grep | 44 | 34/49 |","-| search | 34 | 33/49 |","-| def | 24 | 19/49 |","-| callers | 3 | 3/49 |","-| **impact** | **0** | **0/49** |","+| **V0** offline, $0 | 0 | probe returns a runnable command on cargo/pytest/phpunit/gotest/mvn repos; VERIFY coverage ≥ 80% of payloads (from 8/33); zero regressions on existing verbs |","+| **V1** replay, $0 | 49 | on recorded loser sessions, the probed command would have succeeded where the emitted one failed |","+| **V2** live | 12 | **harness ENV failures per session fall vs rep50**; throwaway scripts do not rise. Mechanism counts only |","+| **V3** live | 50 | first token claim, bootstrap CI, total **and** median |"," ","-**`impact` is named in all 49 prompts and was used zero times.** A capability line in the","-affordance tail therefore has a documented **0% adoption precedent**. Shipping `verify` that way","-would very likely produce no behaviour change at all.","+**Winner-protection tripwire, binding at every gate:** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,","+`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` are included in every sample from V2 on. If any shows a rise in","+post-edit harness runs or turns versus its rep50 record, the change is reverted regardless of the","+loser-group result. lombok alone is 29% of all lift — losing it costs more than repairing the","+five worst losers gains."," ","-**Mitigation — surface it where the agent is already looking, at the moment of need.** The","-`VERIFY:` block already appears *inside search output*. Change it from a passive string the","-agent must re-type into Bash:","-```","-VERIFY: vendor/bin/phpunit tests/CarbonInterval/TotalTest.php","-```","-into an executable affordance offered right after localization, e.g. a line stating that","-`eg-q verify` runs exactly this and reports only the tests **this** edit changed. Tool output,","-delivered at the point of relevance — strictly stronger than a prompt line.","+**Kill criteria.** V1 under 50% → the probe does not address the observed failures; stop.","+V2 without a fall in env-failures → mechanism absent; stop. Any winner regression >10pt → revert."," ","-**Sub-requirement:** VERIFY appeared in only **8 of 33** payloads. Coverage must rise toward","-~100% or L1 reaches only a quarter of Class B. Raising it is work in","-`internal/sem/search_verify.go`, and it is a hard prerequisite, not a nice-to-have.","+---"," ","-Change set for L1:","-1. `eg-q` gains a `verify` branch with auto-derived command + auto-managed baseline (kills RISK 1).","-2. Search's VERIFY block advertises the executable path (kills RISK 2).","-3. VERIFY derivation coverage raised from 8/33 (kills the coverage cap).","-4. One capability line in the affordance tail — necessary but, on the `impact` evidence,","-   nowhere near sufficient on its own.","+## 7. Verification"," ","-*Fairness:* a **verb** is not an instruction — the baseline cannot invoke it. This is the same","-class of difference as the search payload itself. The affordance line states capability only","-(the existing tail was audited clean, see below).","-*Scope honesty:* this measures \"the tool as shipped, including its verification affordance\",","-not \"the graph's marginal retrieval value\". **Say which, in any writeup.**","+- Tool: `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race tests + build;","+  CGO required for tree-sitter). Add unit tests for the probe beside `search_verify.go`.","+- Offline replay: recorded queries at `results/<tag>/eg/<instance>/gq_calls.log`, payloads at the","+  same path + `.payload`. Replay against the binary at zero model cost and assert both that the","+  probe changes the emitted command *and* that nothing else moved.","+- Harness deploys to VMs by temp path + atomic `mv` only, with a live-session guard — never","+  overwrite a script a session is reading.","+- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** Δturns **and** harness/env-failure counts."," ","-### L2 — symmetric harness clamp — **REJECTED, modelled net-negative**","+---"," ","-A clamp inside `published_exact_prompt()` (`run_3arm.sh:1227`, no arm argument → symmetric by","-construction) was the obvious fair way to cut retries. **Modelled against measured runner counts","-and per-call context, it makes the suite WORSE:**","+## 8. What to tell stakeholders"," ","-| clamp K | winner group | loser group | combined 13 |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| none | +55.6% | −57.1% | **−2.7%** |","-| 2 | +55.6% | −48.5% | **−9.7%** |","-| 3 | +55.2% | −48.4% | **−9.6%** |","-| 5 | +54.5% | −48.7% | **−9.7%** |","-","-Losers improve (bat −79.6→−50.1, javaparser −145.1→−89.1) but winners pay more than losers gain:","-`laravel-48636` **+50.6→+30.5**, `lombok-3674` **+71.0→+59.7**. In the winners it is the","-**baseline** that flails (lombok baseline `javac`×68 vs eg ×23), so a symmetric clamp hands the","-baseline the savings.","-","-**Do not ship a shared frugality clamp.** The asymmetry that makes eg win is precisely that the","-baseline over-runs the harness; suppressing that suppresses the win.","-","-### L1-BLOCKER — the shipped binary has no `verify`","-","-`./entire-graph verify` → **`unknown command`**. The checked-in binary (2026-08-04 21:41)","-predates source HEAD `ecaba15` (2026-08-05). rep50 therefore ran a binary in which `verify`","-does not exist at all, and `stats.verify_tier` is absent. **L1 requires a rebuild and a","-provenance check before anything else.**","-","-### L4 — the higher-value graph work the architecture review surfaced","-","-Ranked by (turn impact ÷ build cost), all data already in the graph:","-","-| # | change | data | turns | build |","-|---|---|---|---|---|","-| **R2** | a **working-tree `changed` verb** — \"what did I just edit, and what else needs it\" | yes | **3–5** | med |","-| R4 | probe the VERIFY command; wire `verify --from-search` | mostly | 1–3 | **low** |","-| R1 | warm the dirty-worktree index | yes | 0 direct, **unblocks R2–R4** | med |","-| R3 | covering-test verb keyed on the diff | machinery yes, **edges weak** | 2–4 | med |","-| R5 | co-change / CHANGE SET block | yes | 1–2 | low |","-","-**R2 is the strongest and is genuinely missing:** `diff --base HEAD --head HEAD` returns","-`{\"files\": null}` — **no verb can see an uncommitted edit.** Yet post-edit is where 97.7% of the","-loss lives. `gitutil.ChangedFiles` (`git.go:379`), `dependents.go` (repo-wide reference counts)","-and `search_related.go` (siblings/callers from an anchor) all exist; they just point at hit-1","-instead of at the diff hunks.","-","-**R1 is a hard prerequisite:** `worktreeSnapshotCacheable` (`search_cache.go:94`) returns false","-on *any* dirty tree, so **every post-edit search re-indexes from scratch** — measured 1782 ms","-vs 56 ms warm, and 8.9 s search / 22.4 s impact on real SWE-bench repos.","-","-### Structural findings worth acting on regardless","-","-- **`search` defaults to `--profile fast`**, which excludes `TESTS`, `SIMILAR_TO`, all type","-  relations, `DATA_FLOWS` and `FILE_CHANGES_WITH` (`provider.go:462`). At the default the","-  covering-test block, type card, signature types and half of RELATED SITES are *structurally","-  empty*. eg-q sets `full`, so rep50 was fine — but the shipped default is misleading.","-- **`TESTS` = 10 edges out of 36,114.** It is name-convention only (`provider.go:8875`) and is","-  the covering-test block's advertised \"strongest evidence\". Fix the edge source before","-  betting on R3.","-- **`searchTestIntentWords` foot-gun** (`search.go:4402`): any query containing \"test\"/\"spec\"","-  disables the −12 test demotion. Bug reports say \"test\" constantly; reproduced live returning","-  a `_test.go` file at rank 1.","-- **Signals computed but never used by search:** `DATA_FLOWS` (2,997), `FILE_CHANGES_WITH`","-  (387), `HANDLES_ROUTE` (48), relation `Evidence` (exact call-site lines), `Confidence` (used","-  only as a ≥0.7 gate, the value discarded), `dependents.go` counts, `SymbolRecord.Aliases`.","-","-### ⚠️ FAIRNESS LANDMINE — `.entire/graph-agent.md`","-","-It contains exactly the arm-asymmetric methodology the doctrine forbids: *\"ONE search, then","-act\"*, *\"Do NOT re-read what search already gave you\"*, *\"NEVER read a whole file\"*, *\"measured","-to cut session tokens roughly in half\"* — and it is `@`-included into `CLAUDE.md`.","-**It did NOT leak into rep50** (`--safe-mode` disables CLAUDE.md for both arms; 0 injected files","-verified in both checkouts). But any future cell run without `--safe-mode`, or on a machine","-where that file is present, is invalid on arrival. **Add an explicit preflight assertion.**","-","-### L3 — secondary fixes (cheap, independent)","-- Deploy `b5473b0b` never-refuse to the VMs — **built and offline-verified, not yet deployed**","-  (local eg-q `d1d115eb` vs VM `3878e23c`). Targets Class A, 9.12M burn.","-- Checkout-layout leak: 2 instances spent 13–15 calls mining an *adjacent instance's* tree.","-- Payload truncation at 4096/8192 B (10 of 33) — determine if the agent's stream truncated too.","-- `O35_STRIP_ADVICE` eats the LOW CONFIDENCE notice (`eg-q:160` greps `verify before editing`).","-- 6 flags inert (`EG_PREFETCH=0` kills all prefetch consumers; 0 `prefetch.payload` in 49","-  sessions) and 15 knobs are inheritance-only, incl. `EG_VERIFY_PROBE` — bake into `eg-q.run`.","-","-## ⛔ ADDRESSABLE-FRACTION AUDIT — the fix is worth +2.67%, not +24%","-","-All **763** post-edit tool calls hand-classified across the 8 worst losers (counts reproduce","-exactly: 442/321 tool calls, 370/248 API calls, +122).","-","-| bucket | excess | addressable |","-|---|---|---|","-| F code reading/editing | +31 (26%) | **0** |","-| A real test iteration | +30 (25%) | ~4 |","-| E scratch harnesses | +26 (21%) | 5 strict |","-| C output recovery | +18 (15%) | 7 |","-| B polling/timeout | +13 (11%) | 6 |","-| **D environment repair** | **+1** | — (eg 30 vs base 29: a **wash**) |","-","-| | calls | tokens | suite |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| conservative | 17/122 (14%) | 1.92M | **+2.67%** |","-| optimistic | 46/122 (38%) | 4.68M | **+4.57%** |","-","-**14 of the 17 conservative calls are one instance.** Drop `bat-1892` → **2.5% addressable**.","-In dollars it is ~$1.40 per 8 instances, because 97.8% of the removed tokens are cache reads.","-","-**Strongest counter-evidence, and it is decisive:** the baseline was *not verifying at all* on","-half these instances — baseline test-run counts: javaparser **0**, lombok **0**, bat-3108 2,","-openlibrary 3. Cause is environmental:","-```","-base bat-1892 [9]  cargo build → netjail: no real 'cargo' found on PATH behind the guard","-```","-The baseline gave up and hand-rolled `rustc /tmp/mock_check.rs`; the eg agent found","-`~/.cargo/bin/cargo` and ran the real suite. **Part of \"eg waste\" is eg doing verification the","-baseline skipped.** Any tool that makes testing easy raises the *baseline's* count too.","-","-Also: the agent re-ran commands whose output already fit (bat-3108 `cargo test --offline` ×3,","-943–2,231 B, never truncated). An output cap cannot prevent that.","-","-## MEASUREMENT-INTEGRITY DEFECTS (fix these regardless of any lever)","-","-1. **Rust toolchain not persisted to the session PATH.** The 2026-08-04 toolchain-PATH fix is","-   symmetric and covers ruby/node/python — **not cargo**. Both arms hunt for it; whether an arm","-   finds it decides whether it runs real tests or a stub. Huge variance, not bias.","-2. **Shipped binary predates source** — `./entire-graph verify` → `unknown command`;","-   `stats.verify_tier` absent though the harness reads it.","-3. **`.entire/graph-agent.md`** carries arm-asymmetric methodology (*\"ONE search, then act\"*,","-   *\"NEVER read a whole file\"*) and is `@`-included into `CLAUDE.md`. Did **not** leak into rep50","-   (`--safe-mode`, 0 injected files verified both arms) but voids any cell run without it.","-4. **`_tee` fix and never-refuse fix are committed locally but NOT deployed to the VMs.**","-","-## Arithmetic — each fix priced against the class it targets","-","-Winner-group ratio eg/base = **0.604**. Suite base pool 145.6M.","-","-| fix | targets | burn | → neutral | → winner-quality |","-|---|---|---|---|---|","-| never-refuse `b5473b0b` (**built, offline-verified**) | Class A, 8 inst | 9.12M | +7.62% | **+11.33%** |","-| `verify` verb (**exists, needs wiring**) | Class B, 13 inst | 18.96M | +14.37% | **+24.49%** |","-| **both** | 21 of 22 losers | 28.1M | +20.64% | **+34.46%** |","-| + last loser (Class C) | 22 | 28.6M | +20.99% | **+35.06%** |","-","-**Both fixes at winner quality = +34.46%; with the last loser, +35.06%.**","-If Class B converts but A only neutralises: **+30.75%**.","-","-Cross-check by a second route — driving post-edit call ratio to the winner's 0.474×: the 8","-worst go **−57.1% → +40.7%** (30.3M recovered), suite **+22.17%**, and **+27.41%** with 70% of","-the remaining burn. The two routes agree within a few points.","-","-**`javaparser-4538` does not convert** (−145% → −59%; pre-edit dominant). Budget 1–3","-non-converters — that is the difference between +31% and +35%, so **35% requires near-total","-conversion and has no margin.**","-","-## Gate ladder — escalate only on pass","-","-Every gate: both arms, fresh, same instances, reporting **total + median + Δturns + harness-run","-counts**.","-","-**MEASURED NOISE FLOOR — this dictates the gate design.** 28 instances have been run in ≥2","-independent cells. Same instance, same config:","-","-| instance | cells | range | swing |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| fluentd-4655 | 7 | −263.6% .. +30.7% | **294pt** |","-| ruff-15626 | 7 | −206.4% .. +47.3% | 254pt |","-| caddy-5995 | 7 | −172.1% .. +63.7% | 236pt |","-| hugo-12562 | 9 | −106.8% .. +62.4% | 169pt |","-","-**Median same-instance swing 99.9pt, mean 118pt, max 294pt.**","-","-Two consequences, both binding:","-1. **No per-instance token delta can ever be a gate criterion.** A 30pt improvement is invisible.","-2. **The identity of \"the 22 losers\" is itself unstable** — many would not be losers on a re-run.","-   The fix is still valid because it is a *tool change applied to every instance*, not per-instance","-   surgery. But do not treat the loser list as a fixed target set.","-","-**Gates therefore read MECHANISM COUNTS (low noise, directly observable), not tokens.**","-","-| gate | sample | n | pass criterion — mechanism, not tokens |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| **G0** | offline, no model, $0 | 0 | `eg-q verify` returns a parsed result on cargo/pytest/phpunit/gotest/unknown repos; auto-baseline works; 0 regressions on existing verbs |","-| **G1** | 4 losers + 2 winners | 6 | **`verify` is called in ≥4/6 sessions** (kills the `impact` 0/49 risk) and **raw harness invocations fall ≥50%** vs the rep50 run. **No token claim at this n.** |","-| **G2** | 8 losers + 4 winners | 12 | median post-edit call count ≤ baseline; VERIFY block present in ≥80% of payloads; winners' harness counts unchanged |","-| **G3** | all 22 losers + 10 winners | 32 | **first token claim**: loser group ≥ −5% and winner group ≥ +30%, both with bootstrap CI |","-| **G4** | full rep50, both arms | 49 | **≥35%** with bootstrap CI; report total, median, Δturns |","-","-G1 sample: losers `bat-1892`, `valkey-790`, `ansible-395e`, `prometheus-9248`; winners","-`lombok-3674` (+71.0, 8.87M) and `fmt-2457` (+62.1, 3.18M) as the regression tripwire —","-**lombok alone is worth more than the four losers gained.** Its role at G1/G2 is to confirm its","-harness behaviour is *unchanged*, not to measure its tokens.","-","-## Kill criteria","-","-1. If G1 cannot flip ≥3 of 4 worst losers, this does not reach 35% — report and stop.","-2. If any gate regresses a top winner >10pt, the fix is net-negative.","-3. If losers land near 0% rather than winner-quality, ceiling is +20.99% — **snapshot that","-   result** and continue only with a new mechanism, not a re-roll.","-4. **No arm-asymmetric instruction, ever**, even if it would hit the number.","-5. No claim from one cell: between-cell spread on identical config is ~20pt (opus max measured","-   +1.35% / −4.65% / −25.04%).","-","-## Prompt fairness — VERIFIED CLEAN, do not re-audit","-","-n=49, all pairs. Shared block **byte-identical** after normalising the arm path. One eg-only","-tail, identical across all 49, **capability-only** — no \"search first\", no \"do not grep\", no","-turn/token language. Zero frugality sentences in one arm only. Baseline has no graph affordance","-by any route: 0 payloads, 0 `eg-q.run`, 0 `entire` shim, 0 mentions across 49 transcripts.","-","-## Verification","-","-- **G0 offline, $0**: run `entire graph verify` directly in `replay-wt/` checkouts for valkey,","-  bat, laravel, ansible, redis; confirm it returns a parsed pass/fail inside the timeout and","-  that output is capped.","-- Harness canonical at `/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench`; deploy to VMs by","-  temp-path + **atomic `mv`** only — never overwrite a script sessions are reading.","-- Tool source `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph`; `mise run build`, gate with `mise run check`","-  (CGO required for tree-sitter).","-- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** Δturns **and** harness-run counts — the last","-  is the direct read on whether L1 actually changed behaviour.","+The defensible claim is **not** a token saving. On Opus the tool is centrally neutral","+(+1.35%, t=−0.17; −0.26% winsorised). What it demonstrably does at n=49 is suppress whole-file","+reads — 119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B, >8 KB tail 39 → 25 — and that is measurable now","+without another cell. Report that, plus the interval on tokens, and stop quoting a percentage the","+data does not support."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b69ef432-aa28-450d-aef4-1970dede59b3","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
