{"parentUuid":"7d590992-d96b-48a3-8a17-ba0720402228","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqhXzQAy2H78hnygcuaz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed, and worse than the review said:\n\n| estimator | value |\n|---|---|\n| total (headline) | +1.35% |\n| **drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n| drop `bat-1892` | +4.32% |\n| median | **−4.16%** |\n| **10% trimmed mean** | **−7.65%** |\n\n**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg *loses* on Opus. Launching the workflow over all artifacts and data before I finalize:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2743,"cache_read_input_tokens":714837,"output_tokens":5924,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2743,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5924,"cache_read_input_tokens":714837,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2743},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqhXs7cmcQ6YEmWSPE6u","type":"assistant","uuid":"7729578f-c251-40da-b304-6d28e859efa5","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:46:43.494Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"7729578f-c251-40da-b304-6d28e859efa5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqhXzQAy2H78hnygcuaz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XXiqYKECd7fF1hMZraRjEu","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'eg-opus-final-audit',\n  description: 'Read-only audit of every entire-graph artifact and dataset to settle what is true on Opus and what plan survives',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Read', detail: 'four lenses over artifacts, ledger, memory and raw data' },\n    { title: 'Refute', detail: 'adversarial verification of each surviving claim' },\n    { title: 'Decide', detail: 'single synthesis' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst FACTS = `\nREAD-ONLY AUDIT. Do not modify any file. Do not run any cell or spend model budget on the\nbenchmark. Analysis and reading only.\n\nPROJECT: entire-graph, a local code-graph CLI. Benchmarked against a no-tool baseline on\nSWE-bench Multilingual via Claude Code sessions. Metric: tokens. GOAL SET BY THE USER: 35% token\nsavings on Opus, fairly measured. Sign convention: POSITIVE = graph arm SAVED tokens.\n\nHEADLINE STATE (rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs) — freshly verified:\n  total +1.35%   median -4.16%   10% trimmed mean -7.65%   wins 24/49\n  paired sd (log ratio) 0.494   t = -0.17 (indistinguishable from zero)\n  LEAVE-ONE-OUT: drop lombok-3674 -> -5.18%; drop bat-1892 -> +4.32%. Range spans zero.\n  => the positive headline is ONE instance. Robust estimators all say eg LOSES on Opus.\n  drag pool -19.86 pts (25 instances); lift pool +21.21 pts (24). lombok-3674 alone = +6.09 pts.\n\nLOSER vs WINNER BEHAVIOUR (group sums, eg minus baseline):\n  pre-edit exploration:  losers -46,  winners -58   (the graph WORKS pre-edit in BOTH groups)\n  post-edit exploration: losers +159, winners -81\n  post-edit harness:     losers +50,  winners -88\n  edits:                 losers +42,  winners -25\n  turns:                 losers +296, winners -258\n  graph calls: 94 total, 91 PRE-edit, 3 post. 42/49 sessions never call it after the first edit.\n  harness ENV failures: losers eg 102 vs base 80; winners eg 85 vs base 130. corr -0.442.\n  throwaway scripts run: losers +16, winners -48. corr -0.350.\n\nCORRELATES with token saving: harness runs -0.612, exploration eliminated +0.485,\nrepeat-edits-to-same-file -0.457, edit calls -0.449, env-failures -0.442, first-edit turn -0.342.\n\nCONTEXT-COST MODEL (persist-weighted: bytes/4 x turns-remaining), validated per instance\n(corr +0.916, slope 0.822, R2 0.839):\n  baseline 38.6M total. exploration 45.1%, whole-file Read 30.3% (only 119 calls, 98k each,\n  7x any other class), harness 11.2%, range Read 9.3%. eg is 38.5M = CONTEXT-NEUTRAL (+0.2%).\n  cache_read is 95.5% of all tokens; output 1.5%.\n\nPOWER: n to demonstrate +1.35% = 12,900 pairs (~$78k). +6% = 499 pairs (~$4k). 35% = 11 pairs ($88).\nSame-instance spread across cells: median 99.9pt, max 294pt. 93% of losers flip sign between cells.\n\nEVERYTHING ALREADY CLOSED (do not re-propose):\n  - new verb in prompt affordance tail: 0/66 adoption (impact 0/49, changed 0/5, --path 0/12)\n  - G2 post-edit rider: -12.19% n=10, fired 0/5\n  - G3 displacement: ratio 0.76 vs 0.96 baseline (went backwards)\n  - graph-backed grep: 38.9% interception ceiling; graph output median 1,124 B is LARGER than a\n    median grep 732 B\n  - next-query coverage: only 40.4% of missed identifiers are graph symbols; of those 89% remain\n    missing at 4x payload budget (ranking-limited, not budget-limited)\n  - 12 payload-quality metrics incl. complete-symbol density (r = -0.170)\n  - retrieval/ranking quality: ANTI-correlated (gold-at-rank-1 sessions lost more often)\n  - tail-risk endpoint P(ratio>T): arms blow up at identical rates, n=6,338 to resolve\n  - symmetric frugality clamp: net-negative (in WINNERS the BASELINE flails, so a shared clamp\n    hands savings to the baseline)\n  - post-edit static-consistency hook: stress-tested and rejected — the fair (symmetric) form's\n    biggest beneficiary is the BASELINE in lombok-3674, i.e. it eats 29% of the lift; ~48% of the\n    corpus is dynamically typed where arity checks are unreliable; cost -2% to -6%.\n\nSTILL LIVE:\n  - R-A \"zero-toll delivery\": pre-compute the search payload, inject at turn 0, and make any\n    residual search an echo (EG_PRESEARCH). Built, offline-gated, deployed. Measured two ways:\n    counterfactual on this cell +4.3% to +6.0% (CI spans zero); and a prior 178-pair base giving\n    one call = 1.61 messages and a +7.0% CI[1.9,13.2] tax for merely having called.\n  - VERIFY runnability probe: derived test command is only checked with exec.LookPath, never run.\n    Add a collect-only probe. VERIFY appears in only 8 of 33 payloads.\n  - MOD vs ADD task kind (ledger's best idea): pooled MOD +14.35% (n=36) vs ADD -3.37% (n=21),\n    same sign in 4/4 cells. BLOCKER: routing on the gold patch is answer leakage; a keyword\n    classifier scores 57.5% against a 56% base rate.\n\nFAIRNESS DOCTRINE (binding): tool OUTPUT differences are legitimate; arm-asymmetric INSTRUCTIONS\nare not. Test: \"would this sentence/change help an arm with NO tool?\" If yes -> both arms or\nneither. A published -35% was withdrawn because the tool arm had two extra frugality sentences;\nremoving them moved that cell from -14.9% to +9.1%.\n\nUSER CONSTRAINTS: Opus only. Must be fair, no cheating. Wants the best token outcome that is\nstill fair.\n\nKEY PATHS (read-only):\n  /Users/suhaan/devenv/EG-FINAL-PLAN.md\n  /Users/suhaan/devenv/EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md\n  /Users/suhaan/devenv/PREREG-FABLE82.md\n  /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md   (canonical ledger, LIVE vs STRUCK)\n  /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/   (MEMORY.md + per-finding notes)\n  /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/   (tool source; internal/sem/search_verify.go, internal/cli/)\n  /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench/   (harness; tools/run_3arm.sh, tools/eg-q)\n`\n\nphase('Read')\n\nconst LENSES = [\n  { key: 'ledger', prompt: `${FACTS}\n\nYOUR LENS: the canonical ledger and memory. Read TokensNotes.md in full plus every memory note in\nthe memory directory. Produce: (a) every idea currently marked LIVE that has NOT been closed by\nthe facts above, with its measured evidence; (b) any claim in the ledger or memory that the facts\nabove CONTRADICT and must be corrected; (c) anything the ledger records as tried that the facts\nabove wrongly treat as untried. Be specific with numbers and file/section references.` },\n\n  { key: 'artifacts', prompt: `${FACTS}\n\nYOUR LENS: the three plan documents (EG-FINAL-PLAN.md, EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md, PREREG-FABLE82.md).\nRead them fully. Produce: (a) every internal inconsistency or arithmetic error you can find,\nquoting the numbers; (b) any claim that is stated more confidently than its evidence supports;\n(c) claims that are now superseded by the LOO/median/trimmed-mean result showing eg LOSES on\nOpus. These documents were written by me across a long session and contain several retractions —\nfind the ones I have NOT yet caught.` },\n\n  { key: 'source', prompt: `${FACTS}\n\nYOUR LENS: the tool source at /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph. Read the search, verify and\npayload-construction paths (internal/sem/search_verify.go, internal/sem/search.go,\ninternal/cli/search.go, internal/cli/def.go). Produce: (a) capabilities that already exist but\nare unreachable, disabled by default, or gated behind an unset flag — the project has repeatedly\nfound capabilities that shipped but were never wired up; (b) defaults that are actively harmful\ngiven the facts above (e.g. anything that grows payload size, since eg is context-neutral and\nwhole-file reads cost 98k persist each); (c) any place where a cheap change would reduce emitted\nBYTES without reducing answer quality. Cite file:line.` },\n\n  { key: 'harness', prompt: `${FACTS}\n\nYOUR LENS: the benchmark harness at /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench (tools/run_3arm.sh,\ntools/eg-q, tools/collect_patch.sh, the runners). Produce: (a) any remaining arm-asymmetry, however\nsmall — instructions, environment, PATH, tool availability, timeouts, retries; (b) measurement\ndefects that inflate variance or lose sample (a 0-byte cc_out.json sweep just removed 90 corpses);\n(c) whether the gate (subtype==success AND non-empty patch) admits junk — one baseline patch was\n371KB of vendor/build output and passed. Quote file:line for anything you find.` },\n]\n\nconst FINDINGS = {\n  type: 'object', additionalProperties: false,\n  required: ['lens', 'findings'],\n  properties: {\n    lens: { type: 'string' },\n    headline: { type: 'string', description: 'One sentence: the most important thing this lens found' },\n    findings: {\n      type: 'array', maxItems: 8,\n      items: {\n        type: 'object', additionalProperties: false,\n        required: ['claim', 'evidence', 'action', 'confidence'],\n        properties: {\n          claim: { type: 'string' },\n          evidence: { type: 'string', description: 'file:line or measured numbers' },\n          action: { type: 'string', description: 'what should change as a result' },\n          confidence: { type: 'string', enum: ['high', 'medium', 'low'] },\n          contradicts_existing: { type: 'boolean' },\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n}\n\nconst VERDICT = {\n  type: 'object', additionalProperties: false,\n  required: ['refuted', 'reason'],\n  properties: {\n    refuted: { type: 'boolean' },\n    reason: { type: 'string' },\n    corrected_action: { type: 'string' },\n  },\n}\n\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  LENSES,\n  (l) => agent(l.prompt, { label: `read:${l.key}`, phase: 'Read', schema: FINDINGS, effort: 'high' }),\n  (r, l) => {\n    if (!r || !r.findings) return { lens: l.key, headline: null, kept: [] }\n    const worth = r.findings.filter((f) => f.confidence !== 'low')\n    return parallel(\n      worth.map((f) => () =>\n        agent(`${FACTS}\\n\\nA claim from the ${l.key} audit:\\nCLAIM: ${f.claim}\\nEVIDENCE: ${f.evidence}\\nPROPOSED ACTION: ${f.action}\\n\\n` +\n          `REFUTE IT. This project has retracted a dozen findings; the failure mode is always the same — a correlate ` +\n          `mistaken for a cause, a subset selected on the outcome, or an effect below the noise floor. Check specifically: ` +\n          `(1) is the evidence real — open the file or re-derive the number; (2) is it already in the closed list; ` +\n          `(3) would the proposed action survive the fairness test; (4) is the effect larger than the ~100pt same-instance ` +\n          `noise floor, and if not, say so. Default to refuted=true unless you can independently confirm it.`,\n          { label: `refute:${f.claim.slice(0, 26)}`, phase: 'Refute', schema: VERDICT })\n          .then((v) => ({ ...f, verdict: v }))),\n    ).then((judged) => ({ lens: l.key, headline: r.headline, kept: judged.filter(Boolean) }))\n  },\n)\n\nconst all = results.filter(Boolean)\nconst survivors = all.flatMap((r) => r.kept).filter((f) => f.verdict && !f.verdict.refuted)\nconst killed = all.flatMap((r) => r.kept).filter((f) => f.verdict && f.verdict.refuted)\nlog(`${survivors.length} findings survived refutation; ${killed.length} killed`)\n\nphase('Decide')\n\nconst decision = await agent(\n  `${FACTS}\\n\\n` +\n  `Four read-only audits ran (ledger+memory, plan documents, tool source, benchmark harness). ` +\n  `Every finding was put to an adversarial refuter that defaults to refuted.\\n\\n` +\n  `LENS HEADLINES: ${JSON.stringify(all.map((r) => ({ lens: r.lens, headline: r.headline })))}\\n\\n` +\n  `SURVIVED: ${JSON.stringify(survivors)}\\n\\n` +\n  `KILLED: ${JSON.stringify(killed.map((f) => ({ claim: f.claim, why: f.verdict.reason })))}\\n\\n` +\n  `Write the decision document. The user's constraint is Opus-only, fair, best token outcome. ` +\n  `Answer plainly:\\n` +\n  `1. On Opus, does entire-graph save tokens? Give the number and the estimator, and say whether ` +\n  `the answer changes with the estimator (total +1.35%, median -4.16%, trimmed -7.65%, LOO spans zero).\\n` +\n  `2. Is 35% reachable on Opus by any fair change? Yes/no with the arithmetic.\\n` +\n  `3. What is the single best fair action, and what is its honest expected effect WITH an interval?\\n` +\n  `4. What must be corrected in the existing documents and memory because it is now known wrong?\\n` +\n  `5. What should be STOPPED entirely?\\n` +\n  `Be concrete, cite measured numbers, and do not restate anything already in the closed list as if new.`,\n  { label: 'decision', phase: 'Decide', effort: 'high' },\n)\n\nreturn { survivors, killed_count: killed.length, decision }\n","description":"Read-only audit of all artifacts and data"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2743,"cache_read_input_tokens":714837,"output_tokens":5924,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2743,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5924,"cache_read_input_tokens":714837,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2743},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqhXs7cmcQ6YEmWSPE6u","type":"assistant","uuid":"1575c09b-0d92-4a98-992c-a75ce131fdcd","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:47:45.691Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
