{"parentUuid":"5b14433e-4194-4113-a590-6e9ed5771679","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqhdPNg5rL45KDJjHJd9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That reframing is much better and I think it's right: **a code graph should not make things worse, and on 25 of 49 instances it does.** Dropping 35% and targeting \"losers behave like median winners\" is both more logical and more tractable — the drag pool is −19.86 pts and eliminating it alone gives +21.21%.\n\nLaunching investigators on the worst losers, on Opus, to work the actual failures turn-by-turn:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6772,"cache_read_input_tokens":717580,"output_tokens":2815,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6772,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2815,"cache_read_input_tokens":717580,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6772},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqhdHBriSsvw2uZo7DrU","type":"assistant","uuid":"a9d72add-5c6b-4a88-9df6-93031f248e7d","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:48:13.655Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"a9d72add-5c6b-4a88-9df6-93031f248e7d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqhdPNg5rL45KDJjHJd9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LeVWSqPm6XBdu6Ps36SzSX","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Investigate bat-1892 and valkey-790 losses","model":"opus","prompt":"READ-ONLY investigation. Do not modify any file. Caveman-ultra compressed output — dense bullets, numbers, file:line. No prose padding. Use RTK where it saves tokens.\n\nGOAL: entire-graph (a local code-graph CLI) makes 25 of 49 SWE-bench instances WORSE than a no-tool baseline. That is illogical — a code graph should help. Your job: work out, TURN BY TURN, exactly what happened in two of the worst losses, and say what capability added to or changed in entire-graph would have collapsed those turns.\n\nYOUR TWO INSTANCES:\n  sharkdp__bat-1892       eg 100 turns / 9.23M tok  vs  baseline 65 turns / 5.13M tok  (-79.8%)\n  valkey-io__valkey-790   eg  93 turns / 7.07M tok  vs  baseline 54 turns / 3.11M tok  (-127.4%)\n  bat-1892:    eg exploration 44 vs base 18; harness 23 vs 14; first edit at turn 37 vs 21\n  valkey-790:  eg exploration 57 vs base 34; harness 20 vs 11; first edit at turn 25 vs 18\n  Both made exactly ONE graph call, pre-edit.\n\nHOW TO GET THE DATA (VM, via IAP tunnel; each ssh takes ~30-60s so batch your commands):\n  P=graph-benchmarks-504800\n  gcloud compute ssh graphbench-c --project=$P --zone=us-east1-b --tunnel-through-iap --quiet --command='...'\n\n  Session results:   ~/work/graphmark/agentic-swebench/results/REP50_r1_eg/eg/<iid>/cc_out.json\n                     ~/work/graphmark/agentic-swebench/results/REP50_r1_baseline/baseline/<iid>/cc_out.json\n  The graph call + payload the eg arm received:\n                     results/REP50_r1_eg/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log   and  gq_calls.log.payload\n  Full transcripts:  ~/.claude/projects/*/<session_id>.jsonl  where session_id comes from cc_out.json\n  The problem statement is in the first user message of the transcript.\n  The graded patch:  results/<tag>/<arm>/<iid>/patch.diff\n\nWHAT TO PRODUCE, for EACH instance:\n1. The task in one line, and whether it is a MOD (fix existing broken code) or an ADD (introduce\n   behaviour that does not exist). This matters: pooled MOD +14.35% vs ADD -3.37% across 4 cells.\n2. The graph payload the eg arm actually got — did it point at the right code? Quote the top hits.\n3. A turn-by-turn account of where the eg arm's EXTRA turns went versus baseline. Bucket them:\n   localization / environment setup / test-harness wrangling / repeated edit-test cycles /\n   reading files / recovering truncated output / dead ends. Give counts per bucket.\n4. THE KEY QUESTION: name the specific moments where a graph capability would have removed turns.\n   For each, state: what the agent was trying to learn, what it actually did (how many turns),\n   and what exact command/output would have answered it in one turn.\n5. Was the eg arm's extra work CAUSED by the graph payload (e.g. it followed the payload to the\n   wrong place, or the payload gave it more to read), or merely coincident with it? Give evidence\n   either way. Be honest if the graph is simply innocent here.\n\nCONSTRAINTS ON ANY PROPOSAL YOU MAKE:\n- Must be TOOL OUTPUT, not an instruction. Fairness test: \"would this sentence help an arm with\n  NO tool?\" If yes, it is forbidden.\n- Already tried and dead, do not propose: new verbs advertised in the prompt tail (0/66 adoption:\n  impact 0/49, changed 0/5, --path 0/12); post-edit riders attached to graph calls (fired 0/5);\n  better ranking (gold-at-rank-1 sessions LOST more often); bigger payloads (eg is already\n  context-neutral, and whole-file reads cost 98k persist-tokens each); graph-backed grep (graph\n  output median 1,124 B is LARGER than a median grep at 732 B).\n- 42/49 sessions make NO graph call after their first edit, so anything requiring the agent to\n  call the tool post-edit reaches almost nobody.\n\nRank your proposals by (turns removed) / (bytes added). Say plainly if the honest answer is that\nnothing in the graph's power would have helped these two instances."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6772,"cache_read_input_tokens":717580,"output_tokens":2815,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6772,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2815,"cache_read_input_tokens":717580,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6772},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqhdHBriSsvw2uZo7DrU","type":"assistant","uuid":"8141f085-9490-4408-8154-5501b1096fda","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:48:36.460Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
