_eg/eg/<iid>/cc_out.json\n                     ~/work/graphmark/agentic-swebench/results/REP50_r1_baseline/baseline/<iid>/cc_out.json\n  Graph call + payload delivered:  results/REP50_r1_eg/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log  and  gq_calls.log.payload\n  Full transcripts:  ~/.claude/projects/*/<session_id>.jsonl   (session_id is in cc_out.json)\n  Problem statement: first user message of the transcript.\n  Graded patch:      results/<tag>/<arm>/<iid>/patch.diff\n\nWHAT TO PRODUCE, for EACH instance:\n1. The task in one line, and whether it is a MOD (fix existing broken code) or an ADD (introduce\n   behaviour that does not exist). Pooled MOD +14.35% vs ADD -3.37% across 4 cells, so this matters.\n2. The graph payload actually delivered — did it point at the right code? Quote the top hits. For\n   prometheus especially: did the payload send the agent somewhere wrong?\n3. Turn-by-turn account of where eg's extra turns went vs baseline, bucketed: localization /\n   environment setup / test-harness wrangling / repeated edit-test cycles / reading files /\n   recovering truncated output / dead ends. Counts per bucket.\n4. THE KEY QUESTION: name specific moments where a graph capability would have removed turns. For\n   each: what the agent was trying to learn, what it did instead (how many turns), and the exact\n   command/output that would have answered it in one turn.\n5. Was eg's extra work CAUSED by the payload (followed it to the wrong place; given more to read)\n   or merely coincident? Evidence either way. Be honest if the graph is innocent.\n6. These are dynamically-typed repos (Python). ~48% of this corpus is Ruby/PHP/JS/TS. State\n   whether any static-analysis capability could even work here, or whether dynamic dispatch,\n   **kwargs, and duck typing make it unreliable.\n\nCONSTRAINTS ON ANY PROPOSAL:\n- Must be TOOL OUTPUT, not an instruction. Fairness test: \"would this sentence help an arm with\n  NO tool?\" If yes, forbidden.\n- Dead, do not propose: new verbs advertised in the prompt tail (0/66 adoption); post-edit riders\n  attached to graph calls (fired 0/5); better ranking (gold-at-rank-1 sessions LOST more often);\n  bigger payloads (eg is already context-neutral; whole-file reads cost 98k persist-tokens each);\n  graph-backed grep (graph output median 1,124 B is LARGER than a median grep at 732 B).\n- 42/49 sessions make NO graph call after their first edit.\n\nRank proposals by (turns removed) / (bytes added). Say plainly if nothing in the graph's power\nwould have helped these two."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3179,"cache_read_input_tokens":724352,"output_tokens":1827,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3179,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1827,"cache_read_input_tokens":724352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3179,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3179},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqhh5Jqraj6rbvTn3F27","type":"assistant","uuid":"234b5034-4fd2-4c0f-869f-99d087268387","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:49:01.539Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
