{"parentUuid":"94282aaa-d407-4326-a9ab-b85daeeb684b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"explain to me the payload and tokens js explain it to me","commandMode":"prompt","origin":{"kind":"human"},"timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:48:51.522Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d1f4d78e-a639-47a9-b671-d176224928e6","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:48:51.522Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"d1f4d78e-a639-47a9-b671-d176224928e6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqhizHnCKG33UDJEqjgo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2302,"cache_read_input_tokens":727531,"output_tokens":1609,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2302,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1609,"cache_read_input_tokens":727531,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2302},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqhisHbJc55dXkeM5WUj","type":"assistant","uuid":"ec3e0f66-ba23-4575-b56c-87b280206734","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:49:09.922Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"ec3e0f66-ba23-4575-b56c-87b280206734","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqhizHnCKG33UDJEqjgo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sure — here's the whole picture, plainly.\n\n## What \"the payload\" is\n\nWhen the agent runs `entire graph search \"...\"`, the tool prints a block of text: ranked hits, each with `file:line`, a score, and usually the source of the matching function. That block is **the payload**. It gets pasted into the conversation as the tool's result.\n\nTypical sizes in this benchmark:\n\n| thing the agent receives | median size | ≈ tokens |\n|---|---|---|\n| graph payload | 1,124 B | ~280 |\n| a `grep` result | 732 B | ~183 |\n| a **whole-file `Read`** | 5,125 B | ~1,280 |\n| a big whole-file `Read` (p90) | 20,181 B | ~5,000 |\n\nNote the graph's payload is *bigger* than a typical grep. That's why \"replace grep with the graph\" doesn't automatically save anything.\n\n## How tokens get charged\n\nA session is ~54 turns. On each turn the model is sent **the entire conversation so far** — the prompt, plus every tool result received up to that point. So:\n\n- **95.5%** of all tokens billed are `cache_read` — re-reading context that already exists\n- 3.0% is `cache_creation`, 1.5% is `output` (what the model actually writes)\n\nThis is the crucial part: **you don't pay for a tool result once. You pay for it on every turn that follows.**\n\n## Why that changes everything\n\nA result injected at turn 10 of a 54-turn session is re-charged ~44 more times. So its true cost is roughly:\n\n```\ncost ≈ (bytes ÷ 4) × turns_remaining\n```\n\nI call that a **persist-token**. Measured across the baseline arm's 38.6M persist-tokens:\n\n| what | calls | cost each | share of total |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| exploration (grep/ls/sed/cat) | 1,206 | 14k | **45%** |\n| **whole-file `Read`** | **119** | **98k** | **30%** |\n| harness runs (tests/builds) | 576 | 7k | 11% |\n\n**119 whole-file reads cost as much as 1,206 greps.** One whole-file read is 7× a grep, because it's both bigger *and* sits in context for the rest of the session.\n\n## So how does a graph call pay for itself?\n\nThree ways, and only three:\n\n1. **It replaces something bigger** — one 280-token payload instead of a 1,280-token file read. Real, and it's the one place eg measurably works: whole-file reads fell 119 → 105 and their median size fell 5,125 → 4,081 B.\n2. **It removes a turn** — fewer messages means less context re-read by everything after.\n3. **It gets the fix right sooner** — no edit→test→fix loop.\n\nAnd the cost side: the call itself is a turn, and its payload then persists. Measured, **one graph call prices at ~1.61 messages**, and a regression holding call-count fixed charges **+7.0%** for merely having made the call.\n\n## What actually happened on Opus\n\n- 94 graph calls made, costing ~151 messages\n- they eliminated ~26 exploration calls and 31 harness runs\n- net: eg spent **38 more turns** than baseline\n- but each turn was **2.7% cheaper** (less junk in context)\n- those nearly cancel → **+1.35%**, which is one instance away from negative\n\nThat's the whole thing: **the graph is paying a turn to buy context that's slightly cleaner, and the two roughly cancel.** It's context-neutral overall — 38.5M vs 38.6M persist-tokens.\n\nWhich is exactly why \"make the losers behave like winners\" is the right target you named: in losers the payload buys nothing (post-edit exploration +159), while in winners it buys convergence (−81). Same tool, opposite outcome — and the two investigators are digging into precisely why right now."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2302,"cache_read_input_tokens":727531,"output_tokens":1609,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2302,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1609,"cache_read_input_tokens":727531,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2302},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqhisHbJc55dXkeM5WUj","type":"assistant","uuid":"46e0bdc5-0e12-40fa-a20c-aa15611bcda2","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:49:29.102Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
