{"parentUuid":"c86f8ba5-7115-4372-84c8-d5f01ba5ffc3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqiBYxn8HSQXUC1ixUYP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's how the graph actually works, measured on this repo (36,359 edges, 7,370 symbols).\n\n## The pipeline\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  subgraph BUILD[\"BUILD — deterministic, local, no network, no model\"]\n    A[\"repo working tree\"] --> B[\"tree-sitter parse<br/>205 file extensions\"]\n    B --> C{\"language tier\"}\n    C -->|\"36 semantic langs<br/>Go Rust Java Py Rb PHP TS…\"| D[\"full extraction:<br/>symbols + 30 relation types\"]\n    C -->|\"149 inventory-only<br/>ABAP, Awk, BASIC…\"| E[\"symbols only:<br/>CONTAINS + DEFINES\"]\n    D --> F[\"graph: 7,370 symbols<br/>36,359 edges\"]\n    E --> F\n    F --> G[\"gzip snapshot cache<br/>keyed by tree hash\"]\n  end\n\n  subgraph QUERY[\"QUERY — what the agent calls\"]\n    G --> H[\"search --query<br/>hybrid rank\"]\n    G --> I[\"def / neighbors / impact<br/>changed / grep\"]\n    H --> J[\"payload: ranked hits<br/>file:line + source<br/>median 1,124 B\"]\n    I --> J\n  end\n\n  J --> K[\"agent's context<br/>re-charged EVERY later turn\"]\n```\n\n## There are no custom groups or per-repo rules\n\nThis is the part worth being clear about: **the same code path runs for every repo.** No per-repo config, no per-language principles, no tuned profiles. What varies is only:\n\n| axis | what changes |\n|---|---|\n| **language tier** | 36 languages get semantic relations; **149 get only `CONTAINS`+`DEFINES`** (a file/symbol inventory, no call graph) |\n| **profile** | `syntax-only` = 2 relation types · `fast` (default) = **9** · `full` = **30** |\n| nothing else | ranking, budgets, output shape are identical everywhere |\n\n## The edge distribution, and why it matters\n\n| relation | edges | share |\n|---|---|---|\n| CALLS | 12,636 | 34.8% |\n| DEFINES | 7,370 | 20.3% |\n| SIMILAR_TO | 3,279 | 9.0% |\n| DATA_FLOWS | 3,010 | 8.3% |\n| USES_TYPE | 2,303 | 6.3% |\n| IMPORTS | 1,100 | 3.0% |\n| FILE_CHANGES_WITH | 378 | 1.0% |\n| **TESTS** | **10** | **0.03%** |\n| EXTENDS / INHERITS / IMPLEMENTS | 9 / 9 / 7 | ~0.02% each |\n\nThree things fall out of that:\n\n1. **The graph is 55% \"who calls what\" and \"what is defined where.\"** That's genuinely what it's good at — and it's a *pre-edit* capability, which matches the measurement: exploration falls in both winners and losers before the first edit.\n\n2. **`TESTS` has 10 edges.** It's heuristic (name-convention only), as are `HANDLES_ROUTE`, `SIMILAR_TO`, `EMITS`, `LISTENS_ON`, `HTTP_CALLS`, `HANDLES_TOOL`. So \"which test covers this code\" — the single most useful thing for the verify-repair spiral — is effectively **not implemented**.\n\n3. **The default profile is `fast` = 9 relation types.** At the default, `TESTS`, `SIMILAR_TO`, `DATA_FLOWS`, `FILE_CHANGES_WITH` and every type relation are *structurally absent*, so any output block depending on them comes back empty. The benchmark sets `full`, so rep50 was fine — but the shipped default is misleading.\n\n## Resolution quality\n\nOf 36,359 edges: **19,430 exact** (53%), 4,238 import-external, 4,052 pattern, 3,561 package, 3,000 name-only, 1,310 type-inferred, 378 from git history. So roughly **half the graph is heuristic**, and the heuristic half is concentrated in exactly the relations that would answer post-edit questions.\n\n## Where this points\n\nThe architecture explains the three loss reasons cleanly: the graph is a strong *pre-edit* call/definition index, and pre-edit is where it demonstrably works. It has almost nothing for \"what test covers this\" or \"did my edit break a contract\" — the post-edit phase carrying 97.7% of the cost.\n\nThree investigations are running against exactly this: two on the worst losers, one on what capability should exist and doesn't. I'll fold their answers into the plan when they land."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_read_input_tokens":753019,"output_tokens":1585,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1585,"cache_read_input_tokens":753019,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqiBSNQKECHJLYknZ3Wx","type":"assistant","uuid":"62c18892-2571-47c2-af67-cc8632b9fb3e","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:55:25.967Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
