{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01TQjcV9RFKrapFue4SWczEa","lastSequenceNum":0}
{"parentUuid":"bf2f1a61-e331-4463-8f28-12613b739052","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqiFLERLeComd6JKuXj1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Status**\n\n| cell | arm | n | TOKEN | median | 10% trimmed | wins |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| rep50 4-arm | eg | 49/49 | +1.35% | −4.16% | −7.65% | 24/49 |\n| | cmm | 49/49 | −5.95% | −2.9% | — | 22/49 |\n| | graphify | 48/49 | −0.50% | −8.1% | — | 18/48 |\n| G2 (rider) | eg vs base | 10 | −12.19% | −14.45% | — | 3/10 |\n| G3 (displacement) | eg vs base | 11 | −1.24% | −0.40% | — | 5/11 |\n| Gemini 300 | — | 207 | −8.78% | — | — | VM A terminated |\n| rep30 | — | — | — | — | — | VM B terminated, 52 unfinished |\n\n**Flags:** wt 0 · cmm SKIP 0 · graphify SKIP 0 · max-turns 1 · none arm-asymmetric. Nothing running.\n\n**Changed: nothing.** Three investigations still in flight, no benchmark spend.\n\n---\n\n**On per-repo configs — I'd hold off, and here's my honest read.**\n\nYou asked me not to launch if I think it's useless. I think it's *premature* rather than useless, for three measured reasons:\n\n1. **Per-repo/per-language gating is already struck.** TokensNotes §2.2 — \"Language / repo gating\" was tried and killed. Re-running it as \"groups of repos\" is the same lever with new words, which is exactly how a dozen findings got retracted here.\n\n2. **The power isn't there.** rep50 has 49 instances across ~10 languages — 3–8 per language. MDE is 25–30pt at n=30, and same-instance spread is ~100pt. Any per-group difference at n=5 is noise. This is precisely the sub-group analysis that produced the withdrawn \"VERIFY-off is a −12pt lever\" claim.\n\n3. **The one grouping with real evidence isn't a repo grouping — it's a *task* grouping.** MOD +14.35% vs ADD −3.37%, same sign 4/4 cells. That cuts across repos and languages, and it's already being worked by the running workflow.\n\n**What I think of the architecture, plainly:** it's a strong pre-edit call/definition index with a weak heuristic tail. 55% of edges are CALLS+DEFINES; `TESTS` has 10 edges of 36,359 and is name-convention only; `EXTENDS`/`INHERITS`/`IMPLEMENTS` are ~9 each. Half the graph is heuristic (19,430 exact of 36,359), and the heuristic half is concentrated in exactly the relations that would answer post-edit questions. That matches the measurement precisely — the tool works where it's strong (pre-edit, both groups) and is absent where the cost is.\n\n**What I'd launch instead, if you want a workflow now:** a per-language *correctness* audit — does extraction actually work in each of the 36 semantic languages, or are some silently degraded to inventory-only? That's a bug hunt with a definite answer at n=1 per language, not a statistical claim needing n=30. Ruby/PHP/JS are 48% of the corpus; if their call graphs are thin, that's a real defect and it would explain part of the loss.\n\nSay the word and I'll launch that version."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1005,"cache_read_input_tokens":756036,"output_tokens":1146,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1005,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1146,"cache_read_input_tokens":756036,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1005},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqiFAmeVAXHxmdACY2X2","type":"assistant","uuid":"6a56517b-6db5-4f2c-8a31-06b41db0ba94","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:56:13.033Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranc