{"parentUuid":"df5fa40f-fc5c-4c5d-8757-28cc6ba4ee75","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqiNqNorrduXkQSFjLAk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3684,"cache_read_input_tokens":758291,"output_tokens":1267,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3684,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":758291,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3684,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3684},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqiNhEugeibQKAALBGCa","type":"assistant","uuid":"be6a6df7-6c66-4dd8-8d80-2ee365b55b5b","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:57:48.242Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"be6a6df7-6c66-4dd8-8d80-2ee365b55b5b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqiNqNorrduXkQSFjLAk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Understood — holding the full plan until every result is in.\n\nOne finding landed that directly answers your question though, and it's a clean negative:\n\n**It is not a harness problem.**\n\n| | n | paired sd | n needed to detect +6% |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| sessions with ≥1 harness ENV failure | 41 (84%) | **0.501** | 499 |\n| sessions with a clean environment | 8 | **0.489** | 490 |\n\n84% of sessions hit at least one environment failure — but removing them changes the variance by **1.2%** and the required sample by **nine pairs**. Environment noise is real but it is not what's driving the winner/loser split.\n\nSo the answer to \"if it's good for the task and repo, why doesn't everything win?\" is neither harness nor eg in the way I'd been framing it. It's that **run-level stochasticity is ~87% of paired variance** — the same instance, same config, same tool lands anywhere across a ~100-point range depending on which path the agent happens to wander down. That's why 93% of losers flip sign between cells: **the \"losers\" are mostly not a stable set.**\n\nWhich reframes the fix. \"Make the losers win\" partly means chasing a coin flip. The things that *are* stable and fixable are the ones with a mechanism behind them — the ADD-task defect (same sign 4/4 cells), the call toll (arithmetic), and the verify derivation. Those three are exactly what the running workflow is designing against.\n\nStill in flight: the 4-lens artifact audit, two loser dissections (`bat-1892`/`valkey-790`, `ansible`/`prometheus`), the capability-inventory review, and the three-defect fix workflow. I'll synthesise everything into the full plan once they land — and I'm not launching the repo-grouping workflow, since per-repo/language gating is already struck and n=3–8 per language can't support it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3684,"cache_read_input_tokens":758291,"output_tokens":1267,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3684,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":758291,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3684,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3684},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqiNhEugeibQKAALBGCa","type":"assistant","uuid":"1424c5f6-4d76-43f1-815b-d06460559425","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:57:57.647Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
