o:10,93                | default=\"\"                              | gates: repo-path resolution fallback    | documented: docs/DETAILS.md:157\nENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR     | internal/cli/env.go:11,94                | default=\"\"                              | gates: cache-dir location + doctor probe| documented: docs/DETAILS.md\nENTIRE_GRAPH_REFERENCE_BLOCKS | internal/cli/env.go:15,95              | default=\"\" (blocks OFF)                 | gates: session-wide on-switch for 3 ref blocks | documented: YES, --help Notes text (root.go printHelp)\nENTIRE_GRAPH_PRESEARCH     | internal/cli/env.go:23,96                | default=\"\"                              | gates: total bypass of search pipeline, echo precomputed file | documented: no\nEG_PRESEARCH               | internal/cli/env.go:24,89                | alias of above                          | gates: same                             | documented: no\nEG_SEARCH_SESSION          | internal/cli/env.go:28,97                | default=\"\" (cap/echo OFF)               | gates: enables one-search-per-task cap+echo | documented: no\nEG_MAX_SEARCHES            | internal/cli/env.go:31,98                | default=1 when session file set; \"0\"=uncapped | gates: how many searches/session run for real | documented: no\n```\nNo test-only `os.Getenv`/`LookupEnv` found in internal/cmd (`_test.go` grep = 0 hits).\n\nNon-Go (shell, outside grep scope but real toggles): `scripts/entire-graph-statusline.sh` reads `ENTIRE_GRAPH_BIN`, `ENTIRE_GRAPH_STATUSLINE_SCOPE`, `ENTIRE_GRAPH_STATUSLINE_SINCE`, `ENTIRE_GRAPH_STATUSLINE_CACHE`, `NO_COLOR` — all documented in README.md.\n\n## HIDDEN FLAGS (case \"--X\" in dispatch, absent from root.go printHelp usage block)\n\n`changed` subcommand — **entire subcommand is hidden**: `case \"changed\"` at root.go:80 dispatches to runChanged, but zero mention anywhere in printHelp's `Usage:` block (root.go:113-175). All its flags are consequently undocumented: `--repo --format --profile --cache-d