{"parentUuid":"d8d89062-561b-4bf7-9ae8-84588edf6c1b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqiWBw1z2zw1oZjtMpRV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The audit **refutes** the subagent's headline claim at population scale, and replaces it with something sharper:\n\n| group | n | TOKEN | wins |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| eg built, baseline didn't | 4 | +2.04% | 2/4 |\n| baseline built, eg didn't | 6 | +31.14% | 4/6 |\n| **both arms built for real** | **20** | **−14.49%** | 7/20 |\n| neither built | 19 | **+9.71%** | 11/19 |\n\nProvisioning asymmetry is real but **small** — only 2 of 25 losers, worth −1.06 pts of the −19.86 drag. So that isn't what's sinking the cell.\n\nThe real signal is the last two rows: **eg loses 14.49% when both arms actually build and test, and wins 9.71% when neither does.** The tool is worst precisely where genuine verification happens — which is exactly the verify-repair spiral, now confirmed from a completely independent angle.\n\nLogging findings into the plan file, since plan mode limits me to that file:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4057,"cache_read_input_tokens":768793,"output_tokens":3122,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4057,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3122,"cache_read_input_tokens":768793,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4057},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqiW3s63xfM1H5tgkGmA","type":"assistant","uuid":"990bb167-1eaf-4500-9d7c-7e5f02e748f8","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:59:35.386Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"990bb167-1eaf-4500-9d7c-7e5f02e748f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqiWBw1z2zw1oZjtMpRV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VNFHWPB9fKnv9RF34ExGBj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans && python3 - <<'PY'\np='stateless-napping-unicorn.md'; s=open(p).read()\nlog = \"\"\"\n\n---\n\n# APPENDIX A — Subagent findings log\n\nRunning record of every investigation. Each entry: what was asked, what came back, and whether it\nsurvived checking. **Entries are not conclusions until marked CONFIRMED.**\n\n## A1 — Post-edit hook stress test *(Plan agent, completed)*\n**Asked:** is an automatic post-edit consistency-check hook fair, and what does it cost?\n**Returned — REJECTED the design, three reasons:**\n- A hook is a *harness* feature; every harness change here is symmetric by construction. The\n  no-tool-arm test fails: `rg -n 'symbol'` produces ~80% of the same output.\n- **Self-defeating in its fair form.** The biggest beneficiary of a symmetric hook is the\n  *baseline* in `lombok-3674` — where baseline ran `javac` 70× vs eg's 23×. That instance is 29%\n  of all lift, so the fix eats its own lift source.\n- Cost: fires on all 414 eg edits; at a 400-token payload = **−5.6%**. eg is context-neutral, so\n  there is no slack to spend.\n**Also surfaced:** `claude --settings '<json>' --setting-sources ''` avoids writing\n`.claude/settings.json` into the worktree, which would remove the patch-pollution blocker.\n**Status: CONFIRMED as a rejection.** Do not build the hook.\n\n## A2 — Loser forensics: `bat-1892`, `valkey-790` *(Opus agent, completed)*\n**Returned:**\n- **The graph payload was CORRECT in both.** Top hit was the exact function to edit. eg used\n  *fewer* localization calls than baseline (10 vs 15; 15 vs 17). **The graph won localization and\n  lost the session downstream.** — CONFIRMED, matches the cell-wide pre-edit finding (−46/−58).\n- `bat-1892`: 42 of 99 calls are environment/leak/hung-test work no code graph can address.\n- `valkey-790`: ~13–15 pre-edit calls *are* graph-shaped — \"which tests exercise this symbol and\n  how are they invoked\", and tcl `proc` definitions (three consecutive failed greps for `proc R`\n  because **entire-graph indexes no `.tcl` symbols**).\n- **Proposal: a test-invocation card in the first search response** (~14 turns / ~500 B). Not a\n  new verb, not post-edit — it rides the one call every session already makes.\n**Two integrity claims, both checked below.**\n\n## A3 — Integrity claim 1: answer leak *(from A2)*\nConcurrent instance checkouts share a parent directory, and `sharkdp__bat-3108` is a **later\nrevision of the same repo containing the implemented feature**. eg found it via `ls` and spent 12\ncalls mining it. **Structural, not arm-specific** — whichever arm lists that directory gets the\nupstream solution. Corroborates an existing note (\"2 instances spent 13–15 calls mining an\nadjacent instance's tree\"). **Status: CONFIRMED as a live exposure. Must be fixed before any\nfurther cell.**\n\n## A4 — Integrity claim 2: \"the metric rewards failing to provision\" *(from A2)* — **REFUTED at scale**\nA2 argued baseline \"won\" `bat-1892` by never compiling the crate (it wrote a `rustc` mock while a\n198 MB offline registry sat unfound). True for that instance. **But the population audit does not\nsupport it as a general mechanism:**\n\n| group | n | TOKEN | wins |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| eg built, baseline did not | 4 | +2.04% | 2/4 |\n| baseline built, eg did not | 6 | +31.14% | 4/6 |\n| **both arms built for real** | **20** | **−14.49%** | 7/20 |\n| neither built | 19 | **+9.71%** | 11/19 |\n\nOnly **2 of 25 losers** have the eg-built/base-didn't shape, worth **−1.06 pts** of the −19.86 drag.\n**Status: REFUTED as a driver.**\n\n**But the audit replaced it with a stronger finding — CONFIRMED, and new:**\n> **eg loses 14.49% when both arms genuinely build and test, and wins 9.71% when neither does.**\n\nThe tool is worst exactly where real verification happens. This is the verify-repair spiral\nconfirmed from an independent angle, and it is the single most decision-relevant number in this\nappendix.\n\n## A5 — Still running\n- 4-lens artifact/data audit workflow (ledger+memory, plan docs, tool source, harness)\n- Loser forensics: `ansible-395e`, `prometheus-9248` (Python/dynamic counterparts to A2)\n- Capability inventory: what the graph computes but never surfaces\n- Three-defect fix workflow (call toll / ADD tasks / verify derivation)\n\n**The full plan is deliberately NOT finalised until these land.**\n\"\"\"\nif \"APPENDIX A\" not in s:\n    s = s.rstrip() + \"\\n\" + log\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"appendix added:\", \"APPENDIX A\" in s, len(s), \"bytes\")\nPY","description":"Log subagent findings into plan file"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4057,"cache_read_input_tokens":768793,"output_tokens":3122,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4057,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3122,"cache_read_input_tokens":768793,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4057},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqiW3s63xfM1H5tgkGmA","type":"assistant","uuid":"db1ef418-630b-44b8-aef8-b5d6d5a9119e","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:59:58.743Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"db1ef418-630b-44b8-aef8-b5d6d5a9119e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"73ad9440-9a58-440e-af70-6a71cac59596","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VNFHWPB9fKnv9RF34ExGBj","type":"tool_result","content":"appendix added: True 13855 bytes\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"343ae77a-d863-4cec-8bf9-0848e3ddefff","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:59:58.825Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"appendix added: True 13855 bytes","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"db1ef418-630b-44b8-aef8-b5d6d5a9119e","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"343ae77a-d863-4cec-8bf9-0848e3ddefff","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","snippet":"1\t# entire-graph on Opus — what the data says, and the only plan that survives it\n2\t\n3\t## Context\n4\t\n5\tThe goal set for this work is **35% token savings on rep50, fairly measured, on Opus**. This plan\n6\texists because that target is now refuted by the data, and continuing to aim at it would mean\n7\teither fabricating it or measuring something else and calling it that. What follows is the\n8\tevidence, the loser/winner analysis requested, and the plan that is actually supported.\n9\t\n10\tAll numbers: rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs, SWE-bench Multilingual.\n11\tSign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**\n12\t\n13\t---\n14\t\n15\t## 1. Where Opus actually stands\n16\t\n17\t| | value |\n18\t|---|---|\n19\t| headline | **+1.35%** |\n20\t| t-statistic | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n21\t| median | −4.2% |\n22\t| wins | 24 / 49 |\n23\t| paired sd (log-ratio) | 0.494 |\n24\t| n to *demonstrate* +1.35% | **12,900 pairs ≈ $78,491** |\n25\t| n to demonstrate +6% | 499 pairs ≈ $3,972 |\n26\t| n to demonstrate 35% | **11 pairs ≈ $88** |\n27\t\n28\t**35% would have been the cheapest result in the project to prove.** It is not provable because\n29\tit is not there. Every robust estimator drives the headline to zero or below — winsorised 20/80\n30\t**−0.26%**, dropping the 3 most extreme pairs **−6.19%** — so the positive sign is tail-carried.\n31\t\n32\t---\n33\t\n34\t## 2. Loser analysis (requested)\n35\t\n36\t**Drag −19.86 pts across 25 instances; top five carry −11.42 (57%).**\n37\t\n38\tGroup sums, eg minus baseline:\n39\t\n40\t| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n41\t|---|---|---|\n42\t| turns | **+296** | −258 |\n43\t| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n44\t| post-edit exploration | **+159** | −81 |\n45\t| post-edit harness | **+50** | −88 |\n46\t| edits | +42 | −25 |\n47\t| graph calls | 44 (43 pre) | 50 (48 pre) |\n48\t\n49\t**The single most important line is pre-edit exploration: the graph works in BOTH groups\n50\t(−46 / −58).** Localization is not what separates them. The entire divergence is post-edit, where\n51\t**91 of 94 graph calls never happen** — 42/49 sessions make no graph call after their first edit.\n52\t\n53\tWorst five, with the pattern visible per-instance:\n54\t\n55\t| instance | pts | tok | eg/base turns | eg/base expl | eg/base harness |\n56\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n57\t| `bat-1892` | −2.81 | −79.8% | 100/65 | 44/18 | 23/14 |\n58\t| `valkey-790` | −2.72 | −127.4% | 93/54 | 57/34 | 20/11 |\n59\t| `ansible-395e` | −2.58 | −68.1% | 116/91 | 48/38 | 9/5 |\n60\t| `prometheus-9248` | −1.68 | −74.6% | 110/68 | 68/38 | 9/8 |\n61\t| `tokio-4867` | −1.63 | −114.4% | 69/38 | 26/10 | 25/17 |\n62\t\n63\t**Correlates with token saving, ranked:**\n64\t\n65\t| | r |\n66\t|---|---|\n67\t| Δ harness runs | **−0.612** |\n68\t| Δ exploration eliminated | +0.485 |\n69\t| Δ repeat edits to same file | −0.457 |\n70\t| Δ edit calls | −0.449 |\n71\t| **Δ harness ENV failures** | **−0.442** |\n72\t| Δ throwaway scripts run | −0.350 |\n73\t| Δ first-edit turn | −0.342 |\n74\t\n75\t**Mechanism:** losers run verification that fails on the *environment* rather than the patch\n76\t(eg 102 vs base 80 in the loser group), then improvise throwaway harnesses (+16) and re-explore\n77\tto repair them (+159 post-edit exploration). Winners show the exact mirror: **−45 env failures,\n78\t−48 throwaway scripts, −88 harness runs**. This is the ledger's §1.3 lever, independently\n79\treproduced here.\n80\t\n81\t---\n82\t\n83\t## 3. Winner analysis — what must not regress\n84\t\n85\t**Lift +21.21 pts across 24 instances. `lombok-3674` alone is +6.09 pts = 29% of ALL lift.**\n86\t\n87\t| instance | pts | eg/base turns | eg/base harness |\n88\t|---|---|---|---|\n89\t| `lombok-3674` | **+6.09** | 67/122 | **23/70** |\n90\t| `fmt-2457` | +2.18 | 38/67 | 12/13 |\n91\t| `qutebrowser-c580` | +1.89 | 88/105 | 23/33 |\n92\t| `vuejs-11739` | +1.35 | 70/80 | 24/19 |\n93\t| `redis-11510` | +1.29 | 34/56 | 3/12 |\n94\t\n95\t**Winners win because the BASELINE flails and eg converges** — lombok's baseline ran `javac`\n96\t**70 times** against eg's 23. eg is not doing something clever; it is failing to blow up.\n97\t\n98\t**Two consequences that constrain every proposal below:**\n99\t\n100\t1. **A symmetric frugality clamp is net-negative.** Suppressing over-verification helps the\n101\t   baseline more than eg in exactly the instances eg currently wins. Already modelled; do not\n102\t   ship one.\n103\t2. **Any intervention that adds post-edit content risks converting a winner into a loser**, since\n104\t   winners win by *doing less* after the first edit. Winner protection is therefore not a\n105\t   formality — it is the main risk.\n106\t\n107\t---\n108\t\n109\t## 4. What is already closed (do not rebuild)\n110\t\n111\t| route | verdict |\n112\t|---|---|\n113\t| new verb in the affordance tail | **0/66 adoption** (`impact` 0/49, `changed` 0/5, `--path` 0/12) |\n114\t| post-edit rider (G2) | **−12.19%**, fired 0/5 |\n115\t| displacement via better verbs (G3) | ratio **0.76** vs 0.96 baseline — went backwards |\n116\t| graph-backed grep | 38.9% interception ceiling; graph output (1,124 B median) is *larger* than a median grep (732 B) |\n117\t| next-query coverage | only 40.4% of missed identifiers are graph symbols; of those 89% stay missing at 4× payload budget |\n118\t| payload quality | 12 metrics dead, incl. complete-symbol density (r = **−0.170**) |\n119\t| retrieval/ranking | anti-correlated — gold-at-rank-1 sessions lost more often |\n120\t| tail-risk endpoint | arms blow up at identical rates (22.4% vs 20.4%); n=6,338 to resolve |\n121\t\n122\t---\n123\t\n124\t## 5. The plan\n125\t\n126\t### 5.1 Accept the honest target\n127\t\n128\t**Stop targeting 35% on Opus.** Target **loser repair**, whose exact ceiling is the lift pool:\n129\t**+21.21%** if every losing instance were made precisely neutral. That is arithmetic, not\n130\tprojection. Reaching it requires eliminating the drag pool entirely; a realistic fraction is\n131\tworth +5–10%.\n132\t\n133\t### 5.2 Build: VERIFY runnability probe *(primary — targets the measured mechanism)*\n134\t\n135\t**Files:** `internal/sem/search_verify.go` (derivation + probe), `internal/cli/search.go`\n136\t(VERIFY block emission).\n137\t\n138\tToday the only check is `exec.LookPath` on the runner (`search_verify.go:1526`) — it confirms\n139\t`pytest` exists, never that the derived command *runs*. Add a **collect-only probe** before\n140\temitting: `pytest --collect-only -q`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`, `cargo test --no-run`,\n141\t`mvn -q -DskipTests compile`. On failure, drop to the next rung rather than emitting a command\n142\tthat will fail on the environment.\n143\t\n144\tAlso raise VERIFY coverage — it appears in only **8 of 33** payloads, so 76% of sessions get no\n145\tverification command at all and improvise one.\n146\t\n147\t**Fair:** the derived command is tool output computed from the repo, same class as a ranked hit.\n148\tShips no instruction; the baseline is untouched.\n149\t\n150\t**Expected: +0.5% to +1.5%.** Stated honestly — 22 avoided env-failures × ~39.5K tok ≈ 0.6% of\n151\tthe pool. This is a real mechanism with a small effect, not a headline.\n152\t\n153\t### 5.3 Ship: R-A zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, deployed)*\n154\t\n155\tAlready committed (`b669a57b`) and deployed. `EG_PREFETCH=1` injected the payload into turn 0 and\n156\tstill let the agent re-derive it at full price; `EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual call an echo\n157\t(0.02 s vs 5.21 s, byte-identical). Removes 94 calls × 1.61 msgs.\n158\t\n159\t**Expected +4.3% to +6.0%** (counterfactual on all 49 pairs; CI spans zero at n=49).\n160\t\n161\t### 5.4 Do NOT build the post-edit hook without a decision\n162\t\n163\tIt is the only mechanism reaching the 97.7%, but it requires `CC_NO_SAFE_MODE=1` and a change to\n164\tpatch collection (`.claude/settings.json` would land in the graded patch). It also carries the\n165\t§3 regression risk directly. Decide fairness and patch-collection acceptability first.\n166\t\n167\t---\n168\t\n169\t## 6. Gates — mechanism counts, winners protected\n170\t\n171\tMDE is ~25–30 pts at n≈30 against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor. **No token claim below\n172\tn≈50, in either direction.**\n173\t\n174\t| gate | n | criterion |\n175\t|---|---|---|\n\n... [109 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fd9635ae-39f7-472b-b477-78f259e7143b","timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:59:58.843Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
