{"parentUuid":"fbcf77de-abbd-42b7-b0c2-2fef2d7d6365","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqifksAvm2HEjgBoLJRm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have to correct something I told you two messages ago, and it's a real error.\n\n**The −14.49% \"both arms built\" finding was a regex artifact.** Re-running with a stricter definition of \"real test output\" changes the group from n=20 to n=17 and the result from **−14.49% to −0.89%**. The finding was not robust to how I defined the group — exactly the sub-group fragility that killed a dozen earlier claims here. Withdrawing it.\n\nWhat survives, from the stricter run:\n\n| | eg | base | Δ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| harness runs | 242 | 219 | +23 |\n| **distinct commands** | 226 | 211 | **+15 (65% of excess)** |\n| **repeated runs (waste)** | 16 | 8 | **+8 (35%)** |\n| runs with real output | 88 | 88 | 0 |\n| patch bytes | 94,447 | 85,756 | +8,691 |\n| files changed | 38 | 38 | 0 |\n\nSo on pairs where both arms genuinely verify, eg is **−0.89% — essentially neutral**, and its extra work is **65% distinct verification, 35% repeats**. That's mostly genuine work, not thrash. Neither \"verification is the defect\" nor \"the metric is the defect\" is supported at this n; the honest answer is that this split doesn't decide it.\n\nNow validating the inputs, since that's exactly the kind of thing that produced the error above:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3564,"cache_read_input_tokens":781402,"output_tokens":3375,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3564,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3375,"cache_read_input_tokens":781402,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqifdeb3uKwe4JDcu1Kx","type":"assistant","uuid":"af1ae01b-8169-46d7-a2e9-c02a5b462311","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:01:45.220Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"af1ae01b-8169-46d7-a2e9-c02a5b462311","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqifksAvm2HEjgBoLJRm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UhZnygV1LawdZwGB6FwJg9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"P=graph-benchmarks-504800\ncat > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49/scratchpad/validate.sh <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\ncd ~/work/graphmark/agentic-swebench\necho \"=== 1. GRAPH FRESHNESS: is each instance's graph built at the checkout's base_commit? ===\"\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,glob,os,subprocess\nrows=json.load(open('tasks/rep50_run.json'))['instances']\nok=miss=stale=0; bad=[]\nfor r in rows:\n    iid=r['instance_id']; bc=(r.get('base_commit') or '')[:12]\n    g=f\"graphs/{iid}/graph.edges.ndjson\"\n    if not os.path.exists(g): miss+=1; bad.append((iid,'NO GRAPH')); continue\n    hdr=None\n    for cand in (f\"graphs/{iid}/graph.header.json\", f\"graphs/{iid}/header.json\"):\n        if os.path.exists(cand):\n            try: hdr=json.load(open(cand))\n            except: pass\n            break\n    if hdr is None:\n        try:\n            with open(g,errors='ignore') as fh:\n                first=fh.readline()\n            hdr=json.loads(first)\n        except: hdr={}\n    c=(hdr.get('commit') or '')[:12]\n    if not c: ok+=1  # header has no commit field; can't verify\n    elif bc and c!=bc: stale+=1; bad.append((iid,f'graph@{c} != base@{bc}'))\n    else: ok+=1\nprint(f\"   graphs present+consistent: {ok}   missing: {miss}   COMMIT MISMATCH: {stale}\")\nfor b in bad[:6]: print(\"     \",b)\nPY\necho\necho \"=== 2. GRAPH SIZE SANITY: any instance with a suspiciously empty graph? ===\"\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,os,glob\nsizes=[]\nfor d in sorted(glob.glob('graphs/*/graph.edges.ndjson')):\n    sizes.append((os.path.getsize(d), d.split('/')[1]))\nsizes.sort()\nprint(f\"   {len(sizes)} graphs. smallest 6:\")\nfor s,i in sizes[:6]: print(f\"     {s:>10,d} B  {i[:44]}\")\ntiny=[i for s,i in sizes if s<50_000]\nprint(f\"   graphs under 50KB (possible extraction failure): {len(tiny)}\")\nPY\necho\necho \"=== 3. BINARY CONSISTENCY: which binary produced the rep50 payloads? ===\"\nls -la bin/entire-graph-linux* 2>/dev/null | awk '{print \"   \"$NF, $5\" B\"}'\nfor b in bin/entire-graph-linux bin/entire-graph-linux.r3; do\n  [ -x \"$b\" ] && echo \"   $b -> $(md5sum $b | cut -c1-12)\"\ndone\ngrep -oE 'binary=[^ ]+ sha=[a-f0-9]+' logs/*.log 2>/dev/null | awk -F'binary=' '{print $2}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -4\necho\necho \"=== 4. CACHE STALENESS: could a stale index have served rep50? ===\"\ndu -sh /tmp/egq* 2>/dev/null | head -3\necho \"   cache dirs: $(ls -d /tmp/egq* 2>/dev/null | wc -l)\"\necho\necho \"=== 5. ANSWER-LEAK EXPOSURE: do sibling checkouts of the same repo coexist? ===\"\nfor d in checkouts/*/; do\n  a=$(ls \"$d\" 2>/dev/null | head -40)\n  echo \"$a\" | sed 's/-[0-9]*$//;s/__.*//' | sort | uniq -c | awk '$1>1{print \"   MULTI-REVISION: \"$1\"x \"$2}'\ndone 2>/dev/null | sort -u | head -8\necho \"   (a later revision of the same repo in a sibling dir can contain the implemented fix)\"\necho\necho \"=== 6. PROMPT SYMMETRY: diff the two arms' prompts on a sample instance ===\"\ni=$(ls results/REP50_r1_eg/eg | head -1)\nfor f in prompt.txt cc_prompt.txt; do\n  A=\"results/REP50_r1_eg/eg/$i/$f\"; B2=\"results/REP50_r1_baseline/baseline/$i/$f\"\n  if [ -f \"$A\" ] && [ -f \"$B2\" ]; then\n    echo \"   $i: differing lines = $(diff \"$A\" \"$B2\" | grep -c '^[<>]')\"\n    diff \"$A\" \"$B2\" | grep '^[<>]' | head -6 | cut -c1-100 | sed 's/^/     /'\n  fi\ndone\n[ -f \"results/REP50_r1_eg/eg/$i/prompt.txt\" ] || echo \"   (no prompt.txt persisted for $i)\"\nEOF\nperl -e 'alarm shift; exec @ARGV' 300 gcloud compute scp /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49/scratchpad/validate.sh graphbench-c:/tmp/val.sh --project=$P --zone=us-east1-b --tunnel-through-iap --quiet 2>&1 | grep -vE 'WARNING|tcp-forward' | tail -1\nperl -e 'alarm shift; exec @ARGV' 700 gcloud compute ssh graphbench-c --project=$P --zone=us-east1-b --tunnel-through-iap --quiet --command='bash /tmp/val.sh' 2>&1 | grep -vE 'NumPy|tcp-forward|WARNING|Warning'","description":"Validate graphs, binaries, caches, leak exposure, prompt symmetry","timeout":800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3564,"cache_read_input_tokens":781402,"output_tokens":3375,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3564,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3375,"cache_read_input_tokens":781402,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqifdeb3uKwe4JDcu1Kx","type":"assistant","uuid":"1ee6a17f-48ce-400c-b193-9159007503a0","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:02:06.789Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
