{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01TQjcV9RFKrapFue4SWczEa","lastSequenceNum":0}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:08:38.633Z","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad5c11381e8da2811</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/ad5c11381e8da2811.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Find capabilities to add to the graph\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## 0. Method\n\nRead source at HEAD `607b2a4`; ran the in-tree binary. Empirical edge counts from two real trees. **Warning: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/entire-graph` is STALE vs source** — it rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--callee-hop`, `--full-unit-top`, `--edit-site-bodies`, `--path`, `--verify-prefix`. Everything below is from source; anything shipped to agents must be rebuilt first.\n\n---\n\n## 1. CAPABILITY INVENTORY — built, measured, shipped dark\n\n| capability | file:line | LOC | default | reachable by agent? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **FILE OUTLINE** — symbol index of the top-3 hit files, no source | `internal/sem/search_outline.go:1-217`, flag `internal/cli/search.go:1637` | 217 | **OFF** | no — undocumented flag `--file-outline`, absent from `printHelp` (`root.go:113-175`) |\n| **callee hop** — admit top hit's outgoing CALLS as fix sites | `internal/sem/search_callee.go:1-509`, flag `search.go:1666` | 509 | **OFF** | no |\n| **`edges --to/--from/--relation`** targeted edge query | `root.go:576-594` (parse), `root.go:466-511` (`relationMatches`/`idMatches`), `root.go:303-346` (stream) | ~100 | works | **actively denied** — `AGENTS.md:72` says \"there is **no** `--to`/`--from`/`--relation` filter\" |\n| **`verify`** — adjudicated verdict w/ PRE-EXISTING labelling, no raw output | `internal/cli/verify.go:1-?`, `verify_parse.go`; dispatch `root.go:82` | ~700 | exists | **not in `AGENTS.md`, not in `.entire/graph-agent.md`** |\n| **`changed`** — uncommitted edit → symbols → dependents | `internal/cli/changed.go:1-383`, dispatch `root.go:80` | 383 | exists | not in `printHelp` at all |\n| **`def`** — declaration + members from CONTAINS/OVERRIDES edges; multi-name batching; `--brief`; `--from N` resume | `internal/cli/def.go` (971), batching `def.go:329-335`, `--from` `def.go:277`, `--brief` `def.go:299` | 971 | exists | `def` is **absent from both agent guides' Reference tables** |\n| **container map / signature types / type card** | `search_container_map.go` (816) + `nested_containers.go` | 918 | **OFF** (measured to cost turns — correct call) | flag/env only |\n| **`--full-unit-top` / `--edit-site-bodies`** | `search_enclosure.go` (1353), flags `search.go:1654,1661` | shared | **0 / OFF** | no |\n| **`--path` scope** | `search_pathscope.go` (80) | 80 | OFF | no (0/12 adoption already measured) |\n| **search echo / cap** `EG_SEARCH_SESSION` + `EG_MAX_SEARCHES` | `search_session.go` (161) | 161 | **OFF unless harness sets a session file** | harness only |\n| **presearch bypass** `ENTIRE_GRAPH_PRESEARCH` / `EG_PRESEARCH` | `env.go:16-24`, `search.go:132-135,286-293` | ~10 | OFF | harness only — **turn-0 delivery channel, undocumented** |\n| **`--deep`** BM25 fusion | `sem/search.go`, `options.Deep` | — | OFF | documented |\n\n**~2,500 LOC of measured, shipped, default-off search capability.** The bottleneck is not invention.\n\n---\n\n## 2. THE 30 RELATIONS — populated? reachable?\n\nCounts: **A** = `entire-graph` repo (Go + vendored C grammars), 36,354 edges. **B** = `graphmark-bench` (Python-heavy, has `pytest.ini` + `tests/`), 89,587 edges.\n\n| relation | A | B | producer | how | agent-reachable |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CALLS | 12,636 | 21,073 | `provider.go:3287` / `callLikeIdentifiers:13821` | **regex `\\b(name)\\s*(?:&lt;…&gt;)?\\(` over stripped text → a per-file NAME SET**, resolved against symtab. Not AST. | search, neighbors, impact, changed |\n| DEFINES | 7,368 | 30,875 | `provider.go:2586` | structural (tree-sitter) | neighbors only |\n| SIMILAR_TO | 3,279 | 5,327 | `similarity.go:160` | MinHash/LSH | search RELATED, **full only** |\n| DATA_FLOWS | 3,009 | 3,218 | `provider.go:3397` (`returnCallRe`) | regex | impact only (0/49 adoption) |\n| USES_TYPE | 2,302 | 641 | `provider.go:9009` | identifier scan of signature | search, neighbors, impact |\n| CONTAINS | 1,868 | 1,152 | `provider.go:2599` | structural | neighbors, `def` |\n| PARAM_TYPE | 1,606 | 410 | `provider.go:9063` | paren-split text parse | neighbors, impact |\n| IMPORTS | 1,100 | 4,513 | `provider.go:2899` | per-lang regex | search, neighbors |\n| READS_FIELD | 997 | 18 | `provider.go:9371` | regex `x.y` | neighbors only |\n| RETURNS_TYPE | 846 | **0** | `provider.go:9063` | text split | neighbors, impact |\n| FILE_CHANGES_WITH | 378 | 461 | `provider.go:9282` | git co-change | impact only |\n| CONFIGURES | 297 | 20,283 | `provider.go:9236` | pattern | search, neighbors |\n| WRITES_FIELD | 209 | 4 | `provider.go:9371` | regex | neighbors only |\n| HANDLES_GRAPHQL | 207 | 111 | `provider.go:3424` | regex/schema | neighbors only |\n| HTTP_CALLS | 70 | **0** | `provider.go:3479` | pattern | neighbors only |\n| HANDLES_ROUTE | 48 | 21 | `provider.go:3450` | route-literal regex | **neighbors only — not in search's RELATED expansion despite being in `fast`** |\n| ACCESSES | 34 | **0** | `provider.go:9371` | regex `&amp;x.y` | neighbors only |\n| CONSTRUCTS | 32 | 1,283 | `provider.go:3281` | same as CALLS, kind-switched | as CALLS |\n| OVERRIDES | 10 | 26 | `provider.go:9420` | exact name-join over EXTENDS/IMPLEMENTS | neighbors, `def` |\n| **TESTS** | **10** | **0** | `provider.go:8900`, rule `types.go:280-297` | **name convention only** (`TestFoo→Foo`, `test_foo→foo`) | search covering-test, neighbors |\n| EXTENDS / INHERITS | 9 / 9 | 71 / 71 | `provider.go:3959-3989` | signature regex | search, neighbors, `def` |\n| IMPLEMENTS | 7 | 2 | `provider.go:3959` | regex | search, neighbors, `def` |\n| HANDLES_TOOL | 7 | 27 | `provider.go:2613` | pattern | neighbors only |\n| RESOURCE_DEPENDS_ON | 6 | **0** | `provider.go:6825/6878/6938/…` | per-format regex | neighbors only |\n| EMITS | 3 | **0** | `provider.go:3507` | regex `.emit\\|.publish\\|…` (carries WEAK_PATTERN) | neighbors only |\n| LISTENS_ON | 2 | **0** | `provider.go:3507,3535` | regex | neighbors only |\n| ASYNC_CALLS | 1 | **0** | `provider.go:3360` | regex await/go/spawn | search, neighbors, impact |\n| HANDLES_GRPC / HANDLES_TRPC | 1 / 1 | 0 / 0 | `provider.go:3424` | proto kind / regex | neighbors only |\n\n**Findings:**\n- **PRODUCER=NONE: none.** All 30 emit. Your premise of a declared-but-dead relation does not hold — the real failure mode is *emitted-and-empty*.\n- **TESTS confirmed dead**: 10/36,354 (0.03%) on Go; **0/89,587 on a Python repo that has a pytest suite** (Python test names are `test_&lt;behaviour&gt;`, which `testSubjectName` cannot map to a symbol). The relation is advertised in `capabilities --json` and delivers nothing.\n- **13 relations are computed and have no consumer but the generic `neighbors --relation X`**, which the agent never calls. Effectively thrown away: READS_FIELD, WRITES_FIELD, ACCESSES, HANDLES_ROUTE, HANDLES_GRPC/GRAPHQL/TRPC, HTTP_CALLS, EMITS, LISTENS_ON, HANDLES_TOOL, RESOURCE_DEPENDS_ON, DEFINES.\n- `neighbors --relation` is **not** whitelisted (`neighbors.go:246-251`, match at `:600-605`) — a typo silently returns zero. `CALLS` also matches `CONSTRUCTS` (only alias).\n- `capabilities.heuristic_relation_types` lists **7** (`provider.go:512`). By the code, **~27 of 30 are text-pattern derived**; only DEFINES/CONTAINS are true AST captures and OVERRIDES is an exact join over heuristic inputs. **CALLS — 35% of all edges — is a regex name-set, not a call-site set.** That is why `callsite.go:14-24` has to re-derive the call line from disk afterwards. An agent told \"feature-detect before you trust\" gets a materially wrong picture.\n- **Corpus reality**: relation counts per language from `capabilities --json` — Ruby **5/30** (CALLS, CONTAINS, DEFINES, IMPORTS, INHERITS), **C 4/30**, C++ 4/30, JS 10, PHP 12, Go 12, Rust 15, Java 16, TS 17. Ruby (39) + C (22) = 61/213 instances where the graph is barely more than a symbol index. The dynamic/typed split understates it: C is the weakest language in the corpus.\n\n---\n\n## 3. THE MAIN ASK — 3–6 capabilities, ranked by (turns removed)/(bytes added)\n\n**Yardstick used.** persist ≈ bytes/4 × turns-remaining ≈ **5 persist-tokens per byte** at 20 turns left. So: a block ≤2.8 KB pays for itself if it removes **one** grep/session; ≤19.6 KB if it removes **one whole-file Read**/session; ≤1.4 KB if it removes **one harness run**/session.\n\n**Measured payload cost** (this repo, `--profile full`, real query): text **10,822 B** = ~2.7k tokens = **~54k persist ≈ 0.55 whole-file Reads.** One default search already costs about what the read it replaces costs. That is the whole context-neutrality result, arithmetically.\n\n**The one structural insight.** The only agent-facing channel that (a) costs ~40 bytes, (b) is *executed* after the first edit, and (c) is executed repeatedly, is the **`VERIFY: ` command string**. It is the sole existing bridge across your dead end #2. Three of the five proposals below ride it, and none is a new verb: the agent does not choose them, it copies a string it was already given.\n\n---\n\n### R1 — example-level VERIFY filter (`~+15 B`) ★ best ratio\n- **Question burned on**: \"run the test\" → agent runs the whole file/suite, gets 40 unrelated failures, spends turns deciding which are its own.\n- **Today**: `search_covertest.go` already picks **exactly one** test method and its line (`searchCoveringTestLimit = 1`), then the command deriver throws the name away for 5 of 8 ecosystems. Granularity audit of `search_verify.go`: Python `-k &lt;name&gt;` ✅ (`:1092`), Go `-run '^Name$'` ✅ (`:866`), Rust ✅ (`:1358-1366`), Java `-Dtest=Class` **class only** (`:909`), Gradle `--tests 'Class'` **class only** (`:957`), **Ruby `bundle exec rspec &lt;file&gt;` file-only** (`:1120`), **PHP `vendor/bin/phpunit &lt;file&gt;` file-only** (`:1054`), **JS `npx jest &lt;file&gt;` file-only** (`:969-971`).\n- **Command/shape**: unchanged line, longer string — `VERIFY: bundle exec rspec spec/foo_spec.rb:412` · `vendor/bin/phpunit --filter testDecodesNull tests/FooTest.php` · `npx jest tests/foo.test.ts -t \"decodes null\"` · `mvn -q -Dtest=FooTest#decodesNull test`.\n- **Why graph not grep**: the covering test is chosen by inbound CALLS/TESTS edge or mirror-stem + mention scoring, not by name match. Grep cannot pick *which* `it` block.\n- **Dead ends avoided**: no new verb; no post-edit call (it's the same string); ~15 bytes; not a ranking change.\n- **Cost/benefit**: +15 B ≈ 75 persist. Targets **Ruby 39 + PHP 32 + JS 23 + TS 8 + Java 31 = 133/213 (62%)** of the corpus. Removes broad-suite runs from the 11.2% harness pot and, more importantly, removes the unrelated-failure noise that starts the investigation spiral.\n\n### R2 — probe the VERIFY command instead of `LookPath` (net **negative** bytes)\n- **Question burned on**: \"my test command failed — is that me or the box?\" Measured loser: `immutable-js-2006` ran `npm ci`×2, `npx jest`×3, wrote 3 throwaway test files across **14 consecutive post-edit turns**.\n- **Today**: runnability = `exec.LookPath` only (`search_verify.go:135-140`, `RunnerMissing`). `npx` exists → `RunnerMissing=false` → command printed → command fails because deps were never installed. The check is testing the wrong thing.\n- **Command/shape**: same, one probe run at search time on the pristine tree, hard-timeout, then either `VERIFY: &lt;cmd&gt;  [probe: runs · 3 tests already fail here — not yours: a, b, c]` or **strip the block entirely** and print nothing.\n- **Dead ends avoided**: not a verb, not post-edit, and it *removes* 196 B in the loser case.\n- **Evidence it is the lever** (harness `eg-q.impl`, rep30, baseline-matched): `VERIFY real` Sonnet 23.0→27.6 turns (**+4.6**, +37.1% USD); `VERIFY runner-absent` 22.3→16.3 (**−6.0**, −11.8%); `NO VERIFY line` 20.9→16.2 (−4.7, −15.3%). An **11.4-turn swing** on the same axis. Today's answer to this was to *silence* the block (`EG_VERIFY_MODE=off`), which also throws away the good case (Haiku `VERIFY real` −15.8%). A probe keeps the good case and kills the bad one.\n- **Honest cost**: makes the provider *execute* something (it never has). Latency, and a real product decision. Bytes: negative.\n\n### R3 — make the VERIFY string BE the adjudicator (`+45 B`)\n- **Question burned on**: \"did I fix it / did I break something / were these already broken?\" Post-last-edit confirmation is **5.8 messages/session**, the largest asymmetric pot (`verify.go:19-33`), and every cheaper-test attempt had transfer efficiency 0.2–0.35 — two thirds of the saving got re-spent on more testing.\n- **Today**: `entire graph verify` is built, correct (delta not state; verdict not evidence; **no raw output ever**; ≤2048 B) — and shipped as **a verb the agent must choose, after the first edit**. Both of your dead ends, simultaneously. It is undocumented in both agent guides.\n- **Command/shape**: `search` records a pre-edit baseline while it is already reading the tree, and prints\n  `VERIFY: entire graph verify --test \"vendor/bin/phpunit --filter testX tests/FooTest.php\" --pre-edit-baseline .entire/verify-baseline.json`\n  → later: `VERDICT: 1 newly passing, 0 newly failing, 3 PRE-EXISTING failures (unchanged). Verification complete.`\n- **Dead ends avoided**: D1 — the agent never selects a verb, it copies the line it was handed. D2 — this **is** the post-edit graph call, disguised as the test run it was going to make anyway. D4 — 45 B at turn 1; each later verdict is capped at 2 KB delivered late (≈3k persist) replacing raw runner output that is routinely 5–50 KB.\n- **Honest risk**: agents rewrite commands. Must degrade to running the bare command and forwarding it if the wrapper ever errors, or it will be abandoned after one failure.\n\n### R4 — TESTS from call-reachability, not from spelling (`0 B`)\n- **Question burned on**: \"which test proves this?\" — and it is the input to R1/R2/R3 and to the COVERING TEST block.\n- **Today**: pure name convention (`types.go:280-297`). **0 edges on a Python repo with a pytest suite.** So on Python/Ruby/JS the covering test is found only by mirror-stem + name-mention fallback, which fails exactly when the test reaches the target through a helper.\n- **Proposal**: emit TESTS where a symbol in a test file reaches the target within **≤2 CALLS hops**, target restricted to the ranked files. Uses edges that already exist (12.6k / 21.1k CALLS on the two trees).\n- **Why graph not grep**: the test never names the target — it calls a factory/builder that calls it. `grep -rn Foo tests/` returns nothing.\n- **Dynamic half**: CALLS is supported for Ruby, PHP, JS, TS, Python — this is one of the few upgrades that lands on the 48%.\n- **Cost**: **zero payload bytes** — it upgrades two existing blocks in place. Index-time cost; precision bounded by the 2-hop cap and by requiring the target be in the ranked set.\n\n### R5 — FILE OUTLINE on by default (`+1,421 B measured`)\n- **Question burned on**: \"what else is in this file / where in it\". Its own measurement (`search_outline.go:9-16`, 79 sessions): **77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload had already named; 35 were immediately followed by a Read of that same file**; those reads land a median **109 lines** from anything printed and **47/53 land inside another symbol the graph already indexes in that file**.\n- **Measured cost, not estimated**: default text 10,822 B → `--file-outline` 12,243 B = **+1,421 B** = ~7.1k persist.\n- **Ratio**: ~0.44 avoided whole-file Reads/session × 98k + ~1 avoided grep × 14k ≈ 57k saved for 7.1k spent ≈ **8×**. Best ratio of anything already built.\n- **Not new** — it is the answer already in the tree, default-off, undocumented. Ship the default.\n\n*(R6, zero-byte housekeeping: `edges --to X --relation CALLS` is the only route to 13 relation types and is the fallback the benchmark harness itself uses (`eg-q.impl:_edges_callers`). `AGENTS.md:72` tells the agent it does not exist. Delete that sentence.)*\n\n---\n\n## 4. DEFAULTS THAT ARE ACTIVELY HARMFUL\n\n1. **`search` defaults to `--profile fast`** (`cli/search.go:1579`) while **both agent guides instruct `--profile full`.** `fast` carries 9/30 relations (`provider.go:462`). RELATED-site expansion is wired for 12 relations (`sem/search.go:3016-3028`); under the default only 4 populate. **TESTS, SIMILAR_TO, DATA_FLOWS, FILE_CHANGES_WITH, and every type relation come back structurally empty** — your suspicion is confirmed at `provider.go:459-464`. `neighbors`/`impact` default to `full` (`neighbors.go:190`, `impact.go:178`), so `search` is the odd one out. Either flip the default or stop shipping blocks that cannot fire under it.\n2. **Complete bodies to rank 5** (`search_enclosure.go:41`, `searchEnclosureHeadRanks = 5`) against the project's own act-rate data (`search_outline.go:22-25`): rank 1 read 62% / edited 54%; rank 2 27%/20%; **rank 3+ 0–11%.** Measured on a real query: `--body-head-ranks` 5→3 = 10,822→6,143 B (**−43%**); 5→2 = 10,822→**2,590 B (−76%)**. Ranks 3–5 pay full persist price for a ≤11% read rate. Honest caveat: net is close (−41k saved vs ~29k expected extra reads), but the saving is certain and the cost is probabilistic.\n3. **`--max-context-bytes 24576` is denominated in bytes, not persist-tokens.** A 24 KB ceiling at turn 1 in a 25-turn session is charged 25×; the same bytes at turn 20 are charged 5×. **The tool's mandated delivery point (turn 1, search-first) is its most expensive possible moment.** The budget should be a function of expected turns remaining, not a constant.\n4. **VERIFY on by default with a PATH-only runner check** — the +4.6-turn / +37.1% Sonnet case above. Shipped as-is.\n5. **`verify` and `changed` are invisible.** `changed` is not in `printHelp` at all (`root.go:113-175`), and neither appears in `AGENTS.md`'s Reference table. `def` — 971 LOC — is in neither agent guide's Reference block.\n6. **`AGENTS.md:72` states a real feature does not exist.** Anti-documentation.\n7. **`capabilities --json` under-declares heuristics 7 vs ~27** (`provider.go:512`), and does not flag CALLS. Doctrine rule 7 (\"feature-detect before you trust\") is being fed a wrong answer.\n8. **TESTS ships in the relation list at 0.03% / 0.00% density.** Advertising it costs nothing in bytes and everything in trust.\n9. **The in-tree binary is stale.** Whatever the benchmark or a user runs is not HEAD.\n\n---\n\n## 5. BLUNT\n\n**No new capability fixes this, and the arithmetic says why.** One default search payload = 10,822 B text ≈ **54k persist-tokens ≈ 0.55 of the whole-file Read it is supposed to replace**. Meanwhile 45.1% of baseline cost is **1,206 small exploration calls** — no single turn-1 payload pre-empts a thousand scattered greps. Context-neutral is not a bug you can out-feature; it is what those two numbers predict.\n\nTwo things follow.\n\n**(a) The delivery point is wrong, not the content.** Bytes delivered at turn 1 are charged N times; the same bytes delivered post-edit are charged 3–6 times — and **97.7% of the excess cost is post-edit** (`changed.go:20-26`). The tool spends its whole budget at the moment it is most expensive and is absent from the phase where the money goes. The only vehicle that reaches that phase without a new verb is the **VERIFY command string**, because it is the one artifact the agent *executes* rather than *chooses*. R1/R2/R3 are all that string. If you will not execute anything, that door is closed and there is no other one.\n\n**(b) You do not have an invention problem.** You have ~2,500 LOC of measured, shipped, default-off search capability, a `verify` verb that correctly targets the single largest cost pot and is documented nowhere, a `changed` verb absent from `--help`, an `edges` filter your own guide denies exists, and a `capabilities` report that under-declares its heuristics by 20 relations. Every one of those was built after a measurement and then not wired up. **The product bottleneck is the last 10 metres — defaults and the agent-facing guide — not the graph.**\n\nIf R1–R3 are refused, the honest recommendation is to stop optimising for tokens: **remove bytes** (default full-profile, bodies to rank 2, strip unrunnable VERIFY, ship FILE OUTLINE) and position entire-graph as a correctness-and-latency tool. It is a good one. It is not, on this corpus and this cost model, a token tool.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>169552</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>51</tool_uses><duration_ms>876981</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"parentUuid":"747816f9-0167-4b24-a902-0d1d119bfaa1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqj9gwZRbP94DpeB1KPw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3271,"cache_read_input_tokens":801788,"output_tokens":2407,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3271,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2407,"cache_read_input_tokens":801788,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3271},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqj9Rzdn4PurTRwPfEU7","type":"assistant","uuid":"84e91bdf-86ae-45e7-939b-ef2d7bd27c55","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:08:04.725Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"84e91bdf-86ae-45e7-939b-ef2d7bd27c55","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqj9gwZRbP94DpeB1KPw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Leak sizing first, since it's small but **arm-asymmetric**:\n\n| exposure | eg sessions | baseline sessions |\n|---|---|---|\n| sibling-checkout references | **2/49** (14 refs) | **0/49** |\n| shared `/tmp` build artifacts | 3/49 | 1/49 |\n\nOnly 2 pairs, but both hits are eg-only — `bat-1892` (12 refs into `bat-3108`, a later revision of the same repo) is the **worst loser at −2.81 pts**. So the leak *cost eg* there rather than helping it. Contained, not systemic, but it needs fencing before the next cell.\n\n---\n\n**On the VM idea — yes, and it's actually better than what we're doing now.** With one correction: you don't need to copy 100 GB. The benchmark data already lives on `graphbench-c`. Your laptop only holds source code.\n\nThe real win is different: **every query I've run this session has gone over an IAP tunnel at 30–60 s per round-trip.** Running Claude Code *on* the VM removes that entirely — the data is local, queries are instant.\n\nConcretely, that setup is:\n\n```\ngcloud compute ssh graphbench-c --tunnel-through-iap\ntmux new -s work          # survives disconnect\nclaude                    # already installed there; ~/.authenv exists\n```\n\nThen you close the laptop whenever you like and reattach with `tmux attach -t work`.\n\n**The one thing that does not transfer is this conversation's context.** A fresh session on the VM starts cold. That's exactly why the plan file and Appendix A matter — they're the handoff. Everything measured is already written down; what would be lost is only the reasoning thread."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3271,"cache_read_input_tokens":801788,"output_tokens":2407,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3271,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2407,"cache_read_input_tokens":801788,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3271},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqj9Rzdn4PurTRwPfEU7","type":"assistant","uuid":"5981305d-90c4-4e4c-8e3a-e9ab8821379b","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:08:12.080Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
