{"parentUuid":"0a0f68b8-a0b7-485e-958e-7c69660a84e2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqjEe2priCMD8ZRWsi4H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the most actionable result of the whole session, and it inverts the framing. Writing the final plan now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11755,"cache_read_input_tokens":805059,"output_tokens":8529,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11755,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8529,"cache_read_input_tokens":805059,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11755},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqjEXG2k4vrgKKL9rrpU","type":"assistant","uuid":"34ec8ab1-44aa-4d1a-ad15-9b74a32c7aa2","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:09:12.316Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"34ec8ab1-44aa-4d1a-ad15-9b74a32c7aa2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqjEe2priCMD8ZRWsi4H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PvhfUvSS6jqZWSK88mkA7D","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","content":"# entire-graph on Opus — the final plan\n\n## Context\n\nThe original goal was **35% token savings on rep50, on Opus, fairly measured**. That is refuted\nand the reasons are in §1. You then relaxed it to the right target: **make the losers behave like\nwinners — a code graph should not make instances worse.** That is what this plan is built against.\n\nThe decisive discovery came last: **this is not an invention problem.** There are ~2,500 LOC of\nmeasured, shipped, **default-off** capability in the tool, a `verify` verb documented nowhere, a\n`changed` verb missing from `--help`, an `edges` filter the shipped guide says does not exist, and\na `capabilities` report that under-declares its own heuristics by ~20 relations. Every one was\nbuilt after a measurement and then never wired up.\n\n**The bottleneck is the last 10 metres — defaults and the agent-facing guide.**\n\nAll numbers: rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs. Sign: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Where Opus actually stands\n\n| estimator | value |\n|---|---|\n| total (the reported headline) | **+1.35%** |\n| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n| median | **−4.16%** |\n| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |\n| t-statistic | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n| n to demonstrate +1.35% | 12,900 pairs ≈ $78k |\n| n to demonstrate 35% | **11 pairs ≈ $88** |\n\n**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. And 35% would have been\nthe cheapest result in the project to prove — it is not provable because it is not there.\n\n**Do not quote +1.35% without the LOO range and the median.**\n\n---\n\n## 2. Why instances lose — three mechanisms, all measured\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances (top five = −11.42, 57%). Lift +21.21 over 24.\n`lombok-3674` alone is +6.09 = 29% of all lift.**\n\n### 2.1 The call is paid for and removes nothing\nLosers: eg shell exploration **413 vs baseline 415** — two calls displaced out of 415.\nWinners: 370 vs 440. One graph call prices at **1.61 messages**, and a regression holding call\ncount fixed charges **+7.0% CI[1.9,13.2]** for merely having called.\n\n### 2.2 ADD tasks get a confident wrong answer\nSearch always returns something. When the task is to *add* behaviour, the top hit is a plausible\nsibling of the answer.\n\n| | pooled |\n|---|---|\n| MOD (fix existing broken code) | **+14.35%** (n=36) |\n| ADD (behaviour does not exist) | **−3.37%** (n=21) |\n\nSame sign **4/4 cells**. Corroborated: gold at rank 2–3 measures **−85.3%**, *worse* than gold not\nfound at all (−25.6%). Forensics confirmed both `ansible-395e` and `prometheus-9248` are ADD, and\n**80% / 64% of their surplus is PRE-edit** — the graph bled where it operates.\n\n### 2.3 The verify-repair spiral, where the tool is absent\n**91 of 94 graph calls are pre-edit; 42/49 sessions never call it again**, yet 97.7% of excess\ncost lands after the first edit. Losers vs baseline: env-failures **+22**, throwaway scripts\n**+16**, post-edit harness **+50**, post-edit exploration **+159**. Winners mirror it exactly\n(−45, −48, −88, −81). `corr(Δharness, saving) = −0.612`; `corr(Δenv-failures) = −0.442`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. The economics that constrain every fix\n\n`cache_read` is **95.5%** of billed tokens. A result injected at turn *i* is re-charged on every\nlater turn: cost ≈ `(bytes/4) × turns-remaining` — **~5 persist-tokens per byte** at 20 turns left.\n\n**One default search payload is 10,822 B ≈ 54k persist ≈ 0.55 of the whole-file Read it replaces.**\nThat single number *is* the context-neutrality result (eg 38.5M vs baseline 38.6M).\n\n| class | baseline share | calls | each |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| exploration | 45.1% | 1,206 | 14k |\n| **whole-file `Read`** | **30.3%** | **119** | **98k (7×)** |\n| harness | 11.2% | 576 | 7k |\n\n**Break-even:** a block ≤2.8 KB pays for itself if it removes one grep/session; ≤19.6 KB if it\nremoves one whole-file Read; ≤1.4 KB if it removes one harness run.\n\n**Corollary: bytes delivered at turn 1 are charged N times.** The tool spends its whole budget at\nits most expensive moment and is absent from the phase where the money goes.\n\n---\n\n## 4. The plan — remove bytes and fix defaults, in this order\n\nEvery item is **tool output, not instruction**, and passes the no-tool-arm test. Ranked by\n(turns removed) / (bytes added). **Items 4.1–4.4 all reduce or barely move payload size** — the\nfirst proposals in this project with a positive byte ratio.\n\n### 4.1 Fix `graph grep`: exclude vendored / minified / generated files *(NEGATIVE bytes)*\n`internal/cli` grep path shells out to `grep -rInE` over the whole worktree and filters **only\ntests**. On `prometheus-9248` it returned one hit inside minified vendored `d3.v3.js` where plain\ngrep returned a **clean zero** — and a clean zero is *actionable* (\"pivot\"), one noise hit is not.\nBaseline pivoted to the issue's error string at call 2 and found `scalarBinop`; eg reached it at\ncalls 21–22. **~19 turns of delay, caused by the tool's opening answer.**\n\nThis is the only place measured where the graph is **demonstrably worse than no tool at all**, and\nthe fix removes bytes.\n\n### 4.2 Ship FILE OUTLINE by default *(+1,421 B, ~8× return — best ratio of anything built)*\n`internal/sem/search_outline.go` (217 LOC), flag `internal/cli/search.go:1637`. **Default OFF,\nabsent from `printHelp`.** Its own measurement: **77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload\nhad already named; 35 were immediately followed by a Read of that same file**, landing a median\n109 lines from anything printed. Measured cost +1,421 B ≈ 7.1k persist against ~57k saved.\n\n### 4.3 Cut complete bodies from rank 5 to rank 2 *(−76% payload bytes)*\n`search_enclosure.go:41` (`searchEnclosureHeadRanks = 5`). Act-rate data in `search_outline.go:22`:\nrank 1 read 62% / edited 54%; rank 2 27%/20%; **rank 3+ 0–11%.** Measured: `--body-head-ranks`\n5→3 = 10,822→6,143 B; **5→2 = 10,822→2,590 B (−76%)**. Ranks 3–5 pay full persist for a ≤11% read\nrate. Net is close (−41k certain saving vs ~29k probabilistic extra reads) but the saving is the\ncertain half.\n\n### 4.4 Probe the VERIFY command instead of `LookPath` *(NEGATIVE bytes)*\n`internal/sem/search_verify.go:135` checks only that the runner *binary exists* — `npx` exists,\nso the command prints, then fails because deps were never installed. Replace with a collect-only\nprobe on the pristine tree (`pytest --collect-only -q`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`,\n`cargo test --no-run`, `phpunit --list-tests`, `rspec --dry-run`); on failure **strip the block**.\n\nMeasured swing on this exact axis (rep30, baseline-matched): `VERIFY real` **+4.6 turns / +37.1%\nUSD**; `VERIFY runner-absent` **−6.0 turns / −11.8%**; no VERIFY line −4.7 turns. **An 11.4-turn\nswing.** The previous response was to silence VERIFY entirely, which also discarded the good case.\nA probe keeps the good case and kills the bad one.\n\n**Note:** this makes the provider *execute* something for the first time. That is a real product\ndecision — latency, and a category change — and it should be taken deliberately.\n\n### 4.5 Example-level VERIFY granularity *(+15 B, reaches 62% of the corpus)*\n`search_covertest.go` already selects **exactly one** test method and its line, then the deriver\nthrows the name away for 5 of 8 ecosystems: Ruby, PHP, JS file-only; Java/Gradle class-only.\nPython (`-k`), Go (`-run '^Name$'`) and Rust already do it right. Fix: emit\n`rspec spec/foo_spec.rb:412`, `phpunit --filter testX`, `jest -t \"…\"`, `mvn -Dtest=Class#method`.\nTargets Ruby 39 + PHP 32 + JS 23 + TS 8 + Java 31 = **133/213 instances**.\n\n### 4.6 Ship R-A zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, deployed as `b669a57b`)*\n`EG_PREFETCH=1` injected the payload at turn 0 and still let the agent re-derive it at full price.\n`EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual call an echo — 0.02 s vs 5.21 s, byte-identical.\nCounterfactual on this cell **+4.3% to +6.0%** (CI spans zero at n=49).\n\n### 4.7 Documentation and defaults that are simply wrong *(zero bytes)*\n- `search` defaults to `--profile fast` (**9/30 relations**) while both agent guides mandate `full`.\n  Under the default, TESTS, SIMILAR_TO, DATA_FLOWS, FILE_CHANGES_WITH and every type relation are\n  **structurally empty**, so blocks depending on them cannot fire. `neighbors`/`impact` default to\n  `full`; `search` is the odd one out.\n- `AGENTS.md:72` states `edges --to/--from/--relation` **does not exist**. It does\n  (`root.go:576-594`) — and it is the only route to 13 relation types. Delete that sentence.\n- `capabilities --json` declares **7** heuristic relations; by the code **~27 of 30** are\n  text-pattern derived, including **CALLS (35% of all edges), which is a regex name-set, not an\n  AST call-site set.** Doctrine rule 7 says \"feature-detect before you trust\" — it is being fed a\n  wrong answer.\n- `TESTS` ships in the relation list at **10 edges of 36,354 on Go and 0 of 89,587 on a Python repo\n  that has a pytest suite.** Either fix it (§4.8) or stop advertising it.\n- `verify` and `changed` are in neither agent guide; `changed` is absent from `printHelp`.\n- **The in-tree binary is stale vs source** — it rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`.\n  Rebuild before anything ships.\n\n### 4.8 TESTS from call-reachability rather than spelling *(zero payload bytes)*\n`types.go:280-297` maps `TestFoo→Foo` by name only. Emit TESTS where a symbol in a test file\nreaches the target within **≤2 CALLS hops**, restricted to ranked files. Uses edges that already\nexist (12.6k–21.1k CALLS). CALLS is supported for Ruby/PHP/JS/TS/Python, so this is one of the few\nupgrades that lands on the dynamic ~48% of the corpus. It is also the input to §4.4 and §4.5.\n\n### 4.9 DO NOT BUILD\n- **Post-edit consistency hook.** Stress-tested and rejected: its fair (symmetric) form's biggest\n  beneficiary is the **baseline in `lombok-3674`**, i.e. it eats 29% of the lift. Cost −2% to −6%.\n- Any new verb in the affordance tail — **0/66 adoption** measured.\n- Anything requiring an agent-initiated post-edit call — 42/49 sessions make none.\n- Better ranking; bigger payloads; graph-backed grep; the 12 dead payload metrics.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Integrity fixes — before any cell\n\n1. **Sibling-checkout answer leak.** `bat-1892` (the worst loser, −2.81 pts) made **12 references\n   into `bat-3108`, a later revision of the same repo containing the implemented feature.**\n   Measured exposure: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline** — small but **arm-asymmetric**. Fence\n   checkouts so a session cannot read a sibling instance's tree.\n2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells.** `prometheus-9248` found `/tmp/goyacc*` built by\n   *other instances'* sessions and spent 2 calls auditing foreign binaries. eg 3/49, base 1/49.\n   Give each session a private temp root.\n3. **Junk-patch gate.** One baseline patch was 371,308 B of vendor/build output and passed as\n   success. Add a symmetric size/content bound.\n4. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.\n   Fix before any payload forensics.\n5. **0-byte `cc_out.json`** — guard shipped; the sweep removed **90 corpses** across all cells.\n\n**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, **0 commit mismatches**, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches\nsmall, prompt diff is 18 lines all of which are checkout paths.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gates — mechanism counts, winners protected\n\nMDE is ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between\ncells. **No token claim below n≈50, in either direction.**\n\n| gate | n | criterion |\n|---|---|---|\n| **V0** offline, $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; grep excludes vendored/minified on the prometheus query and returns a clean zero; outline/body-rank byte deltas reproduce (10,822 → 2,590 B) |\n| **V1** replay, $0 | 49 | on recorded loser sessions, the probed VERIFY command would have run where the emitted one failed; ≥50% of the 22 env-failures avoided |\n| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: payload bytes/session **down**, env-failures/session **down**, no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |\n| **V3** live | 50 | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together** |\n\n**Winner-protection tripwire (per your instruction, abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,\n`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` are in every sample from V2 on. If any regresses >10pt versus a\n**same-wave** control, revert. Never compare against a previous cell — the noise floor forbids it.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Honest expected outcome\n\n| item | effect | confidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4.1 grep vendor filter | removes a ~19-turn failure mode on ADD tasks | high — mechanism observed |\n| 4.2 FILE OUTLINE default | ~8× return on 1,421 B | high — own measurement |\n| 4.3 bodies rank 5→2 | −76% payload bytes | high on cost, medium on net |\n| 4.4 VERIFY probe | up to 11.4-turn swing on that axis | medium |\n| 4.5 VERIFY granularity | 133/213 instances | medium |\n| 4.6 R-A zero-toll | +4.3% to +6.0% | medium, CI spans zero |\n\n**Combined, realistically: high single digits to low teens, with the drag pool shrinking rather\nthan the lift pool growing.** The ceiling on loser repair is exactly **+21.21%** (the lift pool) —\narithmetic, not projection.\n\n**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change.** The one intervention that would reach it is\nan instruction telling the agent to explore and re-test less — which helps a no-tool arm equally\nand is precisely what the withdrawn −35% contained.\n\n**If §4.4 (executing a probe) is refused,** the honest recommendation is to stop optimising tokens\nhere: remove bytes (4.1–4.3, 4.7), and position entire-graph on correctness and latency, where it\nis demonstrably good. It is not, on this corpus and this cost model, a token tool.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Verification\n\n- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO needed).\n  **Rebuild the in-tree binary — it is stale.** Add unit tests beside `search_verify.go` and the\n  grep filter.\n- Offline replay: recorded queries at `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log`, payloads at the same\n  path + `.payload`. Re-run against the binary at zero model cost; assert both that the change\n  fires and that nothing else moved.\n- Harness deploys to VMs by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a\n  script a running session is reading.\n- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** trimmed **and** LOO **and** Δturns **and**\n  env-failure counts.\n\n---\n\n# APPENDIX A — Subagent findings log\n\n## A1 — Post-edit hook stress test — **REJECTED**\nFair (symmetric) form's biggest beneficiary is the baseline in `lombok-3674` = 29% of all lift;\ncost −2% to −6%; ~48% of corpus is dynamically typed where arity checks are unreliable.\nAlso surfaced: `claude --settings '<json>' --setting-sources ''` avoids writing\n`.claude/settings.json` into the worktree, removing the patch-pollution blocker.\n\n## A2 — Loser forensics: `bat-1892`, `valkey-790` — **graph INNOCENT**\nPayload was correct in both; top hit was the exact function to edit; eg used *fewer* localization\ncalls than baseline (10 vs 15; 15 vs 17). Losses were environment, answer-leak and a hung pty test.\n`valkey`: ~13–15 pre-edit calls were graph-shaped (test invocation, tcl `proc` sites — **no `.tcl`\nsymbols are indexed**).\n\n## A3 — Loser forensics: `ansible-395e`, `prometheus-9248` — **graph GUILTY on prometheus**\nBoth ADD tasks; 80%/64% of surplus is PRE-edit. `graph grep` returned a minified-vendor false\npositive where plain grep returned a clean zero → ~19 turns of delay. `ansible` innocent\n(environment). **`EG_LITERALS` — the error-string→symbol index that would have collapsed\nprometheus's delay — is built and was switched OFF in this cell.**\n\n## A4 — Capability inventory — **the decisive result**\n~2,500 LOC shipped default-off; `verify`/`changed`/`def` undocumented; `AGENTS.md:72` denies a\nreal feature; `capabilities` under-declares heuristics 7 vs ~27; **CALLS is a regex name-set, not\nAST**; TESTS 10/36,354 on Go and **0/89,587 on a Python repo with pytest**; Ruby 5/30 relations,\nC 4/30 (61/213 instances where the graph is barely a symbol index).\n\n## A5 — Claims I made and then RETRACTED\n- \"eg verifies more than baseline\" — **false**, eg 545 vs base 576. Came from the 8 worst losers,\n  a set selected on the outcome.\n- \"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\" — **regex artifact**; stricter definition gives n=17 and\n  **−0.89%**.\n- \"the metric rewards failing to provision\" — real on `bat-1892`, but only **2/25 losers**, worth\n  −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.\n- \"+35.06% is reachable by loser repair\" — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.\n- ×0.54 persist calibration — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**\n  (corr +0.916, R² 0.839).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11755,"cache_read_input_tokens":805059,"output_tokens":8529,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11755,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8529,"cache_read_input_tokens":805059,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11755},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqjEXG2k4vrgKKL9rrpU","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0e86ac8-af36-4913-9b0a-e1f9a4f7bb78","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:10:40.362Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"f0e86ac8-af36-4913-9b0a-e1f9a4f7bb78","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b7965a18-5291-4d2a-a1dc-1c15a7c60369","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PvhfUvSS6jqZWSK88mkA7D","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"fb621ef7-8d26-47f0-922e-1467ab4e6de0","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:10:40.426Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","content":"# entire-graph on Opus — the final plan\n\n## Context\n\nThe original goal was **35% token savings on rep50, on Opus, fairly measured**. That is refuted\nand the reasons are in §1. You then relaxed it to the right target: **make the losers behave like\nwinners — a code graph should not make instances worse.** That is what this plan is built against.\n\nThe decisive discovery came last: **this is not an invention problem.** There are ~2,500 LOC of\nmeasured, shipped, **default-off** capability in the tool, a `verify` verb documented nowhere, a\n`changed` verb missing from `--help`, an `edges` filter the shipped guide says does not exist, and\na `capabilities` report that under-declares its own heuristics by ~20 relations. Every one was\nbuilt after a measurement and then never wired up.\n\n**The bottleneck is the last 10 metres — defaults and the agent-facing guide.**\n\nAll numbers: rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs. Sign: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Where Opus actually stands\n\n| estimator | value |\n|---|---|\n| total (the reported headline) | **+1.35%** |\n| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n| median | **−4.16%** |\n| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |\n| t-statistic | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n| n to demonstrate +1.35% | 12,900 pairs ≈ $78k |\n| n to demonstrate 35% | **11 pairs ≈ $88** |\n\n**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. And 35% would have been\nthe cheapest result in the project to prove — it is not provable because it is not there.\n\n**Do not quote +1.35% without the LOO range and the median.**\n\n---\n\n## 2. Why instances lose — three mechanisms, all measured\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances (top five = −11.42, 57%). Lift +21.21 over 24.\n`lombok-3674` alone is +6.09 = 29% of all lift.**\n\n### 2.1 The call is paid for and removes nothing\nLosers: eg shell exploration **413 vs baseline 415** — two calls displaced out of 415.\nWinners: 370 vs 440. One graph call prices at **1.61 messages**, and a regression holding call\ncount fixed charges **+7.0% CI[1.9,13.2]** for merely having called.\n\n### 2.2 ADD tasks get a confident wrong answer\nSearch always returns something. When the task is to *add* behaviour, the top hit is a plausible\nsibling of the answer.\n\n| | pooled |\n|---|---|\n| MOD (fix existing broken code) | **+14.35%** (n=36) |\n| ADD (behaviour does not exist) | **−3.37%** (n=21) |\n\nSame sign **4/4 cells**. Corroborated: gold at rank 2–3 measures **−85.3%**, *worse* than gold not\nfound at all (−25.6%). Forensics confirmed both `ansible-395e` and `prometheus-9248` are ADD, and\n**80% / 64% of their surplus is PRE-edit** — the graph bled where it operates.\n\n### 2.3 The verify-repair spiral, where the tool is absent\n**91 of 94 graph calls are pre-edit; 42/49 sessions never call it again**, yet 97.7% of excess\ncost lands after the first edit. Losers vs baseline: env-failures **+22**, throwaway scripts\n**+16**, post-edit harness **+50**, post-edit exploration **+159**. Winners mirror it exactly\n(−45, −48, −88, −81). `corr(Δharness, saving) = −0.612`; `corr(Δenv-failures) = −0.442`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. The economics that constrain every fix\n\n`cache_read` is **95.5%** of billed tokens. A result injected at turn *i* is re-charged on every\nlater turn: cost ≈ `(bytes/4) × turns-remaining` — **~5 persist-tokens per byte** at 20 turns left.\n\n**One default search payload is 10,822 B ≈ 54k persist ≈ 0.55 of the whole-file Read it replaces.**\nThat single number *is* the context-neutrality result (eg 38.5M vs baseline 38.6M).\n\n| class | baseline share | calls | each |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| exploration | 45.1% | 1,206 | 14k |\n| **whole-file `Read`** | **30.3%** | **119** | **98k (7×)** |\n| harness | 11.2% | 576 | 7k |\n\n**Break-even:** a block ≤2.8 KB pays for itself if it removes one grep/session; ≤19.6 KB if it\nremoves one whole-file Read; ≤1.4 KB if it removes one harness run.\n\n**Corollary: bytes delivered at turn 1 are charged N times.** The tool spends its whole budget at\nits most expensive moment and is absent from the phase where the money goes.\n\n---\n\n## 4. The plan — remove bytes and fix defaults, in this order\n\nEvery item is **tool output, not instruction**, and passes the no-tool-arm test. Ranked by\n(turns removed) / (bytes added). **Items 4.1–4.4 all reduce or barely move payload size** — the\nfirst proposals in this project with a positive byte ratio.\n\n### 4.1 Fix `graph grep`: exclude vendored / minified / generated files *(NEGATIVE bytes)*\n`internal/cli` grep path shells out to `grep -rInE` over the whole worktree and filters **only\ntests**. On `prometheus-9248` it returned one hit inside minified vendored `d3.v3.js` where plain\ngrep returned a **clean zero** — and a clean zero is *actionable* (\"pivot\"), one noise hit is not.\nBaseline pivoted to the issue's error string at call 2 and found `scalarBinop`; eg reached it at\ncalls 21–22. **~19 turns of delay, caused by the tool's opening answer.**\n\nThis is the only place measured where the graph is **demonstrably worse than no tool at all**, and\nthe fix removes bytes.\n\n### 4.2 Ship FILE OUTLINE by default *(+1,421 B, ~8× return — best ratio of anything built)*\n`internal/sem/search_outline.go` (217 LOC), flag `internal/cli/search.go:1637`. **Default OFF,\nabsent from `printHelp`.** Its own measurement: **77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload\nhad already named; 35 were immediately followed by a Read of that same file**, landing a median\n109 lines from anything printed. Measured cost +1,421 B ≈ 7.1k persist against ~57k saved.\n\n### 4.3 Cut complete bodies from rank 5 to rank 2 *(−76% payload bytes)*\n`search_enclosure.go:41` (`searchEnclosureHeadRanks = 5`). Act-rate data in `search_outline.go:22`:\nrank 1 read 62% / edited 54%; rank 2 27%/20%; **rank 3+ 0–11%.** Measured: `--body-head-ranks`\n5→3 = 10,822→6,143 B; **5→2 = 10,822→2,590 B (−76%)**. Ranks 3–5 pay full persist for a ≤11% read\nrate. Net is close (−41k certain saving vs ~29k probabilistic extra reads) but the saving is the\ncertain half.\n\n### 4.4 Probe the VERIFY command instead of `LookPath` *(NEGATIVE bytes)*\n`internal/sem/search_verify.go:135` checks only that the runner *binary exists* — `npx` exists,\nso the command prints, then fails because deps were never installed. Replace with a collect-only\nprobe on the pristine tree (`pytest --collect-only -q`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`,\n`cargo test --no-run`, `phpunit --list-tests`, `rspec --dry-run`); on failure **strip the block**.\n\nMeasured swing on this exact axis (rep30, baseline-matched): `VERIFY real` **+4.6 turns / +37.1%\nUSD**; `VERIFY runner-absent` **−6.0 turns / −11.8%**; no VERIFY line −4.7 turns. **An 11.4-turn\nswing.** The previous response was to silence VERIFY entirely, which also discarded the good case.\nA probe keeps the good case and kills the bad one.\n\n**Note:** this makes the provider *execute* something for the first time. That is a real product\ndecision — latency, and a category change — and it should be taken deliberately.\n\n### 4.5 Example-level VERIFY granularity *(+15 B, reaches 62% of the corpus)*\n`search_covertest.go` already selects **exactly one** test method and its line, then the deriver\nthrows the name away for 5 of 8 ecosystems: Ruby, PHP, JS file-only; Java/Gradle class-only.\nPython (`-k`), Go (`-run '^Name$'`) and Rust already do it right. Fix: emit\n`rspec spec/foo_spec.rb:412`, `phpunit --filter testX`, `jest -t \"…\"`, `mvn -Dtest=Class#method`.\nTargets Ruby 39 + PHP 32 + JS 23 + TS 8 + Java 31 = **133/213 instances**.\n\n### 4.6 Ship R-A zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, deployed as `b669a57b`)*\n`EG_PREFETCH=1` injected the payload at turn 0 and still let the agent re-derive it at full price.\n`EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual call an echo — 0.02 s vs 5.21 s, byte-identical.\nCounterfactual on this cell **+4.3% to +6.0%** (CI spans zero at n=49).\n\n### 4.7 Documentation and defaults that are simply wrong *(zero bytes)*\n- `search` defaults to `--profile fast` (**9/30 relations**) while both agent guides mandate `full`.\n  Under the default, TESTS, SIMILAR_TO, DATA_FLOWS, FILE_CHANGES_WITH and every type relation are\n  **structurally empty**, so blocks depending on them cannot fire. `neighbors`/`impact` default to\n  `full`; `search` is the odd one out.\n- `AGENTS.md:72` states `edges --to/--from/--relation` **does not exist**. It does\n  (`root.go:576-594`) — and it is the only route to 13 relation types. Delete that sentence.\n- `capabilities --json` declares **7** heuristic relations; by the code **~27 of 30** are\n  text-pattern derived, including **CALLS (35% of all edges), which is a regex name-set, not an\n  AST call-site set.** Doctrine rule 7 says \"feature-detect before you trust\" — it is being fed a\n  wrong answer.\n- `TESTS` ships in the relation list at **10 edges of 36,354 on Go and 0 of 89,587 on a Python repo\n  that has a pytest suite.** Either fix it (§4.8) or stop advertising it.\n- `verify` and `changed` are in neither agent guide; `changed` is absent from `printHelp`.\n- **The in-tree binary is stale vs source** — it rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`.\n  Rebuild before anything ships.\n\n### 4.8 TESTS from call-reachability rather than spelling *(zero payload bytes)*\n`types.go:280-297` maps `TestFoo→Foo` by name only. Emit TESTS where a symbol in a test file\nreaches the target within **≤2 CALLS hops**, restricted to ranked files. Uses edges that already\nexist (12.6k–21.1k CALLS). CALLS is supported for Ruby/PHP/JS/TS/Python, so this is one of the few\nupgrades that lands on the dynamic ~48% of the corpus. It is also the input to §4.4 and §4.5.\n\n### 4.9 DO NOT BUILD\n- **Post-edit consistency hook.** Stress-tested and rejected: its fair (symmetric) form's biggest\n  beneficiary is the **baseline in `lombok-3674`**, i.e. it eats 29% of the lift. Cost −2% to −6%.\n- Any new verb in the affordance tail — **0/66 adoption** measured.\n- Anything requiring an agent-initiated post-edit call — 42/49 sessions make none.\n- Better ranking; bigger payloads; graph-backed grep; the 12 dead payload metrics.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Integrity fixes — before any cell\n\n1. **Sibling-checkout answer leak.** `bat-1892` (the worst loser, −2.81 pts) made **12 references\n   into `bat-3108`, a later revision of the same repo containing the implemented feature.**\n   Measured exposure: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline** — small but **arm-asymmetric**. Fence\n   checkouts so a session cannot read a sibling instance's tree.\n2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells.** `prometheus-9248` found `/tmp/goyacc*` built by\n   *other instances'* sessions and spent 2 calls auditing foreign binaries. eg 3/49, base 1/49.\n   Give each session a private temp root.\n3. **Junk-patch gate.** One baseline patch was 371,308 B of vendor/build output and passed as\n   success. Add a symmetric size/content bound.\n4. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.\n   Fix before any payload forensics.\n5. **0-byte `cc_out.json`** — guard shipped; the sweep removed **90 corpses** across all cells.\n\n**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, **0 commit mismatches**, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches\nsmall, prompt diff is 18 lines all of which are checkout paths.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gates — mechanism counts, winners protected\n\nMDE is ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between\ncells. **No token claim below n≈50, in either direction.**\n\n| gate | n | criterion |\n|---|---|---|\n| **V0** offline, $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; grep excludes vendored/minified on the prometheus query and returns a clean zero; outline/body-rank byte deltas reproduce (10,822 → 2,590 B) |\n| **V1** replay, $0 | 49 | on recorded loser sessions, the probed VERIFY command would have run where the emitted one failed; ≥50% of the 22 env-failures avoided |\n| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: payload bytes/session **down**, env-failures/session **down**, no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |\n| **V3** live | 50 | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together** |\n\n**Winner-protection tripwire (per your instruction, abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,\n`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` are in every sample from V2 on. If any regresses >10pt versus a\n**same-wave** control, revert. Never compare against a previous cell — the noise floor forbids it.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Honest expected outcome\n\n| item | effect | confidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4.1 grep vendor filter | removes a ~19-turn failure mode on ADD tasks | high — mechanism observed |\n| 4.2 FILE OUTLINE default | ~8× return on 1,421 B | high — own measurement |\n| 4.3 bodies rank 5→2 | −76% payload bytes | high on cost, medium on net |\n| 4.4 VERIFY probe | up to 11.4-turn swing on that axis | medium |\n| 4.5 VERIFY granularity | 133/213 instances | medium |\n| 4.6 R-A zero-toll | +4.3% to +6.0% | medium, CI spans zero |\n\n**Combined, realistically: high single digits to low teens, with the drag pool shrinking rather\nthan the lift pool growing.** The ceiling on loser repair is exactly **+21.21%** (the lift pool) —\narithmetic, not projection.\n\n**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change.** The one intervention that would reach it is\nan instruction telling the agent to explore and re-test less — which helps a no-tool arm equally\nand is precisely what the withdrawn −35% contained.\n\n**If §4.4 (executing a probe) is refused,** the honest recommendation is to stop optimising tokens\nhere: remove bytes (4.1–4.3, 4.7), and position entire-graph on correctness and latency, where it\nis demonstrably good. It is not, on this corpus and this cost model, a token tool.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Verification\n\n- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO needed).\n  **Rebuild the in-tree binary — it is stale.** Add unit tests beside `search_verify.go` and the\n  grep filter.\n- Offline replay: recorded queries at `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log`, payloads at the same\n  path + `.payload`. Re-run against the binary at zero model cost; assert both that the change\n  fires and that nothing else moved.\n- Harness deploys to VMs by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a\n  script a running session is reading.\n- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** trimmed **and** LOO **and** Δturns **and**\n  env-failure counts.\n\n---\n\n# APPENDIX A — Subagent findings log\n\n## A1 — Post-edit hook stress test — **REJECTED**\nFair (symmetric) form's biggest beneficiary is the baseline in `lombok-3674` = 29% of all lift;\ncost −2% to −6%; ~48% of corpus is dynamically typed where arity checks are unreliable.\nAlso surfaced: `claude --settings '<json>' --setting-sources ''` avoids writing\n`.claude/settings.json` into the worktree, removing the patch-pollution blocker.\n\n## A2 — Loser forensics: `bat-1892`, `valkey-790` — **graph INNOCENT**\nPayload was correct in both; top hit was the exact function to edit; eg used *fewer* localization\ncalls than baseline (10 vs 15; 15 vs 17). Losses were environment, answer-leak and a hung pty test.\n`valkey`: ~13–15 pre-edit calls were graph-shaped (test invocation, tcl `proc` sites — **no `.tcl`\nsymbols are indexed**).\n\n## A3 — Loser forensics: `ansible-395e`, `prometheus-9248` — **graph GUILTY on prometheus**\nBoth ADD tasks; 80%/64% of surplus is PRE-edit. `graph grep` returned a minified-vendor false\npositive where plain grep returned a clean zero → ~19 turns of delay. `ansible` innocent\n(environment). **`EG_LITERALS` — the error-string→symbol index that would have collapsed\nprometheus's delay — is built and was switched OFF in this cell.**\n\n## A4 — Capability inventory — **the decisive result**\n~2,500 LOC shipped default-off; `verify`/`changed`/`def` undocumented; `AGENTS.md:72` denies a\nreal feature; `capabilities` under-declares heuristics 7 vs ~27; **CALLS is a regex name-set, not\nAST**; TESTS 10/36,354 on Go and **0/89,587 on a Python repo with pytest**; Ruby 5/30 relations,\nC 4/30 (61/213 instances where the graph is barely a symbol index).\n\n## A5 — Claims I made and then RETRACTED\n- \"eg verifies more than baseline\" — **false**, eg 545 vs base 576. Came from the 8 worst losers,\n  a set selected on the outcome.\n- \"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\" — **regex artifact**; stricter definition gives n=17 and\n  **−0.89%**.\n- \"the metric rewards failing to provision\" — real on `bat-1892`, but only **2/25 losers**, worth\n  −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.\n- \"+35.06% is reachable by loser repair\" — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.\n- ×0.54 persist calibration — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**\n  (corr +0.916, R² 0.839).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":284,"newStart":1,"newLines":293,"lines":["-# entire-graph on Opus — what the data says, and the only plan that survives it","+# entire-graph on Opus — the final plan"," "," ## Context"," ","-The goal set for this work is **35% token savings on rep50, fairly measured, on Opus**. This plan","-exists because that target is now refuted by the data, and continuing to aim at it would mean","-either fabricating it or measuring something else and calling it that. What follows is the","-evidence, the loser/winner analysis requested, and the plan that is actually supported.","+The original goal was **35% token savings on rep50, on Opus, fairly measured**. That is refuted","+and the reasons are in §1. You then relaxed it to the right target: **make the losers behave like","+winners — a code graph should not make instances worse.** That is what this plan is built against."," ","-All numbers: rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs, SWE-bench Multilingual.","-Sign convention: **positive = the graph arm saved tokens.**","+The decisive discovery came last: **this is not an invention problem.** There are ~2,500 LOC of","+measured, shipped, **default-off** capability in the tool, a `verify` verb documented nowhere, a","+`changed` verb missing from `--help`, an `edges` filter the shipped guide says does not exist, and","+a `capabilities` report that under-declares its own heuristics by ~20 relations. Every one was","+built after a measurement and then never wired up."," ","+**The bottleneck is the last 10 metres — defaults and the agent-facing guide.**","+","+All numbers: rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs. Sign: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.**","+"," ---"," "," ## 1. Where Opus actually stands"," ","-| | value |","+| estimator | value |"," |---|---|","-| headline | **+1.35%** |","+| total (the reported headline) | **+1.35%** |","+| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |","+| median | **−4.16%** |","+| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |"," | t-statistic | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |","-| median | −4.2% |","-| wins | 24 / 49 |","-| paired sd (log-ratio) | 0.494 |","-| n to *demonstrate* +1.35% | **12,900 pairs ≈ $78,491** |","-| n to demonstrate +6% | 499 pairs ≈ $3,972 |","+| n to demonstrate +1.35% | 12,900 pairs ≈ $78k |"," | n to demonstrate 35% | **11 pairs ≈ $88** |"," ","-**35% would have been the cheapest result in the project to prove.** It is not provable because","-it is not there. Every robust estimator drives the headline to zero or below — winsorised 20/80","-**−0.26%**, dropping the 3 most extreme pairs **−6.19%** — so the positive sign is tail-carried.","+**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. And 35% would have been","+the cheapest result in the project to prove — it is not provable because it is not there."," ","+**Do not quote +1.35% without the LOO range and the median.**","+"," ---"," ","-## 2. Loser analysis (requested)","+## 2. Why instances lose — three mechanisms, all measured"," ","-**Drag −19.86 pts across 25 instances; top five carry −11.42 (57%).**","+**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances (top five = −11.42, 57%). Lift +21.21 over 24.","+`lombok-3674` alone is +6.09 = 29% of all lift.**"," ","-Group sums, eg minus baseline:","+### 2.1 The call is paid for and removes nothing","+Losers: eg shell exploration **413 vs baseline 415** — two calls displaced out of 415.","+Winners: 370 vs 440. One graph call prices at **1.61 messages**, and a regression holding call","+count fixed charges **+7.0% CI[1.9,13.2]** for merely having called."," ","-| | losers (25) | winners (24) |","-|---|---|---|","-| turns | **+296** | −258 |","-| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |","-| post-edit exploration | **+159** | −81 |","-| post-edit harness | **+50** | −88 |","-| edits | +42 | −25 |","-| graph calls | 44 (43 pre) | 50 (48 pre) |","+### 2.2 ADD tasks get a confident wrong answer","+Search always returns something. When the task is to *add* behaviour, the top hit is a plausible","+sibling of the answer."," ","-**The single most important line is pre-edit exploration: the graph works in BOTH groups","-(−46 / −58).** Localization is not what separates them. The entire divergence is post-edit, where","-**91 of 94 graph calls never happen** — 42/49 sessions make no graph call after their first edit.","-","-Worst five, with the pattern visible per-instance:","-","-| instance | pts | tok | eg/base turns | eg/base expl | eg/base harness |","-|---|---|---|---|---|---|","-| `bat-1892` | −2.81 | −79.8% | 100/65 | 44/18 | 23/14 |","-| `valkey-790` | −2.72 | −127.4% | 93/54 | 57/34 | 20/11 |","-| `ansible-395e` | −2.58 | −68.1% | 116/91 | 48/38 | 9/5 |","-| `prometheus-9248` | −1.68 | −74.6% | 110/68 | 68/38 | 9/8 |","-| `tokio-4867` | −1.63 | −114.4% | 69/38 | 26/10 | 25/17 |","-","-**Correlates with token saving, ranked:**","-","-| | r |","+| | pooled |"," |---|---|","-| Δ harness runs | **−0.612** |","-| Δ exploration eliminated | +0.485 |","-| Δ repeat edits to same file | −0.457 |","-| Δ edit calls | −0.449 |","-| **Δ harness ENV failures** | **−0.442** |","-| Δ throwaway scripts run | −0.350 |","-| Δ first-edit turn | −0.342 |","+| MOD (fix existing broken code) | **+14.35%** (n=36) |","+| ADD (behaviour does not exist) | **−3.37%** (n=21) |"," ","-**Mechanism:** losers run verification that fails on the *environment* rather than the patch","-(eg 102 vs base 80 in the loser group), then improvise throwaway harnesses (+16) and re-explore","-to repair them (+159 post-edit exploration). Winners show the exact mirror: **−45 env failures,","-−48 throwaway scripts, −88 harness runs**. This is the ledger's §1.3 lever, independently","-reproduced here.","+Same sign **4/4 cells**. Corroborated: gold at rank 2–3 measures **−85.3%**, *worse* than gold not","+found at all (−25.6%). Forensics confirmed both `ansible-395e` and `prometheus-9248` are ADD, and","+**80% / 64% of their surplus is PRE-edit** — the graph bled where it operates."," ","+### 2.3 The verify-repair spiral, where the tool is absent","+**91 of 94 graph calls are pre-edit; 42/49 sessions never call it again**, yet 97.7% of excess","+cost lands after the first edit. Losers vs baseline: env-failures **+22**, throwaway scripts","+**+16**, post-edit harness **+50**, post-edit exploration **+159**. Winners mirror it exactly","+(−45, −48, −88, −81). `corr(Δharness, saving) = −0.612`; `corr(Δenv-failures) = −0.442`.","+"," ---"," ","-## 3. Winner analysis — what must not regress","+## 3. The economics that constrain every fix"," ","-**Lift +21.21 pts across 24 instances. `lombok-3674` alone is +6.09 pts = 29% of ALL lift.**","+`cache_read` is **95.5%** of billed tokens. A result injected at turn *i* is re-charged on every","+later turn: cost ≈ `(bytes/4) × turns-remaining` — **~5 persist-tokens per byte** at 20 turns left."," ","-| instance | pts | eg/base turns | eg/base harness |","+**One default search payload is 10,822 B ≈ 54k persist ≈ 0.55 of the whole-file Read it replaces.**","+That single number *is* the context-neutrality result (eg 38.5M vs baseline 38.6M).","+","+| class | baseline share | calls | each |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| `lombok-3674` | **+6.09** | 67/122 | **23/70** |","-| `fmt-2457` | +2.18 | 38/67 | 12/13 |","-| `qutebrowser-c580` | +1.89 | 88/105 | 23/33 |","-| `vuejs-11739` | +1.35 | 70/80 | 24/19 |","-| `redis-11510` | +1.29 | 34/56 | 3/12 |","+| exploration | 45.1% | 1,206 | 14k |","+| **whole-file `Read`** | **30.3%** | **119** | **98k (7×)** |","+| harness | 11.2% | 576 | 7k |"," ","-**Winners win because the BASELINE flails and eg converges** — lombok's baseline ran `javac`","-**70 times** against eg's 23. eg is not doing something clever; it is failing to blow up.","+**Break-even:** a block ≤2.8 KB pays for itself if it removes one grep/session; ≤19.6 KB if it","+removes one whole-file Read; ≤1.4 KB if it removes one harness run."," ","-**Two consequences that constrain every proposal below:**","+**Corollary: bytes delivered at turn 1 are charged N times.** The tool spends its whole budget at","+its most expensive moment and is absent from the phase where the money goes."," ","-1. **A symmetric frugality clamp is net-negative.** Suppressing over-verification helps the","-   baseline more than eg in exactly the instances eg currently wins. Already modelled; do not","-   ship one.","-2. **Any intervention that adds post-edit content risks converting a winner into a loser**, since","-   winners win by *doing less* after the first edit. Winner protection is therefore not a","-   formality — it is the main risk.","-"," ---"," ","-## 4. What is already closed (do not rebuild)","+## 4. The plan — remove bytes and fix defaults, in this order"," ","-| route | verdict |","-|---|---|","-| new verb in the affordance tail | **0/66 adoption** (`impact` 0/49, `changed` 0/5, `--path` 0/12) |","-| post-edit rider (G2) | **−12.19%**, fired 0/5 |","-| displacement via better verbs (G3) | ratio **0.76** vs 0.96 baseline — went backwards |","-| graph-backed grep | 38.9% interception ceiling; graph output (1,124 B median) is *larger* than a median grep (732 B) |","-| next-query coverage | only 40.4% of missed identifiers are graph symbols; of those 89% stay missing at 4× payload budget |","-| payload quality | 12 metrics dead, incl. complete-symbol density (r = **−0.170**) |","-| retrieval/ranking | anti-correlated — gold-at-rank-1 sessions lost more often |","-| tail-risk endpoint | arms blow up at identical rates (22.4% vs 20.4%); n=6,338 to resolve |","+Every item is **tool output, not instruction**, and passes the no-tool-arm test. Ranked by","+(turns removed) / (bytes added). **Items 4.1–4.4 all reduce or barely move payload size** — the","+first proposals in this project with a positive byte ratio."," ","----","+### 4.1 Fix `graph grep`: exclude vendored / minified / generated files *(NEGATIVE bytes)*","+`internal/cli` grep path shells out to `grep -rInE` over the whole worktree and filters **only","+tests**. On `prometheus-9248` it returned one hit inside minified vendored `d3.v3.js` where plain","+grep returned a **clean zero** — and a clean zero is *actionable* (\"pivot\"), one noise hit is not.","+Baseline pivoted to the issue's error string at call 2 and found `scalarBinop`; eg reached it at","+calls 21–22. **~19 turns of delay, caused by the tool's opening answer.**"," ","-## 5. The plan","+This is the only place measured where the graph is **demonstrably worse than no tool at all**, and","+the fix removes bytes."," ","-### 5.1 Accept the honest target","+### 4.2 Ship FILE OUTLINE by default *(+1,421 B, ~8× return — best ratio of anything built)*","+`internal/sem/search_outline.go` (217 LOC), flag `internal/cli/search.go:1637`. **Default OFF,","+absent from `printHelp`.** Its own measurement: **77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload","+had already named; 35 were immediately followed by a Read of that same file**, landing a median","+109 lines from anything printed. Measured cost +1,421 B ≈ 7.1k persist against ~57k saved."," ","-**Stop targeting 35% on Opus.** Target **loser repair**, whose exact ceiling is the lift pool:","-**+21.21%** if every losing instance were made precisely neutral. That is arithmetic, not","-projection. Reaching it requires eliminating the drag pool entirely; a realistic fraction is","-worth +5–10%.","+### 4.3 Cut complete bodies from rank 5 to rank 2 *(−76% payload bytes)*","+`search_enclosure.go:41` (`searchEnclosureHeadRanks = 5`). Act-rate data in `search_outline.go:22`:","+rank 1 read 62% / edited 54%; rank 2 27%/20%; **rank 3+ 0–11%.** Measured: `--body-head-ranks`","+5→3 = 10,822→6,143 B; **5→2 = 10,822→2,590 B (−76%)**. Ranks 3–5 pay full persist for a ≤11% read","+rate. Net is close (−41k certain saving vs ~29k probabilistic extra reads) but the saving is the","+certain half."," ","-### 5.2 Build: VERIFY runnability probe *(primary — targets the measured mechanism)*","+### 4.4 Probe the VERIFY command instead of `LookPath` *(NEGATIVE bytes)*","+`internal/sem/search_verify.go:135` checks only that the runner *binary exists* — `npx` exists,","+so the command prints, then fails because deps were never installed. Replace with a collect-only","+probe on the pristine tree (`pytest --collect-only -q`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`,","+`cargo test --no-run`, `phpunit --list-tests`, `rspec --dry-run`); on failure **strip the block**."," ","-**Files:** `internal/sem/search_verify.go` (derivation + probe), `internal/cli/search.go`","-(VERIFY block emission).","+Measured swing on this exact axis (rep30, baseline-matched): `VERIFY real` **+4.6 turns / +37.1%","+USD**; `VERIFY runner-absent` **−6.0 turns / −11.8%**; no VERIFY line −4.7 turns. **An 11.4-turn","+swing.** The previous response was to silence VERIFY entirely, which also discarded the good case.","+A probe keeps the good case and kills the bad one."," ","-Today the only check is `exec.LookPath` on the runner (`search_verify.go:1526`) — it confirms","-`pytest` exists, never that the derived command *runs*. Add a **collect-only probe** before","-emitting: `pytest --collect-only -q`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`, `cargo test --no-run`,","-`mvn -q -DskipTests compile`. On failure, drop to the next rung rather than emitting a command","-that will fail on the environment.","+**Note:** this makes the provider *execute* something for the first time. That is a real product","+decision — latency, and a category change — and it should be taken deliberately."," ","-Also raise VERIFY coverage — it appears in only **8 of 33** payloads, so 76% of sessions get no","-verification command at all and improvise one.","+### 4.5 Example-level VERIFY granularity *(+15 B, reaches 62% of the corpus)*","+`search_covertest.go` already selects **exactly one** test method and its line, then the deriver","+throws the name away for 5 of 8 ecosystems: Ruby, PHP, JS file-only; Java/Gradle class-only.","+Python (`-k`), Go (`-run '^Name$'`) and Rust already do it right. Fix: emit","+`rspec spec/foo_spec.rb:412`, `phpunit --filter testX`, `jest -t \"…\"`, `mvn -Dtest=Class#method`.","+Targets Ruby 39 + PHP 32 + JS 23 + TS 8 + Java 31 = **133/213 instances**."," ","-**Fair:** the derived command is tool output computed from the repo, same class as a ranked hit.","-Ships no instruction; the baseline is untouched.","+### 4.6 Ship R-A zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, deployed as `b669a57b`)*","+`EG_PREFETCH=1` injected the payload at turn 0 and still let the agent re-derive it at full price.","+`EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual call an echo — 0.02 s vs 5.21 s, byte-identical.","+Counterfactual on this cell **+4.3% to +6.0%** (CI spans zero at n=49)."," ","-**Expected: +0.5% to +1.5%.** Stated honestly — 22 avoided env-failures × ~39.5K tok ≈ 0.6% of","-the pool. This is a real mechanism with a small effect, not a headline.","+### 4.7 Documentation and defaults that are simply wrong *(zero bytes)*","+- `search` defaults to `--profile fast` (**9/30 relations**) while both agent guides mandate `full`.","+  Under the default, TESTS, SIMILAR_TO, DATA_FLOWS, FILE_CHANGES_WITH and every type relation are","+  **structurally empty**, so blocks depending on them cannot fire. `neighbors`/`impact` default to","+  `full`; `search` is the odd one out.","+- `AGENTS.md:72` states `edges --to/--from/--relation` **does not exist**. It does","+  (`root.go:576-594`) — and it is the only route to 13 relation types. Delete that sentence.","+- `capabilities --json` declares **7** heuristic relations; by the code **~27 of 30** are","+  text-pattern derived, including **CALLS (35% of all edges), which is a regex name-set, not an","+  AST call-site set.** Doctrine rule 7 says \"feature-detect before you trust\" — it is being fed a","+  wrong answer.","+- `TESTS` ships in the relation list at **10 edges of 36,354 on Go and 0 of 89,587 on a Python repo","+  that has a pytest suite.** Either fix it (§4.8) or stop advertising it.","+- `verify` and `changed` are in neither agent guide; `changed` is absent from `printHelp`.","+- **The in-tree binary is stale vs source** — it rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`.","+  Rebuild before anything ships."," ","-### 5.3 Ship: R-A zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, deployed)*","+### 4.8 TESTS from call-reachability rather than spelling *(zero payload bytes)*","+`types.go:280-297` maps `TestFoo→Foo` by name only. Emit TESTS where a symbol in a test file","+reaches the target within **≤2 CALLS hops**, restricted to ranked files. Uses edges that already","+exist (12.6k–21.1k CALLS). CALLS is supported for Ruby/PHP/JS/TS/Python, so this is one of the few","+upgrades that lands on the dynamic ~48% of the corpus. It is also the input to §4.4 and §4.5."," ","-Already committed (`b669a57b`) and deployed. `EG_PREFETCH=1` injected the payload into turn 0 and","-still let the agent re-derive it at full price; `EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual call an echo","-(0.02 s vs 5.21 s, byte-identical). Removes 94 calls × 1.61 msgs.","+### 4.9 DO NOT BUILD","+- **Post-edit consistency hook.** Stress-tested and rejected: its fair (symmetric) form's biggest","+  beneficiary is the **baseline in `lombok-3674`**, i.e. it eats 29% of the lift. Cost −2% to −6%.","+- Any new verb in the affordance tail — **0/66 adoption** measured.","+- Anything requiring an agent-initiated post-edit call — 42/49 sessions make none.","+- Better ranking; bigger payloads; graph-backed grep; the 12 dead payload metrics."," ","-**Expected +4.3% to +6.0%** (counterfactual on all 49 pairs; CI spans zero at n=49).","+---"," ","-### 5.4 Do NOT build the post-edit hook without a decision","+## 5. Integrity fixes — before any cell"," ","-It is the only mechanism reaching the 97.7%, but it requires `CC_NO_SAFE_MODE=1` and a change to","-patch collection (`.claude/settings.json` would land in the graded patch). It also carries the","-§3 regression risk directly. Decide fairness and patch-collection acceptability first.","+1. **Sibling-checkout answer leak.** `bat-1892` (the worst loser, −2.81 pts) made **12 references","+   into `bat-3108`, a later revision of the same repo containing the implemented feature.**","+   Measured exposure: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline** — small but **arm-asymmetric**. Fence","+   checkouts so a session cannot read a sibling instance's tree.","+2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells.** `prometheus-9248` found `/tmp/goyacc*` built by","+   *other instances'* sessions and spent 2 calls auditing foreign binaries. eg 3/49, base 1/49.","+   Give each session a private temp root.","+3. **Junk-patch gate.** One baseline patch was 371,308 B of vendor/build output and passed as","+   success. Add a symmetric size/content bound.","+4. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.","+   Fix before any payload forensics.","+5. **0-byte `cc_out.json`** — guard shipped; the sweep removed **90 corpses** across all cells."," ","+**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, **0 commit mismatches**, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches","+small, prompt diff is 18 lines all of which are checkout paths.","+"," ---"," "," ## 6. Gates — mechanism counts, winners protected"," ","-MDE is ~25–30 pts at n≈30 against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor. **No token claim below","-n≈50, in either direction.**","+MDE is ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between","+cells. **No token claim below n≈50, in either direction.**"," "," | gate | n | criterion |"," |---|---|---|","-| **V0** offline, $0 | 0 | probe returns a runnable command on cargo/pytest/phpunit/gotest/mvn repos; VERIFY coverage ≥ 80% of payloads (from 8/33); zero regressions on existing verbs |","-| **V1** replay, $0 | 49 | on recorded loser sessions, the probed command would have succeeded where the emitted one failed |","-| **V2** live | 12 | **harness ENV failures per session fall vs rep50**; throwaway scripts do not rise. Mechanism counts only |","-| **V3** live | 50 | first token claim, bootstrap CI, total **and** median |","+| **V0** offline, $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; grep excludes vendored/minified on the prometheus query and returns a clean zero; outline/body-rank byte deltas reproduce (10,822 → 2,590 B) |","+| **V1** replay, $0 | 49 | on recorded loser sessions, the probed VERIFY command would have run where the emitted one failed; ≥50% of the 22 env-failures avoided |","+| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: payload bytes/session **down**, env-failures/session **down**, no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |","+| **V3** live | 50 | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together** |"," ","-**Winner-protection tripwire, binding at every gate:** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,","-`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` are included in every sample from V2 on. If any shows a rise in","-post-edit harness runs or turns versus its rep50 record, the change is reverted regardless of the","-loser-group result. lombok alone is 29% of all lift — losing it costs more than repairing the","-five worst losers gains.","+**Winner-protection tripwire (per your instruction, abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,","+`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` are in every sample from V2 on. If any regresses >10pt versus a","+**same-wave** control, revert. Never compare against a previous cell — the noise floor forbids it."," ","-**Kill criteria.** V1 under 50% → the probe does not address the observed failures; stop.","-V2 without a fall in env-failures → mechanism absent; stop. Any winner regression >10pt → revert.","-"," ---"," ","-## 7. Verification","+## 7. Honest expected outcome"," ","-- Tool: `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race tests + build;","-  CGO required for tree-sitter). Add unit tests for the probe beside `search_verify.go`.","-- Offline replay: recorded queries at `results/<tag>/eg/<instance>/gq_calls.log`, payloads at the","-  same path + `.payload`. Replay against the binary at zero model cost and assert both that the","-  probe changes the emitted command *and* that nothing else moved.","-- Harness deploys to VMs by temp path + atomic `mv` only, with a live-session guard — never","-  overwrite a script a session is reading.","-- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** Δturns **and** harness/env-failure counts.","+| item | effect | confidence |","+|---|---|---|","+| 4.1 grep vendor filter | removes a ~19-turn failure mode on ADD tasks | high — mechanism observed |","+| 4.2 FILE OUTLINE default | ~8× return on 1,421 B | high — own measurement |","+| 4.3 bodies rank 5→2 | −76% payload bytes | high on cost, medium on net |","+| 4.4 VERIFY probe | up to 11.4-turn swing on that axis | medium |","+| 4.5 VERIFY granularity | 133/213 instances | medium |","+| 4.6 R-A zero-toll | +4.3% to +6.0% | medium, CI spans zero |"," ","----","+**Combined, realistically: high single digits to low teens, with the drag pool shrinking rather","+than the lift pool growing.** The ceiling on loser repair is exactly **+21.21%** (the lift pool) —","+arithmetic, not projection."," ","-## 8. What to tell stakeholders","+**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change.** The one intervention that would reach it is","+an instruction telling the agent to explore and re-test less — which helps a no-tool arm equally","+and is precisely what the withdrawn −35% contained."," ","-The defensible claim is **not** a token saving. On Opus the tool is centrally neutral","-(+1.35%, t=−0.17; −0.26% winsorised). What it demonstrably does at n=49 is suppress whole-file","-reads — 119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B, >8 KB tail 39 → 25 — and that is measurable now","-without another cell. Report that, plus the interval on tokens, and stop quoting a percentage the","-data does not support.","+**If §4.4 (executing a probe) is refused,** the honest recommendation is to stop optimising tokens","+here: remove bytes (4.1–4.3, 4.7), and position entire-graph on correctness and latency, where it","+is demonstrably good. It is not, on this corpus and this cost model, a token tool."," ","-"," ---"," ","-# APPENDIX A — Subagent findings log","+## 8. Verification"," ","-Running record of every investigation. Each entry: what was asked, what came back, and whether it","-survived checking. **Entries are not conclusions until marked CONFIRMED.**","+- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO needed).","+  **Rebuild the in-tree binary — it is stale.** Add unit tests beside `search_verify.go` and the","+  grep filter.","+- Offline replay: recorded queries at `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log`, payloads at the same","+  path + `.payload`. Re-run against the binary at zero model cost; assert both that the change","+  fires and that nothing else moved.","+- Harness deploys to VMs by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a","+  script a running session is reading.","+- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** trimmed **and** LOO **and** Δturns **and**","+  env-failure counts."," ","-## A1 — Post-edit hook stress test *(Plan agent, completed)*","-**Asked:** is an automatic post-edit consistency-check hook fair, and what does it cost?","-**Returned — REJECTED the design, three reasons:**","-- A hook is a *harness* feature; every harness change here is symmetric by construction. The","-  no-tool-arm test fails: `rg -n 'symbol'` produces ~80% of the same output.","-- **Self-defeating in its fair form.** The biggest beneficiary of a symmetric hook is the","-  *baseline* in `lombok-3674` — where baseline ran `javac` 70× vs eg's 23×. That instance is 29%","-  of all lift, so the fix eats its own lift source.","-- Cost: fires on all 414 eg edits; at a 400-token payload = **−5.6%**. eg is context-neutral, so","-  there is no slack to spend.","-**Also surfaced:** `claude --settings '<json>' --setting-sources ''` avoids writing","-`.claude/settings.json` into the worktree, which would remove the patch-pollution blocker.","-**Status: CONFIRMED as a rejection.** Do not build the hook.","+---"," ","-## A2 — Loser forensics: `bat-1892`, `valkey-790` *(Opus agent, completed)*","-**Returned:**","-- **The graph payload was CORRECT in both.** Top hit was the exact function to edit. eg used","-  *fewer* localization calls than baseline (10 vs 15; 15 vs 17). **The graph won localization and","-  lost the session downstream.** — CONFIRMED, matches the cell-wide pre-edit finding (−46/−58).","-- `bat-1892`: 42 of 99 calls are environment/leak/hung-test work no code graph can address.","-- `valkey-790`: ~13–15 pre-edit calls *are* graph-shaped — \"which tests exercise this symbol and","-  how are they invoked\", and tcl `proc` definitions (three consecutive failed greps for `proc R`","-  because **entire-graph indexes no `.tcl` symbols**).","-- **Proposal: a test-invocation card in the first search response** (~14 turns / ~500 B). Not a","-  new verb, not post-edit — it rides the one call every session already makes.","-**Two integrity claims, both checked below.**","+# APPENDIX A — Subagent findings log"," ","-## A3 — Integrity claim 1: answer leak *(from A2)*","-Concurrent instance checkouts share a parent directory, and `sharkdp__bat-3108` is a **later","-revision of the same repo containing the implemented feature**. eg found it via `ls` and spent 12","-calls mining it. **Structural, not arm-specific** — whichever arm lists that directory gets the","-upstream solution. Corroborates an existing note (\"2 instances spent 13–15 calls mining an","-adjacent instance's tree\"). **Status: CONFIRMED as a live exposure. Must be fixed before any","-further cell.**","+## A1 — Post-edit hook stress test — **REJECTED**","+Fair (symmetric) form's biggest beneficiary is the baseline in `lombok-3674` = 29% of all lift;","+cost −2% to −6%; ~48% of corpus is dynamically typed where arity checks are unreliable.","+Also surfaced: `claude --settings '<json>' --setting-sources ''` avoids writing","+`.claude/settings.json` into the worktree, removing the patch-pollution blocker."," ","-## A4 — Integrity claim 2: \"the metric rewards failing to provision\" *(from A2)* — **REFUTED at scale**","-A2 argued baseline \"won\" `bat-1892` by never compiling the crate (it wrote a `rustc` mock while a","-198 MB offline registry sat unfound). True for that instance. **But the population audit does not","-support it as a general mechanism:**","+## A2 — Loser forensics: `bat-1892`, `valkey-790` — **graph INNOCENT**","+Payload was correct in both; top hit was the exact function to edit; eg used *fewer* localization","+calls than baseline (10 vs 15; 15 vs 17). Losses were environment, answer-leak and a hung pty test.","+`valkey`: ~13–15 pre-edit calls were graph-shaped (test invocation, tcl `proc` sites — **no `.tcl`","+symbols are indexed**)."," ","-| group | n | TOKEN | wins |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| eg built, baseline did not | 4 | +2.04% | 2/4 |","-| baseline built, eg did not | 6 | +31.14% | 4/6 |","-| **both arms built for real** | **20** | **−14.49%** | 7/20 |","-| neither built | 19 | **+9.71%** | 11/19 |","+## A3 — Loser forensics: `ansible-395e`, `prometheus-9248` — **graph GUILTY on prometheus**","+Both ADD tasks; 80%/64% of surplus is PRE-edit. `graph grep` returned a minified-vendor false","+positive where plain grep returned a clean zero → ~19 turns of delay. `ansible` innocent","+(environment). **`EG_LITERALS` — the error-string→symbol index that would have collapsed","+prometheus's delay — is built and was switched OFF in this cell.**"," ","-Only **2 of 25 losers** have the eg-built/base-didn't shape, worth **−1.06 pts** of the −19.86 drag.","-**Status: REFUTED as a driver.**","+## A4 — Capability inventory — **the decisive result**","+~2,500 LOC shipped default-off; `verify`/`changed`/`def` undocumented; `AGENTS.md:72` denies a","+real feature; `capabilities` under-declares heuristics 7 vs ~27; **CALLS is a regex name-set, not","+AST**; TESTS 10/36,354 on Go and **0/89,587 on a Python repo with pytest**; Ruby 5/30 relations,","+C 4/30 (61/213 instances where the graph is barely a symbol index)."," ","-**But the audit replaced it with a stronger finding — CONFIRMED, and new:**","-> **eg loses 14.49% when both arms genuinely build and test, and wins 9.71% when neither does.**","-","-The tool is worst exactly where real verification happens. This is the verify-repair spiral","-confirmed from an independent angle, and it is the single most decision-relevant number in this","-appendix.","-","-## A5 — Still running","-- 4-lens artifact/data audit workflow (ledger+memory, plan docs, tool source, harness)","-- Loser forensics: `ansible-395e`, `prometheus-9248` (Python/dynamic counterparts to A2)","-- Capability inventory: what the graph computes but never surfaces","-- Three-defect fix workflow (call toll / ADD tasks / verify derivation)","-","-**The full plan is deliberately NOT finalised until these land.**","+## A5 — Claims I made and then RETRACTED","+- \"eg verifies more than baseline\" — **false**, eg 545 vs base 576. Came from the 8 worst losers,","+  a set selected on the outcome.","+- \"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\" — **regex artifact**; stricter definition gives n=17 and","+  **−0.89%**.","+- \"the metric rewards failing to provision\" — real on `bat-1892`, but only **2/25 losers**, worth","+  −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.","+- \"+35.06% is reachable by loser repair\" — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.","+- ×0.54 persist calibration — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**","+  (corr +0.916, R² 0.839)."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f0e86ac8-af36-4913-9b0a-e1f9a4f7bb78","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
