{"parentUuid":"c8b18e23-83e4-4206-bb94-d94e949cd115","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqjPWDmn5CKyhnL2aY4C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll hold. The plan file is saved as a checkpoint, but I won't treat it as final.\n\n**Landed so far (4 of 5 investigations):**\n\n| | verdict |\n|---|---|\n| post-edit hook stress test | **rejected** — its fair form's biggest beneficiary is the baseline in `lombok-3674`, eating 29% of the lift |\n| forensics: `bat-1892`, `valkey-790` | **graph innocent** — payload correct, top hit exact, *fewer* localization calls than baseline |\n| forensics: `ansible`, `prometheus` | **graph guilty on prometheus** — `graph grep` returned a minified-vendor false positive where plain grep returned a clean zero; ~19 turns lost |\n| capability inventory | **~2,500 LOC shipped default-off**; `CALLS` is a regex name-set not AST; TESTS 0/89,587 on a Python repo with pytest; `AGENTS.md:72` denies a feature that exists |\n\n**Still running:** the 4-lens artifact/data audit (ledger + memory + plan docs + harness) and the three-defect fix workflow. Those are the two that could contradict what I've written — the audit is specifically tasked with finding claims in my own documents that the newer data breaks, and the fix workflow puts each proposed change through three adversarial refuters.\n\nI'll wait for both, reconcile everything against the retraction list in Appendix A, and only then finalise. Given how many of my own claims have already been overturned on checking — five so far, all in the same direction — assuming these two will merely confirm would be the exact mistake this project keeps making."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":825404,"output_tokens":539,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_cre