{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:14:34.850Z","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wpnth6aws</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NzT7ANk4G4X4qYKGUWHudS</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/wpnth6aws.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Design and offline-validate a fix for each of the three measured loss mechanisms on Opus\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"live_count\":0,\"specs\":[{\"defect\":\"DEFECT 1 as stated is mispriced, and in this cell it is not the defect. Re-measured on all 49 REP50_r1 gated pairs from the raw transcripts (cache_read = 94.6% of billed, confirming the cost model): the first graph search lands at assistant turn median 2 (mean 2.09, p90 2) of a median 85-turn session, where cache_read is 12,231 tokens vs the session mean of 63,137/turn. The call is the CHEAPEST message in the session, 5.2x below the price the +4.3-6.0% estimate charged it at. Delivered payload median 2,152 B (27/34 calls already piped through `head`), so moving it to turn 0 costs only (B/4)x(t0+1) ~1.6k tokens — the estimate's error is on the SAVINGS side, not the persist side. The actual drag is turn inflation, not call toll: LOSERS run 862 shell-exploration Bash calls vs baseline 570 (+51%) and 97.3 turns vs 78.2; WINNERS 668 vs 853 (-22%) and 79.6 vs 100.5. corr(saving, turn delta) = -0.900. The call is ~12k tokens against a ~1.2M/session loser drag: R-A targets ~1% of the thing that is actually losing.\",\"verdict\":\"do-not-build\",\"proposal\":\"Do not spend a cell on R-A. Land two safety fixes and one pre-registered gate instead; all are tool-output/harness hygiene, no prompt bytes on either arm.\\n\\n1. /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/search.go:286-292 — echoPresearchPayload has NO length check (verified live on HEAD 607b2a4; note b669a57b is not in this repo's history). A zero-byte or truncated prefetch.payload yields 0 bytes on stdout with exit 0 — exactly the \\\"payload announced, none shipped\\\" failure behind the withdrawn +22% (TokensNotes §7.4, fix exists as 8a4ffb3 but is not on this tree). eg-q's `[ -s ]` guard (tools/eg-q:172) covers only the shell path; EG_PRESEARCH is exported process-wide (run_3arm.sh:703) so any direct binary invocation hits the unguarded Go path.\\n\\n2. /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/search.go:134-136 and /Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench/tools/eg-q:172-173 — the echo is query-blind and header-less. Any later search on any new symbol returns the turn-0 payload verbatim with no indication it answered a different question, unlike the session-echo path at search.go:141-149 which does emit searchEchoHeader. That makes the 40-word issue-head query (retrieval measured worse: gold-visible@5 0.567 vs the agent's own 0.715) an ABSORBING STATE for the whole session. Fix: echo only when the query matches the prefetch query, else run live; or always prepend searchEchoHeader naming the query actually answered.\\n\\n3. Pre-registered mechanism gate for any future prefetch-family cell (gate on counts, never tokens at n&lt;50): residual agent search-call rate &gt;= 0.5/session AND displacement rate (eg shell-exploration calls &lt; paired baseline) &gt;= 43% (rep50's current 21/49). TokensNotes §2.11 predicts both fail at 0/49.\\n\\nAlso flag, if a cell is ever run: run_3arm.sh:750-766 injects \\\"you do not need to run it yourself\\\" by default (EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=0) — that is instruction-shaped, not output; run with NOSUPPRESS=1 so the delta is output-only. And run_3arm.sh:579-581 swallows prefetch failure with `2&gt;/dev/null || true`, while success flips published_exact_eg_tool's _intro (run_3arm.sh:1377-1387) — one arm then silently mixes two prompt revisions. Shared `$SUITE/.eg_cache/$iid` is warmed by the prefetch and read by concurrent tags (the known A/B cache trap).\",\"expected_pct_low\":-0.3,\"expected_pct_high\":2.2,\"fair\":true,\"fairness_argument\":\"R-A itself passes the doctrine test: the turn-0 payload is tool OUTPUT, and an arm with no tool has no counterpart to receive — the delta is a capability, not advice. Two caveats. (a) The default framing at run_3arm.sh:754-756, \\\"A code-graph search has ALREADY been run ... you do not need to run it yourself\\\", is an instruction about how to behave, not output; it must be dropped (EG_PREFETCH_NOSUPPRESS=1) or the cell carries an eg-only behavioral directive. (b) The search.go:254 design note says the \\\"search first\\\" mandate must be removed alongside pre-delivery. That is arm-legal (an eg-only constraint being lifted, same argument as EG_FREE_MSG1), but it is moot here: I read the actual rep50 eg prompt on the VM and it carries NO search-first line — it is the payload-conditional capability wording only. So R-A cannot bank any saving from removing a directive that is not there, which is part of why its measured ceiling collapses. My proposal adds zero prompt bytes to either arm and is pure tool-output plus harness hygiene.\",\"kill_criterion\":\"Already met, offline, at zero model spend. Pre-registered threshold: R-A must show a pooled persist-model ceiling &gt;= +3% on the rep50 pairs to justify a cell. Measured: pooled +0.96%, bootstrap CI95 [+0.53, +1.38] (n=4000 resamples), with a full sensitivity band of -0.25% (call turn costs only its own cache_read) to +2.16% (whole turn removed). Ceiling is below threshold under every assumption. Second, independent kill: R-A's saving requires a residual agent search call to make free, and the only session-level measurement of payload injection (TokensNotes §2.11) reports 0 of 49 sessions ever queried the tool, with PUB_r1 at 0.20 graph calls vs 24.40 shell greps/session — the zero-toll echo has no surface to act on. Third: prefetch's own paired measurement (run_3arm.sh:486-490, Opus, 3 replicates, n=30) already returned +3.0% WORSE with turns rising 13.40 -&gt; 13.72, in a cell where the agent made ~0 calls, i.e. a cell where zero-toll would have changed nothing. If it is ever revisited, the gate is mechanism-only: residual search-call rate &gt;= 0.5/session and displacement rate &gt;= 43%; do not read tokens below n=50 (n to demonstrate +2% is well past 499 pairs).\",\"offline_evidence\":\"All numbers recomputed from raw REP50_r1 transcripts on graphbench-c (49 gated pairs, both arms, ~/.claude/projects/*/&lt;sid&gt;.jsonl), zero model spend.\\nCOST MODEL CONFIRMED: cache_read = 94.6% of billed tokens; my pooled metric on this cell is +4.35% saved (headline +1.35% uses billed cost).\\nCALL PLACEMENT: 33/49 sessions make &gt;=1 `entire graph search` (dist 0:16, 1:32, 2:1; mean 0.69/session). Non-search graph verbs (def/callers/impact/grep) mean 1.41/session — so zero-toll, which covers `search` only, addresses at most 33% of graph-call tolls. First call at assistant turn median 2, mean 2.09, p90 2. Session length median 85 assistant turns (mean 91.2). cache_read AT the call turn median 12,231 vs session mean 63,137/turn.\\nPAYLOAD: delivered tool_result median 2,152 B (mean 2,854, max 9,836); full eg-q output median 3,293 B/session (EG_TOPK=5, EG_MAXBYTES=32768); 27/34 calls piped through `head`. Turn-0 relocation penalty = (B/4)x(t0+1) ~ 1.6k tokens — negligible, so the persist charge is NOT what kills R-A.\\nR-A PRICED: conservative -0.25%, mid +0.96% CI95[+0.53,+1.38], aggressive +2.16% pooled; mean-of-ratios -0.35/+0.95/+2.25%, median +0.01/+0.98/+1.82%. The published +4.3-6.0% is reproducible only by pricing the removed message at the SESSION-MEAN turn cost (63,137) instead of the actual turn-2 cost (12,231), i.e. a 5.2x overcharge.\\nUNIVERSAL DELIVERY COSTS THE LOSERS: 16/49 sessions never call search; universal injection charges them (P/4)xN ~ 45k tokens each for nothing. Those are the losing cohort — non-callers pooled -1.02%, median -24.94%; callers pooled +6.30%, median +12.61%. Caller rate is 0.76 in winners vs 0.58 in losers. The \\\"+7.0% tax for merely having called\\\" is inverted in this cell: calling is the WINNING behaviour.\\nDISPLACEMENT IS THE DISCRIMINATOR: label nodisp = (eg shell-exploration calls &gt;= baseline). displace&amp;win 19/21 (90.5%); nodisp&amp;win 6/28 (21.4%). AUC(nodisp -&gt; loss) = 0.838. R-A removes the call in exactly the cohort where calling wins.\\nQ3 — NO PRE-RUN SIGNAL (design note independently reproduced): AUC for predicting nodisp at 57% base rate — file paths named in issue 0.532, code fences 0.480, backticked identifiers 0.452, ps len\n... (truncated 96612 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/wpnth6aws.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49/subagents/workflows/wf_1a7518dd-cbb/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49/workflows/scripts/eg-fix-three-defects-wf_1a7518dd-cbb.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_1a7518dd-cbb'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>13</agent_count><agents_done>13</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>1025603</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>211</tool_uses><duration_ms>1269292</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
