{"parentUuid":"9ddd98c2-309e-4965-9df5-1e6e6f142487","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e29715b0-fa37-4eec-809f-11335bf415bc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KV3LqxEbrFxdCDk4aubxmn","type":"tool_result","content":"########## v2:04edc4ddd9963194b5206c240ed5844081cb198ced4246c1333c21f76a58b6a5\nverdict=build-with-changes  fair=True  range=0.5..2.5\nDEFECT: DEFECT 3 — the post-edit verify-repair spiral: a derived VERIFY command that fails on the ENVIRONMENT rather than on the patch, sending the agent into improvised throwaway harnesses and re-exploration. Claimed chain: env-failure -> improvised harness -> post-edit re-explore. The tool's only runnability evidence today is exec.LookPath at internal/sem/search_verify.go:1536, which proves a binary is on PATH and nothing about whether the invocation resolves.\n\nPROPOSAL: COLLECT-ONLY PROBE, annotate-only, default OFF.\n\nHook: internal/sem/search_verify.go:249 — replace the single line `command.RunnerMissing = searchVerifyRunnerMissing(command.Command, &evidence)` with a two-stage gate: (1) keep static searchVerifyRunnerMissing (:1526, LookPath :1536); (2) only if static says PRESENT, call a new searchVerifyProbe.\n\nInjection: new field on searchVerifyEvidence beside lookPath (:139):\n  runProbe func(argv []string, dir string, timeout time.Duration) (exit int, stderr string, ran bool)\nnil => probing disabled => byte-identical to today. Wired from internal/cli/search.go behind --verify-probe / EG_VERIFY_PROBE=1 (default off), so A/B is a flag flip and the default payload is unchanged.\n\nProbe table, keyed by DERIVATION (not by re-parsing the command string; reuse the `dir` the derivation already holds as the probe cwd):\n  pytest :1066/:631  -> python -m pytest\n\nEVIDENCE: REPRODUCED THE STATE independently from graphbench-c:~/work/graphmark/agentic-swebench/results/REP50_r1_{eg,baseline}: 49/49 gated, total +1.35%, 24 wins / 25 losers. baseline 145.6M tok, eg 143.7M tok, cache_read = 95.5% of billed (confirms persist model).\n\nLADDER (internal/sem/search_verify.go, HEAD 607b2a4): buildSearchVerifyCommand :199; subject :295; mirror-test probe :396; rung1 narrow :462 via searchVerifyDerivations :489 (10 ecosystems); rung2 suite :506 via :532 (+CMake suite :1584); rung3 build-check :1421 with ext map :1401 (.php .rb .js .jsx .mjs .cjs .py); rung4 residual floor :264 returned at :209 and :245. Because of :209/:245 the function CANNOT return nil at HEAD -> coverage\n\n########## v2:72cf8bfd306a65e632c6bdf66e83e7aea452881373d0be839c6309ba02a354c3\nverdict=do-not-build  fair=True  range=-0.3..2.2\nDEFECT: DEFECT 1 as stated is mispriced, and in this cell it is not the defect. Re-measured on all 49 REP50_r1 gated pairs from the raw transcripts (cache_read = 94.6% of billed, confirming the cost model): the first graph search lands at assistant turn median 2 (mean 2.09, p90 2) of a median 85-turn session, where cache_read is 12,231 tokens vs the session mean of 63,137/turn. The call is the CHEAPEST message in the session, 5.2x below the price the +4.3-6.0% estimate charged it at. Delivered payload median 2,152 B (27/34 calls already piped through `head`), so moving it to turn 0 costs only (B/4)x(t0+1) ~1.6k tokens — the estimate's error is on the SAVINGS side, not the persist side. The actual dr\n\nPROPOSAL: Do not spend a cell on R-A. Land two safety fixes and one pre-registered gate instead; all are tool-output/harness hygiene, no prompt bytes on either arm.\n\n1. /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/search.go:286-292 — echoPresearchPayload has NO length check (verified live on HEAD 607b2a4; note b669a57b is not in this repo's history). A zero-byte or truncated prefetch.payload yields 0 bytes on stdout with exit 0 — exactly the \"payload announced, none shipped\" failure behind the withdrawn +22% (TokensNotes §7.4, fix exists as 8a4ffb3 but is not on this tree). eg-q's `[ -s ]` guard (tools/eg-q:172) covers only the shell path; EG_PRES