{"parentUuid":"72829736-8751-4a37-8c40-f8b4319a2dd1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"96e03687-14c7-40a5-93eb-a483d24f1540","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wqw2zyaob</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208/tasks/wqw2zyaob.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Read-only audit of every entire-graph artifact and dataset to settle what is true on Opus and what plan survives\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"survivors\":[{\"claim\":\"EG-FINAL-PLAN §2 states three mutually inconsistent context totals for the same table. (a) 'Baseline 38.6M. eg 38.5M. context-neutral (+0.2%)'. (b) The itemised paragraph gives net 0.97M = +2.51%. (c) The table's own columns sum to baseline 35.01M vs eg 33.44M = 1.57M = +4.07%. The itemised (b) is arithmetically wrong: it omits the harness saving of 0.60M (4.30 → 3.70, which is in the table's 'captured 14%' column but appears in neither the 3.77M gross nor the 2.80M adds); 0.97 + 0.60 = 1.57 exactly. Separately the baseline column sums to 35.01M against a stated 38.6M total, so 3.59M (9.3%) of the budget is unlisted — and that unlisted residual is where the entire difference between (a) and (c) has to live, undisclosed. Finally, if eg really were context-neutral (+0.2%) while cache_read is 95.5% of tokens, the remaining 4.5% would have to fall ~24% to produce +1.35% overall; that is stated nowhere.\",\"evidence\":\"EG-FINAL-PLAN.md:28 ('38.6M / 38.5M / +0.2%'); :30-40 (table; baseline column sums 10.48+11.67+1.94+3.60+4.30+1.95+0.76+0.31 = 35.01M, eg column 33.44M); :43-44 ('3.77M gross', '2.80M', 'net 0.97M = +2.51%'); :14 ('cache_read is 95.5%')\",\"action\":\"Rebuild §2 from one reconciled ledger: publish the unclassified residual as its own row, fix the itemised net to 1.57M/+4.07%, and delete the '+0.2% context-neutral' claim or explain the 3.59M gap. §4's 62.4% addressable pool uses 38.6M as denominator and inherits the error.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"contradicts_existing\":true,\"verdict\":{\"refuted\":false,\"reason\":\"CONFIRMED on its core arithmetic, independently re-derived; two subsidiary sentences are wrong and must be dropped.\\n\\nVERIFIED EXACTLY (EG-FINAL-PLAN.md:30-40): baseline column = 35.0100M, eg column = 33.4400M, diff 1.5700M = 4.067% of 38.6M. Itemised paragraph (:43-44) parts also check: gross 3.7700M (src 2.23 + wholefile 2.47 - tests 0.93), adds 2.8000M (graph 1.70 + range 0.80 + logs 0.41 - misc 0.11), net 0.9700M = 2.513%. The harness row's 0.60M saving (4.30-&gt;3.70) is in neither the gross nor the adds; 0.97 + 0.60 = 1.57 exactly. Table shares are all computed on 38.6M and sum to 90.70%, so 3.59M (9.30%) is unlisted. Every figure in the claim's EVIDENCE line is real.\\n\\nSTRONGER THAN THE CLAIM KNEW. Line 60's own calibration ratios reconstruct: 0.54 = 1.35/2.513 (i.e. it is derived FROM the buggy 0.97M) and 7.33 = 1.35/0.1842, which pins the eg full total at 38.529M. That forces eg's unlisted residual to 5.089M vs baseline 3.59M -- a +1.50M (+41.8%) undisclosed growth. This is the missing reconciliation: classified saving 1.57M minus residual growth 1.50M = 0.07M = +0.18%, which rounds to the \\\"+0.2% context-neutral\\\" headline. So (a) and (c) are both true but at different scopes, and the fact that reconciles them -- that the entire classified saving is absorbed by growth in an unlisted bucket -- appears nowhere. Cross-checked against predecessor EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md:130-138 (coarser table, classifies 95.9%): the 3.59M residual = 1.60M never-classified + 1.96M lost when \\\"exploration 17.4M\\\" was split into five sub-rows summing 15.44M. Reconciles to 4 s.f.\\n\\nWRONG IN THE CLAIM (drop both): (i) \\\"§4's 62.4% pool uses 38.6M as denominator and inherits the error\\\" is FALSE -- 38.6M is the correct full-budget denominator and is conservative (35.01M would give a LARGER pool, 68.8%); §4's rows reconcile exactly against §3 (7.53M = 5.59 + 1.94; 5.18M = 1.29 + 3.89). (ii) The cache_read 95.5% inference is invalid by the document's own stated method at :58-62, which forbids converting model aggregates into token ratios; it also yields ~26%, not ~24%.\\n\\nCHECKS: (2) not in the closed list -- that list covers levers; §6.1's four open defects do not include this. (3) fairness N/A -- documentation-only, changes no prompt, tool or arm, so it cannot create arm asymmetry. (4) noise floor N/A -- this is arithmetic, not an effect estimate. But DECISION IMPACT IS ZERO: §5.1's +4.3-6.0% is computed from turns x tokens/turn and explicitly needs no calibration, and §4 uses the regression slope 0.822, which the doc already adopted INSTEAD of the contaminated 0.54. Credibility defect in the flagship document, not a conclusion defect. Fix it as a 5th entry in §6.1; do not re-open any lever on account of it.\",\"corrected_action\":\"Add as §6.1 open defect #5 (documentation integrity, no lever re-opens; zero effect on §5 or §8 recommendations). Rebuild §2 from one ledger with four changes: (1) add an explicit \\\"unclassified / other\\\" row -- baseline 3.59M (9.3%), eg 5.09M (13.2%) -- itemised at least into the 1.96M/2.77M that the \\\"exploration\\\" sub-split drops relative to EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md:132 and the 1.60M/2.32M never classified by either table; (2) fix the itemised net from 0.97M/+2.51% to 1.57M/+4.07% by including the harness saving of 0.60M, and label it \\\"classified categories only\\\"; (3) keep \\\"+0.2%\\\" but restate it as the full-budget figure (+0.18%, 38.600M vs 38.529M) and state the reconciliation explicitly -- the 1.57M classified saving is offset by +1.50M growth in the unclassified bucket -- since that offset, not the headline, is the substantive fact; (4) drop the 0.54 aggregate ratio at :60 or re-derive it, since it equals 1.35/2.513 and is computed from the erroneous 0.97M (the correct classified value gives 0.332); this is cosmetic only because the doc already discards 0.54 in favour of the regression slope 0.822. Do NOT touch §4 -- it does not inherit the error, its 38.6M denominator is correct and conservative, and its rows reconcile exactly against §3. Do NOT add the cache_read 95.5% argument -- it violates :58-62. State plainly in the revision that no number in §5 or §8 moves.\"}},{\"claim\":\"EG-FINAL-PLAN §4 contains an uncaught retraction remnant with its own arithmetic error, and a false summary of the session's corrections. Lines 115 and 140-141 close the coverage lever at '≈ +0.5%. Effectively closed.' Lines 157-159, in the same section, still derive it at '≈ +3.7%' from the pre-retraction chain — and that chain is also wrong on its own terms: 5.6M × 0.404 = 2.26M, ×0.822 = 1.86M = 4.8%, less 0.8M calibrated payload growth = 1.06M = 2.7%, not 3.7%. The two derivations differ only because line 158 silently drops the ×0.11 ranking-limited factor that lines 140-141 apply. Then §4's blockquote claims 'Five consecutive corrections this session, every one downward… Nothing has moved the other way' — false by item 3 of its own list: the 0.54 → 0.822 calibration RAISED every projection by ~52% (the doc itself says at :60-62 that the earlier draft 'understated every projection by ~35%'), and ROUTE §5 is headed 'Revised upward 2026-08-08'.\",\"evidence\":\"EG-FINAL-PLAN.md:115, :140-141 (+0.5%) vs :157-159 (+3.7%, arithmetic gives +2.7%); :192 ('every one downward… Nothing has moved the other way') vs :60-62 and EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md:199\",\"action\":\"Delete lines 157-159 (superseded draft text) and correct the blockquote to 'four downward, one upward'. The 'nothing has moved the other way' sentence is the doc's rhetorical anchor and is factually wrong.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"contradicts_existing\":false,\"verdict\":{\"refuted\":false,\"reason\":\"CONFIRMED on all three limbs; independently reproduced, not accepted on assertion.\\n\\n(1) EVIDENCE IS REAL. Opened /Users/suhaan/d