{"parentUuid":"e769121a-6c5c-4119-b7d2-46c02efe383f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"96e03687-14c7-40a5-93eb-a483d24f1540","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W8CKAxyTVSok8ETVtxwPqR","type":"tool_result","content":"##### LENS: Canonical ledger (TokensNotes.md) + memory directory — reconciliation against the rep50 facts  — The ledger's governing premise (\"tokens are messages\") and two of its three LIVE items are refuted by the rep50 facts; the one genuinely live lever (R-A) is deployed on a tool branch that lacks the em\n  [high] TokensNotes §0 'Tokens are messages… nothing inside a message can move the metric' is the ledger's stated hard constraint and is contradicted by the same cell it was written for. The related claim in the fact set, 'the graph WORKS\n        -> Rewrite TokensNotes §0 as 'log(tok)~log(msgs) is a between-session regression, not a within-pair mechanism; the rep50 saving is context density, not message count.' Re-de\n  [high] Two of the ledger's three LIVE items (§1.2 'one call must remove more than one message', §1.3 'harness suppression') are already closed by the facts and must move to §2 STRUCK. §1.2 additionally states a substitution rate that con\n        -> Strike §1.2 and §1.3 with those reasons. §1.1 (MOD/ADD) then becomes the ledger's ONLY surviving LIVE item, which should be stated explicitly so the next session does not\n  [high] MOD vs ADD (§1.1) is the only ledger LIVE item the facts do not close — but it has never been subjected to the one test that killed the rep50 headline. The headline died to leave-one-out (drop lombok-3674 → −5.18%); the MOD pool h\n        -> Before spending anything on a classifier: re-score the existing MOD and ADD pools offline ($0) with drop-1, winsorised 20/80 and 10% trimmed means, and check whether lomb\n  [high] The fact set treats the VERIFY runnability probe as unbuilt ('only checked with exec.LookPath, never run — add a collect-only probe'). It is built, wired, and has already been measured in a 100-instance cell.\n        -> Do not rebuild it. Record in TokensNotes that EG_VERIFY_PROBE exists and was measured; its ceiling is bounded by its 17/86 firing rate, not by its design. The only untrie\n  [high] The ledger strikes prefetch (§2.11) using a rationale that is R-A's design goal, not a defect — so R-A is a repair of an already-measured-null prefetch, and its mechanism gate has already been observed to pass. The ledger and memo\n        -> Rewrite §2.11's strike as 'struck on the wrong metric; superseded by R-A (EG_PRESEARCH)'. Gate the next R-A cell on the mechanism count (graph calls/session → ~0), not on\n  [high] R-A's tool-side delivery path ships the zero-byte silent failure the campaign already lost a day to. The guard that fixes it is not on the checked-out branch.\n        -> Do not launch any R-A cell from this tree. Land 8a4ffb3's guard (or merge #82) first, and add a preflight assertion that the presearch file is non-empty — TokensNotes §5 \n  [high] Three confirmed answer leaks plus an unfixed repo-cache leak are recorded in memory, are eg-favouring, and appear in NEITHER the fact set nor EG-FINAL-PLAN's open-defect list. Direction matters: closing them moves the headline dow\n        -> Add the four leaks to EG-FINAL-PLAN §6.1 and to the standing pre-cell checklist in benchmark-arm-fairness-bugs.md. State in any writeup that the fair number is bounded AB\n  [medium] Two memory items will actively misroute the next Opus cell and are not covered by the facts: (i) the machine-state two-regime result is unstruck and is the only Opus interval in the corpus whose upper bound reaches 35%, and (ii) a\n        -> Retire bench-run-constraints.md and graphify-arm-queued.md; re-title the two MEMORY.md index lines as SUPERSEDED. Add 'record baseline mean tokens + turns per cell' to th\n\n##### LENS: Plan-document audit: EG-FINAL-PLAN.md, EG-ROUTE-TO-35.md, PREREG-FABLE82.md — internal consistency, over-claiming, and uncaught supersession by the LOO/median/trimmed-mean result  — Every live number in the three plans — the ceiling band, the context budget, and R-A itself — is anchored to the +1.35% total that the LOO/median/trimmed-mean result kills, and R-A (the one item marke\n  [high] R-A's +4.3–6.0% is an INCREMENT on a base the LOO/median now show is negative, but it is presented as a LEVEL and drives the SHIP decision. §5.1 states the counterfactual 'reproduces +1.35% exactly at zero removal' — i.e. it is ex\n        -> Strike the §4 ceiling table and re-issue every projection as a delta against the median (−4.16%), not the total. Remove the R-A+R-B row entirely. Re-run the R-A counterfa\n  [high] R-A is priced entirely in the message model that EG-FINAL-PLAN §1 retires two pages earlier. §1 says 'the saving is not a message saving' and 'the metric is context, not messages'; §5.1 then computes R-A as turns × tokens/turn wit\n        -> Re-price R-A in the persist-token model: compute the payload's turn-0 persist cost against its observed mid-session cost, and net the −2.07-turn displacement lost on the \n  [high] Both documents cite the only live, paired, replicated measurement of prefetch for its favourable half and omit its headline. The harness comment they cite says the payload made turns cheaper (30,302 → 29,334 tok/turn, −3.2%) AND t\n        -> Quote the prefetch measurement in full in both docs, add an induced-reads row to the §5.1 sensitivity table, and state that the only live prefetch cell measured net +3.0%\n  [high] EG-FINAL-PLAN §2 states three mutually inconsistent context totals for the same table. (a) 'Baseline 38.6M. eg 38.5M. context-neutral (+0.2%)'. (b) The itemised paragraph gives net 0.97M = +2.51%. (c) The table's own columns sum t\n        -> Rebuild §2 from one reconciled ledger: publish the unclassified residual as its own row, fix the itemised net to 1.57M/+4.07%, and delete the '+0.2% context-neutral' clai\n  [high] EG-FINAL-PLAN §4 contains an uncaught retraction remnant with its own arithmetic error, and a false summary of the session's corrections. Lines 115 and 140-141 close the coverage lever at '≈ +0.5%. Effectively closed.' Lines 157-1\n        -> Delete lines 157-159 (superseded draft text) and correct the blockquote to 'four downward, one upward'. The 'nothing has moved the other way' sentence is the doc's rhetor\n  [high] EG-ROUTE §0's headline ratio is contradicted by its own §1 table, and its conclusion was never struck after §2A retracted it. §0 says 'net messages saved (103 − 94) = 9' — but §1's table includes edits (−17) and reads (+2), so the\n        -> Strike §0 in full and re-derive it from the corrected classifier: net −37 messages → law predicts −2.3%, which is now the doc's own best structural estimate and agrees wi\n  [high] The claims doing the heaviest killing rest on subgroups far below the docs' own stated MDE, in violation of a rule the same docs state. 'Retrieval/ranking is anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5)' is n=13 (Fi\n        -> Demote the 6/8-vs-2/5 ranking claim to 'not tested' — it cannot support closing a lever at p≈0.29, and it is currently load-bearing for both §5.2 and §6.3. Replace the ou\n  [high] PREREG-FABLE82 is underpowered for its own PASS criterion and mis-sizes its launch. (a) '~90 pairs to land 82' is inconsistent with its own stated 24% pilot loss: 90 × 0.76 = 68 gated pairs, not 82; landing 82 needs ~108 launched.\n        -> Before launch: raise the launch count to ~108, and either lower the PASS threshold to what n=82 can actually resolve or restate the cell as powered only for ≥+14.6%. Move\n\n##### LENS: entire-graph tool source: search / verify / payload-construction paths  — There is no meaningful byte lever left in the renderer (payloads are 79.9% source, 3,680 B mean, ~0.6% of session spend) — but the one block designed to pre-answer post-edit sibling-site exploration (\n  [high] RELATED SITES — the only payload block that names 'the other places this change has to land' — cannot be emitted at all when --top-k <= 5, which is exactly what the headline cell ran. It is not rare, not ranking-dependent, not a t\n        -> Raise EG_TOPK from 5 to 8 in the eg arm (harness one-liner, no rebuild), OR decouple the related block from the ranking floor in source so it is budgeted independently. B\n  [high] `entire graph verify` exists — a purpose-built adjudicated post-edit verdict verb explicitly designed to close the phase where 97.7% of the excess cost lands — and it was NOT in the binary the headline cell executed. The capabilit\n        -> Before any adjudication cell, pin O35_EG_BIN (and EG/EGI) to bin/entire-graph-f4 or a fresh build, and assert the verb exists (`$EG verify` exits non-zero with a usage er\n  [high] run_3arm.sh's DEFAULT entire-graph binary is missing every payload feature added in the last several releases, so any cell run without an explicit ENTIRE_GRAPH override measures a tool that no longer exists.\n        -> Change the run_3arm.sh default to the pinned bin, or add a hard preflight gate on `entire graph capabilities --json` that aborts the cell when the binary lacks the featur\n  [high] The binary hard-codes arm-asymmetric GENERIC METHODOLOGY advice into the search payload, and the only way to remove it is a downstream grep in the harness whose default is OFF. The headline cell happened to have it on; every cell \n        -> Move the switch into the binary (a `--no-advice` flag, defaulted OFF for measurement builds) so fairness does not depend on a grep list in a wrapper. Keep the harness's i\n  [high] Part (c) of this lens is closed: there is no cheap byte reduction available. Emitted payload is dominated by source snippets, and all removable scaffolding together is worth a fraction of one turn.\n        -> Stop spending effort on renderer byte-trimming; redirect it to what the payload PREVENTS (a whole-file Read costs 98k persist each, 7x any other class). Any future propos\n  [high] `search --format` defaults to `json`, which is 1.79x the text payload — and the doctrine file agents actually read prescribes the command WITHOUT `--format`, so every real (non-benchmark) agent invocation gets the fat form.\n        -> Either flip the parser default to `text` (json remains available explicitly, and --format agent/ndjson are unaffected) or add `--format text` to the doctrine line. Zero b\n  [high] The binary's own zero-toll delivery (EG_PRESEARCH) and one-search-per-task echo (EG_SEARCH_SESSION / EG_MAX_SEARCHES) are dead code in the benchmark path — the wrapper reimplements the first and nothing sets the second — so R-A's \n        -> When R-A is written up, attribute the effect to the harness wrapper and state that shipping it requires a binary that contains internal/cli/search.go:286 — otherwise the \n\n##### LENS: benchmark harness (/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench): arm-fairness, measurement defects, gate integrity  — The rep50 prompt path is clean, but the harness silently discards ~18% of all sessions whose token data still exists on disk, its pass/fail gate is content-blind (a 1.9 MB patch of the agent's own com\n  [high] 287 of ~1,560 local arm-sessions produce no usage data and are dropped with their PAIR, yet their token counts survive verbatim in Claude Code transcripts. 132 of 133 zero-byte cc_out.json have an EMPTY cc_err.log — the signature \n        -> Run recover_from_transcripts.py over every rep50 corpse and re-score; make it a mandatory pre-scoring step. This is the only free source of n on the table — the power not\n  [high] LATENT ARM ASYMMETRY, environment not instructions: the eg arm alone runs the repo's real test command before the session, and the harness deliberately keeps the resulting build tree. `restore_checkout` excludes target/build/.grad\n        -> Not active in rep50 (tools/run_r100.sh:77 `export EG_PREFETCH=0` kills the whole block) — do not re-open closed cells. But R-A / EG_PRESEARCH requires prefetch ON. Before\n  [high] The gate's patch check is a byte-count, so it admits arbitrarily large junk. 20 patches over 100 KB passed it locally, worst 2.95 MB. The Opus cell's eg arm shipped 1,892,106 B / 1,708 files for gson-2479 that are almost entirely \n        -> Add `*.class/*.o/*.a/*.jar/*.pyc` and the missing build/dist/target/.claude/.entire/*.log excludes to the tracked pathspec, and make the untracked case arms case-insensit\n  [high] REFUTES a natural hypothesis I tested: the strict gate is NOT inflating the headline. Removing it entirely moves the pooled local total by −0.15 pt. Its cost is sample size and power, not sign.\n        -> Stop treating gate leniency as a candidate explanation for +1.35%; spend the effort on sample recovery (finding 1) instead. Report this number in TokensNotes as a closed \n  [medium] Turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed toward eg: the eg arm hits `error_max_turns` 2.75x more often than the baseline, and every one of those pairs is deleted by the gate. Those are eg's worst sessions, so the deletion flatters eg.\n        -> Report max-turns truncations as a censoring line beside every headline (count per arm), and treat a truncated session as a LOSS for its arm at the cap rather than deletin\n  [high] The one-armed-advice filter is currently COMPLETE against the pinned binary — I verified it rather than assuming — but it is a 9-pattern literal grep coupled to wording in a different repo with no test, and the coupling has alread\n        -> Replace the literal list with a generated one: emit the binary's advice constants from entire-graph as a data file the harness reads, or add a CI assertion that every `se\n  [medium] Two smaller integrity gaps in the scorer and one order-dependent affordance race, all currently inert or low-volume but each capable of flipping a cell.\n        -> Point whatever scorer produced the rep50 headline (sc50.py, not present in this tree) at tools/armcfg.py:marker_reasons so all scorers agree; make the oracle-leak scan ru\n  [medium] A wall-clock cutoff censors the token distribution at exactly the right tail where the arms differ, and the default is below what real Opus sessions need.\n        -> Confirm what CC_TIMEOUT rep50 actually ran with before quoting the headline; if it was 1400, the tail was truncated and the paired sd of 0.494 is an underestimate. Set CC\n\n\n=== refuter tally: 3 not-refuted, 28 refuted ===","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"708e15f2-0464-4c75-9d68-e0df1b807f9a","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:19:47.942Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"##### LENS: Canonical ledger (TokensNotes.md) + memory directory — reconciliation against the rep50 facts  — The ledger's governing premise (\"tokens are messages\") and two of its three LIVE items are refuted by the rep50 facts; the one genuinely live lever (R-A) is deployed on a tool branch that lacks the em\n  [high] TokensNotes §0 'Tokens are messages… nothing inside a message can move the metric' is the ledger's stated hard constraint and is contradicted by the same cell it was written for. The related claim in the fact set, 'the graph WORKS\n        -> Rewrite TokensNotes §0 as 'log(tok)~log(msgs) is a between-session regression, not a within-pair mechanism; the rep50 saving is context density, not message count.' Re-de\n  [high] Two of the ledger's three LIVE items (§1.2 'one call must remove more than one message', §1.3 'harness suppression') are already closed by the facts and must move to §2 STRUCK. §1.2 additionally states a substitution rate that con\n        -> Strike §1.2 and §1.3 with those reasons. §1.1 (MOD/ADD) then becomes the ledger's ONLY surviving LIVE item, which should be stated explicitly so the next session does not\n  [high] MOD vs ADD (§1.1) is the only ledger LIVE item the facts do not close — but it has never been subjected to the one test that killed the rep50 headline. The headline died to leave-one-out (drop lombok-3674 → −5.18%); the MOD pool h\n        -> Before spe