{"parentUuid":"bc3f867c-4140-4538-bf65-d33770351317","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqk5CMMWSpZg5m4E9kiS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6710,"cache_read_input_tokens":861271,"output_tokens":7347,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6710,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7347,"cache_read_input_tokens":861271,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6710},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqk4xpm7yXEGPBKubXFC","type":"assistant","uuid":"3d8e18de-4e5f-4d1f-9cfb-c6c3cedd34d4","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:20:18.052Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"3d8e18de-4e5f-4d1f-9cfb-c6c3cedd34d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqk5CMMWSpZg5m4E9kiS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five investigations are in. The audit found real errors in my own documents — including one that's a straight overreach. Writing the final plan now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6710,"cache_read_input_tokens":861271,"output_tokens":7347,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6710,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7347,"cache_read_input_tokens":861271,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6710},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqk4xpm7yXEGPBKubXFC","type":"assistant","uuid":"54c9f296-97b4-429d-8754-bfbfbc6a610b","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:20:19.098Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"54c9f296-97b4-429d-8754-bfbfbc6a610b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdqk5CMMWSpZg5m4E9kiS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GHMkbLY7DVGyXBy2zFtAZb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","content":"# entire-graph on Opus — final plan\n\n## Context\n\nThe goal was **35% token savings on rep50, Opus, fairly measured**. You later relaxed it to the\nright target: **stop the tool making instances worse** — a code graph should not lose. This plan\nis built against that, after five investigations (two loser dissections, a capability inventory,\na 4-lens artifact audit, and an iterative fix workflow) totalling ~4.5M subagent tokens.\n\n**The headline finding is not about the tool.** It is that the measurement has ~287 recoverable\nsessions, an arm-skewed censoring rule, a content-blind gate, and four eg-favouring leaks — and\nthat the one payload block designed to answer the question losing tasks actually ask **could not\nfire in the headline cell at all**.\n\nSign convention: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.** All figures rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is true on Opus\n\n| estimator | value |\n|---|---|\n| total (the reported headline) | +1.35% |\n| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n| median | **−4.16%** |\n| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |\n| t | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n\n**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. Never quote +1.35% without\nthe LOO range and the median beside it.\n\n**And the fair number is bounded ABOVE by this one.** Four eg-favouring leaks are recorded and\nunfixed (§5). Closing them moves the headline **down**, not up.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Corrections to my own work — the full list\n\nRecorded so they are not re-derived, and because most are mine.\n\n1. **\"eg verifies more than baseline\"** — false. eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576. The claim\n   came from the 8 worst losers, a set selected on the outcome.\n2. **\"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\"** — regex artifact. A stricter definition gives n=17\n   and **−0.89%**.\n3. **\"the metric rewards failing to provision\"** — real on `bat-1892` only; **2 of 25 losers**,\n   worth −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.\n4. **\"+35.06% reachable by loser repair\"** — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.\n5. **×0.54 persist calibration** — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**\n   (corr +0.916, R² 0.839). **This one moved projections UP by ~52%.**\n6. **\"Five consecutive corrections, every one downward… nothing has moved the other way\"** —\n   **false, by item 5 above.** It was four downward and one upward. That sentence was rhetorical\n   overreach and is withdrawn.\n7. **R-A zero-toll at +4.3% to +6.0%** — mispriced by **5.2×**. The first search lands at assistant\n   turn median 2 of a median 85-turn session where `cache_read` is 12,231 vs a session mean of\n   63,137. Correct value **+0.96%**, CI [+0.53, +1.38]; n to demonstrate ≈ **19,504 pairs**.\n   It was also priced in the message model that §1 of my own document retires.\n8. **The VERIFY collect-only probe as a new fix** — `EG_VERIFY_PROBE=1` was **already set in\n   `run_REP50.sh:141`** and live during rep50. Also a no-op on 84% of drag (21/25 losers got no\n   VERIFY line).\n9. **\"Retrieval/ranking is anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5)\"** — this is\n   **n=13, p≈0.29**. It cannot support closing a lever, and it was load-bearing in two sections.\n   Demoted to **not tested**.\n10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the\n    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is\n    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Why instances lose\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances; lift +21.21 over 24; `lombok-3674` alone +6.09 (29% of lift).**\n\n| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n| post-edit exploration | +159 | −81 |\n| post-edit harness | +50 | −88 |\n| turns | +296 | −258 |\n\n**The graph works pre-edit in BOTH groups.** Localization is not the discriminator.\n\n**The discriminator is displacement:** label a session displaced if eg's shell-exploration count is\nbelow its paired baseline. **Displaced & won 19/21 (90.5%); not-displaced & won 6/28 (21.4%);\nAUC 0.838.** Sessions that call the graph: pooled **+6.30%**, median +12.61%. The 16 that never\ncall it: pooled −1.02%, median **−24.94%**. **Calling and displacing is the winning behaviour.**\n\n**Task kind is the largest single concentration:** independent gold-patch labeller gives\ngold-MOD n=36 **+13.59%**, gold-ADD n=13 **−23.19%**. **Gold-ADD is 8 of 25 drag instances and\n−10.68 of the −19.86 drag points — 54% of all drag.** Caveat: **GEM300 inverts the sign**\n(MOD −14.13%, ADD +0.86%), and the MOD/ADD pools have **never been LOO-tested** — the same test\nthat killed the headline. Do that first, offline, before spending anything on it.\n\n**Neither repo nor language predicts outcome.** Language R² = **0.153**; only **5 of 14** repos\nwith >1 instance are internally consistent (`laravel` = [+51, −5, −59, −124, +39]). Per-repo or\nper-language configs are not viable, which is why the ledger already struck that lever.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What to actually do — ranked\n\nEvery item is tool output or harness hygiene. None adds an instruction.\n\n### 4.1 `EG_TOPK` 5 → 8 *(harness one-liner, no rebuild)* — **highest value**\n**RELATED SITES — the only payload block that names \"the other places this change has to land\" —\ncannot be emitted at all when `--top-k <= 5`.** rep50 ran `EG_TOPK=5`. So the block designed to\nanswer the completeness question that ADD tasks actually ask **never fired in the headline cell**.\nThis is not ranking, not a new verb, and not a payload-quality metric; it is a block that was\nswitched off by a numeric floor.\n\n### 4.2 Fix `graph grep`: exclude vendored / minified / generated *(NEGATIVE bytes)*\nIt shells to `grep -rInE` over the worktree and filters **only tests**. On `prometheus-9248` it\nreturned one hit inside minified vendored `d3.v3.js` where plain grep returned a **clean zero** —\nand a clean zero is actionable, one noise hit is not. Baseline pivoted on move 2 and found the fix\nsite; eg reached it at call 21. **~19 turns lost. The only measured case of the graph being worse\nthan no tool at all**, and the fix removes bytes.\n\n### 4.3 Recover the 287 dropped sessions *($0, and it is the only free power on the table)*\n**287 of ~1,560 arm-sessions produce no usage data and are dropped WITH THEIR PAIR — but their\ntoken counts survive verbatim in the Claude Code transcripts.** 132 of 133 zero-byte `cc_out.json`\nhave an **empty** `cc_err.log`. Recovering them is a scoring change, not a cell.\n\n### 4.4 Fix two gate defects that currently flatter eg\n- **Turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed:** eg hits `error_max_turns` **2.75× more often** than\n  baseline, and every such pair is deleted. Those are eg's *worst* sessions. Report censoring per\n  arm beside every headline; treat a truncated session as a loss at the cap rather than deleting it.\n- **The patch gate is a byte count**, so it admits junk: 20 patches over 100 KB passed, worst\n  2.95 MB; eg shipped **1,892,106 B across 1,708 files** on `gson-2479`. Add `*.class/*.o/*.jar/\n  *.pyc/build/dist/target` excludes.\n- *(Verified NOT a problem: gate strictness is not inflating the headline — removing it entirely\n  moves the pooled total by −0.15 pt.)*\n\n### 4.5 Ship FILE OUTLINE by default *(+1,421 B, ~8× return)*\n`internal/sem/search_outline.go` (217 LOC), flag `cli/search.go:1637` — **default OFF, absent from\n`printHelp`**. Its own measurement: 77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload had already\nnamed; 35 were immediately followed by a Read of that same file.\n\n### 4.6 `search --format` default json → text *(1.79× byte reduction for real users)*\nThe parser defaults to `json`, which is **1.79× the text payload**, and the doctrine file agents\nactually read prescribes the command **without** `--format`. Every real (non-benchmark) invocation\ngets the fat form. Zero risk: `json` stays available explicitly.\n\n### 4.7 Binary and default hygiene *(preflight, not a lever)*\n- **`run_3arm.sh`'s default binary is missing every payload feature added in recent releases** —\n  any cell without an explicit `ENTIRE_GRAPH` override measures a tool that no longer exists.\n- **`entire graph verify` was not in the binary the headline cell executed.**\n- The in-tree binary is **stale** (rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`). Rebuild before anything.\n- Add a hard preflight gate on `entire graph capabilities --json` that aborts when the binary lacks\n  the features the cell assumes.\n\n### 4.8 Move the advice switch into the binary\nThe binary **hard-codes arm-asymmetric generic methodology advice** into the payload, and the only\nway to remove it is a 9-pattern literal grep in the harness whose default is OFF. rep50 happened to\nhave it on. Fairness must not depend on a grep list in another repo — add `--no-advice`, defaulted\noff for measurement builds.\n\n### 4.9 DO NOT BUILD — all refuted this session\n| | why |\n|---|---|\n| R-A zero-toll as a token lever | +0.96%, needs 19,504 pairs; and it removes the call in the cohort where calling *wins* |\n| VERIFY collect-only probe | already shipped and ON in rep50; no-op on 84% of drag |\n| MOD/ADD structural router | doesn't separate offline; `exact-symbol` already printed, identical on ADD and MOD (0.36 vs 0.36) |\n| post-edit consistency hook | its fair form's biggest beneficiary is the *baseline* in `lombok-3674` = 29% of lift |\n| new verb in the affordance tail | 0/66 adoption |\n| anything needing a post-edit agent call | 42/49 sessions make none |\n| better ranking · bigger payloads · graph-backed grep · renderer byte-trimming | closed; payload is 79.9% source, ~0.6% of session spend |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Integrity — before any cell\n\n1. **Four eg-favouring answer leaks** are recorded in memory and unfixed. `bat-1892` (worst loser,\n   −2.81 pts) made **12 references into `bat-3108`**, a later revision of the same repo containing\n   the implemented feature. Measured: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline.** Direction matters —\n   closing these moves the headline **down**.\n2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells** — `prometheus-9248` audited `/tmp/goyacc*` built by\n   other instances' sessions. eg 3/49, base 1/49. Give each session a private temp root.\n3. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.\n4. **`CC_TIMEOUT`** may have censored the right tail; if rep50 ran at 1400 s the paired sd of 0.494\n   is an **underestimate** and every power calculation here is optimistic.\n5. **`echoPresearchPayload` has no length check** (`cli/search.go:286`) — a zero-byte payload gives\n   0 bytes on stdout with exit 0, the \"announced but never shipped\" failure class. The guard exists\n   on another branch and is not on this tree.\n\n**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, 0 commit mismatches, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches small,\nprompt diff 18 lines all of which are checkout paths.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gates\n\nMDE ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between cells.\n**No token claim below n≈50 in either direction.**\n\n| gate | n | criterion |\n|---|---|---|\n| **V0** offline $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; RELATED SITES fires at TOPK=8 on recorded queries; grep returns a clean zero on the prometheus query; 287 sessions recovered and re-scored |\n| **V1** offline $0 | 49 | LOO / winsorised / trimmed re-score of the MOD and ADD pools — does MOD survive the test that killed the headline? |\n| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: **displacement rate** (eg shell calls < paired baseline) up from 21/49; RELATED SITES present in payloads; no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |\n| **V3** live | 50+ | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together**, plus per-arm censoring counts |\n\n**Winner tripwire (your instruction: abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,\n`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` in every sample from V2. Compare only against a **same-wave**\ncontrol — never a previous cell.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Honest expected outcome\n\n**No number is promised.** The two items with a real mechanism and no prior art are §4.1 (RELATED\nSITES was structurally off) and §4.2 (grep noise where a clean zero existed). Both are cheap, both\nare fair, and neither has been measured. Everything else in §4 is hygiene that makes the *next*\nmeasurement trustworthy rather than moving the current one.\n\n**The ceiling on loser repair is +21.21%** — arithmetic (the lift pool), not projection.\n**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change**; the only intervention that would reach it is\nan instruction to explore and re-test less, which helps a no-tool arm equally and is exactly what\nthe withdrawn −35% contained.\n\n**If §4.1 and §4.2 do not move the displacement rate at V2, the honest conclusion is that\nentire-graph is not a token tool on this corpus** — and the defensible claim becomes correctness\nand latency, plus whole-file-read suppression (119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B), which is\nmeasurable at n=49 today.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Verification\n\n- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO for\n  tree-sitter). **Rebuild the binary — it is stale.** Unit tests beside the grep filter.\n- Offline replay: `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log` + `.payload`; re-run against the binary at\n  zero model cost; assert the change fires **and** that nothing else moved.\n- Harness deploys by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a script\n  a running session is reading.\n- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** trimmed **and** LOO **and** Δturns **and**\n  per-arm censoring counts.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6710,"cache_read_input_tokens":861271,"output_tokens":7347,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6710,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7347,"cache_read_input_tokens":861271,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6710},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdqk4xpm7yXEGPBKubXFC","type":"assistant","uuid":"9f96945c-8dfa-402c-9361-8fb77e1d1d6c","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:21:27.328Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"9f96945c-8dfa-402c-9361-8fb77e1d1d6c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"96e03687-14c7-40a5-93eb-a483d24f1540","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GHMkbLY7DVGyXBy2zFtAZb","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"1052aa20-b784-48d2-acdd-e2273cb5be82","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:21:27.366Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","content":"# entire-graph on Opus — final plan\n\n## Context\n\nThe goal was **35% token savings on rep50, Opus, fairly measured**. You later relaxed it to the\nright target: **stop the tool making instances worse** — a code graph should not lose. This plan\nis built against that, after five investigations (two loser dissections, a capability inventory,\na 4-lens artifact audit, and an iterative fix workflow) totalling ~4.5M subagent tokens.\n\n**The headline finding is not about the tool.** It is that the measurement has ~287 recoverable\nsessions, an arm-skewed censoring rule, a content-blind gate, and four eg-favouring leaks — and\nthat the one payload block designed to answer the question losing tasks actually ask **could not\nfire in the headline cell at all**.\n\nSign convention: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.** All figures rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is true on Opus\n\n| estimator | value |\n|---|---|\n| total (the reported headline) | +1.35% |\n| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n| median | **−4.16%** |\n| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |\n| t | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n\n**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. Never quote +1.35% without\nthe LOO range and the median beside it.\n\n**And the fair number is bounded ABOVE by this one.** Four eg-favouring leaks are recorded and\nunfixed (§5). Closing them moves the headline **down**, not up.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Corrections to my own work — the full list\n\nRecorded so they are not re-derived, and because most are mine.\n\n1. **\"eg verifies more than baseline\"** — false. eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576. The claim\n   came from the 8 worst losers, a set selected on the outcome.\n2. **\"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\"** — regex artifact. A stricter definition gives n=17\n   and **−0.89%**.\n3. **\"the metric rewards failing to provision\"** — real on `bat-1892` only; **2 of 25 losers**,\n   worth −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.\n4. **\"+35.06% reachable by loser repair\"** — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.\n5. **×0.54 persist calibration** — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**\n   (corr +0.916, R² 0.839). **This one moved projections UP by ~52%.**\n6. **\"Five consecutive corrections, every one downward… nothing has moved the other way\"** —\n   **false, by item 5 above.** It was four downward and one upward. That sentence was rhetorical\n   overreach and is withdrawn.\n7. **R-A zero-toll at +4.3% to +6.0%** — mispriced by **5.2×**. The first search lands at assistant\n   turn median 2 of a median 85-turn session where `cache_read` is 12,231 vs a session mean of\n   63,137. Correct value **+0.96%**, CI [+0.53, +1.38]; n to demonstrate ≈ **19,504 pairs**.\n   It was also priced in the message model that §1 of my own document retires.\n8. **The VERIFY collect-only probe as a new fix** — `EG_VERIFY_PROBE=1` was **already set in\n   `run_REP50.sh:141`** and live during rep50. Also a no-op on 84% of drag (21/25 losers got no\n   VERIFY line).\n9. **\"Retrieval/ranking is anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5)\"** — this is\n   **n=13, p≈0.29**. It cannot support closing a lever, and it was load-bearing in two sections.\n   Demoted to **not tested**.\n10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the\n    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is\n    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Why instances lose\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances; lift +21.21 over 24; `lombok-3674` alone +6.09 (29% of lift).**\n\n| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n| post-edit exploration | +159 | −81 |\n| post-edit harness | +50 | −88 |\n| turns | +296 | −258 |\n\n**The graph works pre-edit in BOTH groups.** Localization is not the discriminator.\n\n**The discriminator is displacement:** label a session displaced if eg's shell-exploration count is\nbelow its paired baseline. **Displaced & won 19/21 (90.5%); not-displaced & won 6/28 (21.4%);\nAUC 0.838.** Sessions that call the graph: pooled **+6.30%**, median +12.61%. The 16 that never\ncall it: pooled −1.02%, median **−24.94%**. **Calling and displacing is the winning behaviour.**\n\n**Task kind is the largest single concentration:** independent gold-patch labeller gives\ngold-MOD n=36 **+13.59%**, gold-ADD n=13 **−23.19%**. **Gold-ADD is 8 of 25 drag instances and\n−10.68 of the −19.86 drag points — 54% of all drag.** Caveat: **GEM300 inverts the sign**\n(MOD −14.13%, ADD +0.86%), and the MOD/ADD pools have **never been LOO-tested** — the same test\nthat killed the headline. Do that first, offline, before spending anything on it.\n\n**Neither repo nor language predicts outcome.** Language R² = **0.153**; only **5 of 14** repos\nwith >1 instance are internally consistent (`laravel` = [+51, −5, −59, −124, +39]). Per-repo or\nper-language configs are not viable, which is why the ledger already struck that lever.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What to actually do — ranked\n\nEvery item is tool output or harness hygiene. None adds an instruction.\n\n### 4.1 `EG_TOPK` 5 → 8 *(harness one-liner, no rebuild)* — **highest value**\n**RELATED SITES — the only payload block that names \"the other places this change has to land\" —\ncannot be emitted at all when `--top-k <= 5`.** rep50 ran `EG_TOPK=5`. So the block designed to\nanswer the completeness question that ADD tasks actually ask **never fired in the headline cell**.\nThis is not ranking, not a new verb, and not a payload-quality metric; it is a block that was\nswitched off by a numeric floor.\n\n### 4.2 Fix `graph grep`: exclude vendored / minified / generated *(NEGATIVE bytes)*\nIt shells to `grep -rInE` over the worktree and filters **only tests**. On `prometheus-9248` it\nreturned one hit inside minified vendored `d3.v3.js` where plain grep returned a **clean zero** —\nand a clean zero is actionable, one noise hit is not. Baseline pivoted on move 2 and found the fix\nsite; eg reached it at call 21. **~19 turns lost. The only measured case of the graph being worse\nthan no tool at all**, and the fix removes bytes.\n\n### 4.3 Recover the 287 dropped sessions *($0, and it is the only free power on the table)*\n**287 of ~1,560 arm-sessions produce no usage data and are dropped WITH THEIR PAIR — but their\ntoken counts survive verbatim in the Claude Code transcripts.** 132 of 133 zero-byte `cc_out.json`\nhave an **empty** `cc_err.log`. Recovering them is a scoring change, not a cell.\n\n### 4.4 Fix two gate defects that currently flatter eg\n- **Turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed:** eg hits `error_max_turns` **2.75× more often** than\n  baseline, and every such pair is deleted. Those are eg's *worst* sessions. Report censoring per\n  arm beside every headline; treat a truncated session as a loss at the cap rather than deleting it.\n- **The patch gate is a byte count**, so it admits junk: 20 patches over 100 KB passed, worst\n  2.95 MB; eg shipped **1,892,106 B across 1,708 files** on `gson-2479`. Add `*.class/*.o/*.jar/\n  *.pyc/build/dist/target` excludes.\n- *(Verified NOT a problem: gate strictness is not inflating the headline — removing it entirely\n  moves the pooled total by −0.15 pt.)*\n\n### 4.5 Ship FILE OUTLINE by default *(+1,421 B, ~8× return)*\n`internal/sem/search_outline.go` (217 LOC), flag `cli/search.go:1637` — **default OFF, absent from\n`printHelp`**. Its own measurement: 77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload had already\nnamed; 35 were immediately followed by a Read of that same file.\n\n### 4.6 `search --format` default json → text *(1.79× byte reduction for real users)*\nThe parser defaults to `json`, which is **1.79× the text payload**, and the doctrine file agents\nactually read prescribes the command **without** `--format`. Every real (non-benchmark) invocation\ngets the fat form. Zero risk: `json` stays available explicitly.\n\n### 4.7 Binary and default hygiene *(preflight, not a lever)*\n- **`run_3arm.sh`'s default binary is missing every payload feature added in recent releases** —\n  any cell without an explicit `ENTIRE_GRAPH` override measures a tool that no longer exists.\n- **`entire graph verify` was not in the binary the headline cell executed.**\n- The in-tree binary is **stale** (rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`). Rebuild before anything.\n- Add a hard preflight gate on `entire graph capabilities --json` that aborts when the binary lacks\n  the features the cell assumes.\n\n### 4.8 Move the advice switch into the binary\nThe binary **hard-codes arm-asymmetric generic methodology advice** into the payload, and the only\nway to remove it is a 9-pattern literal grep in the harness whose default is OFF. rep50 happened to\nhave it on. Fairness must not depend on a grep list in another repo — add `--no-advice`, defaulted\noff for measurement builds.\n\n### 4.9 DO NOT BUILD — all refuted this session\n| | why |\n|---|---|\n| R-A zero-toll as a token lever | +0.96%, needs 19,504 pairs; and it removes the call in the cohort where calling *wins* |\n| VERIFY collect-only probe | already shipped and ON in rep50; no-op on 84% of drag |\n| MOD/ADD structural router | doesn't separate offline; `exact-symbol` already printed, identical on ADD and MOD (0.36 vs 0.36) |\n| post-edit consistency hook | its fair form's biggest beneficiary is the *baseline* in `lombok-3674` = 29% of lift |\n| new verb in the affordance tail | 0/66 adoption |\n| anything needing a post-edit agent call | 42/49 sessions make none |\n| better ranking · bigger payloads · graph-backed grep · renderer byte-trimming | closed; payload is 79.9% source, ~0.6% of session spend |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Integrity — before any cell\n\n1. **Four eg-favouring answer leaks** are recorded in memory and unfixed. `bat-1892` (worst loser,\n   −2.81 pts) made **12 references into `bat-3108`**, a later revision of the same repo containing\n   the implemented feature. Measured: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline.** Direction matters —\n   closing these moves the headline **down**.\n2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells** — `prometheus-9248` audited `/tmp/goyacc*` built by\n   other instances' sessions. eg 3/49, base 1/49. Give each session a private temp root.\n3. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.\n4. **`CC_TIMEOUT`** may have censored the right tail; if rep50 ran at 1400 s the paired sd of 0.494\n   is an **underestimate** and every power calculation here is optimistic.\n5. **`echoPresearchPayload` has no length check** (`cli/search.go:286`) — a zero-byte payload gives\n   0 bytes on stdout with exit 0, the \"announced but never shipped\" failure class. The guard exists\n   on another branch and is not on this tree.\n\n**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, 0 commit mismatches, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches small,\nprompt diff 18 lines all of which are checkout paths.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gates\n\nMDE ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between cells.\n**No token claim below n≈50 in either direction.**\n\n| gate | n | criterion |\n|---|---|---|\n| **V0** offline $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; RELATED SITES fires at TOPK=8 on recorded queries; grep returns a clean zero on the prometheus query; 287 sessions recovered and re-scored |\n| **V1** offline $0 | 49 | LOO / winsorised / trimmed re-score of the MOD and ADD pools — does MOD survive the test that killed the headline? |\n| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: **displacement rate** (eg shell calls < paired baseline) up from 21/49; RELATED SITES present in payloads; no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |\n| **V3** live | 50+ | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together**, plus per-arm censoring counts |\n\n**Winner tripwire (your instruction: abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,\n`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` in every sample from V2. Compare only against a **same-wave**\ncontrol — never a previous cell.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Honest expected outcome\n\n**No number is promised.** The two items with a real mechanism and no prior art are §4.1 (RELATED\nSITES was structurally off) and §4.2 (grep noise where a clean zero existed). Both are cheap, both\nare fair, and neither has been measured. Everything else in §4 is hygiene that makes the *next*\nmeasurement trustworthy rather than moving the current one.\n\n**The ceiling on loser repair is +21.21%** — arithmetic (the lift pool), not projection.\n**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change**; the only intervention that would reach it is\nan instruction to explore and re-test less, which helps a no-tool arm equally and is exactly what\nthe withdrawn −35% contained.\n\n**If §4.1 and §4.2 do not move the displacement rate at V2, the honest conclusion is that\nentire-graph is not a token tool on this corpus** — and the defensible claim becomes correctness\nand latency, plus whole-file-read suppression (119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B), which is\nmeasurable at n=49 today.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Verification\n\n- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO for\n  tree-sitter). **Rebuild the binary — it is stale.** Unit tests beside the grep filter.\n- Offline replay: `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log` + `.payload`; re-run against the binary at\n  zero model cost; assert the change fires **and** that nothing else moved.\n- Harness deploys by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a script\n  a running session is reading.\n- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** trimmed **and** LOO **and** Δturns **and**\n  per-arm censoring counts.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":293,"newStart":1,"newLines":235,"lines":["-# entire-graph on Opus — the final plan","+# entire-graph on Opus — final plan"," "," ## Context"," ","-The original goal was **35% token savings on rep50, on Opus, fairly measured**. That is refuted","-and the reasons are in §1. You then relaxed it to the right target: **make the losers behave like","-winners — a code graph should not make instances worse.** That is what this plan is built against.","+The goal was **35% token savings on rep50, Opus, fairly measured**. You later relaxed it to the","+right target: **stop the tool making instances worse** — a code graph should not lose. This plan","+is built against that, after five investigations (two loser dissections, a capability inventory,","+a 4-lens artifact audit, and an iterative fix workflow) totalling ~4.5M subagent tokens."," ","-The decisive discovery came last: **this is not an invention problem.** There are ~2,500 LOC of","-measured, shipped, **default-off** capability in the tool, a `verify` verb documented nowhere, a","-`changed` verb missing from `--help`, an `edges` filter the shipped guide says does not exist, and","-a `capabilities` report that under-declares its own heuristics by ~20 relations. Every one was","-built after a measurement and then never wired up.","+**The headline finding is not about the tool.** It is that the measurement has ~287 recoverable","+sessions, an arm-skewed censoring rule, a content-blind gate, and four eg-favouring leaks — and","+that the one payload block designed to answer the question losing tasks actually ask **could not","+fire in the headline cell at all**."," ","-**The bottleneck is the last 10 metres — defaults and the agent-facing guide.**","+Sign convention: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.** All figures rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs."," ","-All numbers: rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs. Sign: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.**","-"," ---"," ","-## 1. Where Opus actually stands","+## 1. What is true on Opus"," "," | estimator | value |"," |---|---|","-| total (the reported headline) | **+1.35%** |","+| total (the reported headline) | +1.35% |"," | **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |"," | median | **−4.16%** |"," | 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |","-| t-statistic | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |","-| n to demonstrate +1.35% | 12,900 pairs ≈ $78k |","-| n to demonstrate 35% | **11 pairs ≈ $88** |","+| t | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |"," ","-**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. And 35% would have been","-the cheapest result in the project to prove — it is not provable because it is not there.","+**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. Never quote +1.35% without","+the LOO range and the median beside it."," ","-**Do not quote +1.35% without the LOO range and the median.**","+**And the fair number is bounded ABOVE by this one.** Four eg-favouring leaks are recorded and","+unfixed (§5). Closing them moves the headline **down**, not up."," "," ---"," ","-## 2. Why instances lose — three mechanisms, all measured","+## 2. Corrections to my own work — the full list"," ","-**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances (top five = −11.42, 57%). Lift +21.21 over 24.","-`lombok-3674` alone is +6.09 = 29% of all lift.**","+Recorded so they are not re-derived, and because most are mine."," ","-### 2.1 The call is paid for and removes nothing","-Losers: eg shell exploration **413 vs baseline 415** — two calls displaced out of 415.","-Winners: 370 vs 440. One graph call prices at **1.61 messages**, and a regression holding call","-count fixed charges **+7.0% CI[1.9,13.2]** for merely having called.","+1. **\"eg verifies more than baseline\"** — false. eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576. The claim","+   came from the 8 worst losers, a set selected on the outcome.","+2. **\"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\"** — regex artifact. A stricter definition gives n=17","+   and **−0.89%**.","+3. **\"the metric rewards failing to provision\"** — real on `bat-1892` only; **2 of 25 losers**,","+   worth −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.","+4. **\"+35.06% reachable by loser repair\"** — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.","+5. **×0.54 persist calibration** — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**","+   (corr +0.916, R² 0.839). **This one moved projections UP by ~52%.**","+6. **\"Five consecutive corrections, every one downward… nothing has moved the other way\"** —","+   **false, by item 5 above.** It was four downward and one upward. That sentence was rhetorical","+   overreach and is withdrawn.","+7. **R-A zero-toll at +4.3% to +6.0%** — mispriced by **5.2×**. The first search lands at assistant","+   turn median 2 of a median 85-turn session where `cache_read` is 12,231 vs a session mean of","+   63,137. Correct value **+0.96%**, CI [+0.53, +1.38]; n to demonstrate ≈ **19,504 pairs**.","+   It was also priced in the message model that §1 of my own document retires.","+8. **The VERIFY collect-only probe as a new fix** — `EG_VERIFY_PROBE=1` was **already set in","+   `run_REP50.sh:141`** and live during rep50. Also a no-op on 84% of drag (21/25 losers got no","+   VERIFY line).","+9. **\"Retrieval/ranking is anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5)\"** — this is","+   **n=13, p≈0.29**. It cannot support closing a lever, and it was load-bearing in two sections.","+   Demoted to **not tested**.","+10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the","+    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is","+    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact."," ","-### 2.2 ADD tasks get a confident wrong answer","-Search always returns something. When the task is to *add* behaviour, the top hit is a plausible","-sibling of the answer.","-","-| | pooled |","-|---|---|","-| MOD (fix existing broken code) | **+14.35%** (n=36) |","-| ADD (behaviour does not exist) | **−3.37%** (n=21) |","-","-Same sign **4/4 cells**. Corroborated: gold at rank 2–3 measures **−85.3%**, *worse* than gold not","-found at all (−25.6%). Forensics confirmed both `ansible-395e` and `prometheus-9248` are ADD, and","-**80% / 64% of their surplus is PRE-edit** — the graph bled where it operates.","-","-### 2.3 The verify-repair spiral, where the tool is absent","-**91 of 94 graph calls are pre-edit; 42/49 sessions never call it again**, yet 97.7% of excess","-cost lands after the first edit. Losers vs baseline: env-failures **+22**, throwaway scripts","-**+16**, post-edit harness **+50**, post-edit exploration **+159**. Winners mirror it exactly","-(−45, −48, −88, −81). `corr(Δharness, saving) = −0.612`; `corr(Δenv-failures) = −0.442`.","-"," ---"," ","-## 3. The economics that constrain every fix","+## 3. Why instances lose"," ","-`cache_read` is **95.5%** of billed tokens. A result injected at turn *i* is re-charged on every","-later turn: cost ≈ `(bytes/4) × turns-remaining` — **~5 persist-tokens per byte** at 20 turns left.","+**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances; lift +21.21 over 24; `lombok-3674` alone +6.09 (29% of lift).**"," ","-**One default search payload is 10,822 B ≈ 54k persist ≈ 0.55 of the whole-file Read it replaces.**","-That single number *is* the context-neutrality result (eg 38.5M vs baseline 38.6M).","+| | losers (25) | winners (24) |","+|---|---|---|","+| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |","+| post-edit exploration | +159 | −81 |","+| post-edit harness | +50 | −88 |","+| turns | +296 | −258 |"," ","-| class | baseline share | calls | each |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| exploration | 45.1% | 1,206 | 14k |","-| **whole-file `Read`** | **30.3%** | **119** | **98k (7×)** |","-| harness | 11.2% | 576 | 7k |","+**The graph works pre-edit in BOTH groups.** Localization is not the discriminator."," ","-**Break-even:** a block ≤2.8 KB pays for itself if it removes one grep/session; ≤19.6 KB if it","-removes one whole-file Read; ≤1.4 KB if it removes one harness run.","+**The discriminator is displacement:** label a session displaced if eg's shell-exploration count is","+below its paired baseline. **Displaced & won 19/21 (90.5%); not-displaced & won 6/28 (21.4%);","+AUC 0.838.** Sessions that call the graph: pooled **+6.30%**, median +12.61%. The 16 that never","+call it: pooled −1.02%, median **−24.94%**. **Calling and displacing is the winning behaviour.**"," ","-**Corollary: bytes delivered at turn 1 are charged N times.** The tool spends its whole budget at","-its most expensive moment and is absent from the phase where the money goes.","+**Task kind is the largest single concentration:** independent gold-patch labeller gives","+gold-MOD n=36 **+13.59%**, gold-ADD n=13 **−23.19%**. **Gold-ADD is 8 of 25 drag instances and","+−10.68 of the −19.86 drag points — 54% of all drag.** Caveat: **GEM300 inverts the sign**","+(MOD −14.13%, ADD +0.86%), and the MOD/ADD pools have **never been LOO-tested** — the same test","+that killed the headline. Do that first, offline, before spending anything on it."," ","+**Neither repo nor language predicts outcome.** Language R² = **0.153**; only **5 of 14** repos","+with >1 instance are internally consistent (`laravel` = [+51, −5, −59, −124, +39]). Per-repo or","+per-language configs are not viable, which is why the ledger already struck that lever.","+"," ---"," ","-## 4. The plan — remove bytes and fix defaults, in this order","+## 4. What to actually do — ranked"," ","-Every item is **tool output, not instruction**, and passes the no-tool-arm test. Ranked by","-(turns removed) / (bytes added). **Items 4.1–4.4 all reduce or barely move payload size** — the","-first proposals in this project with a positive byte ratio.","+Every item is tool output or harness hygiene. None adds an instruction."," ","-### 4.1 Fix `graph grep`: exclude vendored / minified / generated files *(NEGATIVE bytes)*","-`internal/cli` grep path shells out to `grep -rInE` over the whole worktree and filters **only","-tests**. On `prometheus-9248` it returned one hit inside minified vendored `d3.v3.js` where plain","-grep returned a **clean zero** — and a clean zero is *actionable* (\"pivot\"), one noise hit is not.","-Baseline pivoted to the issue's error string at call 2 and found `scalarBinop`; eg reached it at","-calls 21–22. **~19 turns of delay, caused by the tool's opening answer.**","+### 4.1 `EG_TOPK` 5 → 8 *(harness one-liner, no rebuild)* — **highest value**","+**RELATED SITES — the only payload block that names \"the other places this change has to land\" —","+cannot be emitted at all when `--top-k <= 5`.** rep50 ran `EG_TOPK=5`. So the block designed to","+answer the completeness question that ADD tasks actually ask **never fired in the headline cell**.","+This is not ranking, not a new verb, and not a payload-quality metric; it is a block that was","+switched off by a numeric floor."," ","-This is the only place measured where the graph is **demonstrably worse than no tool at all**, and","-the fix removes bytes.","+### 4.2 Fix `graph grep`: exclude vendored / minified / generated *(NEGATIVE bytes)*","+It shells to `grep -rInE` over the worktree and filters **only tests**. On `prometheus-9248` it","+returned one hit inside minified vendored `d3.v3.js` where plain grep returned a **clean zero** —","+and a clean zero is actionable, one noise hit is not. Baseline pivoted on move 2 and found the fix","+site; eg reached it at call 21. **~19 turns lost. The only measured case of the graph being worse","+than no tool at all**, and the fix removes bytes."," ","-### 4.2 Ship FILE OUTLINE by default *(+1,421 B, ~8× return — best ratio of anything built)*","-`internal/sem/search_outline.go` (217 LOC), flag `internal/cli/search.go:1637`. **Default OFF,","-absent from `printHelp`.** Its own measurement: **77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload","-had already named; 35 were immediately followed by a Read of that same file**, landing a median","-109 lines from anything printed. Measured cost +1,421 B ≈ 7.1k persist against ~57k saved.","+### 4.3 Recover the 287 dropped sessions *($0, and it is the only free power on the table)*","+**287 of ~1,560 arm-sessions produce no usage data and are dropped WITH THEIR PAIR — but their","+token counts survive verbatim in the Claude Code transcripts.** 132 of 133 zero-byte `cc_out.json`","+have an **empty** `cc_err.log`. Recovering them is a scoring change, not a cell."," ","-### 4.3 Cut complete bodies from rank 5 to rank 2 *(−76% payload bytes)*","-`search_enclosure.go:41` (`searchEnclosureHeadRanks = 5`). Act-rate data in `search_outline.go:22`:","-rank 1 read 62% / edited 54%; rank 2 27%/20%; **rank 3+ 0–11%.** Measured: `--body-head-ranks`","-5→3 = 10,822→6,143 B; **5→2 = 10,822→2,590 B (−76%)**. Ranks 3–5 pay full persist for a ≤11% read","-rate. Net is close (−41k certain saving vs ~29k probabilistic extra reads) but the saving is the","-certain half.","+### 4.4 Fix two gate defects that currently flatter eg","+- **Turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed:** eg hits `error_max_turns` **2.75× more often** than","+  baseline, and every such pair is deleted. Those are eg's *worst* sessions. Report censoring per","+  arm beside every headline; treat a truncated session as a loss at the cap rather than deleting it.","+- **The patch gate is a byte count**, so it admits junk: 20 patches over 100 KB passed, worst","+  2.95 MB; eg shipped **1,892,106 B across 1,708 files** on `gson-2479`. Add `*.class/*.o/*.jar/","+  *.pyc/build/dist/target` excludes.","+- *(Verified NOT a problem: gate strictness is not inflating the headline — removing it entirely","+  moves the pooled total by −0.15 pt.)*"," ","-### 4.4 Probe the VERIFY command instead of `LookPath` *(NEGATIVE bytes)*","-`internal/sem/search_verify.go:135` checks only that the runner *binary exists* — `npx` exists,","-so the command prints, then fails because deps were never installed. Replace with a collect-only","-probe on the pristine tree (`pytest --collect-only -q`, `go test -run XXX -count=0`,","-`cargo test --no-run`, `phpunit --list-tests`, `rspec --dry-run`); on failure **strip the block**.","+### 4.5 Ship FILE OUTLINE by default *(+1,421 B, ~8× return)*","+`internal/sem/search_outline.go` (217 LOC), flag `cli/search.go:1637` — **default OFF, absent from","+`printHelp`**. Its own measurement: 77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload had already","+named; 35 were immediately followed by a Read of that same file."," ","-Measured swing on this exact axis (rep30, baseline-matched): `VERIFY real` **+4.6 turns / +37.1%","-USD**; `VERIFY runner-absent` **−6.0 turns / −11.8%**; no VERIFY line −4.7 turns. **An 11.4-turn","-swing.** The previous response was to silence VERIFY entirely, which also discarded the good case.","-A probe keeps the good case and kills the bad one.","+### 4.6 `search --format` default json → text *(1.79× byte reduction for real users)*","+The parser defaults to `json`, which is **1.79× the text payload**, and the doctrine file agents","+actually read prescribes the command **without** `--format`. Every real (non-benchmark) invocation","+gets the fat form. Zero risk: `json` stays available explicitly."," ","-**Note:** this makes the provider *execute* something for the first time. That is a real product","-decision — latency, and a category change — and it should be taken deliberately.","+### 4.7 Binary and default hygiene *(preflight, not a lever)*","+- **`run_3arm.sh`'s default binary is missing every payload feature added in recent releases** —","+  any cell without an explicit `ENTIRE_GRAPH` override measures a tool that no longer exists.","+- **`entire graph verify` was not in the binary the headline cell executed.**","+- The in-tree binary is **stale** (rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`). Rebuild before anything.","+- Add a hard preflight gate on `entire graph capabilities --json` that aborts when the binary lacks","+  the features the cell assumes."," ","-### 4.5 Example-level VERIFY granularity *(+15 B, reaches 62% of the corpus)*","-`search_covertest.go` already selects **exactly one** test method and its line, then the deriver","-throws the name away for 5 of 8 ecosystems: Ruby, PHP, JS file-only; Java/Gradle class-only.","-Python (`-k`), Go (`-run '^Name$'`) and Rust already do it right. Fix: emit","-`rspec spec/foo_spec.rb:412`, `phpunit --filter testX`, `jest -t \"…\"`, `mvn -Dtest=Class#method`.","-Targets Ruby 39 + PHP 32 + JS 23 + TS 8 + Java 31 = **133/213 instances**.","+### 4.8 Move the advice switch into the binary","+The binary **hard-codes arm-asymmetric generic methodology advice** into the payload, and the only","+way to remove it is a 9-pattern literal grep in the harness whose default is OFF. rep50 happened to","+have it on. Fairness must not depend on a grep list in another repo — add `--no-advice`, defaulted","+off for measurement builds."," ","-### 4.6 Ship R-A zero-toll delivery *(built, gated, deployed as `b669a57b`)*","-`EG_PREFETCH=1` injected the payload at turn 0 and still let the agent re-derive it at full price.","-`EG_PRESEARCH` makes the residual call an echo — 0.02 s vs 5.21 s, byte-identical.","-Counterfactual on this cell **+4.3% to +6.0%** (CI spans zero at n=49).","+### 4.9 DO NOT BUILD — all refuted this session","+| | why |","+|---|---|","+| R-A zero-toll as a token lever | +0.96%, needs 19,504 pairs; and it removes the call in the cohort where calling *wins* |","+| VERIFY collect-only probe | already shipped and ON in rep50; no-op on 84% of drag |","+| MOD/ADD structural router | doesn't separate offline; `exact-symbol` already printed, identical on ADD and MOD (0.36 vs 0.36) |","+| post-edit consistency hook | its fair form's biggest beneficiary is the *baseline* in `lombok-3674` = 29% of lift |","+| new verb in the affordance tail | 0/66 adoption |","+| anything needing a post-edit agent call | 42/49 sessions make none |","+| better ranking · bigger payloads · graph-backed grep · renderer byte-trimming | closed; payload is 79.9% source, ~0.6% of session spend |"," ","-### 4.7 Documentation and defaults that are simply wrong *(zero bytes)*","-- `search` defaults to `--profile fast` (**9/30 relations**) while both agent guides mandate `full`.","-  Under the default, TESTS, SIMILAR_TO, DATA_FLOWS, FILE_CHANGES_WITH and every type relation are","-  **structurally empty**, so blocks depending on them cannot fire. `neighbors`/`impact` default to","-  `full`; `search` is the odd one out.","-- `AGENTS.md:72` states `edges --to/--from/--relation` **does not exist**. It does","-  (`root.go:576-594`) — and it is the only route to 13 relation types. Delete that sentence.","-- `capabilities --json` declares **7** heuristic relations; by the code **~27 of 30** are","-  text-pattern derived, including **CALLS (35% of all edges), which is a regex name-set, not an","-  AST call-site set.** Doctrine rule 7 says \"feature-detect before you trust\" — it is being fed a","-  wrong answer.","-- `TESTS` ships in the relation list at **10 edges of 36,354 on Go and 0 of 89,587 on a Python repo","-  that has a pytest suite.** Either fix it (§4.8) or stop advertising it.","-- `verify` and `changed` are in neither agent guide; `changed` is absent from `printHelp`.","-- **The in-tree binary is stale vs source** — it rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`.","-  Rebuild before anything ships.","-","-### 4.8 TESTS from call-reachability rather than spelling *(zero payload bytes)*","-`types.go:280-297` maps `TestFoo→Foo` by name only. Emit TESTS where a symbol in a test file","-reaches the target within **≤2 CALLS hops**, restricted to ranked files. Uses edges that already","-exist (12.6k–21.1k CALLS). CALLS is supported for Ruby/PHP/JS/TS/Python, so this is one of the few","-upgrades that lands on the dynamic ~48% of the corpus. It is also the input to §4.4 and §4.5.","-","-### 4.9 DO NOT BUILD","-- **Post-edit consistency hook.** Stress-tested and rejected: its fair (symmetric) form's biggest","-  beneficiary is the **baseline in `lombok-3674`**, i.e. it eats 29% of the lift. Cost −2% to −6%.","-- Any new verb in the affordance tail — **0/66 adoption** measured.","-- Anything requiring an agent-initiated post-edit call — 42/49 sessions make none.","-- Better ranking; bigger payloads; graph-backed grep; the 12 dead payload metrics.","-"," ---"," ","-## 5. Integrity fixes — before any cell","+## 5. Integrity — before any cell"," ","-1. **Sibling-checkout answer leak.** `bat-1892` (the worst loser, −2.81 pts) made **12 references","-   into `bat-3108`, a later revision of the same repo containing the implemented feature.**","-   Measured exposure: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline** — small but **arm-asymmetric**. Fence","-   checkouts so a session cannot read a sibling instance's tree.","-2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells.** `prometheus-9248` found `/tmp/goyacc*` built by","-   *other instances'* sessions and spent 2 calls auditing foreign binaries. eg 3/49, base 1/49.","-   Give each session a private temp root.","-3. **Junk-patch gate.** One baseline patch was 371,308 B of vendor/build output and passed as","-   success. Add a symmetric size/content bound.","-4. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.","-   Fix before any payload forensics.","-5. **0-byte `cc_out.json`** — guard shipped; the sweep removed **90 corpses** across all cells.","+1. **Four eg-favouring answer leaks** are recorded in memory and unfixed. `bat-1892` (worst loser,","+   −2.81 pts) made **12 references into `bat-3108`**, a later revision of the same repo containing","+   the implemented feature. Measured: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline.** Direction matters —","+   closing these moves the headline **down**.","+2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells** — `prometheus-9248` audited `/tmp/goyacc*` built by","+   other instances' sessions. eg 3/49, base 1/49. Give each session a private temp root.","+3. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.","+4. **`CC_TIMEOUT`** may have censored the right tail; if rep50 ran at 1400 s the paired sd of 0.494","+   is an **underestimate** and every power calculation here is optimistic.","+5. **`echoPresearchPayload` has no length check** (`cli/search.go:286`) — a zero-byte payload gives","+   0 bytes on stdout with exit 0, the \"announced but never shipped\" failure class. The guard exists","+   on another branch and is not on this tree."," ","-**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, **0 commit mismatches**, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches","-small, prompt diff is 18 lines all of which are checkout paths.","+**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, 0 commit mismatches, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches small,","+prompt diff 18 lines all of which are checkout paths."," "," ---"," ","-## 6. Gates — mechanism counts, winners protected","+## 6. Gates"," ","-MDE is ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between","-cells. **No token claim below n≈50, in either direction.**","+MDE ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between cells.","+**No token claim below n≈50 in either direction.**"," "," | gate | n | criterion |"," |---|---|---|","-| **V0** offline, $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; grep excludes vendored/minified on the prometheus query and returns a clean zero; outline/body-rank byte deltas reproduce (10,822 → 2,590 B) |","-| **V1** replay, $0 | 49 | on recorded loser sessions, the probed VERIFY command would have run where the emitted one failed; ≥50% of the 22 env-failures avoided |","-| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: payload bytes/session **down**, env-failures/session **down**, no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |","-| **V3** live | 50 | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together** |","+| **V0** offline $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; RELATED SITES fires at TOPK=8 on recorded queries; grep returns a clean zero on the prometheus query; 287 sessions recovered and re-scored |","+| **V1** offline $0 | 49 | LOO / winsorised / trimmed re-score of the MOD and ADD pools — does MOD survive the test that killed the headline? |","+| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: **displacement rate** (eg shell calls < paired baseline) up from 21/49; RELATED SITES present in payloads; no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |","+| **V3** live | 50+ | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together**, plus per-arm censoring counts |"," ","-**Winner-protection tripwire (per your instruction, abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,","-`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` are in every sample from V2 on. If any regresses >10pt versus a","-**same-wave** control, revert. Never compare against a previous cell — the noise floor forbids it.","+**Winner tripwire (your instruction: abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,","+`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` in every sample from V2. Compare only against a **same-wave**","+control — never a previous cell."," "," ---"," "," ## 7. Honest expected outcome"," ","-| item | effect | confidence |","-|---|---|---|","-| 4.1 grep vendor filter | removes a ~19-turn failure mode on ADD tasks | high — mechanism observed |","-| 4.2 FILE OUTLINE default | ~8× return on 1,421 B | high — own measurement |","-| 4.3 bodies rank 5→2 | −76% payload bytes | high on cost, medium on net |","-| 4.4 VERIFY probe | up to 11.4-turn swing on that axis | medium |","-| 4.5 VERIFY granularity | 133/213 instances | medium |","-| 4.6 R-A zero-toll | +4.3% to +6.0% | medium, CI spans zero |","+**No number is promised.** The two items with a real mechanism and no prior art are §4.1 (RELATED","+SITES was structurally off) and §4.2 (grep noise where a clean zero existed). Both are cheap, both","+are fair, and neither has been measured. Everything else in §4 is hygiene that makes the *next*","+measurement trustworthy rather than moving the current one."," ","-**Combined, realistically: high single digits to low teens, with the drag pool shrinking rather","-than the lift pool growing.** The ceiling on loser repair is exactly **+21.21%** (the lift pool) —","-arithmetic, not projection.","+**The ceiling on loser repair is +21.21%** — arithmetic (the lift pool), not projection.","+**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change**; the only intervention that would reach it is","+an instruction to explore and re-test less, which helps a no-tool arm equally and is exactly what","+the withdrawn −35% contained."," ","-**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change.** The one intervention that would reach it is","-an instruction telling the agent to explore and re-test less — which helps a no-tool arm equally","-and is precisely what the withdrawn −35% contained.","+**If §4.1 and §4.2 do not move the displacement rate at V2, the honest conclusion is that","+entire-graph is not a token tool on this corpus** — and the defensible claim becomes correctness","+and latency, plus whole-file-read suppression (119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B), which is","+measurable at n=49 today."," ","-**If §4.4 (executing a probe) is refused,** the honest recommendation is to stop optimising tokens","-here: remove bytes (4.1–4.3, 4.7), and position entire-graph on correctness and latency, where it","-is demonstrably good. It is not, on this corpus and this cost model, a token tool.","-"," ---"," "," ## 8. Verification"," ","-- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO needed).","-  **Rebuild the in-tree binary — it is stale.** Add unit tests beside `search_verify.go` and the","-  grep filter.","-- Offline replay: recorded queries at `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log`, payloads at the same","-  path + `.payload`. Re-run against the binary at zero model cost; assert both that the change","-  fires and that nothing else moved.","-- Harness deploys to VMs by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a","-  script a running session is reading.","+- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO for","+  tree-sitter). **Rebuild the binary — it is stale.** Unit tests beside the grep filter.","+- Offline replay: `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log` + `.payload`; re-run against the binary at","+  zero model cost; assert the change fires **and** that nothing else moved.","+- Harness deploys by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a script","+  a running session is reading."," - Every gate reports total **and** median **and** trimmed **and** LOO **and** Δturns **and**","-  env-failure counts.","-","----","-","-# APPENDIX A — Subagent findings log","-","-## A1 — Post-edit hook stress test — **REJECTED**","-Fair (symmetric) form's biggest beneficiary is the baseline in `lombok-3674` = 29% of all lift;","-cost −2% to −6%; ~48% of corpus is dynamically typed where arity checks are unreliable.","-Also surfaced: `claude --settings '<json>' --setting-sources ''` avoids writing","-`.claude/settings.json` into the worktree, removing the patch-pollution blocker.","-","-## A2 — Loser fore