{"parentUuid":"a13b4e63-d4b4-45c6-a429-7f141a52cf2d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqkFVBAT5Jb5dUgc4EJq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tested it properly, and the answer is **no — and this kills the last surviving lever**.\n\n**Task kind (MOD vs ADD), put through the same leave-one-out test that killed the headline:**\n\n| | n | TOTAL | median | **10% trimmed** | wins | **LOO** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MOD | 32 | +4.38% | +8.90% | **−3.44%** | 16/32 | −0.18% … +10.52% — **spans zero** |\n| ADD | 17 | −1.44% | −16.82% | −18.14% | 8/17 | −15.76% … +4.25% — **spans zero** |\n\nThree things break it:\n\n1. **Drop ADD's single worst instance and ADD flips to +0.60%.** The penalty is not a property of the group.\n2. **`lombok-3674` is an ADD task that eg won by +71%** — dropping it makes ADD *worse* (−15.76%). The same instance that carries the headline also carries this.\n3. **The labeller decides the answer.** The workflow's labeller gave MOD +13.59% / ADD −23.19% at n=36/13; mine gives **+4.38% / −1.44% at n=32/17**. A 36.8-point gap became 5.8 points on a labelling choice. That is researcher degrees of freedom, not a finding.\n\n**Prompt/ask features predict nothing:**\n\n| feature | corr with outcome |\n|---|---|\n| quoted error strings | −0.278 |\n| traceback present | −0.229 |\n| distinct identifiers | +0.150 |\n| file paths named | −0.135 |\n| code fences | +0.089 |\n| prompt length | −0.027 |\n| backticked spans | +0.013 |\n\nSo: **not repo, not language (R² 0.153), not task kind (fails LOO), not prompt text.** Nothing knowable in advance predicts whether the tool helps. That's the eleventh correction, and it retires the ledger's ⭐ \"best current idea.\"\n\nWhat survives is only what's *structurally* broken — RELATED SITES never firing at `TOPK=5`, `graph grep` returning noise where plain grep returns a clean zero, 287 recoverable sessions, and the arm-skewed censoring that currently flatters eg."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3753,"cache_read_input_tokens":875514,"output_tokens":2851,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3753,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2851,"cache_read_input_tokens":875514,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3753},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqkFLSYuxbyXMVMVQH5c","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd3801a4-7030-404c-8446-79826f9e0b0c","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:22:32.370Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"dd3801a4-7030-404c-8446-79826f9e0b0c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqkFVBAT5Jb5dUgc4EJq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01561jGSfdEhpP4oWzyvmmdF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans && python3 - <<'PY'\np='stateless-napping-unicorn.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold = s[s.index(\"**Task kind is the largest single concentration:**\"):s.index(\"**Neither repo nor language predicts outcome.**\")]\nnew = \"\"\"**Task kind does NOT predict outcome — this retires the ledger's best remaining idea.**\nPut through the same leave-one-out test that killed the headline:\n\n| | n | TOTAL | median | 10% trimmed | wins | LOO range |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MOD | 32 | +4.38% | +8.90% | **−3.44%** | 16/32 | −0.18% … +10.52% — **spans zero** |\n| ADD | 17 | −1.44% | −16.82% | −18.14% | 8/17 | −15.76% … +4.25% — **spans zero** |\n\nThree independent breaks: (a) dropping ADD's worst instance flips ADD to **+0.60%**;\n(b) `lombok-3674` is an **ADD** task eg won by +71%, so dropping it makes ADD *worse* — the same\ninstance carries both the headline and this; (c) **the labeller decides the answer** — one\nlabeller gives MOD +13.59% / ADD −23.19% (n=36/13), mine gives +4.38% / −1.44% (n=32/17). A\n36.8-pt gap collapses to 5.8 pt on a labelling choice. GEM300 also inverts the sign.\n**Do not build a MOD/ADD router or spend on a classifier.**\n\n**No prompt/ask feature predicts the outcome either:** quoted error strings −0.278, traceback\n−0.229, distinct identifiers +0.150, file paths named −0.135, code fences +0.089, prompt length\n−0.027, backticked spans +0.013.\n\n\"\"\"\ns = s.replace(old, new)\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the\n    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is\n    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the\n    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is\n    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact.\n11. **\"gold-ADD is 54% of all drag\"** — does not survive leave-one-out, and is labeller-dependent\n    (36.8-pt gap between two labellers). Task kind is **not** a usable predictor. Retracted, and\n    with it the ledger's §1.1 \"best current idea\".\"\"\")\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"| **V1** offline $0 | 49 | LOO / winsorised / trimmed re-score of the MOD and ADD pools — does MOD survive the test that killed the headline? |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| ~~V1~~ | — | **Already run: MOD/ADD fails LOO and is labeller-dependent. Lever closed.** |\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"plan updated:\", \"retires the ledger's best remaining idea\" in s, \"labeller-dependent\" in s)\nPY\ngrep -c \"\" /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","description":"Record the task-kind retraction in the plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3753,"cache_read_input_tokens":875514,"output_tokens":2851,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3753,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2851,"cache_read_input_tokens":875514,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3753},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqkFLSYuxbyXMVMVQH5c","type":"assistant","uuid":"5dda10c5-822b-4996-9ab2-0466a2c3deb3","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:22:44.880Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"5dda10c5-822b-4996-9ab2-0466a2c3deb3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"96e03687-14c7-40a5-93eb-a483d24f1540","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01561jGSfdEhpP4oWzyvmmdF","type":"tool_result","content":"plan updated: True True\n251\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dcf2efd4-95e5-4097-9d6b-40349db9ecc4","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:22:44.951Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"plan updated: True True\n251","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5dda10c5-822b-4996-9ab2-0466a2c3deb3","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"dcf2efd4-95e5-4097-9d6b-40349db9ecc4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md","snippet":"1\t# entire-graph on Opus — final plan\n2\t\n3\t## Context\n4\t\n5\tThe goal was **35% token savings on rep50, Opus, fairly measured**. You later relaxed it to the\n6\tright target: **stop the tool making instances worse** — a code graph should not lose. This plan\n7\tis built against that, after five investigations (two loser dissections, a capability inventory,\n8\ta 4-lens artifact audit, and an iterative fix workflow) totalling ~4.5M subagent tokens.\n9\t\n10\t**The headline finding is not about the tool.** It is that the measurement has ~287 recoverable\n11\tsessions, an arm-skewed censoring rule, a content-blind gate, and four eg-favouring leaks — and\n12\tthat the one payload block designed to answer the question losing tasks actually ask **could not\n13\tfire in the headline cell at all**.\n14\t\n15\tSign convention: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.** All figures rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs.\n16\t\n17\t---\n18\t\n19\t## 1. What is true on Opus\n20\t\n21\t| estimator | value |\n22\t|---|---|\n23\t| total (the reported headline) | +1.35% |\n24\t| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n25\t| median | **−4.16%** |\n26\t| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |\n27\t| t | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n28\t\n29\t**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. Never quote +1.35% without\n30\tthe LOO range and the median beside it.\n31\t\n32\t**And the fair number is bounded ABOVE by this one.** Four eg-favouring leaks are recorded and\n33\tunfixed (§5). Closing them moves the headline **down**, not up.\n34\t\n35\t---\n36\t\n37\t## 2. Corrections to my own work — the full list\n38\t\n39\tRecorded so they are not re-derived, and because most are mine.\n40\t\n41\t1. **\"eg verifies more than baseline\"** — false. eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576. The claim\n42\t   came from the 8 worst losers, a set selected on the outcome.\n43\t2. **\"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\"** — regex artifact. A stricter definition gives n=17\n44\t   and **−0.89%**.\n45\t3. **\"the metric rewards failing to provision\"** — real on `bat-1892` only; **2 of 25 losers**,\n46\t   worth −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.\n47\t4. **\"+35.06% reachable by loser repair\"** — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.\n48\t5. **×0.54 persist calibration** — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**\n49\t   (corr +0.916, R² 0.839). **This one moved projections UP by ~52%.**\n50\t6. **\"Five consecutive corrections, every one downward… nothing has moved the other way\"** —\n51\t   **false, by item 5 above.** It was four downward and one upward. That sentence was rhetorical\n52\t   overreach and is withdrawn.\n53\t7. **R-A zero-toll at +4.3% to +6.0%** — mispriced by **5.2×**. The first search lands at assistant\n54\t   turn median 2 of a median 85-turn session where `cache_read` is 12,231 vs a session mean of\n55\t   63,137. Correct value **+0.96%**, CI [+0.53, +1.38]; n to demonstrate ≈ **19,504 pairs**.\n56\t   It was also priced in the message model that §1 of my own document retires.\n57\t8. **The VERIFY collect-only probe as a new fix** — `EG_VERIFY_PROBE=1` was **already set in\n58\t   `run_REP50.sh:141`** and live during rep50. Also a no-op on 84% of drag (21/25 losers got no\n59\t   VERIFY line).\n60\t9. **\"Retrieval/ranking is anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5)\"** — this is\n61\t   **n=13, p≈0.29**. It cannot support closing a lever, and it was load-bearing in two sections.\n62\t   Demoted to **not tested**.\n63\t10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the\n64\t    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is\n65\t    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact.\n66\t11. **\"gold-ADD is 54% of all drag\"** — does not survive leave-one-out, and is labeller-dependent\n67\t    (36.8-pt gap between two labellers). Task kind is **not** a usable predictor. Retracted, and\n68\t    with it the ledger's §1.1 \"best current idea\".\n69\t\n70\t---\n71\t\n72\t## 3. Why instances lose\n73\t\n74\t**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances; lift +21.21 over 24; `lombok-3674` alone +6.09 (29% of lift).**\n75\t\n76\t| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n77\t|---|---|---|\n78\t| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n79\t| post-edit exploration | +159 | −81 |\n80\t| post-edit harness | +50 | −88 |\n81\t| turns | +296 | −258 |\n82\t\n83\t**The graph works pre-edit in BOTH groups.** Localization is not the discriminator.\n84\t\n85\t**The discriminator is displacement:** label a session displaced if eg's shell-exploration count is\n86\tbelow its paired baseline. **Displaced & won 19/21 (90.5%); not-displaced & won 6/28 (21.4%);\n87\tAUC 0.838.** Sessions that call the graph: pooled **+6.30%**, median +12.61%. The 16 that never\n88\tcall it: pooled −1.02%, median **−24.94%**. **Calling and displacing is the winning behaviour.**\n89\t\n90\t**Task kind does NOT predict outcome — this retires the ledger's best remaining idea.**\n91\tPut through the same leave-one-out test that killed the headline:\n92\t\n93\t| | n | TOTAL | median | 10% trimmed | wins | LOO range |\n94\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n95\t| MOD | 32 | +4.38% | +8.90% | **−3.44%** | 16/32 | −0.18% … +10.52% — **spans zero** |\n96\t| ADD | 17 | −1.44% | −16.82% | −18.14% | 8/17 | −15.76% … +4.25% — **spans zero** |\n97\t\n98\tThree independent breaks: (a) dropping ADD's worst instance flips ADD to **+0.60%**;\n99\t(b) `lombok-3674` is an **ADD** task eg won by +71%, so dropping it makes ADD *worse* — the same\n100\tinstance carries both the headline and this; (c) **the labeller decides the answer** — one\n101\tlabeller gives MOD +13.59% / ADD −23.19% (n=36/13), mine gives +4.38% / −1.44% (n=32/17). A\n102\t36.8-pt gap collapses to 5.8 pt on a labelling choice. GEM300 also inverts the sign.\n103\t**Do not build a MOD/ADD router or spend on a classifier.**\n104\t\n105\t**No prompt/ask feature predicts the outcome either:** quoted error strings −0.278, traceback\n106\t−0.229, distinct identifiers +0.150, file paths named −0.135, code fences +0.089, prompt length\n107\t−0.027, backticked spans +0.013.\n108\t\n109\t**Neither repo nor language predicts outcome.** Language R² = **0.153**; only **5 of 14** repos\n110\twith >1 instance are internally consistent (`laravel` = [+51, −5, −59, −124, +39]). Per-repo or\n111\tper-language configs are not viable, which is why the ledger already struck that lever.\n112\t\n113\t---\n114\t\n115\t## 4. What to actually do — ranked\n116\t\n117\tEvery item is tool output or harness hygiene. None adds an instruction.\n118\t\n119\t### 4.1 `EG_TOPK` 5 → 8 *(harness one-liner, no rebuild)* — **highest value**\n120\t**RELATED SITES — the only payload block that names \"the other places this change has to land\" —\n121\tcannot be emitted at all when `--top-k <= 5`.** rep50 ran `EG_TOPK=5`. So the block designed to\n122\tanswer the completeness question that ADD tasks actually ask **never fired in the headline cell**.\n123\tThis is not ranking, not a new verb, and not a payload-quality metric; it is a block that was\n124\tswitched off by a numeric floor.\n125\t\n126\t### 4.2 Fix `graph grep`: exclude vendored / minified / generated *(NEGATIVE bytes)*\n127\tIt shells to `grep -rInE` over the worktree and filters **only tests**. On `prometheus-9248` it\n128\treturned one hit inside minified vendored `d3.v3.js` where plain grep returned a **clean zero** —\n129\tand a clean zero is actionable, one noise hit is not. Baseline pivoted on move 2 and found the fix\n130\tsite; eg reached it at call 21. **~19 turns lost. The only measured case of the graph being worse\n131\tthan no tool at all**, and the fix removes bytes.\n132\t\n133\t### 4.3 Recover the 287 dropped sessions *($0, and it is the only free power on the table)*\n134\t**287 of ~1,560 arm-sessions produce no usage data and are dropped WITH THEIR PAIR — but their\n135\ttoken counts survive verbatim in the Claude Code transcripts.** 132 of 133 zero-byte `cc_out.json`\n136\thave an **empty** `cc_err.log`. Recovering them is a scoring change, not a cell.\n137\t\n138\t### 4.4 Fix two gate defects that currently flatter eg\n139\t- **Turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed:** eg hits `error_max_turns` **2.75× more often** than\n\n... [112 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"be1ac74a-d924-4d96-b92b-b98aa7c16f0d","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:22:44.965Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
