{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01TQjcV9RFKrapFue4SWczEa","lastSequenceNum":0}
{"parentUuid":"be1ac74a-d924-4d96-b92b-b98aa7c16f0d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqkJ9b2UpvBthpZK6ejg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan is complete. Eleven corrections, five investigations, and the honest position on every axis you asked about.\n\n**What predicts win/loss: nothing knowable in advance.**\n\n| axis | result |\n|---|---|\n| repo | 5/14 multi-instance repos internally consistent; `laravel` = [+51, −5, −59, −124, +39] |\n| language | R² = **0.153** |\n| task kind (MOD/ADD) | fails LOO, labeller-dependent (36.8pt → 5.8pt) |\n| prompt text | best correlate −0.278 |\n\n**What's actually broken and fixable** — all structural, none requiring a new capability:\n\n1. **`EG_TOPK=5` silenced RELATED SITES entirely.** The one payload block that names \"the other places this change must land\" cannot emit below top-k 6. The headline cell ran 5.\n2. **`graph grep` returns noise where plain grep returns a clean zero** — cost ~19 turns on prometheus, and the fix *removes* bytes.\n3. **287 sessions are droppable-but-recoverable** — their token data survives in transcripts. Free statistical power, no cell needed.\n4. **Turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed** — eg truncates 2.75× more often and those pairs are deleted, which flatters eg.\n\nAnd the honest headline: **+1.35% is one instance** (drop `lombok-3674` → −5.18%; median −4.16%; trimmed −7.65%), and the fair number is bounded *above* by it because four eg-favouring leaks are still open."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6495,"cache_read_input_tokens":879267,"output_tokens":1546,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6495,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1546,"cache_read_input_tokens":879267,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6495,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6495},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqkJ1cJiYTa9s4zTHgvU","type":"assistant","uuid":"acca63fa-1eb9-4afd-90c8-e1734c0fd041","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:22:56.503Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"acca63fa-1eb9-4afd-90c8-e1734c0fd041","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqkJ9b2UpvBthpZK6ejg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BshG6pdaXF7JRfMH5rvkdt","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"plan":"# entire-graph on Opus — final plan\n\n## Context\n\nThe goal was **35% token savings on rep50, Opus, fairly measured**. You later relaxed it to the\nright target: **stop the tool making instances worse** — a code graph should not lose. This plan\nis built against that, after five investigations (two loser dissections, a capability inventory,\na 4-lens artifact audit, and an iterative fix workflow) totalling ~4.5M subagent tokens.\n\n**The headline finding is not about the tool.** It is that the measurement has ~287 recoverable\nsessions, an arm-skewed censoring rule, a content-blind gate, and four eg-favouring leaks — and\nthat the one payload block designed to answer the question losing tasks actually ask **could not\nfire in the headline cell at all**.\n\nSign convention: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.** All figures rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is true on Opus\n\n| estimator | value |\n|---|---|\n| total (the reported headline) | +1.35% |\n| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n| median | **−4.16%** |\n| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |\n| t | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n\n**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. Never quote +1.35% without\nthe LOO range and the median beside it.\n\n**And the fair number is bounded ABOVE by this one.** Four eg-favouring leaks are recorded and\nunfixed (§5). Closing them moves the headline **down**, not up.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Corrections to my own work — the full list\n\nRecorded so they are not re-derived, and because most are mine.\n\n1. **\"eg verifies more than baseline\"** — false. eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576. The claim\n   came from the 8 worst losers, a set selected on the outcome.\n2. **\"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\"** — regex artifact. A stricter definition gives n=17\n   and **−0.89%**.\n3. **\"the metric rewards failing to provision\"** — real on `bat-1892` only; **2 of 25 losers**,\n   worth −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.\n4. **\"+35.06% reachable by loser repair\"** — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.\n5. **×0.54 persist calibration** — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**\n   (corr +0.916, R² 0.839). **This one moved projections UP by ~52%.**\n6. **\"Five consecutive corrections, every one downward… nothing has moved the other way\"** —\n   **false, by item 5 above.** It was four downward and one upward. That sentence was rhetorical\n   overreach and is withdrawn.\n7. **R-A zero-toll at +4.3% to +6.0%** — mispriced by **5.2×**. The first search lands at assistant\n   turn median 2 of a median 85-turn session where `cache_read` is 12,231 vs a session mean of\n   63,137. Correct value **+0.96%**, CI [+0.53, +1.38]; n to demonstrate ≈ **19,504 pairs**.\n   It was also priced in the message model that §1 of my own document retires.\n8. **The VERIFY collect-only probe as a new fix** — `EG_VERIFY_PROBE=1` was **already set in\n   `run_REP50.sh:141`** and live during rep50. Also a no-op on 84% of drag (21/25 losers got no\n   VERIFY line).\n9. **\"Retrieval/ranking is anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5)\"** — this is\n   **n=13, p≈0.29**. It cannot support closing a lever, and it was load-bearing in two sections.\n   Demoted to **not tested**.\n10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the\n    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is\n    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact.\n11. **\"gold-ADD is 54% of all drag\"** — does not survive leave-one-out, and is labeller-dependent\n    (36.8-pt gap between two labellers). Task kind is **not** a usable predictor. Retracted, and\n    with it the ledger's §1.1 \"best current idea\".\n\n---\n\n## 3. Why instances lose\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances; lift +21.21 over 24; `lombok-3674` alone +6.09 (29% of lift).**\n\n| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n| post-edit exploration | +159 | −81 |\n| post-edit harness | +50 | −88 |\n| turns | +296 | −258 |\n\n**The graph works pre-edit in BOTH groups.** Localization is not the discriminator.\n\n**The discriminator is displacement:** label a session displaced if eg's shell-exploration count is\nbelow its paired baseline. **Displaced & won 19/21 (90.5%); not-displaced & won 6/28 (21.4%);\nAUC 0.838.** Sessions that call the graph: pooled **+6.30%**, median +12.61%. The 16 that never\ncall it: pooled −1.02%, median **−24.94%**. **Calling and displacing is the winning behaviour.**\n\n**Task kind does NOT predict outcome — this retires the ledger's best remaining idea.**\nPut through the same leave-one-out test that killed the headline:\n\n| | n | TOTAL | median | 10% trimmed | wins | LOO range |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MOD | 32 | +4.38% | +8.90% | **−3.44%** | 16/32 | −0.18% … +10.52% — **spans zero** |\n| ADD | 17 | −1.44% | −16.82% | −18.14% | 8/17 | −15.76% … +4.25% — **spans zero** |\n\nThree independent breaks: (a) dropping ADD's worst instance flips ADD to **+0.60%**;\n(b) `lombok-3674` is an **ADD** task eg won by +71%, so dropping it makes ADD *worse* — the same\ninstance carries both the headline and this; (c) **the labeller decides the answer** — one\nlabeller gives MOD +13.59% / ADD −23.19% (n=36/13), mine gives +4.38% / −1.44% (n=32/17). A\n36.8-pt gap collapses to 5.8 pt on a labelling choice. GEM300 also inverts the sign.\n**Do not build a MOD/ADD router or spend on a classifier.**\n\n**No prompt/ask feature predicts the outcome either:** quoted error strings −0.278, traceback\n−0.229, distinct identifiers +0.150, file paths named −0.135, code fences +0.089, prompt length\n−0.027, backticked spans +0.013.\n\n**Neither repo nor language predicts outcome.** Language R² = **0.153**; only **5 of 14** repos\nwith >1 instance are internally consistent (`laravel` = [+51, −5, −59, −124, +39]). Per-repo or\nper-language configs are not viable, which is why the ledger already struck that lever.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What to actually do — ranked\n\nEvery item is tool output or harness hygiene. None adds an instruction.\n\n### 4.1 `EG_TOPK` 5 → 8 *(harness one-liner, no rebuild)* — **highest value**\n**RELATED SITES — the only payload block that names \"the other places this change has to land\" —\ncannot be emitted at all when `--top-k <= 5`.** rep50 ran `EG_TOPK=5`. So the block designed to\nanswer the completeness question that ADD tasks actually ask **never fired in the headline cell**.\nThis is not ranking, not a new verb, and not a payload-quality metric; it is a block that was\nswitched off by a numeric floor.\n\n### 4.2 Fix `graph grep`: exclude vendored / minified / generated *(NEGATIVE bytes)*\nIt shells to `grep -rInE` over the worktree and filters **only tests**. On `prometheus-9248` it\nreturned one hit inside minified vendored `d3.v3.js` where plain grep returned a **clean zero** —\nand a clean zero is actionable, one noise hit is not. Baseline pivoted on move 2 and found the fix\nsite; eg reached it at call 21. **~19 turns lost. The only measured case of the graph being worse\nthan no tool at all**, and the fix removes bytes.\n\n### 4.3 Recover the 287 dropped sessions *($0, and it is the only free power on the table)*\n**287 of ~1,560 arm-sessions produce no usage data and are dropped WITH THEIR PAIR — but their\ntoken counts survive verbatim in the Claude Code transcripts.** 132 of 133 zero-byte `cc_out.json`\nhave an **empty** `cc_err.log`. Recovering them is a scoring change, not a cell.\n\n### 4.4 Fix two gate defects that currently flatter eg\n- **Turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed:** eg hits `error_max_turns` **2.75× more often** than\n  baseline, and every such pair is deleted. Those are eg's *worst* sessions. Report censoring per\n  arm beside every headline; treat a truncated session as a loss at the cap rather than deleting it.\n- **The patch gate is a byte count**, so it admits junk: 20 patches over 100 KB passed, worst\n  2.95 MB; eg shipped **1,892,106 B across 1,708 files** on `gson-2479`. Add `*.class/*.o/*.jar/\n  *.pyc/build/dist/target` excludes.\n- *(Verified NOT a problem: gate strictness is not inflating the headline — removing it entirely\n  moves the pooled total by −0.15 pt.)*\n\n### 4.5 Ship FILE OUTLINE by default *(+1,421 B, ~8× return)*\n`internal/sem/search_outline.go` (217 LOC), flag `cli/search.go:1637` — **default OFF, absent from\n`printHelp`**. Its own measurement: 77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload had already\nnamed; 35 were immediately followed by a Read of that same file.\n\n### 4.6 `search --format` default json → text *(1.79× byte reduction for real users)*\nThe parser defaults to `json`, which is **1.79× the text payload**, and the doctrine file agents\nactually read prescribes the command **without** `--format`. Every real (non-benchmark) invocation\ngets the fat form. Zero risk: `json` stays available explicitly.\n\n### 4.7 Binary and default hygiene *(preflight, not a lever)*\n- **`run_3arm.sh`'s default binary is missing every payload feature added in recent releases** —\n  any cell without an explicit `ENTIRE_GRAPH` override measures a tool that no longer exists.\n- **`entire graph verify` was not in the binary the headline cell executed.**\n- The in-tree binary is **stale** (rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`). Rebuild before anything.\n- Add a hard preflight gate on `entire graph capabilities --json` that aborts when the binary lacks\n  the features the cell assumes.\n\n### 4.8 Move the advice switch into the binary\nThe binary **hard-codes arm-asymmetric generic methodology advice** into the payload, and the only\nway to remove it is a 9-pattern literal grep in the harness whose default is OFF. rep50 happened to\nhave it on. Fairness must not depend on a grep list in another repo — add `--no-advice`, defaulted\noff for measurement builds.\n\n### 4.9 DO NOT BUILD — all refuted this session\n| | why |\n|---|---|\n| R-A zero-toll as a token lever | +0.96%, needs 19,504 pairs; and it removes the call in the cohort where calling *wins* |\n| VERIFY collect-only probe | already shipped and ON in rep50; no-op on 84% of drag |\n| MOD/ADD structural router | doesn't separate offline; `exact-symbol` already printed, identical on ADD and MOD (0.36 vs 0.36) |\n| post-edit consistency hook | its fair form's biggest beneficiary is the *baseline* in `lombok-3674` = 29% of lift |\n| new verb in the affordance tail | 0/66 adoption |\n| anything needing a post-edit agent call | 42/49 sessions make none |\n| better ranking · bigger payloads · graph-backed grep · renderer byte-trimming | closed; payload is 79.9% source, ~0.6% of session spend |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Integrity — before any cell\n\n1. **Four eg-favouring answer leaks** are recorded in memory and unfixed. `bat-1892` (worst loser,\n   −2.81 pts) made **12 references into `bat-3108`**, a later revision of the same repo containing\n   the implemented feature. Measured: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline.** Direction matters —\n   closing these moves the headline **down**.\n2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells** — `prometheus-9248` audited `/tmp/goyacc*` built by\n   other instances' sessions. eg 3/49, base 1/49. Give each session a private temp root.\n3. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.\n4. **`CC_TIMEOUT`** may have censored the right tail; if rep50 ran at 1400 s the paired sd of 0.494\n   is an **underestimate** and every power calculation here is optimistic.\n5. **`echoPresearchPayload` has no length check** (`cli/search.go:286`) — a zero-byte payload gives\n   0 bytes on stdout with exit 0, the \"announced but never shipped\" failure class. The guard exists\n   on another branch and is not on this tree.\n\n**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, 0 commit mismatches, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches small,\nprompt diff 18 lines all of which are checkout paths.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gates\n\nMDE ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between cells.\n**No token claim below n≈50 in either direction.**\n\n| gate | n | criterion |\n|---|---|---|\n| **V0** offline $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; RELATED SITES fires at TOPK=8 on recorded queries; grep returns a clean zero on the prometheus query; 287 sessions recovered and re-scored |\n| ~~V1~~ | — | **Already run: MOD/ADD fails LOO and is labeller-dependent. Lever closed.** |\n| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: **displacement rate** (eg shell calls < paired baseline) up from 21/49; RELATED SITES present in payloads; no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |\n| **V3** live | 50+ | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together**, plus per-arm censoring counts |\n\n**Winner tripwire (your instruction: abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,\n`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` in every sample from V2. Compare only against a **same-wave**\ncontrol — never a previous cell.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Honest expected outcome\n\n**No number is promised.** The two items with a real mechanism and no prior art are §4.1 (RELATED\nSITES was structurally off) and §4.2 (grep noise where a clean zero existed). Both are cheap, both\nare fair, and neither has been measured. Everything else in §4 is hygiene that makes the *next*\nmeasurement trustworthy rather than moving the current one.\n\n**The ceiling on loser repair is +21.21%** — arithmetic (the lift pool), not projection.\n**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change**; the only intervention that would reach it is\nan instruction to explore and re-test less, which helps a no-tool arm equally and is exactly what\nthe withdrawn −35% contained.\n\n**If §4.1 and §4.2 do not move the displacement rate at V2, the honest conclusion is that\nentire-graph is not a token tool on this corpus** — and the defensible claim becomes correctness\nand latency, plus whole-file-read suppression (119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B), which is\nmeasurable at n=49 today.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Verification\n\n- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO for\n  tree-sitter). **Rebuild the binary — it is stale.** Unit tests beside the grep filter.\n- Offline replay: `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log` + `.payload`; re-run against the binary at\n  zero model cost; assert the change fires **and** that nothing else moved.\n- Harness deploys by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a script\n  a running session is reading.\n- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** trimmed **and** LOO **and** Δturns **and**\n  per-arm censoring counts.\n","planFilePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6495,"cache_read_input_tokens":879267,"output_tokens":1546,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6495,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1546,"cache_read_input_tokens":879267,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6495,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6495},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqkJ1cJiYTa9s4zTHgvU","type":"assistant","uuid":"94953be0-f80e-4227-86e0-9b264ee9eef9","tim