{"parentUuid":"1aab2325-92f8-4318-abe5-a7c3044431f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqkSijZ2UiZz7ckCcHhw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right, and I've been mis-framing this. Let me correct two things.\n\n**First: eg is demonstrably not in its best state.** The inventory is damning —\n\n| capability | state |\n|---|---|\n| RELATED SITES (\"other places this change must land\") | **cannot emit at `TOPK≤5`** — the cell ran 5 |\n| FILE OUTLINE | built, 217 LOC, **default OFF**, absent from `--help` |\n| `--format` | defaults to **json = 1.79× the text bytes** |\n| complete bodies | emitted to **rank 5**, where rank 3+ is read 0–11% of the time |\n| `verify` / `changed` / `def` | in **neither** agent guide |\n| `AGENTS.md:72` | **denies a feature that exists** (`edges --to/--from/--relation`) |\n| in-tree binary | **stale** — rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path` |\n\nThat's ~2,500 LOC of measured capability shipped dark. You're right that I've been measuring why it loses instead of turning it on.\n\n**Second: your logic is the right target.** Call → find → edit → test → done is ~7 turns. Sessions run **85**. The agent still makes **24.6 exploration calls per session even with the graph** — because one search answers \"where is it\" and then it has to go find *what calls it, what tests it, how to run that test, and what else must change*. eg computes all four. It just doesn't ship them in the one call the agent actually makes.\n\nSo the fix isn't a new capability — it's **restructuring the payload: fewer source dumps, more answers**, paying for the additions with the removals:\n\n| change | bytes |\n|---|---|\n| bodies rank 5 → 2 | **−8,232 B** (10,822 → 2,590) |\n| `--format` json → text | **−44%** |\n| grep vendor/minified filter | **negative** |\n| **+ RELATED SITES** (TOPK 5→8) | +~600 B |\n| **+ FILE OUTLINE** | +1,421 B |\n| **+ covering test & runnable VERIFY** | +~200 B |\n\nNet still **negative**, and the one call now answers all four questions instead of one.\n\nThat's a real implementation plan, not hygiene. Let me rewrite the plan around it — and I'll be explicit that the measured-effect claims stay unproven until gated, because that part of my discipline shouldn't loosen just because the direction is now obvious."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":885762,"output_tokens":4685,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4685,"cache_read_input_tokens":885762,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqkSbiNtyUFPKmebJWPh","type":"assistant","uuid":"e7401e1c-b81b-4348-ad2b-2c64a2b8b0fb","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:25:18.080Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"e7401e1c-b81b-4348-ad2b-2c64a2b8b0fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqkSijZ2UiZz7ckCcHhw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011Dah4dzmvnFhTfdFiFmW9X","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans && python3 - <<'PY'\np='stateless-napping-unicorn.md'; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## 4. What to actually do — ranked\")\nj=s.index(\"## 5. Integrity — before any cell\")\nnew = \"\"\"## 4. THE BUILD — make one call answer the whole task\n\n### 4.0 The thesis\n\nThe ideal session is: **call the graph → find the site → edit → test → done.** ~7 turns.\nSessions run a **median of 85**, and the agent still makes **24.6 exploration calls per session\neven with the graph**. It is not exploring because the graph failed to locate — pre-edit\nexploration falls in BOTH winners and losers. It is exploring because one search answers *where\nis it*, and it then has to discover **what calls it**, **what tests it**, **how to run that test**,\nand **what else must change**.\n\n**entire-graph computes all four.** It ships none of them in the one call the agent makes:\n\n| the agent's next question | eg has the answer | why it never arrives |\n|---|---|---|\n| what else must change? | RELATED SITES block | **cannot emit at `--top-k ≤ 5`**; cell ran 5 |\n| what else is in this file? | FILE OUTLINE (`search_outline.go`, 217 LOC) | **default OFF**, absent from `--help` |\n| what test covers this? | covering-test selection | present in only **8 of 33** payloads |\n| how do I run it? | derived VERIFY command | same 8/33; and 21/25 losers got none |\n| who calls this? | CALLS edges (12.6k) | only via `neighbors`/`impact` — **0/49 adoption** |\n\n**So the build is not new capability. It is restructuring the payload to answer all five in the\none call the agent already makes — and paying for it by deleting source dumps nobody reads.**\n\n### 4.1 Pay for it first — remove bytes *(all measured)*\n\n| change | file | delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| complete bodies rank 5 → 2 | `search_enclosure.go:41` | **10,822 → 2,590 B (−76%)** — rank 1 read 62%/edited 54%, rank 2 27%/20%, **rank 3+ 0–11%** |\n| `--format` default json → text | `cli/search.go` parser | **−44%** (json is 1.79× text); doctrine agents read prescribes no `--format`, so real users get the fat form |\n| `graph grep`: exclude vendored/minified/generated | grep path | **negative bytes**, and fixes the only measured case of the graph being *worse than no tool* (prometheus: one hit in minified `d3.v3.js` where plain grep gave a clean zero → **~19 turns lost**) |\n\n### 4.2 Spend it on answers\n\n| change | file | delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| `EG_TOPK` 5 → 8 so RELATED SITES can emit | harness one-liner, no rebuild | +~600 B |\n| FILE OUTLINE on by default | `search_outline.go`, flag `cli/search.go:1637` | +1,421 B — its own measurement: 77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload already named, 35 immediately followed by a Read of it |\n| raise covering-test + VERIFY coverage from 8/33 | `search_verify.go` | +~200 B |\n\n**Net still negative**, and the payload changes from *five source bodies* to *one body plus four\nanswers*.\n\n### 4.3 Preconditions — non-negotiable, all currently violated\n\n- **Rebuild the binary.** The in-tree one is stale (rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`), and\n  `run_3arm.sh`'s DEFAULT binary is missing every recent payload feature — any cell without an\n  explicit `ENTIRE_GRAPH` override measures a tool that no longer exists.\n- Add a preflight that aborts on `capabilities --json` lacking the features the cell assumes.\n- Fix `AGENTS.md:72`, which states `edges --to/--from/--relation` does not exist. It does\n  (`root.go:576-594`) and is the only route to 13 relation types.\n- Document `verify`, `changed`, `def` — 971 LOC of `def` is in neither agent guide.\n- Move the arm-asymmetric advice switch **into the binary** (`--no-advice`); today fairness depends\n  on a 9-pattern literal grep in another repo whose default is OFF.\n\n### 4.4 Free statistical power — do this before any cell\n\n**287 of ~1,560 arm-sessions are dropped WITH THEIR PAIR, but their token counts survive verbatim\nin the Claude Code transcripts.** 132 of 133 zero-byte `cc_out.json` have an *empty* `cc_err.log`.\nRecovering them is a scoring change, not a cell — and it is the only free n available.\n\nAlso fix two gate defects that currently **flatter eg**: turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed (eg\ntruncates **2.75×** more often and those pairs are deleted — they are eg's worst sessions), and the\npatch gate is a byte count that admitted a **1,892,106 B / 1,708-file** patch on `gson-2479`.\n\n### 4.5 DO NOT BUILD — refuted this session\n\nR-A zero-toll (+0.96%, needs 19,504 pairs, and it removes the call in the cohort where calling\n*wins*) · VERIFY collect-only probe (already ON in rep50, no-op on 84% of drag) · MOD/ADD router\n(fails LOO, labeller-dependent) · post-edit consistency hook (its fair form's biggest beneficiary\nis the *baseline* in `lombok-3674`) · any new verb in the affordance tail (0/66) · anything needing\na post-edit agent call (42/49 make none) · better ranking · bigger payloads · graph-backed grep.\n\n### 4.6 What this is expected to do — stated honestly\n\n**No number is promised.** Every measured-effect claim in this project has been retracted at least\nonce (§2 lists eleven). What is *certain* is the byte arithmetic and that RELATED SITES was\nstructurally off. What is *unproven* is whether answering the agent's next four questions in the\nfirst call reduces its 24.6 exploration calls.\n\n**That is the hypothesis the gate exists to test**, and it is the first one in this project where\nthe mechanism is a capability being switched on rather than a correlate being chased.\n\n\"\"\"\ns = s[:i] + new + s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"rewritten:\", \"THE BUILD\" in s, \"24.6 exploration calls\" in s)\nPY\ngrep -n \"^## \\|^### \" /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md | head -20","description":"Rewrite plan as a build plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":885762,"output_tokens":4685,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4685,"cache_read_input_tokens":885762,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqkSbiNtyUFPKmebJWPh","type":"assistant","uuid":"13f2d07a-ad52-4c3d-b886-ca4871dd9dbc","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:25:47.291Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
