{"parentUuid":"99d5bf61-d178-4a4d-b3f7-449dc09fecc7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqmS6CDj4QuR6xZe4peK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":910716,"output_tokens":1500,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":705,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1500,"cache_read_input_tokens":910716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":705},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqmRuuLuePPD6kRTzos2","type":"assistant","uuid":"903ff995-8837-48c9-a364-8b9a7f3c01ca","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:37:54.138Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"903ff995-8837-48c9-a364-8b9a7f3c01ca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqmS6CDj4QuR6xZe4peK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verified as a diagnosis. Not verified as a saving.** That distinction matters, so let me be exact.\n\n**What is verified** — reproducible offline, $0, from the raw data:\n\n| claim | status |\n|---|---|\n| +1.35% is one instance (drop `lombok-3674` → −5.18%; median −4.16%; trimmed −7.65%; t = −0.17) | verified |\n| nothing predicts win/loss: repo 5/14 consistent, language R²=0.153, task kind fails LOO, prompt best corr −0.278 | verified |\n| payload is median 98 lines; agent reads first ~50 | verified |\n| VERIFY sits at median line 80 → reaches the agent in **2 of 33** | verified |\n| RELATED SITES **0/33** — never emitted at `TOPK≤5` | verified |\n| bytes past line 50 are discarded before billing | verified |\n| 287 dropped sessions are recoverable from transcripts | verified |\n| turn-cap censoring is **2.75× arm-skewed** and currently flatters eg | verified |\n| graphs clean: 49/49 present, 0 commit mismatches | verified |\n\n**What is not verified:** that any of it yields ≥0.1% tokens. The one free change — reordering so answers precede ranks 3–5 — cannot *cost* tokens, because delivered volume is fixed by the agent's own `head` cut. But its benefit is behavioural, and behaviour needs a cell.\n\nYou asked for a verified ≥0.1% saving. I can't certify that, and I won't. Twelve claims in this project have been retracted, seven of them mine, every one because a mechanism was mistaken for a measured effect. The mechanism here is solid; the response isn't measured.\n\n**So: ready to execute, not ready to promise a number.** The gate is 12 pairs, mechanism-only — does VERIFY delivery rise from 2/33, and do exploration calls fall? If exploration falls at all, 0.1% follows arithmetically (one avoided exploration call per five sessions clears it)."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":910716,"output_tokens":1500,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":705,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1500,"cache_read_input_tokens":910716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":705},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqmRuuLuePPD6kRTzos2","type":"assistant","uuid":"5bccc021-df68-4b4e-a081-478df5c36e80","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:38:02.443Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"5bccc021-df68-4b4e-a081-478df5c36e80","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqmS6CDj4QuR6xZe4peK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DMfdEL9zfEd6R1MvJo7ucA","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"plan":"# entire-graph on Opus — final plan\n\n## Context\n\nThe goal was **35% token savings on rep50, Opus, fairly measured**. You later relaxed it to the\nright target: **stop the tool making instances worse** — a code graph should not lose. This plan\nis built against that, after five investigations (two loser dissections, a capability inventory,\na 4-lens artifact audit, and an iterative fix workflow) totalling ~4.5M subagent tokens.\n\n**The headline finding is not about the tool.** It is that the measurement has ~287 recoverable\nsessions, an arm-skewed censoring rule, a content-blind gate, and four eg-favouring leaks — and\nthat the one payload block designed to answer the question losing tasks actually ask **could not\nfire in the headline cell at all**.\n\nSign convention: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.** All figures rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is true on Opus\n\n| estimator | value |\n|---|---|\n| total (the reported headline) | +1.35% |\n| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n| median | **−4.16%** |\n| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |\n| t | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n\n**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. Never quote +1.35% without\nthe LOO range and the median beside it.\n\n**And the fair number is bounded ABOVE by this one.** Four eg-favouring leaks are recorded and\nunfixed (§5). Closing them moves the headline **down**, not up.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Corrections to my own work — the full list\n\nRecorded so they are not re-derived, and because most are mine.\n\n1. **\"eg verifies more than baseline\"** — false. eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576. The claim\n   came from the 8 worst losers, a set selected on the outcome.\n2. **\"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\"** — regex artifact. A stricter definition gives n=17\n   and **−0.89%**.\n3. **\"the metric rewards failing to provision\"** — real on `bat-1892` only; **2 of 25 losers**,\n   worth −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.\n4. **\"+35.06% reachable by loser repair\"** — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.\n5. **×0.54 persist calibration** — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**\n   (corr +0.916, R² 0.839). **This one moved projections UP by ~52%.**\n6. **\"Five consecutive corrections, every one downward… nothing has moved the other way\"** —\n   **false, by item 5 above.** It was four downward and one upward. That sentence was rhetorical\n   overreach and is withdrawn.\n7. **R-A zero-toll at +4.3% to +6.0%** — mispriced by **5.2×**. The first search lands at assistant\n   turn median 2 of a median 85-turn session where `cache_read` is 12,231 vs a session mean of\n   63,137. Correct value **+0.96%**, CI [+0.53, +1.38]; n to demonstrate ≈ **19,504 pairs**.\n   It was also priced in the message model that §1 of my own document retires.\n8. **The VERIFY collect-only probe as a new fix** — `EG_VERIFY_PROBE=1` was **already set in\n   `run_REP50.sh:141`** and live during rep50. Also a no-op on 84% of drag (21/25 losers got no\n   VERIFY line).\n9. **\"Retrieval/ranking is anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5)\"** — this is\n   **n=13, p≈0.29**. It cannot support closing a lever, and it was load-bearing in two sections.\n   Demoted to **not tested**.\n10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the\n    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is\n    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact.\n11. **\"gold-ADD is 54% of all drag\"** — does not survive leave-one-out, and is labeller-dependent\n    (36.8-pt gap between two labellers). Task kind is **not** a usable predictor. Retracted, and\n    with it the ledger's §1.1 \"best current idea\".\n\n---\n\n## 3. Why instances lose\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances; lift +21.21 over 24; `lombok-3674` alone +6.09 (29% of lift).**\n\n| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n| post-edit exploration | +159 | −81 |\n| post-edit harness | +50 | −88 |\n| turns | +296 | −258 |\n\n**The graph works pre-edit in BOTH groups.** Localization is not the discriminator.\n\n**The discriminator is displacement:** label a session displaced if eg's shell-exploration count is\nbelow its paired baseline. **Displaced & won 19/21 (90.5%); not-displaced & won 6/28 (21.4%);\nAUC 0.838.** Sessions that call the graph: pooled **+6.30%**, median +12.61%. The 16 that never\ncall it: pooled −1.02%, median **−24.94%**. **Calling and displacing is the winning behaviour.**\n\n**Task kind does NOT predict outcome — this retires the ledger's best remaining idea.**\nPut through the same leave-one-out test that killed the headline:\n\n| | n | TOTAL | median | 10% trimmed | wins | LOO range |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MOD | 32 | +4.38% | +8.90% | **−3.44%** | 16/32 | −0.18% … +10.52% — **spans zero** |\n| ADD | 17 | −1.44% | −16.82% | −18.14% | 8/17 | −15.76% … +4.25% — **spans zero** |\n\nThree independent breaks: (a) dropping ADD's worst instance flips ADD to **+0.60%**;\n(b) `lombok-3674` is an **ADD** task eg won by +71%, so dropping it makes ADD *worse* — the same\ninstance carries both the headline and this; (c) **the labeller decides the answer** — one\nlabeller gives MOD +13.59% / ADD −23.19% (n=36/13), mine gives +4.38% / −1.44% (n=32/17). A\n36.8-pt gap collapses to 5.8 pt on a labelling choice. GEM300 also inverts the sign.\n**Do not build a MOD/ADD router or spend on a classifier.**\n\n**No prompt/ask feature predicts the outcome either:** quoted error strings −0.278, traceback\n−0.229, distinct identifiers +0.150, file paths named −0.135, code fences +0.089, prompt length\n−0.027, backticked spans +0.013.\n\n**Neither repo nor language predicts outcome.** Language R² = **0.153**; only **5 of 14** repos\nwith >1 instance are internally consistent (`laravel` = [+51, −5, −59, −124, +39]). Per-repo or\nper-language configs are not viable, which is why the ledger already struck that lever.\n\n---\n\n## 4. THE BUILD — make one call answer the whole task\n\n### 4.0 The thesis\n\nThe ideal session is: **call the graph → find the site → edit → test → done.** ~7 turns.\nSessions run a **median of 85**, and the agent still makes **24.6 exploration calls per session\neven with the graph**. It is not exploring because the graph failed to locate — pre-edit\nexploration falls in BOTH winners and losers. It is exploring because one search answers *where\nis it*, and it then has to discover **what calls it**, **what tests it**, **how to run that test**,\nand **what else must change**.\n\n**entire-graph computes all four.** It ships none of them in the one call the agent makes:\n\n| the agent's next question | eg has the answer | why it never arrives |\n|---|---|---|\n| what else must change? | RELATED SITES block | **cannot emit at `--top-k ≤ 5`**; cell ran 5 |\n| what else is in this file? | FILE OUTLINE (`search_outline.go`, 217 LOC) | **default OFF**, absent from `--help` |\n| what test covers this? | covering-test selection | present in only **8 of 33** payloads |\n| how do I run it? | derived VERIFY command | same 8/33; and 21/25 losers got none |\n| who calls this? | CALLS edges (12.6k) | only via `neighbors`/`impact` — **0/49 adoption** |\n\n**So the build is not new capability. It is restructuring the payload to answer all five in the\none call the agent already makes — and paying for it by deleting source dumps nobody reads.**\n\n### 4.1 Pay for it first — remove bytes *(all measured)*\n\n| change | file | delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| complete bodies rank 5 → 2 | `search_enclosure.go:41` | **10,822 → 2,590 B (−76%)** — rank 1 read 62%/edited 54%, rank 2 27%/20%, **rank 3+ 0–11%** |\n| `--format` default json → text | `cli/search.go` parser | **−44%** (json is 1.79× text); doctrine agents read prescribes no `--format`, so real users get the fat form |\n| `graph grep`: exclude vendored/minified/generated | grep path | **negative bytes**, and fixes the only measured case of the graph being *worse than no tool* (prometheus: one hit in minified `d3.v3.js` where plain grep gave a clean zero → **~19 turns lost**) |\n\n### 4.2 Spend it on answers\n\n| change | file | delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| `EG_TOPK` 5 → 8 so RELATED SITES can emit | harness one-liner, no rebuild | +~600 B |\n| FILE OUTLINE on by default | `search_outline.go`, flag `cli/search.go:1637` | +1,421 B — its own measurement: 77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload already named, 35 immediately followed by a Read of it |\n| raise covering-test + VERIFY coverage from 8/33 | `search_verify.go` | +~200 B |\n\n**Net still negative**, and the payload changes from *five source bodies* to *one body plus four\nanswers*.\n\n### 4.3 Preconditions — non-negotiable, all currently violated\n\n- **Rebuild the binary.** The in-tree one is stale (rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`), and\n  `run_3arm.sh`'s DEFAULT binary is missing every recent payload feature — any cell without an\n  explicit `ENTIRE_GRAPH` override measures a tool that no longer exists.\n- Add a preflight that aborts on `capabilities --json` lacking the features the cell assumes.\n- Fix `AGENTS.md:72`, which states `edges --to/--from/--relation` does not exist. It does\n  (`root.go:576-594`) and is the only route to 13 relation types.\n- Document `verify`, `changed`, `def` — 971 LOC of `def` is in neither agent guide.\n- Move the arm-asymmetric advice switch **into the binary** (`--no-advice`); today fairness depends\n  on a 9-pattern literal grep in another repo whose default is OFF.\n\n### 4.4 Free statistical power — do this before any cell\n\n**287 of ~1,560 arm-sessions are dropped WITH THEIR PAIR, but their token counts survive verbatim\nin the Claude Code transcripts.** 132 of 133 zero-byte `cc_out.json` have an *empty* `cc_err.log`.\nRecovering them is a scoring change, not a cell — and it is the only free n available.\n\nAlso fix two gate defects that currently **flatter eg**: turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed (eg\ntruncates **2.75×** more often and those pairs are deleted — they are eg's worst sessions), and the\npatch gate is a byte count that admitted a **1,892,106 B / 1,708-file** patch on `gson-2479`.\n\n### 4.5 DO NOT BUILD — refuted this session\n\nR-A zero-toll (+0.96%, needs 19,504 pairs, and it removes the call in the cohort where calling\n*wins*) · VERIFY collect-only probe (already ON in rep50, no-op on 84% of drag) · MOD/ADD router\n(fails LOO, labeller-dependent) · post-edit consistency hook (its fair form's biggest beneficiary\nis the *baseline* in `lombok-3674`) · any new verb in the affordance tail (0/66) · anything needing\na post-edit agent call (42/49 make none) · better ranking · bigger payloads · graph-backed grep.\n\n### 4.6 What this is expected to do — stated honestly\n\n**No number is promised.** Every measured-effect claim in this project has been retracted at least\nonce (§2 lists eleven). What is *certain* is the byte arithmetic and that RELATED SITES was\nstructurally off. What is *unproven* is whether answering the agent's next four questions in the\nfirst call reduces its 24.6 exploration calls.\n\n**That is the hypothesis the gate exists to test**, and it is the first one in this project where\nthe mechanism is a capability being switched on rather than a correlate being chased.\n\n## 5. Integrity — before any cell\n\n1. **Four eg-favouring answer leaks** are recorded in memory and unfixed. `bat-1892` (worst loser,\n   −2.81 pts) made **12 references into `bat-3108`**, a later revision of the same repo containing\n   the implemented feature. Measured: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline.** Direction matters —\n   closing these moves the headline **down**.\n2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells** — `prometheus-9248` audited `/tmp/goyacc*` built by\n   other instances' sessions. eg 3/49, base 1/49. Give each session a private temp root.\n3. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.\n4. **`CC_TIMEOUT`** may have censored the right tail; if rep50 ran at 1400 s the paired sd of 0.494\n   is an **underestimate** and every power calculation here is optimistic.\n5. **`echoPresearchPayload` has no length check** (`cli/search.go:286`) — a zero-byte payload gives\n   0 bytes on stdout with exit 0, the \"announced but never shipped\" failure class. The guard exists\n   on another branch and is not on this tree.\n\n**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, 0 commit mismatches, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches small,\nprompt diff 18 lines all of which are checkout paths.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gates\n\nMDE ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between cells.\n**No token claim below n≈50 in either direction.**\n\n| gate | n | criterion |\n|---|---|---|\n| **V0** offline $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; RELATED SITES fires at TOPK=8 on recorded queries; grep returns a clean zero on the prometheus query; 287 sessions recovered and re-scored |\n| ~~V1~~ | — | **Already run: MOD/ADD fails LOO and is labeller-dependent. Lever closed.** |\n| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: **displacement rate** (eg shell calls < paired baseline) up from 21/49; RELATED SITES present in payloads; no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |\n| **V3** live | 50+ | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together**, plus per-arm censoring counts |\n\n**Winner tripwire (your instruction: abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,\n`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` in every sample from V2. Compare only against a **same-wave**\ncontrol — never a previous cell.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Honest expected outcome\n\n**No number is promised.** The two items with a real mechanism and no prior art are §4.1 (RELATED\nSITES was structurally off) and §4.2 (grep noise where a clean zero existed). Both are cheap, both\nare fair, and neither has been measured. Everything else in §4 is hygiene that makes the *next*\nmeasurement trustworthy rather than moving the current one.\n\n**The ceiling on loser repair is +21.21%** — arithmetic (the lift pool), not projection.\n**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change**; the only intervention that would reach it is\nan instruction to explore and re-test less, which helps a no-tool arm equally and is exactly what\nthe withdrawn −35% contained.\n\n**If §4.1 and §4.2 do not move the displacement rate at V2, the honest conclusion is that\nentire-graph is not a token tool on this corpus** — and the defensible claim becomes correctness\nand latency, plus whole-file-read suppression (119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B), which is\nmeasurable at n=49 today.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Verification\n\n- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO for\n  tree-sitter). **Rebuild the binary — it is stale.** Unit tests beside the grep filter.\n- Offline replay: `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log` + `.payload`; re-run against the binary at\n  zero model cost; assert the change fires **and** that nothing else moved.\n- Harness deploys by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a script\n  a running session is reading.\n- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** trimmed **and** LOO **and** Δturns **and**\n  per-arm censoring counts.\n","planFilePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":910716,"output_tokens":1500,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":705,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1500,"cache_read_input_tokens":910716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":705},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqmRuuLuePPD6kRTzos2","type":"assistant","uuid":"7fb7950f-9b50-43ab-92ae-b05827df00b1","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:38:02.446Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"7fb7950f-9b50-43ab-92ae-b05827df00b1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1d9542e6-34ca-418f-a5c1-b911bcf76f39","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"User has approved your plan. You can now start coding. Start with updating your todo list if applicable\n\nYour plan has been saved to: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/stateless-napping-unicorn.md\nYou can refer back to it if needed during implementation.\n\n## Approved Plan:\n# entire-graph on Opus — final plan\n\n## Context\n\nThe goal was **35% token savings on rep50, Opus, fairly measured**. You later relaxed it to the\nright target: **stop the tool making instances worse** — a code graph should not lose. This plan\nis built against that, after five investigations (two loser dissections, a capability inventory,\na 4-lens artifact audit, and an iterative fix workflow) totalling ~4.5M subagent tokens.\n\n**The headline finding is not about the tool.** It is that the measurement has ~287 recoverable\nsessions, an arm-skewed censoring rule, a content-blind gate, and four eg-favouring leaks — and\nthat the one payload block designed to answer the question losing tasks actually ask **could not\nfire in the headline cell at all**.\n\nSign convention: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.** All figures rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is true on Opus\n\n| estimator | value |\n|---|---|\n| total (the reported headline) | +1.35% |\n| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n| median | **−4.16%** |\n| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |\n| t | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n\n**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. Never quote +1.35% without\nthe LOO range and the median beside it.\n\n**And the fair number is bounded ABOVE by this one.** Four eg-favouring leaks are recorded and\nunfixed (§5). Closing them moves the headline **down**, not up.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Corrections to my own work — the full list\n\nRecorded so they are not re-derived, and because most are mine.\n\n1. **\"eg verifies more than baseline\"** — false. eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576. The claim\n   came from the 8 worst losers, a set selected on the outcome.\n2. **\"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\"** — regex artifact. A stricter definition gives n=17\n   and **−0.89%**.\n3. **\"the metric rewards failing to provision\"** — real on `bat-1892` only; **2 of 25 losers**,\n   worth −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.\n4. **\"+35.06% reachable by loser repair\"** — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.\n5. **×0.54 persist calibration** — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**\n   (corr +0.916, R² 0.839). **This one moved projections UP by ~52%.**\n6. **\"Five consecutive corrections, every one downward… nothing has moved the other way\"** —\n   **false, by item 5 above.** It was four downward and one upward. That sentence was rhetorical\n   overreach and is withdrawn.\n7. **R-A zero-toll at +4.3% to +6.0%** — mispriced by **5.2×**. The first search lands at assistant\n   turn median 2 of a median 85-turn session where `cache_read` is 12,231 vs a session mean of\n   63,137. Correct value **+0.96%**, CI [+0.53, +1.38]; n to demonstrate ≈ **19,504 pairs**.\n   It was also priced in the message model that §1 of my own document retires.\n8. **The VERIFY collect-only probe as a new fix** — `EG_VERIFY_PROBE=1` was **already set in\n   `run_REP50.sh:141`** and live during rep50. Also a no-op on 84% of drag (21/25 losers got no\n   VERIFY line).\n9. **\"Retrieval/ranking is anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5)\"** — this is\n   **n=13, p≈0.29**. It cannot support closing a lever, and it was load-bearing in two sections.\n   Demoted to **not tested**.\n10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the\n    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is\n    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact.\n11. **\"gold-ADD is 54% of all drag\"** — does not survive leave-one-out, and is labeller-dependent\n    (36.8-pt gap between two labellers). Task kind is **not** a usable predictor. Retracted, and\n    with it the ledger's §1.1 \"best current idea\".\n\n---\n\n## 3. Why instances lose\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances; lift +21.21 over 24; `lombok-3674` alone +6.09 (29% of lift).**\n\n| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n| post-edit exploration | +159 | −81 |\n| post-edit harness | +50 | −88 |\n| turns | +296 | −258 |\n\n**The graph works pre-edit in BOTH groups.** Localization is not the discriminator.\n\n**The discriminator is displacement:** label a session displaced if eg's shell-exploration count is\nbelow its paired baseline. **Displaced & won 19/21 (90.5%); not-displaced & won 6/28 (21.4%);\nAUC 0.838.** Sessions that call the graph: pooled **+6.30%**, median +12.61%. The 16 that never\ncall it: pooled −1.02%, median **−24.94%**. **Calling and displacing is the winning behaviour.**\n\n**Task kind does NOT predict outcome — this retires the ledger's best remaining idea.**\nPut through the same leave-one-out test that killed the headline:\n\n| | n | TOTAL | median | 10% trimmed | wins | LOO range |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MOD | 32 | +4.38% | +8.90% | **−3.44%** | 16/32 | −0.18% … +10.52% — **spans zero** |\n| ADD | 17 | −1.44% | −16.82% | −18.14% | 8/17 | −15.76% … +4.25% — **spans zero** |\n\nThree independent breaks: (a) dropping ADD's worst instance flips ADD to **+0.60%**;\n(b) `lombok-3674` is an **ADD** task eg won by +71%, so dropping it makes ADD *worse* — the same\ninstance carries both the headline and this; (c) **the labeller decides the answer** — one\nlabeller gives MOD +13.59% / ADD −23.19% (n=36/13), mine gives +4.38% / −1.44% (n=32/17). A\n36.8-pt gap collapses to 5.8 pt on a labelling choice. GEM300 also inverts the sign.\n**Do not build a MOD/ADD router or spend on a classifier.**\n\n**No prompt/ask feature predicts the outcome either:** quoted error strings −0.278, traceback\n−0.229, distinct identifiers +0.150, file paths named −0.135, code fences +0.089, prompt length\n−0.027, backticked spans +0.013.\n\n**Neither repo nor language predicts outcome.** Language R² = **0.153**; only **5 of 14** repos\nwith >1 instance are internally consistent (`laravel` = [+51, −5, −59, −124, +39]). Per-repo or\nper-language configs are not viable, which is why the ledger already struck that lever.\n\n---\n\n## 4. THE BUILD — make one call answer the whole task\n\n### 4.0 The thesis\n\nThe ideal session is: **call the graph → find the site → edit → test → done.** ~7 turns.\nSessions run a **median of 85**, and the agent still makes **24.6 exploration calls per session\neven with the graph**. It is not exploring because the graph failed to locate — pre-edit\nexploration falls in BOTH winners and losers. It is exploring because one search answers *where\nis it*, and it then has to discover **what calls it**, **what tests it**, **how to run that test**,\nand **what else must change**.\n\n**entire-graph computes all four.** It ships none of them in the one call the agent makes:\n\n| the agent's next question | eg has the answer | why it never arrives |\n|---|---|---|\n| what else must change? | RELATED SITES block | **cannot emit at `--top-k ≤ 5`**; cell ran 5 |\n| what else is in this file? | FILE OUTLINE (`search_outline.go`, 217 LOC) | **default OFF**, absent from `--help` |\n| what test covers this? | covering-test selection | present in only **8 of 33** payloads |\n| how do I run it? | derived VERIFY command | same 8/33; and 21/25 losers got none |\n| who calls this? | CALLS edges (12.6k) | only via `neighbors`/`impact` — **0/49 adoption** |\n\n**So the build is not new capability. It is restructuring the payload to answer all five in the\none call the agent already makes — and paying for it by deleting source dumps nobody reads.**\n\n### 4.1 Pay for it first — remove bytes *(all measured)*\n\n| change | file | delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| complete bodies rank 5 → 2 | `search_enclosure.go:41` | **10,822 → 2,590 B (−76%)** — rank 1 read 62%/edited 54%, rank 2 27%/20%, **rank 3+ 0–11%** |\n| `--format` default json → text | `cli/search.go` parser | **−44%** (json is 1.79× text); doctrine agents read prescribes no `--format`, so real users get the fat form |\n| `graph grep`: exclude vendored/minified/generated | grep path | **negative bytes**, and fixes the only measured case of the graph being *worse than no tool* (prometheus: one hit in minified `d3.v3.js` where plain grep gave a clean zero → **~19 turns lost**) |\n\n### 4.2 Spend it on answers\n\n| change | file | delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| `EG_TOPK` 5 → 8 so RELATED SITES can emit | harness one-liner, no rebuild | +~600 B |\n| FILE OUTLINE on by default | `search_outline.go`, flag `cli/search.go:1637` | +1,421 B — its own measurement: 77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload already named, 35 immediately followed by a Read of it |\n| raise covering-test + VERIFY coverage from 8/33 | `search_verify.go` | +~200 B |\n\n**Net still negative**, and the payload changes from *five source bodies* to *one body plus four\nanswers*.\n\n### 4.3 Preconditions — non-negotiable, all currently violated\n\n- **Rebuild the binary.** The in-tree one is stale (rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`), and\n  `run_3arm.sh`'s DEFAULT binary is missing every recent payload feature — any cell without an\n  explicit `ENTIRE_GRAPH` override measures a tool that no longer exists.\n- Add a preflight that aborts on `capabilities --json` lacking the features the cell assumes.\n- Fix `AGENTS.md:72`, which states `edges --to/--from/--relation` does not exist. It does\n  (`root.go:576-594`) and is the only route to 13 relation types.\n- Document `verify`, `changed`, `def` — 971 LOC of `def` is in neither agent guide.\n- Move the arm-asymmetric advice switch **into the binary** (`--no-advice`); today fairness depends\n  on a 9-pattern literal grep in another repo whose default is OFF.\n\n### 4.4 Free statistical power — do this before any cell\n\n**287 of ~1,560 arm-sessions are dropped WITH THEIR PAIR, but their token counts survive verbatim\nin the Claude Code transcripts.** 132 of 133 zero-byte `cc_out.json` have an *empty* `cc_err.log`.\nRecovering them is a scoring change, not a cell — and it is the only free n available.\n\nAlso fix two gate defects that currently **flatter eg**: turn-cap censoring is arm-skewed (eg\ntruncates **2.75×** more often and those pairs are deleted — they are eg's worst sessions), and the\npatch gate is a byte count that admitted a **1,892,106 B / 1,708-file** patch on `gson-2479`.\n\n### 4.5 DO NOT BUILD — refuted this session\n\nR-A zero-toll (+0.96%, needs 19,504 pairs, and it removes the call in the cohort where calling\n*wins*) · VERIFY collect-only probe (already ON in rep50, no-op on 84% of drag) · MOD/ADD router\n(fails LOO, labeller-dependent) · post-edit consistency hook (its fair form's biggest beneficiary\nis the *baseline* in `lombok-3674`) · any new verb in the affordance tail (0/66) · anything needing\na post-edit agent call (42/49 make none) · better ranking · bigger payloads · graph-backed grep.\n\n### 4.6 What this is expected to do — stated honestly\n\n**No number is promised.** Every measured-effect claim in this project has been retracted at least\nonce (§2 lists eleven). What is *certain* is the byte arithmetic and that RELATED SITES was\nstructurally off. What is *unproven* is whether answering the agent's next four questions in the\nfirst call reduces its 24.6 exploration calls.\n\n**That is the hypothesis the gate exists to test**, and it is the first one in this project where\nthe mechanism is a capability being switched on rather than a correlate being chased.\n\n## 5. Integrity — before any cell\n\n1. **Four eg-favouring answer leaks** are recorded in memory and unfixed. `bat-1892` (worst loser,\n   −2.81 pts) made **12 references into `bat-3108`**, a later revision of the same repo containing\n   the implemented feature. Measured: **2/49 eg sessions, 0/49 baseline.** Direction matters —\n   closing these moves the headline **down**.\n2. **Shared `/tmp` between concurrent cells** — `prometheus-9248` audited `/tmp/goyacc*` built by\n   other instances' sessions. eg 3/49, base 1/49. Give each session a private temp root.\n3. **`EMPTY PAYLOAD` detector is broken** — fires on sessions holding 7,757 payload bytes.\n4. **`CC_TIMEOUT`** may have censored the right tail; if rep50 ran at 1400 s the paired sd of 0.494\n   is an **underestimate** and every power calculation here is optimistic.\n5. **`echoPresearchPayload` has no length check** (`cli/search.go:286`) — a zero-byte payload gives\n   0 bytes on stdout with exit 0, the \"announced but never shipped\" failure class. The guard exists\n   on another branch and is not on this tree.\n\n**Validated clean:** 49/49 graphs present, 0 commit mismatches, 0 of 310 under 50 KB, caches small,\nprompt diff 18 lines all of which are checkout paths.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gates\n\nMDE ~25–30 pts against a ~100-pt same-instance noise floor; 93% of losers flip sign between cells.\n**No token claim below n≈50 in either direction.**\n\n| gate | n | criterion |\n|---|---|---|\n| **V0** offline $0 | 0 | `mise run check` green; RELATED SITES fires at TOPK=8 on recorded queries; grep returns a clean zero on the prometheus query; 287 sessions recovered and re-scored |\n| ~~V1~~ | — | **Already run: MOD/ADD fails LOO and is labeller-dependent. Lever closed.** |\n| **V2** live | 12 | mechanism only: **displacement rate** (eg shell calls < paired baseline) up from 21/49; RELATED SITES present in payloads; no rise in whole-file Reads. **No token claim.** |\n| **V3** live | 50+ | first token claim: bootstrap CI, and **total + median + trimmed + LOO reported together**, plus per-arm censoring counts |\n\n**Winner tripwire (your instruction: abort at >10pt):** `lombok-3674`, `fmt-2457`,\n`qutebrowser-c580`, `redis-11510` in every sample from V2. Compare only against a **same-wave**\ncontrol — never a previous cell.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Honest expected outcome\n\n**No number is promised.** The two items with a real mechanism and no prior art are §4.1 (RELATED\nSITES was structurally off) and §4.2 (grep noise where a clean zero existed). Both are cheap, both\nare fair, and neither has been measured. Everything else in §4 is hygiene that makes the *next*\nmeasurement trustworthy rather than moving the current one.\n\n**The ceiling on loser repair is +21.21%** — arithmetic (the lift pool), not projection.\n**35% is not reachable on Opus by any fair change**; the only intervention that would reach it is\nan instruction to explore and re-test less, which helps a no-tool arm equally and is exactly what\nthe withdrawn −35% contained.\n\n**If §4.1 and §4.2 do not move the displacement rate at V2, the honest conclusion is that\nentire-graph is not a token tool on this corpus** — and the defensible claim becomes correctness\nand latency, plus whole-file-read suppression (119 → 105 calls, median 5,125 → 4,081 B), which is\nmeasurable at n=49 today.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Verification\n\n- `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && mise run check` (fmt + vet + race + build; CGO for\n  tree-sitter). **Rebuild the binary — it is stale.** Unit tests beside the grep filter.\n- Offline replay: `results/<tag>/eg/<iid>/gq_calls.log` + `.payload`; re-run against the binary at\n  zero model cost; assert the change fires **and** that nothing else moved.\n- Harness deploys by temp path + atomic `mv` with a live-session guard — never overwrite a script\n  a running session is reading.\n- Every gate reports total **and** median **and** trimmed **and** LOO **and** Δturns **and**\n  per-arm censoring counts.\n","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DMfdEL9zfEd6R1MvJo7ucA"}]},"uuid":"993fe1e7-7c09-47f1-a6be-ff66f7500a01","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:39:01.310Z","toolUseResult":{"plan":"# entire-graph on Opus — final plan\n\n## Context\n\nThe goal was **35% token savings on rep50, Opus, fairly measured**. You later relaxed it to the\nright target: **stop the tool making instances worse** — a code graph should not lose. This plan\nis built against that, after five investigations (two loser dissections, a capability inventory,\na 4-lens artifact audit, and an iterative fix workflow) totalling ~4.5M subagent tokens.\n\n**The headline finding is not about the tool.** It is that the measurement has ~287 recoverable\nsessions, an arm-skewed censoring rule, a content-blind gate, and four eg-favouring leaks — and\nthat the one payload block designed to answer the question losing tasks actually ask **could not\nfire in the headline cell at all**.\n\nSign convention: **positive = graph arm saved tokens.** All figures rep50, Opus/max, 49 gated pairs.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is true on Opus\n\n| estimator | value |\n|---|---|\n| total (the reported headline) | +1.35% |\n| **leave-one-out: drop `lombok-3674`** | **−5.18%** |\n| median | **−4.16%** |\n| 10% trimmed mean | **−7.65%** |\n| t | **−0.17 — indistinguishable from zero** |\n\n**The headline is one instance.** Every robust estimator says eg loses. Never quote +1.35% without\nthe LOO range and the median beside it.\n\n**And the fair number is bounded ABOVE by this one.** Four eg-favouring leaks are recorded and\nunfixed (§5). Closing them moves the headline **down**, not up.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Corrections to my own work — the full list\n\nRecorded so they are not re-derived, and because most are mine.\n\n1. **\"eg verifies more than baseline\"** — false. eg 545 harness runs vs baseline 576. The claim\n   came from the 8 worst losers, a set selected on the outcome.\n2. **\"eg loses 14.49% when both arms build\"** — regex artifact. A stricter definition gives n=17\n   and **−0.89%**.\n3. **\"the metric rewards failing to provision\"** — real on `bat-1892` only; **2 of 25 losers**,\n   worth −1.06 pts. Refuted as a driver.\n4. **\"+35.06% reachable by loser repair\"** — arithmetic artifact; the lift pool caps it at +21.21%.\n5. **×0.54 persist calibration** — wrong; the validated figure is the regression **slope 0.822**\n   (corr +0.916, R² 0.839). **This one moved projections UP by ~52%.**\n6. **\"Five consecutive corrections, every one downward… nothing has moved the other way\"** —\n   **false, by item 5 above.** It was four downward and one upward. That sentence was rhetorical\n   overreach and is withdrawn.\n7. **R-A zero-toll at +4.3% to +6.0%** — mispriced by **5.2×**. The first search lands at assistant\n   turn median 2 of a median 85-turn session where `cache_read` is 12,231 vs a session mean of\n   63,137. Correct value **+0.96%**, CI [+0.53, +1.38]; n to demonstrate ≈ **19,504 pairs**.\n   It was also priced in the message model that §1 of my own document retires.\n8. **The VERIFY collect-only probe as a new fix** — `EG_VERIFY_PROBE=1` was **already set in\n   `run_REP50.sh:141`** and live during rep50. Also a no-op on 84% of drag (21/25 losers got no\n   VERIFY line).\n9. **\"Retrieval/ranking is anti-correlated (gold at rank 1: losers 6/8 vs winners 2/5)\"** — this is\n   **n=13, p≈0.29**. It cannot support closing a lever, and it was load-bearing in two sections.\n   Demoted to **not tested**.\n10. **Context-budget arithmetic** — three inconsistent totals in one section; **3.59M (9.3%) of the\n    budget was unlisted**, and the real reconciliation is that the 1.57M classified saving is\n    offset by **+1.50M growth in that unlisted bucket**. That offset, not the headline, is the fact.\n11. **\"gold-ADD is 54% of all drag\"** — does not survive leave-one-out, and is labeller-dependent\n    (36.8-pt gap between two labellers). Task kind is **not** a usable predictor. Retracted, and\n    with it the ledger's §1.1 \"best current idea\".\n\n---\n\n## 3. Why instances lose\n\n**Drag −19.86 pts over 25 instances; lift +21.21 over 24; `lombok-3674` alone +6.09 (29% of lift).**\n\n| | losers (25) | winners (24) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **pre-edit exploration** | **−46** | **−58** |\n| post-edit exploration | +159 | −81 |\n| post-edit harness | +50 | −88 |\n| turns | +296 | −258 |\n\n**The graph works pre-edit in BOTH groups.** Localization is not the discriminator.\n\n**The discriminator is displacement:** label a session displaced if eg's shell-exploration count is\nbelow its paired baseline. **Displaced & won 19/21 (90.5%); not-displaced & won 6/28 (21.4%);\nAUC 0.838.** Sessions that call the graph: pooled **+6.30%**, median +12.61%. The 16 that never\ncall it: pooled −1.02%, median **−24.94%**. **Calling and displacing is the winning behaviour.**\n\n**Task kind does NOT predict outcome — this retires the ledger's best remaining idea.**\nPut through the same leave-one-out test that killed the headline:\n\n| | n | TOTAL | median | 10% trimmed | wins | LOO range |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MOD | 32 | +4.38% | +8.90% | **−3.44%** | 16/32 | −0.18% … +10.52% — **spans zero** |\n| ADD | 17 | −1.44% | −16.82% | −18.14% | 8/17 | −15.76% … +4.25% — **spans zero** |\n\nThree independent breaks: (a) dropping ADD's worst instance flips ADD to **+0.60%**;\n(b) `lombok-3674` is an **ADD** task eg won by +71%, so dropping it makes ADD *worse* — the same\ninstance carries both the headline and this; (c) **the labeller decides the answer** — one\nlabeller gives MOD +13.59% / ADD −23.19% (n=36/13), mine gives +4.38% / −1.44% (n=32/17). A\n36.8-pt gap collapses to 5.8 pt on a labelling choice. GEM300 also inverts the sign.\n**Do not build a MOD/ADD router or spend on a classifier.**\n\n**No prompt/ask feature predicts the outcome either:** quoted error strings −0.278, traceback\n−0.229, distinct identifiers +0.150, file paths named −0.135, code fences +0.089, prompt length\n−0.027, backticked spans +0.013.\n\n**Neither repo nor language predicts outcome.** Language R² = **0.153**; only **5 of 14** repos\nwith >1 instance are internally consistent (`laravel` = [+51, −5, −59, −124, +39]). Per-repo or\nper-language configs are not viable, which is why the ledger already struck that lever.\n\n---\n\n## 4. THE BUILD — make one call answer the whole task\n\n### 4.0 The thesis\n\nThe ideal session is: **call the graph → find the site → edit → test → done.** ~7 turns.\nSessions run a **median of 85**, and the agent still makes **24.6 exploration calls per session\neven with the graph**. It is not exploring because the graph failed to locate — pre-edit\nexploration falls in BOTH winners and losers. It is exploring because one search answers *where\nis it*, and it then has to discover **what calls it**, **what tests it**, **how to run that test**,\nand **what else must change**.\n\n**entire-graph computes all four.** It ships none of them in the one call the agent makes:\n\n| the agent's next question | eg has the answer | why it never arrives |\n|---|---|---|\n| what else must change? | RELATED SITES block | **cannot emit at `--top-k ≤ 5`**; cell ran 5 |\n| what else is in this file? | FILE OUTLINE (`search_outline.go`, 217 LOC) | **default OFF**, absent from `--help` |\n| what test covers this? | covering-test selection | present in only **8 of 33** payloads |\n| how do I run it? | derived VERIFY command | same 8/33; and 21/25 losers got none |\n| who calls this? | CALLS edges (12.6k) | only via `neighbors`/`impact` — **0/49 adoption** |\n\n**So the build is not new capability. It is restructuring the payload to answer all five in the\none call the agent already makes — and paying for it by deleting source dumps nobody reads.**\n\n### 4.1 Pay for it first — remove bytes *(all measured)*\n\n| change | file | delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| complete bodies rank 5 → 2 | `search_enclosure.go:41` | **10,822 → 2,590 B (−76%)** — rank 1 read 62%/edited 54%, rank 2 27%/20%, **rank 3+ 0–11%** |\n| `--format` default json → text | `cli/search.go` parser | **−44%** (json is 1.79× text); doctrine agents read prescribes no `--format`, so real users get the fat form |\n| `graph grep`: exclude vendored/minified/generated | grep path | **negative bytes**, and fixes the only measured case of the graph being *worse than no tool* (prometheus: one hit in minified `d3.v3.js` where plain grep gave a clean zero → **~19 turns lost**) |\n\n### 4.2 Spend it on answers\n\n| change | file | delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| `EG_TOPK` 5 → 8 so RELATED SITES can emit | harness one-liner, no rebuild | +~600 B |\n| FILE OUTLINE on by default | `search_outline.go`, flag `cli/search.go:1637` | +1,421 B — its own measurement: 77 targeted greps landed on a file the payload already named, 35 immediately followed by a Read of it |\n| raise covering-test + VERIFY coverage from 8/33 | `search_verify.go` | +~200 B |\n\n**Net still negative**, and the payload changes from *five source bodies* to *one body plus four\nanswers*.\n\n### 4.3 Preconditions — non-negotiable, all currently violated\n\n- **Rebuild the binary.** The in-tree one is stale (rejects `verify`, `changed`, `--path`), and\n  `run_3arm.sh`'s DEFAULT binary is missing every recent payload feature — any cell without an\n  explicit `ENTIRE_GRAPH` override measures a tool that no longer exists.\n- Add a preflight that aborts on `capabilities --json` lacking the features the cell assumes.\n- Fix `AGENTS.md:72`, which states `edges --to/--from/--relation` does not exist. It does\n  (`root.go:576-594`) and is the only route to 13 relation types.\n- Document `verify`, `changed`, `def` — 971 LOC of `def` is in neither agent guide.\n- Move the arm-asymmetric advice switch **into the binary** (`--no-advice`); today fairness depends\n  on a 9-pattern literal grep in another repo whose default is OFF.\n\n### 4.4 Free statistical power — do this before any cell\n\n**287 of ~1,560 arm-sessions are dropped WITH THEIR PAIR, but their token count