{"parentUuid":"56ef5b94-3c74-47b1-b48d-fad3aa10608c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1d9542e6-34ca-418f-a5c1-b911bcf76f39","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HzdRFnGPjse7VsJ1Ci6Uhr","type":"tool_result","content":"1:func writeTextSearch(out interface{ Write([]byte) (int, error) }, response sem.SearchResponse) error {\n7:\t// The closed-set warning precedes everything, including the map: it is the only block that\n8:\t// changes what the patch has to CONTAIN, and a reader who has already written the edit will not\n9:\t// come back for it.\n15:\t// The map is printed before any body: it is what tells the reader whether the ranked\n16:\t// bodies below it are the whole change, and an agent that has already decided to read the\n17:\t// file will not scroll back for it.\n23:\tprimary, related, docs, tests := partitionSearchSections(response.Results)\n24:\t// THE DIET. A body is printed for the first searchTextMaxFullBodies entries that carry source, and\n25:\t// every entry after that prints as a locator whatever the allocator gave it. Ranks the caller\n26:\t// explicitly forced (full-unit / callee-hop) are exempt: asking for a unit and being handed a\n27:\t// locator would make the flag a no-op.\n29:\t// POSITION IN THE BODY QUEUE, not index in the group. A low-value path that is demoted below\n30:\t// spends no body slot AND no rank tier: charging its rank against the full-snippet tier would\n31:\t// leave the agent one full window short for exactly the hits that are real source, which is the\n32:\t// same reason a sectioned-away non-code hit does not charge its rank either (see the doc comment\n33:\t// above). Without low-value hits in the group this is the group index, so the ordinary payload is\n34:\t// byte-identical.\n37:\t// THE RE-ANCHOR FUNDING INVARIANT, the renderer's half. A body a hit can only claim because it was\n38:\t// re-anchored onto code (sem/search_reanchor.go) is funded out of SPARE slots, never out of a slot 