{"parentUuid":"4ab1f246-9611-4467-a4cb-068aee7b4cd2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqnkPNhb6kKWu5b9EWTs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now implementing the `graph grep` filter. The prometheus false positive was `web/ui/static/vendor/rickshaw/vendor/d3.v3.js` — a path rule catches it. Writing it with the same anchoring discipline as `_istest.py`:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1592,"cache_read_input_tokens":945949,"output_tokens":2853,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1592,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2853,"cache_read_input_tokens":945949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1592},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqnkEoGWxk27vWKptv5F","type":"assistant","uuid":"5d7fce41-d28c-429a-88b0-7a3163c50c7a","timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:55:09.532Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"73009f6a-a642-4aaa-8da3-51eb6bcc5b49","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"stateless-napping-unicorn"}
{"parentUuid":"5d7fce41-d28c-429a-88b0-7a3163c50c7a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqnkPNhb6kKWu5b9EWTs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LVvgETGCY6nDMJK8epmsg6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench/agentic-swebench/tools/_isvendor.py","content":"r\"\"\"Vendored / minified / generated path predicate for the tool-arm grep verb.\n\nWHY THIS EXISTS (measured, prometheus__prometheus-9248):\n\nThe task was to make `atan2` a first-class binary operator — an ADD task, so the identifier does\nnot exist in the repo yet. Both arms opened with the same query:\n\n    baseline   grep -rn \"atan2\\|ATAN2\" --include=*.go --include=*.y .\n               -> 31 B: \"(Bash completed with no output)\"\n\n    eg         entire graph grep \"atan2|ATAN2\"\n               -> 165 B: web/ui/static/vendor/rickshaw/vendor/d3.v3.js:1 | d3=function(){...\n                  \"(1 matches)\"\n\n`entire graph grep` shells out to `grep -rInE` over the whole worktree and filters ONLY test\npaths, so it manufactured a hit inside a minified vendored copy of d3 where plain grep returned a\nclean zero.\n\nThat inversion is the defect, and the direction matters: **a clean zero is actionable** — it says\n\"this identifier does not exist here, stop looking for it and pivot\" — while one hit in minified\nvendored JS is not. Baseline pivoted on its very next call to the error string from the issue text\nand pinned `promql/engine.go:2089 scalarBinop` (a gold edit site) at call 2. eg never grepped the\nerror string; it spent calls 3, 5, 6, 7 and 8 re-confirming atan2's absence — call 7 re-derived\nthis same d3.js hit — and reached `scalarBinop` at calls 21-22. **~19 turns, seeded by the tool's\nopening answer.**\n\nThis is the only case measured in the rep50 corpus where the graph arm's output was WORSE than\nhaving no tool at all, and the fix REMOVES bytes rather than adding them.\n\nDESIGN, mirroring tools/_istest.py:\n  * every directory alternative is anchored at a path-component boundary `(?:^|/)`, so it fires on\n    repo-relative paths and never mid-word — \"vendored_test.go\", \"my_vendor_api.py\" and\n    \"distributed/\" do NOT match;\n  * only HIGH-CONFIDENCE vendoring is listed. `dist/` and `build/` are deliberately NOT here:\n    they are product source in enough repos (and are the edit target in some) that excluding them\n    would suppress real hits. The cost of a missed exclusion is one noisy line; the cost of a\n    wrong exclusion is hiding the answer;\n  * `vendor/` IS included: it is Go's standard vendoring directory and PHP's Composer target. Note\n    the predicate is applied to grep RESULT paths only, never to commands, so filtering it cannot\n    hide `vendor/bin/phpunit` from anything that needs to run it;\n  * minified files are matched on the `.min.` infix and on source maps, both of which are\n    unambiguous;\n  * lockfiles are excluded: they contain every dependency name in the tree and match almost any\n    identifier query, which is exactly the noise mode this predicate exists to stop.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport re\n\n# Directory components that mean \"this subtree is not this repo's source\".\n_VENDOR_DIR = (\n    r\"(?:vendor|vendored|node_modules|third_party|third-party|thirdparty\"\n    r\"|bower_components|jspm_packages|Godeps|site-packages|\\.venv|venv\"\n    r\"|\\.yarn|\\.pnpm-store|eggs|\\.eggs)\"\n)\n\n# Lockfiles: every dependency name in the tree, so they match nearly any identifier query.\n_LOCKFILES = (\n    r\"(?:package-lock\\.json|yarn\\.lock|pnpm-lock\\.yaml|Gemfile\\.lock|composer\\.lock\"\n    r\"|Cargo\\.lock|poetry\\.lock|Pipfile\\.lock|go\\.sum|mix\\.lock|pubspec\\.lock)\"\n)\n\n_RX = re.compile(\n    # --- vendored subtree, anchored at a path-component boundary ---------------------------\n    r\"(?:^|/)\" + _VENDOR_DIR + r\"/\"\n    # --- minified bundles and source maps --------------------------------------------------\n    r\"|\\.min\\.(?:js|mjs|cjs|css)$\"\n    r\"|\\.map$\"\n    # --- lockfiles, anchored so a repo-relative or nested path both match -------------------\n    r\"|(?:^|/)\" + _LOCKFILES + r\"$\"\n)\n\n\ndef isvendor(path: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True when a grep hit at this path is vendored, minified or a lockfile.\n\n    `path` is repo-relative, matching how tools/_istest.py is called.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not path:\n        return False\n    return _RX.search(path.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\")) is not None\n\n\n# A single physical line this long with no whitespace is minified regardless of its path — this\n# catches generated bundles that live outside any vendor directory. Deliberately generous: real\n# source lines run long (URLs, base64 fixtures, long string literals), and a false positive here\n# suppresses a hit, so the bar is set where only machine-generated output clears it.\n_MINIFIED_LINE_CHARS = 400\n\n\ndef isminified_line(text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True when the matched LINE itself looks machine-generated rather than authored.\"\"\"\n    if len(text) < _MINIFIED_LINE_CHARS:\n        return False\n    # Authored code of this length still breaks into words; minified output does not.\n    return (text.count(\" \") / len(text)) < 0.02\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1592,"cache_read_input_tokens":945949,"output_tokens":2853,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1592,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2853,"cache_read_input_tokens":945949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1592},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdqnkEoGWxk27vWKptv5F"