{"parentUuid":"16723185-ed52-4a26-832f-5a69bf7fce7c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdqoB4yNGibFkM37RK2rE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Plan progress — 2 done, 5 dead, 6 open**\n\n| # | item | status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4.3a | rebuild stale binary | ✅ done |\n| 4.1c | `graph grep` vendor/minified filter | ✅ done — `1075f1d9` |\n| 4.1a | bodies rank 5→2 | ❌ dead — bytes past line 50 never billed |\n| 4.2a | `TOPK` 5→8 | ❌ dead — rank 6+ reaches agent 2/33 |\n| 4.2c | VERIFY coverage | ❌ dropped (your call) |\n| — | answers-first reorder | ❌ reverted |\n| **4.4a** | **recover 287 dropped sessions** | ❌ **dead — see below** |\n| 4.4b | turn-cap censoring (2.75× arm-skewed) | ⬜ next |\n| 4.4c | byte-count patch gate | ⬜ |\n| 4.2b | FILE OUTLINE default on | ⬜ |\n| 4.1b | `--format` json→text default | ⬜ |\n| 4.3b | fix `AGENTS.md:72` | ⬜ |\n| 4.3c | document `verify`/`changed`/`def` | ⬜ |\n\n**Changed: 4.4a is dead, and the plan overstated it twice.**\n\n- **The headline cell is already complete**: REP50 is **49/49 on all four arms**. Recovery adds *zero* power to the number everything is argued from.\n- The real recoverable count is **107, not 287**, and it's concentrated in **GEM300** (43) and the **SW model-sweep** cells (42) — Gemini and Fable, not the Opus cell.\n- `tools/recover_from_transcripts.py` **already exists** and documents this exact failure mode, so it wasn't unbuilt work either.\n\nI also nearly filed a false report: my first scan used the wrong directory depth and claimed rep50 was 49-missing-of-49. Caught it against the explicit per-arm count before reporting it as fact.\n\nThat's the fifth plan item to die on contact. The pattern is consistent — items sourced from a subagent's framing rather than from data I'd checked myself.\n\nNext: **4.4b turn-cap censoring** — eg hits `error_max_turns` 2.75× more often than baseline and those pairs are deleted, which removes eg's *wor