{"parentUuid":"658a3e86-768e-4448-9a0f-534ffdc51cb3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/AGENTS.md","snippet":"64\t\n65\t```sh\n66\tentire graph symbols --repo . --format ndjson [--worktree]\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\t**When:** you need the complete definition inventory (e.g. ingesting into a store), not a single lookup.\n70\t\n71\t### 🔗 edges — *relations*\n72\tRelation records across all 30 types (`CALLS`, `IMPORTS`, `EXTENDS`, `HANDLES_ROUTE`, …), each tagged with resolution and confidence, plus the call-site `evidence` for resolved calls. Unfiltered it is the **whole-repo stream**, but it also takes `--to`, `--from` and `--relation`, and that is the ONLY route to the 13 relation types no other verb surfaces (`READS_FIELD`, `WRITES_FIELD`, `ACCESSES`, `HANDLES_ROUTE`, `HANDLES_GRPC`/`GRAPHQL`/`TRPC`, `HTTP_CALLS`, `EMITS`, `LISTENS_ON`, `HANDLES_TOOL`, `RESOURCE_DEPENDS_ON`, `DEFINES`):\n73\t\n74\t```sh\n75\tentire graph edges --repo . --to NAME --relation CALLS --format ndjson   # who calls NAME\n76\tentire graph edges --repo . --from NAME --relation IMPORTS --format ndjson\n77\t```\n78\t\n79\tFor a single symbol's callers/callees `neighbors` is still the better answer — it resolves definitions and prints locations. Reach for `edges --to/--relation` when you want a relation type `neighbors` does not expose, or the raw evidence records.\n80\t\n81\t```sh\n82\tentire graph edges --repo . --format ndjson [--worktree]\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\t**When:** you want every relation (bulk export / ingestion). For a targeted question, use `neighbors`.\n86\t\n87\t### 🗺️ snapshot — *the whole graph*\n88\tOne header record, then file, external-endpoint, symbol, and relation records, streamed so memory stays bounded. Superset of `symbols` + `edges` + files.\n89\t"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"80615bce-5fc1-4853-ba19-0b6155026286","timestamp":"2026-08-08T19:18:46.671Z","session_id":"0d4c4262-2100-4779-8745-e855e0a78208","u